{"global_index": "GeoBench_15", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When Mount Vesuvius erupted in 79 A.D., most people were killed by\n\nOptions: \nA. lava\nB. pyroclastic flow\nC. volcanic rock\nD. poisonous volcanic gases\nE. the hysterical crowd running toward the sea\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Most people were killed by pyroclastic flows, which are fast-moving currents of hot gas and volcanic matter that can reach high speeds and temperatures. These flows were the primary cause of death during the eruption, rather than lava or other volcanic phenomena.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 117, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 175}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Most people were killed by pyroclastic flows, which are fast-moving currents of hot gas and volcanic matter that can reach high speeds and temperatures. These flows were the primary cause of death during the eruption, rather than lava or other volcanic phenomena.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.235e-05}}
{"global_index": "GeoBench_691", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: From a linguistic perspective, the birth of modern English is typically dated to which year?\n\nOptions: \nA. 711 c.e.\nB. 814 c.e.\nC. 1066 c.e.\nD. 1492 c.e.\nE. 1588 c.e.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The birth of modern English is typically dated to the year 1066 c.e., which marks the Norman Conquest of England. This event introduced a significant influx of Norman French vocabulary and influences into the English language, leading to the development of Middle English and eventually modern English. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{C}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 186}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The birth of modern English is typically dated to the year 1066 c.e., which marks the Norman Conquest of England. This event introduced a significant influx of Norman French vocabulary and influences into the English language, leading to the development of Middle English and eventually modern English. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{C}.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.7600000000000004e-05}}
{"global_index": "GeoBench_815", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The primary purpose of the European Court of Justice is to\n\nOptions: \nA. ensure that no taxes or tariffs are charged on goods and services that cross the internal borders of the European Union\nB. provide a legal venue for cases between litigants in separate European Union member states\nC. set the European Union's annual policy agenda\nD. propose and approve laws within the European Union\nE. act as the executive branch of the European Union to enact programs and enforce regulations set by the European Union Parliament and Counci\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The primary purpose of the European Court of Justice is to provide a legal venue for cases between litigants in separate EU member states, ensuring the uniform interpretation and application of EU law across the member states. This role is crucial for upholding the rule of law within the EU.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 168, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 232}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The primary purpose of the European Court of Justice is to provide a legal venue for cases between litigants in separate EU member states, ensuring the uniform interpretation and application of EU law across the member states. This role is crucial for upholding the rule of law within the EU.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.36e-05}}
{"global_index": "GeoBench_1040", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When Norman Borlaug developed new wheat strains, he most directly\n\nOptions: \nA. saved almost a million people worldwide from mass starvation\nB. showed that GMO crops were commercially viable\nC. transformed Mexico from an importer to an exporter of wheat\nD. spurred the popularity of heirloom crops on organic farms\nE. helped create the so-called \"noodle line\" in China\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Norman Borlaug's development of new wheat strains, particularly during the Green Revolution, played a crucial role in increasing agricultural yields, which in turn helped prevent mass starvation in various parts of the world. While options C and B may also reflect his contributions, option A directly highlights the global impact of his work on food security.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 142, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 217}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Norman Borlaug's development of new wheat strains, particularly during the Green Revolution, played a crucial role in increasing agricultural yields, which in turn helped prevent mass starvation in various parts of the world. While options C and B may also reflect his contributions, option A directly highlights the global impact of his work on food security.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.63e-05}}
{"global_index": "GeoBench_444", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The replacement birth rate is always\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\nB. the number an industrial country allows each couple\nC. one-half the number of children a couple has\nD. the number of children a couple needs to replace themselves in a population\nE. the number of grandchildren divided by the number of parents\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The replacement birth rate refers to the number of children each couple needs to have in order to maintain a stable population, accounting for mortality rates. Typically, this figure is around 2.1 children per couple in developed countries to ensure that each generation can replace itself.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 191}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The replacement birth rate refers to the number of children each couple needs to have in order to maintain a stable population, accounting for mortality rates. Typically, this figure is around 2.1 children per couple in developed countries to ensure that each generation can replace itself.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.6550000000000006e-05}}
