{"global_index": "GeoBench_881", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The long-term demographic effect of the One-Child Policy in China has been\n\nOptions: \nA. large-scale out-migration of Chinese to foreign countries\nB. reduction of the total fertility rate below the replacement rate\nC. mass rural-to-urban migration\nD. smaller total population of China\nE. in-migration of foreign guest workers to fill low-paying service jobs\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The One-Child Policy significantly reduced the total fertility rate in China, resulting in rates that have fallen below the replacement level necessary to maintain the population. This demographic shift has contributed to an aging population and future challenges related to workforce sustainability.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 140, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 196}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The One-Child Policy significantly reduced the total fertility rate in China, resulting in rates that have fallen below the replacement level necessary to maintain the population. This demographic shift has contributed to an aging population and future challenges related to workforce sustainability.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.46e-05}}
