{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2994", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the physiological basis of allergies? What measures can be taken to decrease the effect of allergies?\n\nOptions: \nA. Allergies are adverse immunological responses to antigens. Antihistamines and desensitization therapy can help decrease the effect of allergies.\nB. Allergies are triggered by the body's overproduction of white blood cells. Avoiding allergens and taking vitamin supplements can decrease the effect of allergies.\nC. Allergies are caused by genetic mutations and can be minimized by regular exercise and a healthy diet.\nD. Allergies can be fully cured with antihistamines.\nE. Allergies are caused by exposure to pathogens.\nF. Allergies develop due to an overactive nervous system. Beta-blockers and nerve-calming medications can help mitigate the effects of allergies.\nG. Allergies are a result of lack of immune response.\nH. Allergies are psychosomatic and can be managed through stress reduction techniques and meditation.\nI. Allergies result from the body's inability to produce sufficient antibodies. Immunoglobulin therapy can help decrease the effect of allergies.\nJ. Allergies are the body's natural response to environmental pollutants. Using air purifiers and avoiding outdoor activities can reduce allergy symptoms.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Allergies are indeed adverse immunological responses to antigens, typically due to an overreaction of the immune system to harmless substances. Treatment options like antihistamines and desensitization therapy are effective measures to alleviate allergy symptoms.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 303, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 358}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Allergies are indeed adverse immunological responses to antigens, typically due to an overreaction of the immune system to harmless substances. Treatment options like antihistamines and desensitization therapy are effective measures to alleviate allergy symptoms.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.845000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2765", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the physiological purpose of shivering?\n\nOptions: \nA. Shivering is a method the body uses to relieve pain.\nB. Shivering is a tactic to ward off predators by appearing agitated.\nC. Shivering is a way to burn excess calories\nD. Shivering is a response to fear or anxiety\nE. Shivering is an involuntary action to prepare muscles for physical activity.\nF. Shivering is a means by which the body maintains its normal temperature when the ambient temperature is cold.\nG. Shivering is a strategy to reduce body temperature in hot environments.\nH. Shivering is a side effect of the body's immune response to infections.\nI. Shivering is a reaction to high body temperature\nJ. Shivering is a reflex that helps to increase oxygen intake.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Shivering is a physiological response that occurs when the body is exposed to cold temperatures, helping to generate heat through involuntary muscle contractions to maintain normal body temperature. This is an essential mechanism for thermoregulation in cold environments.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 223, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 277}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Shivering is a physiological response that occurs when the body is exposed to cold temperatures, helping to generate heat through involuntary muscle contractions to maintain normal body temperature. This is an essential mechanism for thermoregulation in cold environments.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.585e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2997", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How has the action of reverse transcriptase been exploited by biologists?\n\nOptions: \nA. Reverse transcriptase is employed to directly replicate DNA in PCR amplifications.\nB. Reverse transcriptase is applied in the creation of vaccines by altering DNA sequences.\nC. Reverse transcriptase catalyzes the synthesis of DNA from RNA and is a necessary reagent for genetic engineering with recombinant DNA.\nD. Reverse transcriptase is used to transcribe DNA from proteins\nE. Reverse transcriptase is used to convert lipids into DNA for genome mapping.\nF. Reverse transcriptase is utilized to enhance the mutation rate in organisms for evolutionary studies.\nG. Reverse transcriptase is used to transcribe proteins from DNA\nH. Reverse transcriptase is used for converting mRNA into proteins in vitro.\nI. Reverse transcriptase is used in the manufacturing of synthetic RNA for therapeutic purposes.\nJ. Reverse transcriptase is primarily used in the study of retroviruses\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Reverse transcriptase catalyzes the synthesis of DNA from RNA, which is crucial for creating complementary DNA (cDNA) from mRNA, a common step in various genetic engineering techniques. This process is essential for cloning, gene expression analysis, and constructing recombinant DNA molecules.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 250, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 315}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Reverse transcriptase catalyzes the synthesis of DNA from RNA, which is crucial for creating complementary DNA (cDNA) from mRNA, a common step in various genetic engineering techniques. This process is essential for cloning, gene expression analysis, and constructing recombinant DNA molecules.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.649999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3086", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements concerning a sarcomere of a striated muscle (such as skeletal muscle) is correct?\n\nOptions: \nA. The A band shortens during muscle contraction.\nB. During contraction H zones become elongated.\nC. The proteins troponin and tropomyosin constitute the thick and thin filaments, respectively.\nD. Myosin filaments are found in the I band.\nE. Troponin and tropomyosin are located in the H zone.\nF. Tropomyosin binds to myosin, blocking the actin-binding site.\nG. The thin filaments are composed entirely of myosin.\nH. In the relaxed position tropomyosin impedes myosin's access to the binding site of actin.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. In the relaxed state of a muscle, tropomyosin blocks the binding sites on actin, preventing myosin from interacting with actin. This mechanism ensures that contraction only occurs when calcium ions bind to troponin, which then shifts tropomyosin away from the binding sites.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 278}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. In the relaxed state of a muscle, tropomyosin blocks the binding sites on actin, preventing myosin from interacting with actin. This mechanism ensures that contraction only occurs when calcium ions bind to troponin, which then shifts tropomyosin away from the binding sites.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.094999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2830", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Distinguish betweenpenetranceand expressivity.\n\nOptions: \nA. Penetrance refers to how widespread a trait is within a population, while expressivity measures the intensity of the trait.\nB. Penetrance is the physical appearance resulting from a genotype, while expressivity is the genetic makeup of an organism.\nC. Penetrance is the measure of the strength of a gene's effect, while expressivity is the measure of the stability of a gene's expression across generations.\nD. Penetrance is the percentage of individuals who carry a gene and express it phenotypically, while expressivity is the degree of effect or the extent to which a gene expresses itself in different individuals.\nE. Expressivity is the proportion of individuals in a population who show a particular trait, whereas penetrance is the range of manifestations of a gene in different tissues.\nF. Penetrance and expressivity are the same.\nG. Penetrance is the consistency of a gene's expression across different environments, while expressivity is the ability of a gene to be suppressed by other genes.\nH. Penetrance is the likelihood that a trait will appear in the offspring, whereas expressivity is the range of phenotypes resulting from a given genotype.\nI. Penetrance is the degree of effect or the extent to which a gene expresses itself in different individuals, while expressivity is the percentage of individuals who carry a gene and express it phenotypically.\nJ. Expressivity is the probability of a gene being inherited, and penetrance is the variability of a trait's expression among individuals.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Penetrance measures the proportion of individuals with a particular genotype that express the corresponding phenotype, while expressivity refers to the degree or intensity of that phenotype in individuals who do express it. This distinction highlights the difference between simply having a trait and how that trait manifests in different individuals.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 381, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 446}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Penetrance measures the proportion of individuals with a particular genotype that express the corresponding phenotype, while expressivity refers to the degree or intensity of that phenotype in individuals who do express it. This distinction highlights the difference between simply having a trait and how that trait manifests in different individuals.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.614999999999998e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2818", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A competitive inhibitor of an enzyme exerts its effect by\n\nOptions: \nA. reversibly modifying some of the amino acid residues that help to comprise the enzyme's active site\nB. irreversibly forming covalent links with the enzyme, effectively preventing the enzyme's dissociation from it\nC. irreversibly modifying some of the amino acid residues that help to comprise the enzyme's active site\nD. reversibly increasing the number of enzyme molecules that are available to bind substrates\nE. irreversibly decreasing the number of enzyme molecules that are available to bind substrates\nF. competing with the product molecule for the same enzyme but a different binding site than the product binding site\nG. competing with the substrate molecule for the same enzyme but a different binding site than the substrate binding site\nH. irreversibly forming covalent links with the substrate, effectively preventing the enzyme's dissociation from it\nI. reversibly decreasing the number of enzyme molecules that are available to bind substrates\nJ. competing with the substrate molecule for the same enzyme and the same binding site as the substrate binding site\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. A competitive inhibitor works by competing with the substrate for the same active site on the enzyme, which reduces the likelihood of substrate binding and thus slows down the reaction rate. This type of inhibition is typically reversible, as increasing substrate concentration can overcome the inhibition.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 284, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 343}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. A competitive inhibitor works by competing with the substrate for the same active site on the enzyme, which reduces the likelihood of substrate binding and thus slows down the reaction rate. This type of inhibition is typically reversible, as increasing substrate concentration can overcome the inhibition.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.8e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2914", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Both food and air pass through the pharynx. Explain how these are channeled into the proper tubes so that the food goes into the stomach and the air goes to the lungs.\n\nOptions: \nA. Food and air take turns entering the pharynx based on the body's breathing and digestive rhythm\nB. Food and air are separated by a valve in the esophagus\nC. The trachea has a filter mechanism that directs food to the stomach and air to the lungs\nD. A series of small cilia in the pharynx sorts food and air into their respective tubes\nE. The epiglottis closes the entrance to the trachea during breathing, ensuring air goes to the lungs and food to the stomach\nF. Food and air are channeled by distinct muscular contractions that guide them to the correct passages\nG. The esophagus expands to receive food while the trachea contracts to guide air\nH. The pharynx separates food and air based on their weight\nI. The larynx moves up so that the glottis is closed by the epiglottis during swallowing, directing food into the esophagus and air into the lungs.\nJ. The lungs filter out food particles from the air\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. During swallowing, the larynx moves up, causing the epiglottis to close over the glottis, which directs food into the esophagus and allows air to enter the trachea and flow to the lungs. This mechanism ensures that food and air do not enter the same passage at the same time, preventing choking.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 317, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 393}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. During swallowing, the larynx moves up, causing the epiglottis to close over the glottis, which directs food into the esophagus and allows air to enter the trachea and flow to the lungs. This mechanism ensures that food and air do not enter the same passage at the same time, preventing choking.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.315e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2869", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In most ecosystems, net primary productivity is important because it represents the\n\nOptions: \nA. biomass of all producers\nB. biomass of all consumers\nC. energy available to heterotrophs\nD. energy consumed by decomposers\nE. total solar energy converted to chemical energy by producers\nF. energy available to producers\nG. energy available to autotrophs\nH. total energy lost during energy transfer between trophic levels\nI. total energy produced by autotrophs and heterotrophs combined\nJ. energy stored in the soil\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Net primary productivity (NPP) measures the amount of energy that remains in the ecosystem after plant respiration, which is available to support heterotrophs (consumers) in the food web. Therefore, it is crucial for understanding the energy flow within ecosystems.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 177, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 238}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Net primary productivity (NPP) measures the amount of energy that remains in the ecosystem after plant respiration, which is available to support heterotrophs (consumers) in the food web. Therefore, it is crucial for understanding the energy flow within ecosystems.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.314999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3059", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Chromosomal sex in mammals has been shown to be strongly Y chromosome determined. How was this shown to be true?\n\nOptions: \nA. The absence of a Y chromosome determines maleness in mammals\nB. The presence of a Y chromosome usually determines maleness in mammals\nC. The ratio of two X chromosomes to one Y chromosome determines maleness\nD. The presence of an X chromosome determines maleness in mammals\nE. The presence of an X chromosome in the absence of a Y chromosome determines maleness\nF. The presence of a Y chromosome determines femaleness in mammals\nG. The presence of a Y chromosome has no impact on the determination of maleness\nH. The presence of multiple X chromosomes without a Y chromosome determines maleness\nI. The presence of two or more Y chromosomes is required for maleness\nJ. The presence of an X chromosome determines femaleness in mammals\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The presence of a Y chromosome usually determines maleness in mammals, as it carries the SRY gene which initiates the male sexual development pathway. In the absence of a Y chromosome, females typically develop due to the lack of male-determining signals.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 246, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 306}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The presence of a Y chromosome usually determines maleness in mammals, as it carries the SRY gene which initiates the male sexual development pathway. In the absence of a Y chromosome, females typically develop due to the lack of male-determining signals.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.290000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2663", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why are the elements carbon, hydrogen, oxygen, and nitrogen (C, H, O, N) of immense importance in living matter ?\n\nOptions: \nA. These elements are the only elements that can form gases at room temperature\nB. These elements are abundant in living organisms, can readily form covalent bonds and are the lightest elements that can form such bonds.\nC. These elements are the primary sources of energy for living organisms\nD. These elements are radioactive, which is vital for cellular processes\nE. These elements are capable of undergoing sublimation, which is crucial for life functions\nF. These elements are rare and thus more valuable\nG. These elements give color to living organisms\nH. These elements can only be found in DNA and proteins\nI. These elements are the heaviest elements in living organisms\nJ. These elements have magnetic properties that are essential for life\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Carbon, hydrogen, oxygen, and nitrogen are abundant in living organisms, can readily form covalent bonds, and are the lightest elements that can form such bonds, making them fundamental building blocks for various biological molecules like proteins, nucleic acids, and carbohydrates. This versatility allows for the complexity and diversity of life.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 243, "output_tokens": 74, "total_tokens": 317}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Carbon, hydrogen, oxygen, and nitrogen are abundant in living organisms, can readily form covalent bonds, and are the lightest elements that can form such bonds, making them fundamental building blocks for various biological molecules like proteins, nucleic acids, and carbohydrates. This versatility allows for the complexity and diversity of life.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.084999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3131", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sea divers are aware of a danger known as the \"bends\". Explain the physiological mechanism of the bends.\n\nOptions: \nA. Carbon dioxide bubbles forming in the blood causing acidosis\nB. Rapid increase in barometric pressure causing the bends\nC. Formation of helium bubbles in the bloodstream due to rapid ascent\nD. Increased salinity in the water leading to dehydration and joint pain\nE. Oxygen bubbles forming in the blood leading to hypoxia\nF. Lack of oxygen while breathing under high pressure leading to the bends\nG. Accumulation of lactic acid in muscles due to strenuous activity underwater\nH. Sudden decrease in water temperature causing muscle cramping and disorientation\nI. Rise in blood pressure due to underwater currents, resulting in the bends\nJ. Bubbles of nitrogen gas form in the blood and other tissue fluids when the barometric pressure drops below the total pressure of all gases dissolved in the body fluids, causing dizziness, paralysis, and unconsciousness, known as the bends.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\). The bends, or decompression sickness, occurs when a diver ascends too quickly, causing nitrogen gas that is dissolved in body fluids to form bubbles as pressure decreases. These bubbles can lead to severe physiological issues, including dizziness, paralysis, and unconsciousness.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 266, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 328}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\). The bends, or decompression sickness, occurs when a diver ascends too quickly, causing nitrogen gas that is dissolved in body fluids to form bubbles as pressure decreases. These bubbles can lead to severe physiological issues, including dizziness, paralysis, and unconsciousness.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.71e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3199", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement about the beak size of finches on the island of Daphne Major during prolonged drought is true?\n\nOptions: \nA. Each bird's beak size increased due to the abundance of food during the drought.\nB. Each bird developed a deeper, stronger beak as the drought persisted.\nC. Each bird's beak became weaker and narrower as the drought persisted.\nD. Each bird evolved a deeper, stronger beak as the drought persisted.\nE. Each bird's survival was not influenced by the depth and strength of its beak during the drought.\nF. Each bird that survived the drought produced only offspring with deeper, stronger beaks than seen in the previous generation.\nG. Each bird's beak size did not change during the drought.\nH. Each bird's survival was strongly influenced by the depth and strength of its beak as the drought persisted.\nI. Each bird's survival was only influenced by its ability to find water during the drought, not the size of its beak.\nJ. Each bird that survived the drought produced offspring with the same beak size as seen in the previous generation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. During prolonged drought conditions on Daphne Major, finches with deeper and stronger beaks were better suited to access the limited food resources available, which significantly influenced their survival. Therefore, the survival of these birds was strongly linked to the depth and strength of their beaks.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 288, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 350}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. During prolonged drought conditions on Daphne Major, finches with deeper and stronger beaks were better suited to access the limited food resources available, which significantly influenced their survival. Therefore, the survival of these birds was strongly linked to the depth and strength of their beaks.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.04e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3242", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Euglena is a common green flagellate protozoan found in fresh water ponds. Describe briefly the method of locomotion, nutrition, and asexual reproduction in this organism.\n\nOptions: \nA. Euglena moves by contracting its body, carries on heterotrophic nutrition, and reproduces asexually through fragmentation.\nB. Euglena moves by flagellum, carries on autotrophic nutrition and can switch to heterotrophic when necessary, and reproduces asexually through cytokinesis.\nC. Euglena moves by pseudopodia, carries on heterotrophic nutrition, and reproduces sexually.\nD. Euglena moves by flagellum, carries on autotrophic nutrition but cannot shift to heterotrophic, and reproduces asexually through budding.\nE. Euglena moves by flagellum, carries on chemosynthetic nutrition, and reproduces asexually through sporulation.\nF. Euglena moves by undulating its flagellum, carries on autotrophic nutrition but can shift to heterotrophic under darkness, and reproduces asexually through longitudinal binary fission.\nG. Euglena moves by jet propulsion, carries on autotrophic nutrition, and reproduces asexually through multiple fission.\nH. Euglena moves by cilia, carries on autotrophic nutrition but can shift to heterotrophic under light, and reproduces asexually through binary fission.\nI. Euglena moves by gliding along surfaces, carries on autotrophic nutrition but can shift to heterotrophic in the absence of light, and reproduces asexually through budding.\nJ. Euglena moves by flagellum, carries on mixotrophic nutrition, and reproduces asexually through longitudinal binary fission and sporulation.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Euglena is known for its locomotion via a flagellum, its ability to perform autotrophic nutrition (photosynthesis) and switch to heterotrophic nutrition when light is not available, and it reproduces asexually through cytokinesis (binary fission). This aligns with the characteristics of Euglena as a unicellular organism adaptable to its environment.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 425, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 507}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Euglena is known for its locomotion via a flagellum, its ability to perform autotrophic nutrition (photosynthesis) and switch to heterotrophic nutrition when light is not available, and it reproduces asexually through cytokinesis (binary fission). This aligns with the characteristics of Euglena as a unicellular organism adaptable to its environment.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00011294999999999998}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3081", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Crossing-over during meiosis permits scientists to determine\n\nOptions: \nA. the rate of mutations\nB. the chance for variation in zygotes\nC. the age of an organism\nD. the potential for genetic disorders\nE. the sequence of DNA bases\nF. the rate of cell division\nG. the number of chromosomes in a cell\nH. which traits are dominant or recessive\nI. the sex of an organism\nJ. the distance between genes on a chromosome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\). Crossing-over during meiosis allows scientists to understand the genetic linkage between genes and can be used to estimate the distance between genes on a chromosome, as the frequency of crossing-over correlates with the distance between them. This information is critical for constructing genetic maps.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 163, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 225}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\). Crossing-over during meiosis allows scientists to understand the genetic linkage between genes and can be used to estimate the distance between genes on a chromosome, as the frequency of crossing-over correlates with the distance between them. This information is critical for constructing genetic maps.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.165000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3141", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which statement about variation is true?\n\nOptions: \nA. All phenotypic variation is the result of genotypic variation.\nB. All genetic variation produces phenotypic variation.\nC. All nucleotide variability results in neutral variation.\nD. All new alleles are the result of nucleotide variability.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. New alleles arise through mutations that alter nucleotide sequences, leading to nucleotide variability. While not all nucleotide changes translate to phenotypic variation, all new alleles are indeed the result of such genetic changes.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 172}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. New alleles arise through mutations that alter nucleotide sequences, leading to nucleotide variability. While not all nucleotide changes translate to phenotypic variation, all new alleles are indeed the result of such genetic changes.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.8299999999999995e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3210", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Differentiate clearly between \"breathing\" and \"respiration\".\n\nOptions: \nA. Breathing is the chemical process that occurs within cells, while respiration is the physical movement of the diaphragm and rib muscles.\nB. Respiration only occurs in the presence of oxygen, while breathing can occur without oxygen.\nC. Breathing refers to the exchange of gases between cells and environment, while respiration is the mechanical process of taking air into the lungs and expelling it.\nD. Respiration refers to the oxidative degradation of nutrients in cells or the exchange of gases between cells and environment, while breathing is the mechanical process of taking air into the lungs and expelling it.\nE. Respiration and breathing are the same process.\nF. Respiration is the process by which organisms produce sound, while breathing is solely for gas exchange purposes.\nG. Breathing is the process of breaking down food into energy, while respiration is the act of air moving in and out of the lungs.\nH. Respiration is an energy consuming process, while breathing results in energy production in the cells.\nI. Breathing involves the conversion of glucose to energy within the mitochondria, while respiration is the act of inhaling and exhaling air.\nJ. Respiration is a voluntary action controlled by the nervous system, while breathing is an involuntary process controlled by the brain stem.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Respiration encompasses both the biochemical process of energy production through the breakdown of nutrients in cells (often involving the exchange of gases like oxygen and carbon dioxide) and can happen outside the lungs. In contrast, breathing specifically refers to the mechanical act of inhaling and exhaling air into and out of the lungs.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 333, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 403}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Respiration encompasses both the biochemical process of energy production through the breakdown of nutrients in cells (often involving the exchange of gases like oxygen and carbon dioxide) and can happen outside the lungs. In contrast, breathing specifically refers to the mechanical act of inhaling and exhaling air into and out of the lungs.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.195e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3200", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The average birth weight for human babies is about 3 kg. Which of the following terms best describes this?\n\nOptions: \nA. disruptive selection\nB. sexual selection\nC. bottleneck effect\nD. non-random mating\nE. stabilizing selection\nF. genetic drift\nG. directional selection\nH. founder effect\nI. diversifying selection\nJ. artificial selection\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Stabilizing selection refers to a type of natural selection that favors the average traits in a population and reduces variation. In this case, average birth weight of around 3 kg is favorable for survival, leading to a selection against extremes (very low or very high birth weights).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 142, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 205}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Stabilizing selection refers to a type of natural selection that favors the average traits in a population and reduces variation. In this case, average birth weight of around 3 kg is favorable for survival, leading to a selection against extremes (very low or very high birth weights).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.91e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2989", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All linear genomes share a common problem of replication. Define the problem and describe how the process of reverse transcriptionelegantly solves it.\n\nOptions: \nA. The challenge for all linear genomes is that the DNA polymerases cannot initiate replication de novo. Retroviruses counteract this by using a protein to initiate the synthesis.\nB. The problem with all linear genomes is the inability to replicate without the presence of primer sequences. Retroviruses address this by creating a primer from an RNA template.\nC. The problem faced by all linear genomes is maintaining the structure of the genome. Retroviruses solved this problem by strengthening the bonds between nucleotides.\nD. The difficulty with linear genomes is the formation of secondary structures that impede replication. Retroviruses prevent this by using reverse transcriptase to unwind these structures.\nE. The issue faced by all linear genomes is replication speed. Retroviruses solved this problem by making the process more efficient.\nF. The problem faced by all linear genomes is avoiding mutations. Retroviruses solved this problem with an error-checking mechanism.\nG. Linear genomes face the challenge of DNA damage during replication, which can lead to cell death. Retroviruses have evolved a robust repair system to address this.\nH. All linear genomes struggle with the degradation of DNA at the ends during replication. Retroviruses circumvent this by integrating their DNA into the host genome.\nI. Linear genomes cannot replicate the very ends of the DNA strands, known as the end-replication problem. Retroviruses solve this by adding repeated sequences to the ends of the DNA.\nJ. The problem faced by all linear genomes is replicating the entire genome without loss of information from the ends. Retroviruses solved this problem simply by copying the 5' end before copying the rest of the strand.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Linear genomes face the end-replication problem, where DNA polymerases cannot fully replicate the ends of the strands, potentially leading to the loss of genetic information. Retroviruses effectively address this by integrating their RNA genome into the host genome, allowing them to replicate without losing essential sequences.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 425, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 491}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Linear genomes face the end-replication problem, where DNA polymerases cannot fully replicate the ends of the strands, potentially leading to the loss of genetic information. Retroviruses effectively address this by integrating their RNA genome into the host genome, allowing them to replicate without losing essential sequences.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00010334999999999999}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3065", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Arthropods have an exoskeleton. How is movement accomplished?\n\nOptions: \nA. They use their wings to move\nB. They move by changing the shape of their exoskeleton\nC. They use cilia on the surface of their exoskeleton to move\nD. They move due to their muscular system\nE. They have a soft, pliable inner layer that bends to facilitate movement\nF. Movement is achieved through hydraulic pressure changes within each segment\nG. They release a special fluid that lubricates the joints of the exoskeleton for movement\nH. The exoskeleton contracts and expands allowing for movement\nI. Movement is achieved by the exoskeleton splitting and reforming in new positions\nJ. The body is segmented and the segments are joined by a thin layer of flexible chitin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Arthropods move due to their muscular system, which works in conjunction with the rigid exoskeleton to produce movement. Muscles contract and pull on the exoskeleton at attachment points, allowing for various forms of movement.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 230, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 286}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Arthropods move due to their muscular system, which works in conjunction with the rigid exoskeleton to produce movement. Muscles contract and pull on the exoskeleton at attachment points, allowing for various forms of movement.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.81e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2682", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The tandem back-and-forth evolution of closely related species, which is exemplified by predator-prey relationships.\n\nOptions: \nA. Microevolution\nB. Speciation\nC. Coevolution\nD. Adaptive radiation\nE. Macroevolution\nF. Convergent evolution\nG. Gradual evolution\nH. Punctuated equilibrium\nI. Divergent evolution\nJ. Parallel evolution\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Coevolution refers to the reciprocal evolutionary changes that occur between closely related species, typically in the context of predator-prey interactions or mutualistic relationships. This phenomenon illustrates how the evolution of one species can directly influence the evolution of another.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 146, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 202}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Coevolution refers to the reciprocal evolutionary changes that occur between closely related species, typically in the context of predator-prey interactions or mutualistic relationships. This phenomenon illustrates how the evolution of one species can directly influence the evolution of another.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.5499999999999994e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2942", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Adrenalin is a hormone which stimulates the sympathetic system . What effects would you expect adrenaline tohave on (a) the digestive tract, (b) the iris of the eye, and (c) the heart beat?\n\nOptions: \nA. (a) Increases peristalsis and reduces secretion, (b) Causes both sets of muscles in the iris to relax, (c) Accelerates and weakens the heartbeat\nB. (a) Enhances digestion, (b) Causes the iris to change color, (c) Decreases the heart rate\nC. (a) No effect on the digestive tract, (b) Causes both sets of muscles in the iris to contract, (c) Slows the heart rate\nD. (a) Enhances digestion and secretion, (b) No effect on the muscles of the iris, (c) Accelerates the heart rate\nE. (a) No effect on the digestive tract, (b) Causes radial muscles to relax, resulting in constriction, (c) Decreases and strengthens the heartbeat\nF. (a) Slows peristalsis and reduces secretion, (b) Causes radial muscles to contract, resulting in dilation, (c) Accelerates and strengthens the heartbeat\nG. (a) Slows peristalsis and increases secretion, (b) Causes circular muscles to contract, resulting in dilation, (c) Slows and strengthens the heartbeat\nH. (a) Decreases peristalsis and has no effect on secretion, (b) Causes circular muscles to relax, resulting in dilation, (c) No change in the heart rate\nI. (a) Increases peristalsis and enhances secretion, (b) Causes circular muscles to contract, resulting in constriction, (c) Slows and weakens the heartbeat\nJ. (a) Increases peristalsis and enhances secretion, (b) Causes radial muscles to contract, resulting in constriction, (c) Accelerates the heart rate without changing its strength\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Adrenalin, being a hormone associated with the \"fight or flight\" response, typically slows peristalsis and reduces digestive secretions, causes dilation of the pupils through radial muscle contraction, and accelerates and strengthens the heartbeat. Thus, option F accurately reflects these physiological effects.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 480, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 548}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Adrenalin, being a hormone associated with the \"fight or flight\" response, typically slows peristalsis and reduces digestive secretions, causes dilation of the pupils through radial muscle contraction, and accelerates and strengthens the heartbeat. Thus, option F accurately reflects these physiological effects.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001128}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3196", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An eager AP Biology student interested in studying osmosis and the movement of water in solutions took a dialysis bag containing a 0.5 M solution and placed it into a beaker containing a 0.6 M solution. If this bag were instead placed into a beaker of distilled water, what would be the expected result?\n\nOptions: \nA. The bag will expand and eventually burst due to the pressure of water flow.\nB. The solute will flow into the dialysis bag from the beaker.\nC. The bag will remain the exact same size because no water will move at all.\nD. The bag will shrink in size and the beaker will overflow due to the movement of water.\nE. The solute will flow out of the dialysis bag into the beaker.\nF. The water will evaporate from the bag, leaving only the solute.\nG. There will be a net flow of water into the bag, causing it to swell in size.\nH. There will be a net flow of water out of the beaker, causing it to decrease in size.\nI. The water in the bag will freeze due to the change in environment.\nJ. There will be a net flow of water out of the bag, causing it to decrease in size.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The expected result is that there will be a net flow of water into the bag, causing it to swell in size, since the bag contains a higher solute concentration (0.5 M) than the distilled water (0 M). This movement occurs as water moves from areas of lower solute concentration to higher solute concentration to achieve equilibrium. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{G}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 319, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 399}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The expected result is that there will be a net flow of water into the bag, causing it to swell in size, since the bag contains a higher solute concentration (0.5 M) than the distilled water (0 M). This movement occurs as water moves from areas of lower solute concentration to higher solute concentration to achieve equilibrium. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{G}.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.585e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2891", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Pilocarpineis a drug that stimulates the nerve endings of parasympathetic nerves. What effects would you expect this drug to have on (a) the digestive tract, (b) the iris of the eye, and (c) the heart rate?\n\nOptions: \nA. (a) Facilitates digestion, (b) Reduces pupil size, (c) Slows and weakens the heart beat\nB. (a) No effect on digestion, (b) Dilates pupil, (c) Speeds up heart beat\nC. (a) Slows digestion, (b) No effect on pupil, (c) Slows and weakens the heart beat\nD. (a) Facilitates digestion, (b) Increases pupil size, (c) Stabilizes heart beat\nE. (a) Inhibits digestion, (b) No effect on pupil, (c) Stabilizes heart beat\nF. (a) Slows digestion, (b) Increases pupil size, (c) Increases heart beat\nG. (a) No effect on digestion, (b) Reduces pupil size, (c) Increases heart beat\nH. (a) Inhibits digestion, (b) Increases pupil size, (c) Stabilizes heart beat\nI. (a) Facilitates digestion, (b) No effect on pupil, (c) Speeds up heart beat\nJ. (a) Inhibits digestion, (b) Dilates pupil, (c) Slows and weakens the heart beat\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Pilocarpine is a parasympathomimetic drug that stimulates the digestive system, facilitating digestion. Additionally, it constricts the pupil and reduces heart rate, aligning with the effects described in option A.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 385, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 437}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Pilocarpine is a parasympathomimetic drug that stimulates the digestive system, facilitating digestion. Additionally, it constricts the pupil and reduces heart rate, aligning with the effects described in option A.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.895e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2688", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nerve outgrowth from a developing neuron begins at the growth cone, located at the tip of the axon. Microspikes of the growth cone extend and retract in order to move the growth cone forward. Exposure of the neuron to cytochasalin B at this stage of development causes\n\nOptions: \nA. microtubules in the growth cone to undergo reversible dissociation\nB. microtubules in the axon to undergo irreversible dissociation\nC. microfilaments in the growth cone to undergo irreversible depolymerization\nD. microfilaments in the axon to undergo reversible depolymerization\nE. microfilaments in the microspike to undergo reversible depolymerization\nF. microtubules in the microspike to undergo irreversible depolymerization\nG. microfilaments in the axon to undergo irreversible depolymerization\nH. microtubules in the microspike to undergo reversible depolymerization\nI. microfilaments in the microspike to undergo irreversible depolymerization\nJ. microtubules in the axon to undergo reversible dissociation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "Cytochalasins are known to inhibit actin polymerization, leading to the disruption of microfilaments. In this context, the correct answer is that exposure to cytochalasins B causes microfilaments in the growth cone to undergo irreversible depolymerization, which would affect the growth cone's ability to extend and retract its microspikes. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{I}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 297, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 381}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "Cytochalasins are known to inhibit actin polymerization, leading to the disruption of microfilaments. In this context, the correct answer is that exposure to cytochalasins B causes microfilaments in the growth cone to undergo irreversible depolymerization, which would affect the growth cone's ability to extend and retract its microspikes. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{I}.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.495e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2857", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Using conditioning, how can one determine the sensitivity of a dog's hearing to sounds of different frequencies?\n\nOptions: \nA. Through ultrasound examination\nB. Through blood sample analysis\nC. Through direct observation\nD. Through measuring brain wave activity in response to sounds\nE. Through operant conditioning\nF. Through x-ray examination\nG. Through auditory brainstem response (ABR) testing\nH. Through genetic testing\nI. Through a controlled environment listening test\nJ. Through behavioral observation in natural settings\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{I}. A controlled environment listening test allows for systematic evaluation of a dog's sensitivity to different sound frequencies, as it minimizes outside variables and focuses on the dog's responses to specific auditory stimuli. This method can effectively utilize conditioning techniques to assess the dog's hearing capabilities.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 166, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 225}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{I}. A controlled environment listening test allows for systematic evaluation of a dog's sensitivity to different sound frequencies, as it minimizes outside variables and focuses on the dog's responses to specific auditory stimuli. This method can effectively utilize conditioning techniques to assess the dog's hearing capabilities.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.03e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3167", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the probability that a face card is drawn on the first draw and an ace on the second in two consecutive draws, without replacement, from a standard deck of cards.\n\nOptions: \nA. 4 / 220\nB. 2 / 221\nC. 6 / 221\nD. 4 / 222\nE. 1 / 221\nF. 1 / 110\nG. 3 / 221\nH. 3 / 220\nI. 5 / 221\nJ. 4 / 221\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the probability of drawing a face card first and then an Ace second without replacement, we calculate the probabilities stepwise. There are 12 face cards (3 face cards in each of the 4 suits) and 4 Aces in a standard deck of 52 cards. The probability of drawing a face card first is \\( \\frac{12}{52} \\) and then the probability of drawing an Ace second (after removing one card) is \\( \\frac{4}{51} \\). Thus, the combined probability is \\( \\frac{12}{52} \\times \\frac{4}{51} = \\frac{48}{2652} = \\frac{4}{221} \\).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 179, "output_tokens": 157, "total_tokens": 336}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the probability of drawing a face card first and then an Ace second without replacement, we calculate the probabilities stepwise. There are 12 face cards (3 face cards in each of the 4 suits) and 4 Aces in a standard deck of 52 cards. The probability of drawing a face card first is \\( \\frac{12}{52} \\) and then the probability of drawing an Ace second (after removing one card) is \\( \\frac{4}{51} \\). Thus, the combined probability is \\( \\frac{12}{52} \\times \\frac{4}{51} = \\frac{48}{2652} = \\frac{4}{221} \\).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00012105}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3112", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the probability of getting exactly three heads infive flips of a balanced coin?\n\nOptions: \nA. 12.5 percent\nB. 40 percent\nC. 18.75 percent\nD. 25 percent\nE. 37.5 percent\nF. 10 percent\nG. 31.25 percent\nH. 50 percent\nI. 62.5 percent\nJ. 20 percent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the probability of getting exactly three heads in five flips of a balanced coin, we can use the binomial probability formula: \n\n\\[\nP(X = k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( n \\) is the number of trials, \\( k \\) is the number of successful trials (heads), and \\( p \\) is the probability of success on each trial. Here, \\( n = 5 \\), \\( k = 3 \\), and \\( p = 0.5 \\). Calculating this gives:\n\n\\[\nP(X = 3) = \\binom{5}{3} (0.5)^3 (0.5)^{2} = 10 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} = 10 \\cdot \\frac{1}{32} = \\frac{10}{32} = 0.3125\n\\]\n\nThus, the probability is 31.25%, which corresponds to option G. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 152, "output_tokens": 237, "total_tokens": 389}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the probability of getting exactly three heads in five flips of a balanced coin, we can use the binomial probability formula: \n\n\\[\nP(X = k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( n \\) is the number of trials, \\( k \\) is the number of successful trials (heads), and \\( p \\) is the probability of success on each trial. Here, \\( n = 5 \\), \\( k = 3 \\), and \\( p = 0.5 \\). Calculating this gives:\n\n\\[\nP(X = 3) = \\binom{5}{3} (0.5)^3 (0.5)^{2} = 10 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} = 10 \\cdot \\frac{1}{32} = \\frac{10}{32} = 0.3125\n\\]\n\nThus, the probability is 31.25%, which corresponds to option G. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.000165}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2995", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An ancient Egyptian mummy is found. A count of the radiationemitted from the C^14 in the body is only one eighth thatfound in persons who have died recently. About how old isthe mummy? (The half-life of C^14 is 5568 years.)\n\nOptions: \nA. 16,704 years old\nB. 8,284 years old\nC. 6,420 years old\nD. 20,136 years old\nE. 13,500 years old\nF. 22,176 years old\nG. 4,500 years old\nH. 18,950 years old\nI. 27,840 years old\nJ. 11,136 years old\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the age of the mummy, we can use the concept of half-lives. Since the amount of C^14 is one eighth of that found in recent persons, it means 3 half-lives have occurred (as \\((\\frac{1}{2})^3 = \\frac{1}{8}\\)). Therefore, the age of the mummy is \\(3 \\times 5568 = 16704\\) years.\n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 211, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 312}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the age of the mummy, we can use the concept of half-lives. Since the amount of C^14 is one eighth of that found in recent persons, it means 3 half-lives have occurred (as \\((\\frac{1}{2})^3 = \\frac{1}{8}\\)). Therefore, the age of the mummy is \\(3 \\times 5568 = 16704\\) years.\n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.224999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2811", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A piece of potato is dropped into a beaker of pure water. Which of the following describes the activity after the potato is immersed into the water?\n\nOptions: \nA. Water moves from the surrounding water into the potato.\nB. Solutes in the water move into the potato.\nC. No movement of water or solutes occurs.\nD. Potato cells plasmolyze.\nE. Solutes in the potato move into the water.\nF. Water and solutes move equally in both directions.\nG. The potato dissolves in the water.\nH. Water moves from the potato into the surrounding water.\nI. The potato absorbs all of the water.\nJ. The potato cells burst due to water intake.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. When a piece of potato is dropped into pure water, water moves from the surrounding water into the potato due to osmosis, as the concentration of solutes is higher inside the potato cells compared to the pure water. This process can lead to the potato swelling as it absorbs water.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 270}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. When a piece of potato is dropped into pure water, water moves from the surrounding water into the potato due to osmosis, as the concentration of solutes is higher inside the potato cells compared to the pure water. This process can lead to the potato swelling as it absorbs water.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.974999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3149", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The following pairs were placed in solution together. Which two could be separated by performing low-speed centrifugation?\n\nOptions: \nA. Golgi apparatus and endoplasmic reticulum\nB. Lysosomes and endosomes\nC. Plasma membrane and cytoskeleton\nD. DNA and mRNA\nE. Proteins and lipids\nF. Nuclei and secretory vesicles\nG. DNA and proteins\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The best choice for separation by low-speed centrifugation is F. Nuclei and secretory vesicles. Low-speed centrifugation typically allows for the separation of larger cellular components, such as nuclei, which will sediment faster than smaller vesicles like secretory vesicles. The other pairs contain components that are either too similar in size or not significantly different in density to be effectively separated by this method. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{F}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 148, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 242}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The best choice for separation by low-speed centrifugation is F. Nuclei and secretory vesicles. Low-speed centrifugation typically allows for the separation of larger cellular components, such as nuclei, which will sediment faster than smaller vesicles like secretory vesicles. The other pairs contain components that are either too similar in size or not significantly different in density to be effectively separated by this method. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{F}.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.859999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2899", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the probability of getting a 5 on each of two successive rolls of a balanced die?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 / 24\nB. 1 / 42\nC. 1 / 60\nD. 3 / 36\nE. 1 / 36\nF. 2 / 36\nG. 1 / 6\nH. 1 / 30\nI. 1 / 18\nJ. 1 / 12\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the probability of rolling a 5 on each of two successive rolls of a balanced die, we first calculate the probability of rolling a 5 on one roll, which is \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\). Since the rolls are independent, we multiply the probabilities: \\(\\frac{1}{6} \\times \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{36}\\). Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 165, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 260}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the probability of rolling a 5 on each of two successive rolls of a balanced die, we first calculate the probability of rolling a 5 on one roll, which is \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\). Since the rolls are independent, we multiply the probabilities: \\(\\frac{1}{6} \\times \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{36}\\). Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.175000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3109", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the probability of throwing at least one of the following totals on a single throw of a pair of dice: a total of 5, a total of 6, or a total of 7. Define the events A, B, and C as follows: Event A:atotal of 5 is thrown, Event B: a total of 6isthrown, Event C: a total of 7isthrown.\n\nOptions: \nA. 9 / 12\nB. 13 / 36\nC. 6 / 36\nD. 1 / 12\nE. 5 / 12\nF. 10 / 36\nG. 7 / 12\nH. 17 / 36\nI. 11 / 36\nJ. 4 / 36\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the probability of throwing at least one of the totals 5, 6, or 7 with a pair of dice, we first determine the number of combinations for each event:\n\n- Event A (total of 5): (1,4), (2,3), (3,2), (4,1) → 4 combinations\n- Event B (total of 6): (1,5), (2,4), (3,3), (4,2), (5,1) → 5 combinations\n- Event C (total of 7): (1,6), (2,5), (3,4), (4,3), (5,2), (6,1) → 6 combinations\n\nAdding these gives us 4 + 5 + 6 = 15 successful outcomes. Since there are a total of 36 combinations when rolling two dice, the probability is 15/36, which simplifies to 5/12.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 233, "output_tokens": 216, "total_tokens": 449}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the probability of throwing at least one of the totals 5, 6, or 7 with a pair of dice, we first determine the number of combinations for each event:\n\n- Event A (total of 5): (1,4), (2,3), (3,2), (4,1) → 4 combinations\n- Event B (total of 6): (1,5), (2,4), (3,3), (4,2), (5,1) → 5 combinations\n- Event C (total of 7): (1,6), (2,5), (3,4), (4,3), (5,2), (6,1) → 6 combinations\n\nAdding these gives us 4 + 5 + 6 = 15 successful outcomes. Since there are a total of 36 combinations when rolling two dice, the probability is 15/36, which simplifies to 5/12.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00016454999999999996}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3119", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If a random variable X is normally distributed with a mean of 118 and a standard deviation of 11, what Z-scores correspond to raw scores of 115, 134, and 99?\n\nOptions: \nA. -.27, 1.45, 1.73\nB. -.27, -1.45, -1.73\nC. -2.18, 0.15, -1.82\nD. 0, 1.5, -2\nE. .27, 1.45, 1.73\nF. -.27, 1.45, -1.73\nG. -1, 2, -2\nH. -0.5, 1.2, -1.5\nI. .27, -1.45, .73\nJ. 2.73, -0.27, 0.45\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the Z-scores for the raw scores of 115, 134, and 99, we use the formula \\( Z = \\frac{(X - \\mu)}{\\sigma} \\) where \\( \\mu \\) is the mean and \\( \\sigma \\) is the standard deviation. \n\nCalculating:\n- For 115: \\( Z = \\frac{(115 - 118)}{11} = -0.27 \\)\n- For 134: \\( Z = \\frac{(134 - 118)}{11} = 1.45 \\)\n- For 99: \\( Z = \\frac{(99 - 118)}{11} = -1.73 \\)\n\nThe Z-scores are approximately -0.27, 1.45, and -1.73, which corresponds to option F. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 254, "output_tokens": 189, "total_tokens": 443}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the Z-scores for the raw scores of 115, 134, and 99, we use the formula \\( Z = \\frac{(X - \\mu)}{\\sigma} \\) where \\( \\mu \\) is the mean and \\( \\sigma \\) is the standard deviation. \n\nCalculating:\n- For 115: \\( Z = \\frac{(115 - 118)}{11} = -0.27 \\)\n- For 134: \\( Z = \\frac{(134 - 118)}{11} = 1.45 \\)\n- For 99: \\( Z = \\frac{(99 - 118)}{11} = -1.73 \\)\n\nThe Z-scores are approximately -0.27, 1.45, and -1.73, which corresponds to option F. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001515}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3279", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If X has a normal distribution with mean 9 and standard deviation 3, find P(5 < X < 11).\n\nOptions: \nA. - .09176\nB. .21185\nC. .37748\nD. .55962\nE. .65361\nF. .09176\nG. .92715\nH. .47568\nI. .81743\nJ. .74537\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find \\( P(5 < X < 11) \\) for a normally distributed variable \\( X \\) with mean \\( \\mu = 9 \\) and standard deviation \\( \\sigma = 3 \\), we first convert the values to z-scores:\n\n\\[\nz_1 = \\frac{5 - 9}{3} = -\\frac{4}{3} \\approx -1.33\n\\]\n\\[\nz_2 = \\frac{11 - 9}{3} = \\frac{2}{3} \\approx 0.67\n\\]\n\nUsing standard normal distribution tables or a calculator, we find \\( P(Z < -1.33) \\approx 0.09176 \\) and \\( P(Z < 0.67) \\approx 0.74857 \\). Therefore, \n\n\\[\nP(5 < X < 11) = P(Z < 0.67) - P(Z < -1.33) \\approx 0.74857 - 0.09176 \\approx 0.65681.\n\\]\n\nThis value is closest to option E, which is 0.65361.\n\nThus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 152, "output_tokens": 253, "total_tokens": 405}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find \\( P(5 < X < 11) \\) for a normally distributed variable \\( X \\) with mean \\( \\mu = 9 \\) and standard deviation \\( \\sigma = 3 \\), we first convert the values to z-scores:\n\n\\[\nz_1 = \\frac{5 - 9}{3} = -\\frac{4}{3} \\approx -1.33\n\\]\n\\[\nz_2 = \\frac{11 - 9}{3} = \\frac{2}{3} \\approx 0.67\n\\]\n\nUsing standard normal distribution tables or a calculator, we find \\( P(Z < -1.33) \\approx 0.09176 \\) and \\( P(Z < 0.67) \\approx 0.74857 \\). Therefore, \n\n\\[\nP(5 < X < 11) = P(Z < 0.67) - P(Z < -1.33) \\approx 0.74857 - 0.09176 \\approx 0.65681.\n\\]\n\nThis value is closest to option E, which is 0.65361.\n\nThus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00017460000000000002}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2868", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An organism exposed to wild temperature fluctuations shows very little, if any, change in its metabolic rate. This organism is most probably a\n\nOptions: \nA. thermophyle.\nB. poikilotherm.\nC. ascospore.\nD. endotherm.\nE. stenotherm.\nF. mesotherm.\nG. ectotherm.\nH. homeotherm.\nI. eurytherm.\nJ. heterotherm.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. An organism that exhibits very little change in its metabolic rate despite wild temperature fluctuations is most likely eurytherm, meaning it can tolerate a wide range of temperatures. This contrasts with stenotherms, which can only thrive within a narrow temperature range.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 154, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 213}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. An organism that exhibits very little change in its metabolic rate despite wild temperature fluctuations is most likely eurytherm, meaning it can tolerate a wide range of temperatures. This contrasts with stenotherms, which can only thrive within a narrow temperature range.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.85e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3107", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Given a mean of 50 and a standard deviation of 10 for a set of measurements that is normally distributed, find the probability that a randomly selected observation is between 50 and 55.\n\nOptions: \nA. .125\nB. .341\nC. .180\nD. .210\nE. .274\nF. .159\nG. .300\nH. .191\nI. .200\nJ. .230\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the probability that a randomly selected observation is between 50 and 55, we first convert these values into z-scores using the formula \\( z = \\frac{(X - \\mu)}{\\sigma} \\). For 50, the z-score is \\( z = \\frac{(50 - 50)}{10} = 0 \\) and for 55, \\( z = \\frac{(55 - 50)}{10} = 0.5 \\). Using the standard normal distribution table, the area to the left of z = 0.5 is approximately 0.6915, and since the area to the left of z = 0 is 0.5, the probability between 50 and 55 is \\( 0.6915 - 0.5 = 0.1915 \\), which corresponds to option H.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 154, "output_tokens": 193, "total_tokens": 347}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the probability that a randomly selected observation is between 50 and 55, we first convert these values into z-scores using the formula \\( z = \\frac{(X - \\mu)}{\\sigma} \\). For 50, the z-score is \\( z = \\frac{(50 - 50)}{10} = 0 \\) and for 55, \\( z = \\frac{(55 - 50)}{10} = 0.5 \\). Using the standard normal distribution table, the area to the left of z = 0.5 is approximately 0.6915, and since the area to the left of z = 0 is 0.5, the probability between 50 and 55 is \\( 0.6915 - 0.5 = 0.1915 \\), which corresponds to option H.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001389}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2652", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The antisense (noncoding) strand of DNA is 5' ATG GAT AAA GIT TTA AAC AGA GAG GAA TCT 3' What is the a)sensestrand? b)mRNAtranscribed? c)polypeptidechain that is translated?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3' TAG GAT AAA GCT TTA AAC AGA GAG GAA TCT 5', 5' AUC CUA UUU CGA AAU UUG UCU CUC CUU AGA 3', Ile-Leu-Phe-Arg-Asn-Leu-Ser-Leu-Leu-Arg\nB. 3' TAC CTA TTT CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTTAGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu\nC. 3' TAC CTA TTT CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTT AGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu\nD. 3' ATG GAT AAA GIT TTA AAC AGA GAG GAA TCT 5', 5' UAC CUA UUU GUA AAU UUG UCU CUC CUU AGA 3', Tyr-Leu-Phe-Val-Asn-Leu-Ser-Leu-Leu-Arg\nE. 3' UAC CUA UUU CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTT AGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUC UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu-Glu-Ser\nF. 3' TAC CTA TTT CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTTAGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu-Glu\nG. 3' TAG GAT AAA GIT TTA AAC AGA GAG GAA TCT 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu-Glu-Ser\nH. 3' TAC CTA TTT CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTTAGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn-Arg-Glu-Glu-Ser\nI. 3' TAC CTA TTT CAA AAT TTG TCT CTC CTTAGA 5', 5' AUG GAU AAA GUU UUA AAC AGA GAG GAA UCU 3', Met-Asp-Lys-Val-Leu-Asn\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the answers, we first need to correctly transcribe the antisense strand into the sense strand (which is the actual coding sequence) and then generate the mRNA from this coding sequence. Finally, we translate the mRNA into a polypeptide chain. \n\nThe correct choice from the options provided is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). This option includes the accurately computed sense strand, the correct mRNA sequence, and the corresponding polypeptide translation.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 721, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 813}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the answers, we first need to correctly transcribe the antisense strand into the sense strand (which is the actual coding sequence) and then generate the mRNA from this coding sequence. Finally, we translate the mRNA into a polypeptide chain. \n\nThe correct choice from the options provided is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). This option includes the accurately computed sense strand, the correct mRNA sequence, and the corresponding polypeptide translation.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00016334999999999999}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2948", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The radii of five different brands of softballs (in inches) are 2.03, 1.98, 2.24, 2.17, and 2.08. Find the range, variance, standard deviation, mean deviation about the median, and coefficient of variation.\n\nOptions: \nA. Range: 0.26 in, Variance: 0.0105, Standard deviation: 0.102, Mean deviation about the median: 0.085, Coefficient of Variation: 0.048\nB. Range: 0.26 in, Variance: 0.00884, Standard deviation: 0.094, Mean deviation about the median: 0.08, Coefficient of Variation: 0.045\nC. Range: 0.20 in, Variance: 0.010, Standard deviation: 0.1, Mean deviation about the median: 0.07, Coefficient of Variation: 0.050\nD. Range: 0.30 in, Variance: 0.009, Standard deviation: 0.095, Mean deviation about the median: 0.09, Coefficient of Variation: 0.046\nE. Range: 0.22 in, Variance: 0.0095, Standard deviation: 0.097, Mean deviation about the median: 0.088, Coefficient of Variation: 0.047\nF. Range: 0.27 in, Variance: 0.012, Standard deviation: 0.11, Mean deviation about the median: 0.095, Coefficient of Variation: 0.055\nG. Range: 0.24 in, Variance: 0.0065, Standard deviation: 0.081, Mean deviation about the median: 0.078, Coefficient of Variation: 0.042\nH. Range: 0.28 in, Variance: 0.011, Standard deviation: 0.105, Mean deviation about the median: 0.10, Coefficient of Variation: 0.052\nI. Range: 0.21 in, Variance: 0.007, Standard deviation: 0.084, Mean deviation about the median: 0.065, Coefficient of Variation: 0.040\nJ. Range: 0.25 in, Variance: 0.008, Standard deviation: 0.093, Mean deviation about the median: 0.075, Coefficient of Variation: 0.044\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the correct answer, we first calculate the required statistics for the given radii of softballs: the range is \\(2.24 - 1.98 = 0.26\\), the variance and standard deviation can be computed from the data, and the mean deviation about the median and coefficient of variation can also be derived. After calculating all the statistics, option A stands out as the closest match to the expected values found through these calculations. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 600, "output_tokens": 104, "total_tokens": 704}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the correct answer, we first calculate the required statistics for the given radii of softballs: the range is \\(2.24 - 1.98 = 0.26\\), the variance and standard deviation can be computed from the data, and the mean deviation about the median and coefficient of variation can also be derived. After calculating all the statistics, option A stands out as the closest match to the expected values found through these calculations. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001524}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3049", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Miniature poodles are thought to have a mean height of 12 inches and a standard deviation of 1.8 inches. If height is measured to the nearest inch, find the percentage of poodles having a height exceeding 14 inches.\n\nOptions: \nA. 45 percent\nB. 2.5 percent\nC. 5 percent\nD. 30 percent\nE. 20 percent\nF. 10 percent\nG. 15 percent\nH. 35 percent\nI. 40 percent\nJ. 25 percent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the percentage of miniature poodles exceeding a height of 14 inches, we first calculate the z-score: \n\n\\[ z = \\frac{X - \\mu}{\\sigma} = \\frac{14 - 12}{1.8} \\approx 1.11. \\]\n\nUsing a standard normal distribution table, a z-score of 1.11 corresponds to a percentile of about 13.4%, meaning approximately 86.6% are below this height. Therefore, the percentage exceeding 14 inches is approximately 13.4%, which aligns closest with option G (15 percent).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 176, "output_tokens": 136, "total_tokens": 312}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the percentage of miniature poodles exceeding a height of 14 inches, we first calculate the z-score: \n\n\\[ z = \\frac{X - \\mu}{\\sigma} = \\frac{14 - 12}{1.8} \\approx 1.11. \\]\n\nUsing a standard normal distribution table, a z-score of 1.11 corresponds to a percentile of about 13.4%, meaning approximately 86.6% are below this height. Therefore, the percentage exceeding 14 inches is approximately 13.4%, which aligns closest with option G (15 percent).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.000108}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3101", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Three hundred college freshmen are observed to have grad point averages that are approximately normally distributed with mean 2.1 and a standard deviation of 1.2. How many of these freshmen would you expect to have grade point averages between 2.5 and 3.5 if the averages are recorded to the nearest tenth?\n\nOptions: \nA. 103 students\nB. 50 students\nC. 90 students\nD. 110 students\nE. 82 students\nF. 95 students\nG. 120 students\nH. 75 students\nI. 68 students\nJ. 57 students\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the number of freshmen with GPAs between 2.5 and 3.5, we first calculate the z-scores for these values using the formula \\( z = \\frac{(X - \\mu)}{\\sigma} \\), where \\( \\mu = 2.1 \\) and \\( \\sigma = 1.2 \\). For 2.5, \\( z \\approx 0.33 \\) and for 3.5, \\( z \\approx 1.17 \\). Looking up these z-scores in the standard normal distribution table gives approximate probabilities of 0.6293 and 0.8790 respectively, leading to a probability range of \\( 0.8790 - 0.6293 = 0.2497 \\). Multiplying this by 300 students gives about 75 students.\n\nThus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 190, "output_tokens": 186, "total_tokens": 376}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the number of freshmen with GPAs between 2.5 and 3.5, we first calculate the z-scores for these values using the formula \\( z = \\frac{(X - \\mu)}{\\sigma} \\), where \\( \\mu = 2.1 \\) and \\( \\sigma = 1.2 \\). For 2.5, \\( z \\approx 0.33 \\) and for 3.5, \\( z \\approx 1.17 \\). Looking up these z-scores in the standard normal distribution table gives approximate probabilities of 0.6293 and 0.8790 respectively, leading to a probability range of \\( 0.8790 - 0.6293 = 0.2497 \\). Multiplying this by 300 students gives about 75 students.\n\nThus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001401}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3204", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In chloroplasts, a certain protein is found in the lumen of the thylakoid (thylakoid space). It is transcribed in the nucleus and synthesized on cytoplasmic ribosomes. How many membrane bilayers must this protein cross to reach its final location?\n\nOptions: \nA. Four\nB. Nine\nC. Three\nD. Eight\nE. One\nF. Zero\nG. Five\nH. Two\nI. Seven\nJ. Six\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The protein must cross two membrane bilayers to reach the lumen of the thylakoid. First, it crosses the inner membrane of the chloroplast, and then it crosses the thylakoid membrane to enter the thylakoid lumen. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{H}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 162, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 223}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The protein must cross two membrane bilayers to reach the lumen of the thylakoid. First, it crosses the inner membrane of the chloroplast, and then it crosses the thylakoid membrane to enter the thylakoid lumen. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{H}.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.0899999999999996e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3285", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose thecodonsfor amino acids consisted of only two bases rather than three. Would there be a sufficient number ofcodonsfor all twenty amino acids? Show how you obtain your answer.\n\nOptions: \nA. There will be more than 20 codons for 20 amino acids\nB. 4 codons will be enough to code for all 20 amino acids, with some sharing multiple codons\nC. 16 codons will be insufficient to code for all 20 amino acids\nD. Each amino acid will have multiple codons, with a total of 40 codons available\nE. There will be exactly one codon for each amino acid, with no redundancy\nF. 25 codons will be available, providing extra combinations for some amino acids\nG. Each amino acid will have its own unique codon\nH. 16 codons will be enough to code for all 20 amino acids\nI. There will be 64 codons, providing ample combinations for all amino acids and stop signals\nJ. 20 codons will be just enough to code for each amino acid uniquely\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). If codons consisted of only two bases, the maximum number of unique codons would be \\(4^2 = 16\\), which is insufficient to code for all 20 amino acids. Hence, there would not be enough codons to accommodate every amino acid distinctly.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 290, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 356}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). If codons consisted of only two bases, the maximum number of unique codons would be \\(4^2 = 16\\), which is insufficient to code for all 20 amino acids. Hence, there would not be enough codons to accommodate every amino acid distinctly.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.31e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2963", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Fiddler crabs are a dark brown color during the day and change to a pale brown color at night. Is it possible to reverse this pattern and make the crabs turn dark at night and light during the day? How?\n\nOptions: \nA. The crabs can be trained to change color on command using classical conditioning techniques.\nB. The use of hormonal treatments can induce a reverse in the crabs' color change pattern.\nC. Painting the crabs' shells can simulate the appearance of a reversed color pattern.\nD. The color change can be influenced by the presence of predators, causing a reverse pattern.\nE. The crabs can change color based on their mood.\nF. It is possible to reset this biological clock by artificially producing periods of light and darkness.\nG. The pattern is irreversible due to the crabs' hardwired circadian rhythms.\nH. The crabs can be forced to change color through genetic manipulation.\nI. The crabs' color change can be reversed through a diet change.\nJ. The color change can be triggered by altering the temperature of the crabs' environment.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Resetting the biological clock by artificially producing periods of light and darkness might allow the crabs to adapt their color change pattern to a reverse schedule. This is feasible because circadian rhythms can be influenced by changes in light exposure, which could potentially alter their natural behaviors.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 287, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 351}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Resetting the biological clock by artificially producing periods of light and darkness might allow the crabs to adapt their color change pattern to a reverse schedule. This is feasible because circadian rhythms can be influenced by changes in light exposure, which could potentially alter their natural behaviors.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.145e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2856", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A woman opens a can of ham and beans and suspects food poisoning . She boils the contents for half an hour. A few hours after eating the ham and beans, nausea, vomit-ing, and diarrhea set in. Explain.\n\nOptions: \nA. The woman was poisoned by a toxin that came from a food handler's skin sores.\nB. The woman was poisoned by a toxin that is destroyed by boiling.\nC. The symptoms were due to psychological expectation of illness rather than actual food poisoning.\nD. The woman was poisoned by a pesticide residue on the can's surface.\nE. The woman's symptoms were caused by an allergic reaction to an ingredient in the ham and beans.\nF. The woman was poisoned by the botulinus toxin.\nG. The toxin produced by Staphylococcus aureus, which is heat-stable and unaffected by boiling, likely caused the poisoning.\nH. The ham and beans were contaminated with E. coli, which was not eliminated by boiling.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. The symptoms described, including nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea, align with food poisoning caused by toxins produced by Staphylococcus aureus, which is known to be heat-stable and can survive boiling. This explains why the woman's symptoms occurred despite the contents being boiled for half an hour.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 258, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 324}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. The symptoms described, including nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea, align with food poisoning caused by toxins produced by Staphylococcus aureus, which is known to be heat-stable and can survive boiling. This explains why the woman's symptoms occurred despite the contents being boiled for half an hour.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.83e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3062", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the early 1900's, many fruit growers made a practice of ripening fruits by keeping them in a room with a kerosene stove. They believed it was the heat that ripened the fruits. Was this belief based on correct facts? Explain your answer.\n\nOptions: \nA. The ripening was caused by the soot from the kerosene stove settling on the fruits.\nB. The fruits ripened due to the carbon dioxide produced by the kerosene stove.\nC. The fruits ripened faster due to increased humidity from the kerosene stove.\nD. It was the incomplete combustion products of the kerosene, identified as ethylene, that ripened the fruits.\nE. The fruits ripened naturally without any influence from the kerosene stove.\nF. It was the light emitted by the kerosene stove that accelerated the ripening process.\nG. The fruits ripened due to the ozone produced by the kerosene stove.\nH. The ripening was facilitated by the slight increase in temperature, not directly related to the heat of the stove.\nI. The kerosene stove released a specific ripening hormone that caused the fruits to ripen.\nJ. It was the heat from the kerosene stove that ripened the fruits.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The incomplete combustion of kerosene can produce ethylene gas, which is a well-known natural ripening hormone in fruits. Thus, it was the ethylene produced by the kerosene stove, rather than just heat, that contributed to the ripening of the fruits.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 321, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 387}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The incomplete combustion of kerosene can produce ethylene gas, which is a well-known natural ripening hormone in fruits. Thus, it was the ethylene produced by the kerosene stove, rather than just heat, that contributed to the ripening of the fruits.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.774999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3277", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The citrate ion forms a tight bond with calcium ions so that the calcium is unable to react with other substances In view of this, why is sodium citrate added to whole blood immediately after it is drawn from a blood donor?\n\nOptions: \nA. Sodium citrate is added to cause muscle spasms\nB. Sodium citrate is added to catalyze the formation of fibrin\nC. Sodium citrate is added to preserve the blood's color\nD. Sodium citrate is added to stimulate immune responses\nE. Sodium citrate is added to increase calcium ions\nF. Sodium citrate is added to prevent coagulation\nG. Sodium citrate is added to increase the blood's viscosity\nH. Sodium citrate is added to enhance oxygen carrying capacity of the blood\nI. Sodium citrate is added to decrease the blood's pH level\nJ. Sodium citrate is added as a nutrient for blood cells\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Sodium citrate is added to whole blood to bind calcium ions, thereby preventing coagulation and allowing the blood to remain liquid for storage and testing. This action inhibits the blood clotting process, which is essential in blood donation and storage.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 239, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 294}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Sodium citrate is added to whole blood to bind calcium ions, thereby preventing coagulation and allowing the blood to remain liquid for storage and testing. This action inhibits the blood clotting process, which is essential in blood donation and storage.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.884999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2715", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: About 0.5 percent of the American population have epilepsy, the falling sickness. Discuses the genetics of this disease.\n\nOptions: \nA. Epilepsy is the result of a chromosomal aneuploidy, similar to Down syndrome.\nB. Epilepsy is always inherited in an X-linked recessive pattern.\nC. Epilepsy is a dominant trait.\nD. Epilepsy is caused by an autosomal dominant trait.\nE. Epilepsy is due to an autosomal recessive trait.\nF. Epilepsy is caused by an autosomal dominant gene with complete penetrance.\nG. Epilepsy is a mitochondrial inheritance disorder.\nH. Epilepsy is exclusively caused by a single gene mutation.\nI. Epilepsy is not a genetic disorder.\nJ. Epilepsy is a polygenic disorder with no environmental factors involved.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Epilepsy has been shown to have a genetic component and can be influenced by multiple genes, and in some cases, may involve dominant gene mutations that have complete penetrance. However, it is important to note that epilepsy is often a polygenic disorder influenced by both genetic and environmental factors, making its inheritance patterns complex.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 238, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 311}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Epilepsy has been shown to have a genetic component and can be influenced by multiple genes, and in some cases, may involve dominant gene mutations that have complete penetrance. However, it is important to note that epilepsy is often a polygenic disorder influenced by both genetic and environmental factors, making its inheritance patterns complex.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.950000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2860", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In attempting to map out the climatic conditions of the biosphere, would a climatologist find it helpful to correspond withan ecologist who has mapped the vegetation formations orbiomes of the biosphere?\n\nOptions: \nA. No, climatologists would find it more helpful to correspond with a geologist.\nB. Yes, however, it would be more beneficial to collaborate with a meteorologist.\nC. No, because the timescales on which vegetation formations change are too different from climatic shifts.\nD. Yes, but the information would be redundant since climate data already includes vegetation patterns.\nE. Yes, but only for specific types of vegetation.\nF. No, as ecologists' mapping is too detailed for the broad scales used in climatology.\nG. Yes, but only in areas where human activity has not altered the natural vegetation.\nH. Yes, vegetation-formation mapping does provide a basis for climatic mapping.\nI. No, because climatologists use satellite data exclusively for climatic mapping.\nJ. No, vegetation formations have no relation to climatic conditions.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Vegetation-formation mapping can provide valuable insights into climatic conditions, as different vegetation types are adapted to specific climates and can indicate prevailing climate patterns. Collaboration between climatologists and ecologists enriches both fields by integrating climate data with ecological dynamics.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 275, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 332}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Vegetation-formation mapping can provide valuable insights into climatic conditions, as different vegetation types are adapted to specific climates and can indicate prevailing climate patterns. Collaboration between climatologists and ecologists enriches both fields by integrating climate data with ecological dynamics.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.544999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2984", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When estimating the total number of Calories required by a personin a day, we consider such factors as sex, amount of activity, and the temperature in which the person lives. Why arethese factors necessary?\n\nOptions: \nA. Caloric requirements are only influenced by the environmental temperature, not by sex or activity level.\nB. Temperature has no effect on caloric requirements.\nC. Each person's Caloric requirement differs according to sex, amount of activity and environmental temperature.\nD. Caloric requirements are determined by age and sex only, without taking into account activity level or temperature.\nE. Only the sex of the person matters for caloric requirements.\nF. Caloric requirements are determined by a fixed formula that applies universally, regardless of individual differences.\nG. Caloric requirements decrease with increased activity and are independent of sex or environmental factors.\nH. Caloric requirement is the same for everyone.\nI. Caloric requirements increase only with the amount of activity and are unaffected by sex or temperature.\nJ. Caloric requirements are solely based on an individual's weight and height, with no consideration for sex, activity, or temperature.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. This option acknowledges that caloric requirements vary based on individual factors such as sex, activity level, and environmental temperature, reflecting the complexity of metabolic needs in different situations. Other options incorrectly simplify or ignore the factors that influence caloric intake.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 287, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 343}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. This option acknowledges that caloric requirements vary based on individual factors such as sex, activity level, and environmental temperature, reflecting the complexity of metabolic needs in different situations. Other options incorrectly simplify or ignore the factors that influence caloric intake.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.664999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3218", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The muscle fibers innervated by a motor unit will contract if a stimulus of sufficient magnitude is propagated or it will not contract at all. This is known as the all-or- none law. If this is true, how can muscle force be graded? For example, we use the same muscles to lift a one ounce object that we use to lift a 20 lb. object.\n\nOptions: \nA. Muscle force is graded by the frequency of nerve impulses alone.\nB. Muscle force is graded by the weight of the object being lifted.\nC. Muscle force is graded by the amount of energy consumed.\nD. Muscle force is graded by altering the amount of blood flow to the muscle.\nE. Muscle force is graded by the duration of muscle fiber contraction.\nF. Muscle force is graded by the size of the muscle.\nG. Muscle force is graded by the type of muscle fiber being activated.\nH. Muscle force is graded by the number of motor units activated simultaneously.\nI. Muscle force can be graded through the process of recruitment and by varying the tension produced by individual fibers.\nJ. Muscle force is graded by the length of the muscle at the start of contraction.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\). Muscle force can be graded through recruitment, which involves activating more motor units for larger forces, and by varying the tension produced by individual fibers based on the frequency of stimulation. This allows for a range of forces to be exerted despite the all-or-none nature of individual muscle fibers.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 298, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 365}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\). Muscle force can be graded through recruitment, which involves activating more motor units for larger forces, and by varying the tension produced by individual fibers based on the frequency of stimulation. This allows for a range of forces to be exerted despite the all-or-none nature of individual muscle fibers.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.49e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3325", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why is the drop in blood pressure important in retaining fluid within the capillaries?\n\nOptions: \nA. The drop in blood pressure causes blood clotting\nB. The drop in blood pressure causes an increase in plasma protein concentration\nC. The drop in blood pressure stimulates the excretion of fluids by the kidneys\nD. The drop in blood pressure causes dehydration\nE. The drop in blood pressure triggers the release of antidiuretic hormone\nF. The drop in blood pressure decreases the permeability of capillary walls\nG. The drop in blood pressure allows reabsorption of the lost fluid\nH. The drop in blood pressure increases the heart rate\nI. The drop in blood pressure leads to a constriction of the capillaries\nJ. The drop in blood pressure activates the sympathetic nervous system\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. A drop in blood pressure within the capillaries increases osmotic pressure, allowing for the reabsorption of fluid back into the capillaries, thus helping to retain fluid in the circulatory system. This mechanism is important for maintaining proper fluid balance and preventing edema.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 227, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 290}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. A drop in blood pressure within the capillaries increases osmotic pressure, allowing for the reabsorption of fluid back into the capillaries, thus helping to retain fluid in the circulatory system. This mechanism is important for maintaining proper fluid balance and preventing edema.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.184999999999998e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2836", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: High levels of progesterone are essential for the maintenance of the uterine lining during pregnancy. But high levels of progesterone exerts a negative feedback action on LH secretion, with a consequent decrease in LH secretion and eventual atrophy of the corpus luteum. Atrophy of the corpus luteum cuts the progesterone supply resulting in menstruation. Clearly, these events cannot take place after conception, or the embryo would get sloughed off. When conception occurs, the corpus luteum is seen to last through most of pregnancy. How can this be explained?\n\nOptions: \nA. The endometrium produces a hormone that supports the corpus luteum throughout pregnancy.\nB. The body naturally adjusts progesterone levels during pregnancy.\nC. The placenta secretes a hormone, chorionic gonadotrophin, which takes the place of LH in preserving the corpus luteum. This allows the corpus luteum to secrete high levels of progesterone without being shut off.\nD. The corpus luteum spontaneously increases in size during pregnancy, which maintains progesterone levels without hormonal regulation.\nE. The corpus luteum is replaced by a secondary organ that secretes progesterone during pregnancy.\nF. The corpus luteum is not necessary during pregnancy.\nG. The embryo produces progesterone independently, eliminating the need for the corpus luteum after conception.\nH. The corpus luteum's lifespan is extended due to increased blood flow to the ovaries during pregnancy.\nI. The mother's pituitary gland secretes additional LH during pregnancy to maintain the corpus luteum.\nJ. The embryo secretes a hormone to preserve the corpus luteum.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. During early pregnancy, the placenta produces human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG), which mimics the action of LH, thereby maintaining the corpus luteum and ensuring continued secretion of progesterone. This hormonal support is crucial for preserving the uterine lining and supporting the developing embryo.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 386, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 452}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. During early pregnancy, the placenta produces human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG), which mimics the action of LH, thereby maintaining the corpus luteum and ensuring continued secretion of progesterone. This hormonal support is crucial for preserving the uterine lining and supporting the developing embryo.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.75e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2736", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Within a few weeks of treatment with the drug 3TC, a patient's HIV population consists entirely of 3TC-resistant viruses. How can this result best be explained?\n\nOptions: \nA. The patient was initially infected with a 3TC-resistant strain of the virus.\nB. The patient's immune system developed a resistance to 3TC, causing the drug to become ineffective.\nC. The 3TC drug triggered a mutation in the HIV virus, causing it to become resistant.\nD. The patient's body started producing 3TC-resistant viruses in response to the drug treatment.\nE. A few drug-resistant viruses were present at the start of treatment, and natural selection increased their frequency.\nF. The HIV virus can naturally resist any form of drug treatment.\nG. The patient must have become reinfected with 3TC-resistant viruses.\nH. HIV began making drug-resistant versions of reverse transcriptase in response to the drug.\nI. The 3TC drug led to an increase in the production of HIV viruses.\nJ. HIV can change its surface proteins and resist vaccines.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. This option best explains that, although there may have been a few drug-resistant viruses present initially, the use of 3TC applied selective pressure that allowed those resistant strains to proliferate, leading to a population composed entirely of 3TC-resistant viruses. Such a phenomenon is a well-documented occurrence in viral evolution, particularly with HIV.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 278, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 354}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. This option best explains that, although there may have been a few drug-resistant viruses present initially, the use of 3TC applied selective pressure that allowed those resistant strains to proliferate, leading to a population composed entirely of 3TC-resistant viruses. Such a phenomenon is a well-documented occurrence in viral evolution, particularly with HIV.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.730000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3154", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why would it be disadvantageous for a host-specificparasite tokill its host?\n\nOptions: \nA. Parasites cannot harm their hosts\nB. Parasites are not affected by the health status of their host.\nC. Killing the host triggers an immune response that protects other potential hosts.\nD. Parasites always improve the health of their host for long-term survival.\nE. If they cause the extinction of their host, then they themselves would also become extinct.\nF. Host-specific parasites reproduce faster when their host is deceased.\nG. Host-specific parasites can easily find alternative hosts.\nH. Host-specific parasites can survive without a host\nI. Killing the host allows the parasite to spread more easily to new hosts.\nJ. All parasites are deadly to their hosts\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Host-specific parasites rely on their hosts for survival and reproduction; if they kill their host, they risk their own extinction because they have no alternative hosts available. Killing the host can ultimately lead to the downfall of the parasite, as they depend on the host's continued existence to thrive.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 282}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Host-specific parasites rely on their hosts for survival and reproduction; if they kill their host, they risk their own extinction because they have no alternative hosts available. Killing the host can ultimately lead to the downfall of the parasite, as they depend on the host's continued existence to thrive.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.154999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2791", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why would one call a flock of birds a \\textquotedblleftsociety\\textquotedblright?\n\nOptions: \nA. Birds form societies to find food\nB. A flock of birds can be considered an elementary form of society called a motion group. They communicate with one another in order to stay together as they move from place to place. The cooperative behavior enables them to more efficiently detect and avoid predators.\nC. A flock of birds is called a society because they display human-like social structures.\nD. Birds are classified as a society because they share a common language and culture.\nE. Birds form societies to perform complex problem-solving tasks as a group.\nF. Birds form societies to migrate together to the same location every year.\nG. Birds are considered a society because they are governed by a single leader.\nH. Birds form societies primarily for mating purposes.\nI. Birds form societies for social interaction\nJ. Birds form societies to build nests together\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. This option accurately describes the cooperative behavior of birds in a flock, highlighting their communication and collective movement as an elementary form of society. This concept emphasizes the importance of social interaction for survival and predator avoidance, making it the most comprehensive explanation.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 256, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 314}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. This option accurately describes the cooperative behavior of birds in a flock, highlighting their communication and collective movement as an elementary form of society. This concept emphasizes the importance of social interaction for survival and predator avoidance, making it the most comprehensive explanation.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.319999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2640", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mouse sperm contain receptor proteins that bind to a glycoprotein (ZP3) in the zona pellucida of mouse eggs. Binding of ZP3 receptors to ZP3 initiates the sperm’s acrosomal reaction. All of the following experimental observations would be expected EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. Injecting eggs with antibodies that bind to ZP3 blocks in vitro fertilization.\nB. Incubating sperm with purified ZP3 prior to mixing sperm and eggs blocks in vitro fertilization.\nC. Incubating eggs with antibodies that bind to ZP3 blocks in vitro fertilization.\nD. Coating synthetic beads with a different glycoprotein, ZP2, fails to lead to sperm aggregation on the beads.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Incubating sperm with purified ZP3 prior to mixing sperm and eggs would not block in vitro fertilization, as it should allow the sperm to bind to the ZP3 and initiate the acrosomal reaction necessary for fertilization. In contrast, the other options correctly predict outcomes that would hinder fertilization.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 287}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Incubating sperm with purified ZP3 prior to mixing sperm and eggs would not block in vitro fertilization, as it should allow the sperm to bind to the ZP3 and initiate the acrosomal reaction necessary for fertilization. In contrast, the other options correctly predict outcomes that would hinder fertilization.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.544999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3134", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In the popular nursery rhyme \"Mary Had a Little Lamb\", her lambwould follow Mary wherever she went. Discuss a possi-blebiological explanation.\n\nOptions: \nA. The lamb had a habitual path that coincidentally aligned with Mary's route\nB. The lamb might have imprinted on Mary, a form of learning where the lamb forms a strong and lasting bond with the first moving object it sees.\nC. The lamb was guided by a shepherd and instructed to follow Mary\nD. The lamb was genetically programmed to follow Mary\nE. The lamb followed Mary due to a magnetic device she carried\nF. The lamb was trained to follow Mary\nG. The lamb followed Mary because of a distinctive sound she made\nH. The lamb was physically attached to Mary\nI. The lamb was attracted to the color of Mary's clothing\nJ. The lamb had been conditioned to follow a specific scent associated with Mary\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Imprinting is a well-documented phenomenon in which young animals develop a strong attachment to the first moving object they encounter, often their mother. In this case, the lamb may have imprinted on Mary, leading it to follow her wherever she went.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 248, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 309}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Imprinting is a well-documented phenomenon in which young animals develop a strong attachment to the first moving object they encounter, often their mother. In this case, the lamb may have imprinted on Mary, leading it to follow her wherever she went.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.38e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2957", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compare cardiac muscle to skeletal and smooth muscle.\n\nOptions: \nA. Cardiac muscle has a metabolism similar to smooth muscle, designed for quick, short bursts of activity.\nB. Cardiac muscle cells are multinucleated and arranged in a non-striated pattern.\nC. Cardiac muscle shows some characteristics of both skeletal and smooth muscle. It is striated, has numerous nuclei per cell, is innervated by the autonomic nervous system, has intercalated discs, and its metabolism is designed for endurance.\nD. Cardiac muscle lacks intercalated discs, which differentiates it from skeletal and smooth muscle.\nE. Cardiac muscle does not have any similarities with skeletal and smooth muscle\nF. Cardiac muscle is innervated by the somatic nervous system, similar to skeletal muscle.\nG. Cardiac muscle is similar to skeletal muscle but not smooth muscle\nH. Cardiac muscle has a metabolism designed for speed and strength\nI. Cardiac muscle is not striated and has a single nucleus per cell, similar to smooth muscle.\nJ. Cardiac muscle is identical to smooth muscle in both structure and function.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Cardiac muscle shares characteristics with both skeletal and smooth muscle, being striated like skeletal muscle, incorporating intercalated discs, and being innervated by the autonomic nervous system, while its metabolism is adapted for endurance. Unlike skeletal muscle, cardiac muscle cells are typically not multinucleated and have a unique arrangement that supports continuous contraction.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 294, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 372}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Cardiac muscle shares characteristics with both skeletal and smooth muscle, being striated like skeletal muscle, incorporating intercalated discs, and being innervated by the autonomic nervous system, while its metabolism is adapted for endurance. Unlike skeletal muscle, cardiac muscle cells are typically not multinucleated and have a unique arrangement that supports continuous contraction.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.089999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2853", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A biology student from Nebraska, vacationing at a Virginia beach, observes that the level of activity of a fiddler crab changes with the cycle of the tides. When he brings some crabs back with him to Nebraska, he notices that a similar activity cycle is shown, yet there are no ocean beaches for miles. Explain.\n\nOptions: \nA. The level of activity is influenced by the ocean tides only\nB. The activity cycle is a genetic trait that persists regardless of the crabs' habitat\nC. The crabs' internal biological clocks are set to the tidal patterns they experienced in Virginia and continue on the same cycle\nD. Changes in barometric pressure in Nebraska are influencing the crabs' activity levels\nE. The level of activity is regulated by the crab's diet\nF. The crucial determinant of the level of activity of the crab is not the presence of the tides, but the gravitational pull of the moon\nG. The crabs are responding to the light cycles of day and night rather than the tides\nH. The crabs have adapted to a freshwater rhythmic cycle that mimics ocean tides\nI. The crabs are maintaining their Virginia activity schedule out of habit\nJ. The level of activity is being influenced by the temperature fluctuations in their new environment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The crabs likely have an internal biological clock or circadian rhythm that was attuned to the tidal patterns in Virginia, which continues to influence their activity levels even when removed from that environment. This suggests that their behavior is not solely dependent on external tidal cues but is also regulated internally.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 321, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 387}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The crabs likely have an internal biological clock or circadian rhythm that was attuned to the tidal patterns in Virginia, which continues to influence their activity levels even when removed from that environment. This suggests that their behavior is not solely dependent on external tidal cues but is also regulated internally.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.774999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3090", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Cellular uptake of cholesterol occurs through internalization of low density lipoproteincholesterol complexes. Cholesterol uptake involves all of the following EXCEPT\n\nOptions: \nA. cell-surface receptors\nB. adhesion plaques\nC. endosome formation\nD. receptor-mediated endocytosis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Adhesion plaques are structures involved in cell adhesion and signaling but are not directly involved in the process of cholesterol uptake. The other options—cell-surface receptors, endosome formation, and receptor-mediated endocytosis—are all critical components of the mechanism by which cells uptake cholesterol through LDL complexes.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 188}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Adhesion plaques are structures involved in cell adhesion and signaling but are not directly involved in the process of cholesterol uptake. The other options—cell-surface receptors, endosome formation, and receptor-mediated endocytosis—are all critical components of the mechanism by which cells uptake cholesterol through LDL complexes.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.879999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2911", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why isn't a biome map of the earth a true representationof thevegetation formations found on land?\n\nOptions: \nA. Biome maps are outdated\nB. Biome maps are based solely on temperature, ignoring other ecological factors\nC. Biome maps classify vegetation based on animal population distribution rather than plant characteristics\nD. Biome maps are too detailed\nE. Biome maps use inaccurate color coding that does not reflect the true diversity of vegetation\nF. Real vegetation types usually grade one into another so it's hard to draw distinct boundaries\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Biome maps often simplify complex ecological gradients, as real vegetation types can blend into one another rather than having clear, distinct boundaries. This blending makes it challenging to accurately represent the diversity and variability of vegetation across different regions on a map.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 172, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 230}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Biome maps often simplify complex ecological gradients, as real vegetation types can blend into one another rather than having clear, distinct boundaries. This blending makes it challenging to accurately represent the diversity and variability of vegetation across different regions on a map.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.0599999999999996e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3197", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A proficient engineer can easily design skeletal structures that are more functional than those currently found in the forelimbs of such diverse mammals as horses, whales, and bats. That the actual forelimbs of these mammals do not seem to be optimally arranged is because\n\nOptions: \nA. the skeletal structures of these mammals are not designed for functionality, but for other purposes.\nB. these mammals have not evolved to their full potential yet.\nC. natural selection has not had sufficient time to create the optimal design in each case, but will do so given enough time.\nD. natural selection favors variety and diversity over optimal functionality.\nE. the complexity of the skeletal system hinders the possibility of optimal arrangement.\nF. natural selection is generally limited to modifying structures that were present in previous generations and in previous species.\nG. the skeletal structures are indeed optimally arranged, but our understanding of functionality is limited.\nH. optimal design is a human concept that does not apply to natural selection.\nI. in many cases, phenotype is not merely determined by genotype, but by the environment as well.\nJ. natural selection operates in ways that are beyond the capability of the human mind to comprehend.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Natural selection typically works by modifying existing structures rather than creating entirely new ones, which can result in the forelimbs of these mammals reflecting a compromise between different functional demands rather than an optimal design. This choice acknowledges the evolutionary constraints and historical context in which these structures developed.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 300, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 363}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Natural selection typically works by modifying existing structures rather than creating entirely new ones, which can result in the forelimbs of these mammals reflecting a compromise between different functional demands rather than an optimal design. This choice acknowledges the evolutionary constraints and historical context in which these structures developed.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.28e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3322", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An actress with O type blood accused a producer with B type blood of being the father of her child in a paternity suit. The child was also O type. What does the blood type suggest about his guilt?\n\nOptions: \nA. He cannot be the father\nB. The child's blood type suggests the mother has been unfaithful\nC. The child's blood type suggests a mutation occurred\nD. He could have been the father but it does not prove it\nE. The blood type proves he is the father because O type is recessive\nF. He definitely is the father\nG. He must have been the father because B type blood can produce O type offspring\nH. The blood type does not suggest anything\nI. The child's O type blood proves his innocence\nJ. He is probably not the father because B type blood cannot produce O type offspring\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. A person with B type blood has the genotypes BB or BO, and cannot produce an O type offspring if the other parent has O type blood. Since the child is O type, the blood types suggest that the producer cannot be the father.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 239, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 297}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. A person with B type blood has the genotypes BB or BO, and cannot produce an O type offspring if the other parent has O type blood. Since the child is O type, the blood types suggest that the producer cannot be the father.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.065e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2964", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The dorsal root of a nerve leading to the leg of a rat is severed. How will this affect the rat? How would the effect vary if the ventral root were severed instead?\n\nOptions: \nA. Both severing the dorsal and ventral roots cause increased sensation and reflex action.\nB. Severing the dorsal root causes loss of motor function, severing the ventral root causes enhanced sensation.\nC. Both severing the dorsal and ventral roots lead to complete paralysis of the affected part.\nD. Severing the dorsal root causes enhanced movement, severing the ventral root has no effect.\nE. Severing the dorsal root causes loss of sensation and reflex action, severing the ventral root causes inability to move the affected part.\nF. Severing the dorsal root has no effect, severing the ventral root causes loss of sensation.\nG. Severing the dorsal root causes paralysis, severing the ventral root causes heightened sensitivity.\nH. Severing the dorsal root causes involuntary twitching, severing the ventral root causes loss of reflex action.\nI. Severing the dorsal root causes increased reflex action, severing the ventral root causes loss of sensation.\nJ. Severing the dorsal root has no effect, severing the ventral root causes paralysis.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\). Severing the dorsal root of a nerve leads to loss of sensation and reflex action because the dorsal root is responsible for sensory information. In contrast, severing the ventral root would result in the inability to move the affected part since the ventral root carries motor information to the muscles.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 325, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 393}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\). Severing the dorsal root of a nerve leads to loss of sensation and reflex action because the dorsal root is responsible for sensory information. In contrast, severing the ventral root would result in the inability to move the affected part since the ventral root carries motor information to the muscles.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.955e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2658", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Can an extra Y chromosome (XXY) modify behavior?\n\nOptions: \nA. The extra Y chromosome decreases a male's aggression\nB. The extra Y chromosome is linked to an increase in artistic skills\nC. The extra Y chromosome is associated with a significant decrease in risk-taking behavior\nD. The extra Y chromosome leads to a decrease in physical strength\nE. The extra Y chromosome is responsible for a man's level of intelligence\nF. The extra Y chromosome results in a higher level of empathy in males\nG. The extra Y chromosome causes a substantial increase in memory capacity\nH. The extra Y chromosome may predispose a male to a more aggressive attitude\nI. The extra Y chromosome has no effect on a male's behavior\nJ. The extra Y chromosome enhances a male's cognitive abilities significantly\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Research suggests that individuals with an extra Y chromosome (XXY) may display higher levels of aggression or a predisposition towards more aggressive attitudes. This link is not definitive for all individuals, but option H aligns with some observed behavioral tendencies in affected males.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 226, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 285}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Research suggests that individuals with an extra Y chromosome (XXY) may display higher levels of aggression or a predisposition towards more aggressive attitudes. This link is not definitive for all individuals, but option H aligns with some observed behavioral tendencies in affected males.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.93e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2788", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is meant by translocation? What theories have been advanced to explain translocation in plants? Discuss the value and weakness of each.\n\nOptions: \nA. Translocation involves the movement of hormones within the plant; theories include the hormonal signaling theory and the vascular bundle theory.\nB. Translocation is the growth response of plants to gravity; theories include the gravitropism theory and the starch-statolith hypothesis.\nC. Translocation is the process by which plants absorb sunlight for photosynthesis; theories include light-chasing theory and phototropism.\nD. Translocation is explained by the xylem-flow theory\nE. Translocation is the movement of water in plants\nF. Translocation is the exchange of gases in plants; theories include the gas exchange theory and the stomatal pump theory.\nG. Translocation is the movement of nutrients from the leaves to other parts of the plant body. Theories to explain this process include the pressure-flow theory, the cyclosis theory, and the theory of cytoplasmic tubules.\nH. Translocation refers to the movement of plants from one location to another; theories include the wind-dispersal theory and water-dispersal theory.\nI. Translocation is the distribution of seeds by a plant; theories include the seed dispersal theory and the autochory theory.\nJ. Translocation involves the movement of nutrients from roots to leaves\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. Translocation in plants refers to the movement of nutrients, particularly sugars produced in leaves, to other parts of the plant. The pressure-flow theory, cyclosis theory, and the theory of cytoplasmic tubules offer explanations for this process, each with its strengths in explaining how nutrients move within the plant but also having limitations in their applicability across different plant types.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 341, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 422}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. Translocation in plants refers to the movement of nutrients, particularly sugars produced in leaves, to other parts of the plant. The pressure-flow theory, cyclosis theory, and the theory of cytoplasmic tubules offer explanations for this process, each with its strengths in explaining how nutrients move within the plant but also having limitations in their applicability across different plant types.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.975e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2831", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If all the chemical components found in a living cell were to beput together in the right proportion, the mixture would not functionas living matter. What characteristics would enable usto consider something living?\n\nOptions: \nA. Living things are characterized only by their complexity and organization, without the need for energy consumption or reproduction.\nB. Living things are characterized by a specific, complex organization, the ability to consume energy, movement, response to physical or chemical changes, growth, reproduction, and adaptability.\nC. Living things are characterized only by their growth.\nD. Living things are characterized by their ability to maintain homeostasis, without the need for growth, reproduction, or adaptability.\nE. Living things are characterized by their ability to evolve over generations but not by individual growth or energy consumption.\nF. Living things are characterized by their ability to respond to changes and growth, but not by reproduction or energy consumption.\nG. Living things are characterized only by their ability to consume energy.\nH. Living things are characterized only by their movement.\nI. Living things are characterized only by their adaptability to changes.\nJ. Living things are characterized only by their ability to reproduce.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Living things exhibit a combination of characteristics including complex organization, energy consumption, movement, response to environmental changes, growth, reproduction, and adaptability, all of which are essential for defining life. Other options only highlight single aspects or limits of what constitutes a living organism.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 294, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 355}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Living things exhibit a combination of characteristics including complex organization, energy consumption, movement, response to environmental changes, growth, reproduction, and adaptability, all of which are essential for defining life. Other options only highlight single aspects or limits of what constitutes a living organism.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.069999999999998e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2924", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During a study session about evolution, one of your fellow students remarks, \"The giraffe stretched its neck while reaching for higher leaves; its offspring inherited longer necks as a result.\" Which statement is most likely to be helpful in correcting this student's misconception?\n\nOptions: \nA. Genetic traits can be altered by environmental factors after birth.\nB. Giraffes with longer necks are more likely to survive, not necessarily the offspring of giraffes that stretch their necks.\nC. Traits are inherited randomly, not based on necessity or use.\nD. Spontaneous mutations can result in the appearance of new traits.\nE. Disuse of an organ may lead to its eventual disappearance.\nF. The change in the length of the giraffe's neck over generations is a result of genetic drift, not individual effort.\nG. The giraffe's offspring would only inherit a longer neck if the giraffe's genes were modified.\nH. Characteristics acquired during an organism's life are generally not passed on through genes.\nI. The length of a giraffe's neck is determined by its diet and exercise, not its genes.\nJ. Only favorable adaptations have survival value.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most helpful statement to correct the student's misconception is H. Characteristics acquired during an organism's life are generally not passed on through genes. This highlights that traits acquired through use or effort, such as stretching a giraffe's neck, do not influence the genetic makeup of offspring. Instead, genetic changes occur over many generations primarily through natural selection. \n\nThe answer is \\boxed{H}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 296, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 373}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most helpful statement to correct the student's misconception is H. Characteristics acquired during an organism's life are generally not passed on through genes. This highlights that traits acquired through use or effort, such as stretching a giraffe's neck, do not influence the genetic makeup of offspring. Instead, genetic changes occur over many generations primarily through natural selection. \n\nThe answer is \\boxed{H}.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.059999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_2946", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Can complete equilibrium in a gene pool exist in real situations?\n\nOptions: \nA. Genetic equilibrium can be achieved only through selective breeding\nB. Gene pool equilibrium is maintained exclusively by mutation\nC. Gene pool equilibrium is disrupted only by natural selection\nD. Only large populations can achieve genetic equilibrium\nE. Complete equilibrium in a gene pool is not expected\nF. Complete equilibrium in a gene pool can always be achieved\nG. Equilibrium can be achieved when there is no gene flow\nH. Equilibrium is guaranteed when there is a high mutation rate\nI. Complete equilibrium is possible if the population is isolated\nJ. Random reproduction is common in real situations\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\). Complete equilibrium in a gene pool is not expected due to various evolutionary forces such as mutation, natural selection, gene flow, and genetic drift that constantly alter allele frequencies. These influences make it near impossible for a population to maintain complete genetic equilibrium over time.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 258}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\). Complete equilibrium in a gene pool is not expected due to various evolutionary forces such as mutation, natural selection, gene flow, and genetic drift that constantly alter allele frequencies. These influences make it near impossible for a population to maintain complete genetic equilibrium over time.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.615e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3070", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If mating is observed to occur freely between organisms of twodifferent populations in the laboratory, and the cross producesviable offspring, can you assume that the two populationsbelong to the same species?\n\nOptions: \nA. Only if the offspring can also interbreed successfully.\nB. No, successful interbreeding in the laboratory must also be complemented by ecological, behavioral, and morphological studies to confirm they are the same species.\nC. It depends on whether the organisms can interbreed in a controlled environment other than a laboratory.\nD. No, successful interbreeding in the laboratory does not offer enough evidence that two populations must be of the same species.\nE. It depends on the type of organisms being tested.\nF. No, unless the interbreeding also occurs frequently in their natural habitat.\nG. Yes, successful interbreeding in the laboratory is sufficient proof of the same species.\nH. Only if the organisms share identical genetic markers.\nI. Yes, if the offspring show traits that are a mix of both parent populations.\nJ. Yes, as long as the offspring are not sterile.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Successful mating and viable offspring in a laboratory setting do not provide sufficient evidence to categorize them as the same species without considering additional ecological, behavioral, and morphological factors in their natural environments. Thus, a more comprehensive analysis is necessary to confirm species classification beyond laboratory observations.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 284, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 347}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Successful mating and viable offspring in a laboratory setting do not provide sufficient evidence to categorize them as the same species without considering additional ecological, behavioral, and morphological factors in their natural environments. Thus, a more comprehensive analysis is necessary to confirm species classification beyond laboratory observations.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.04e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3158", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is behavior? Are behavior patterns solely inherited or canthey be modified?\n\nOptions: \nA. Behavior patterns cannot be modified\nB. Behavior is limited to the animal kingdom\nC. Behavior is a random set of actions without any pattern or predictability\nD. Behavior patterns are determined exclusively by environmental factors without any genetic influence\nE. Behavior patterns are solely determined by immediate stimuli and are not influenced by past experiences\nF. Behavior patterns are fixed at birth and remain unchanged throughout an individual's life\nG. Behavior is an exclusively human trait not found in other animals\nH. Behavior is only learned through imitation and cannot be innate\nI. Both inheritance and learning are fundamental in the determination of behavioral patterns\nJ. Behavior patterns are solely inherited\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. This option acknowledges that behavior patterns result from both genetic inheritance and environmental learning, reflecting the complexity of how behaviors are developed in individuals. It highlights the interplay between biology and experiences in shaping behavior.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 260}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. This option acknowledges that behavior patterns result from both genetic inheritance and environmental learning, reflecting the complexity of how behaviors are developed in individuals. It highlights the interplay between biology and experiences in shaping behavior.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.015e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3179", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How might you argue that the transmission of impulses does occur in plants?\n\nOptions: \nA. Impulse transmission in plants can be seen in the photosynthesis process\nB. Plants exhibit impulse transmission during pollination, when they attract pollinators to their flowers.\nC. The release of chemical signals in response to herbivore damage, triggering defense mechanisms, is an example of impulse transmission in plants.\nD. The reaction of the sensitive plant, Mimosapudica, to touch demonstrates that transmission of impulses does indeed occur in plants.\nE. The opening and closing of stomata in response to environmental stimuli indicate impulse transmission in plants.\nF. The movement of chloroplasts within plant cells in response to light demonstrates impulse transmission.\nG. The transmission of impulses in plants can be observed through the growth of roots\nH. The process of fruit ripening, which involves a complex interplay of hormones, is a form of impulse transmission in plants.\nI. The bending of plant stems toward a light source, known as phototropism, is evidence of impulse transmission.\nJ. The seed germination process proves the transmission of impulses in plants\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The sensitive plant, Mimosa pudica, shows rapid movement in response to touch, which is a clear example of impulse transmission, demonstrating that plants can respond quickly to stimuli. This movement indicates that there is some form of signaling within the plant system.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 291, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 352}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The sensitive plant, Mimosa pudica, shows rapid movement in response to touch, which is a clear example of impulse transmission, demonstrating that plants can respond quickly to stimuli. This movement indicates that there is some form of signaling within the plant system.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.025e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_biology_3311", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Discuss why one would place Cro-Magnon man higher on the evolution ladder than Neanderthal man.\n\nOptions: \nA. Cro-Magnon man created more sophisticated art and symbolic expressions\nB. Neanderthal man had a smaller cranial capacity\nC. Cro-Magnon man had larger physical size\nD. Cro-Magnon man had a more modern appearance, refined culture, and an increased intelligence\nE. Cro-Magnon man lived in larger, more complex social structures\nF. Neanderthal man had a more limited vocal range and language capability\nG. Cro-Magnon man was less adaptable to the environment\nH. Cro-Magnon man engaged in agriculture while Neanderthal man did not\nI. Neanderthal man had more advanced tool technology\nJ. Cro-Magnon man had a longer lifespan, indicating superior health and diet\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Cro-Magnon man is often considered to be higher on the evolutionary ladder due to his more modern appearance, refined culture, and increased intelligence, which facilitated more complex social structures and artistic expression compared to Neanderthal man. This combination of traits is indicative of a more advanced human evolutionary stage.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 241, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 311}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Cro-Magnon man is often considered to be higher on the evolutionary ladder due to his more modern appearance, refined culture, and increased intelligence, which facilitated more complex social structure