{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4308", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Hund's rule requires that\n\nOptions: \nA. all electrons must have opposite spins in an orbital\nB. no two electrons can have the same four quantum numbers\nC. no two electrons can occupy the same orbital\nD. no two electrons with the same spin can occupy an orbital\nE. all electrons must occupy the highest energy level first\nF. no two electrons can have opposite spins in an orbital\nG. no two electrons can occupy separate orbitals\nH. all electrons must fill the lowest energy level first\nI. no two electrons can pair up if there is an empty orbital at the same energy level available\nJ. no three electrons can occupy the same orbital\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Hund's rule states that electrons will occupy degenerate orbitals singly and with the same spin before pairing up in any orbital, provided that empty orbitals are available at the same energy level. This helps to minimize electron-electron repulsions and is an essential principle in determining electron configurations.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 268}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Hund's rule states that electrons will occupy degenerate orbitals singly and with the same spin before pairing up in any orbital, provided that empty orbitals are available at the same energy level. This helps to minimize electron-electron repulsions and is an essential principle in determining electron configurations.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.035e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3793", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: London dispersion forces are caused by\n\nOptions: \nA. temporary dipoles created by the position of electrons around the nuclei in a molecule\nB. the strong nuclear forces within atomic nuclei\nC. the permanent dipoles created by the shape of the molecule\nD. the intermolecular bonding between ions in an ionic compound\nE. the three-dimensional intermolecular bonding present in all covalent substances\nF. the transfer of electrons in an ionic bond\nG. the electronegativity differences between the different atoms in a molecule\nH. the uneven electron-to-proton ratio found on individual atoms of a molecule\nI. the sharing of electrons in a covalent bond\nJ. the polar covalent bonds within a molecule\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). London dispersion forces arise from temporary dipoles that occur due to the random positioning of electrons around the nuclei in molecules, leading to momentary attractions between adjacent molecules. This phenomenon is prevalent in nonpolar molecules and contributes to their intermolecular interactions.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 209, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 268}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). London dispersion forces arise from temporary dipoles that occur due to the random positioning of electrons around the nuclei in molecules, leading to momentary attractions between adjacent molecules. This phenomenon is prevalent in nonpolar molecules and contributes to their intermolecular interactions.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.675e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3757", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the number of cubic centimeter in one cubic inch.\n\nOptions: \nA. 39.37 cc\nB. 100 cc\nC. 50 cc\nD. 2.54 cc\nE. 5 cc\nF. 16.4 cc\nG. 10 cc\nH. 12 cc\nI. 25.4 cc\nJ. 30 cc\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "One cubic inch is equivalent to approximately 16.387 cubic centimeters. Among the provided options, the closest value to this is 16.4 cc. Thus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{F}", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 144, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 187}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "One cubic inch is equivalent to approximately 16.387 cubic centimeters. Among the provided options, the closest value to this is 16.4 cc. Thus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{F}", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.74e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4418", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the value of the angular-momentum quantum number $l$ for a $t$ orbital?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 12\nC. 10\nD. 7\nE. 6\nF. 3\nG. 2\nH. 16\nI.  14\nJ. 9\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The angular-momentum quantum number \\( l \\) corresponds to the shape of the orbital and is related to the principal quantum number \\( n \\) by the relation \\( l = n - 1 \\) for \\( n \\geq 1 \\). For a \\( t \\) orbital, which corresponds to \\( d \\) orbitals, the value of \\( l \\) is 2 (since \\( d \\) orbitals have \\( l = 2 \\)). Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{G}\\)", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 137, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 246}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The angular-momentum quantum number \\( l \\) corresponds to the shape of the orbital and is related to the principal quantum number \\( n \\) by the relation \\( l = n - 1 \\) for \\( n \\geq 1 \\). For a \\( t \\) orbital, which corresponds to \\( d \\) orbitals, the value of \\( l \\) is 2 (since \\( d \\) orbitals have \\( l = 2 \\)). Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{G}\\)", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.595e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3444", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Pauli exclusion principle states that\n\nOptions: \nA. no two electrons can occupy separate orbitals\nB. no two protons can have the same four quantum numbers\nC. two electrons can share the same quantum number if they are in different orbitals\nD. no two electrons can have the same four quantum numbers\nE. no two electrons can pair up if there is an empty orbital available\nF. no two electrons with the same spin can occupy an orbital\nG. two electrons can share the same quantum number if they have opposite spins\nH. all electrons in an atom must have the same spin\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The Pauli exclusion principle states that no two electrons in an atom can have the same set of four quantum numbers, meaning they cannot occupy the same quantum state simultaneously. This principle is fundamental in quantum mechanics and helps explain the structure of the periodic table.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 188, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 247}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The Pauli exclusion principle states that no two electrons in an atom can have the same set of four quantum numbers, meaning they cannot occupy the same quantum state simultaneously. This principle is fundamental in quantum mechanics and helps explain the structure of the periodic table.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.36e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3348", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An ideal solution is a\n\nOptions: \nA. mixture where the solvents cannot be dissolved in any ratio\nB. mixture that reacts violently when combined\nC. mixture where the solvents repel each other\nD. mixture where the potential energy of the mixture is the same as that of the individual solvents\nE. mixture that changes color when combined\nF. mixture that decreases the potential energy when combined\nG. mixture that increases the potential energy when combined\nH. mixture that is colorless\nI. mixture that has the same physical properties as the individual solvents\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. An ideal solution is characterized by having a potential energy that is the same as that of the individual solvents, meaning there are no significant interactions altering their energies when mixed. This reflects the behavior of an ideal solution where the properties of the mixture resemble those of the pure components.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 176, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 239}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. An ideal solution is characterized by having a potential energy that is the same as that of the individual solvents, meaning there are no significant interactions altering their energies when mixed. This reflects the behavior of an ideal solution where the properties of the mixture resemble those of the pure components.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.419999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4232", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: para-dichlorobenzene is used as \"mothballs.\" This compound can also be named\n\nOptions: \nA. 1,4-dichlorobenzene\nB. 2,6-dichlorobenzene\nC. 1,5-dichlorobenzene\nD. 1,2-dichlorobenzene\nE. 3,4-dichlorobenzene\nF. 2,5-dichlorobenzene\nG. 2,4-dichlorobenzene\nH. 3,5-dichlorobenzene\nI. 2,3-dichlorobenzene\nJ. 1,3-dichlorobenzene\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Para-dichlorobenzene is characterized by having two chlorine atoms attached to the benzene ring at the 1 and 4 positions, which is formally named 1,4-dichlorobenzene. The term \"para\" refers to this specific arrangement of substituents on the benzene ring.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 292}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Para-dichlorobenzene is characterized by having two chlorine atoms attached to the benzene ring at the 1 and 4 positions, which is formally named 1,4-dichlorobenzene. The term \"para\" refers to this specific arrangement of substituents on the benzene ring.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.754999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4244", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the magnetic moment of 205Tl?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.600 x 10^-26 J T-1\nB. [ɣ (205TI = 1.569 x 108 T-1 s-1, I = ½]\nC. 1.433 x 10^-26 J T-1\nD. 0.717 x 10^-26 J T-1\nE. 0.922 x 10^-26 J T-1\nF. 1.569 x 10^-26 J T-1\nG. 0.750 x 10^-26 J T-1\nH. 1.256 x 10^-26 J T-1\nI. 1.100 x 10^-26 J T-1\nJ. 0.827 x 10^-26 J T-1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is based on the known magnetic moment for thallium-205 (205Tl). The magnetic moment can be calculated using the gyromagnetic ratio and spin, but for specific isotopes, it is generally tabulated. The most precise option for the magnetic moment of 205Tl is option B, which gives information on the gyromagnetic ratio.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{B}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 247, "output_tokens": 84, "total_tokens": 331}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is based on the known magnetic moment for thallium-205 (205Tl). The magnetic moment can be calculated using the gyromagnetic ratio and spin, but for specific isotopes, it is generally tabulated. The most precise option for the magnetic moment of 205Tl is option B, which gives information on the gyromagnetic ratio.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{B}.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.745e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4414", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A substance that is NOT generally considered to be a toxic pollutant in water is\n\nOptions: \nA. nitrogen\nB. a halogenated hydrocarbon\nC. chlorine\nD. copper\nE. arsenic\nF. benzene\nG. carbonic acid\nH. mercury\nI. cyanide\nJ. lead\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Nitrogen, while it can contribute to nutrient pollution (eutrophication) in water bodies, is not generally classified as a toxic pollutant like the other substances listed. The others, such as arsenic, mercury, and lead, are known toxic pollutants that can have severe health impacts.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 132, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 200}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Nitrogen, while it can contribute to nutrient pollution (eutrophication) in water bodies, is not generally classified as a toxic pollutant like the other substances listed. The others, such as arsenic, mercury, and lead, are known toxic pollutants that can have severe health impacts.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.0599999999999996e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4278", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One of the two most important uses of ammonia is as a reagent in the first step of theOsfwaldprocess, a synthetic route for the production of nitric acid. This first step proceeds according to the equation 4NH_3(g) + 50_2(g) \\rightleftarrows 4N0(g) + 6H_20(g) . What is the expression for the equilibrium constant of this reaction?\n\nOptions: \nA. K = {{[NH_3]^4 [O_2]^5}} / {{[NO]^4 [H_2O]^6 }}\nB. K = {{[O_2]^5}} / {{ [NO]^4 [NH_3]^4 [H_2O]^6}}\nC. K = {{[NO]^4 [H_2O]^6 }} / {{ [NH_3]^4 [O_2]^5}}\nD. K = {{[NO]^6 [H_2O]^4}} / {{ [NH_3]^5 [O_2]^4}}\nE. K = {{[NO]^4 [H_2O]^6 [NH_3]^4}} / {{[O_2]^5}}\nF. K = {{[NH_3]^4 [O_2]^5 [H_2O]^6}} / {{[NO]^4}}\nG. K = {{[NO]^4 [NH_3]^4}} / {{ [H_2O]^6 [O_2]^5}}\nH. K = {{[NH_3]^5 [O_2]^4}} / {{ [NO]^6 [H_2O]^4}}\nI. K = {{[NO]^4}} / {{ [NH_3]^4 [O_2]^5}}\nJ. K = {{[NO]^4}} / {{ [NH_3]^4 [H_2O]^6}}\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To write the expression for the equilibrium constant \\( K \\) from the given reaction \\( 4NH_3(g) + 5O_2(g) \\rightleftarrows 4NO(g) + 6H_2O(g) \\), we use the general formula \\( K = \\frac{[\\text{products}]^{\\text{coefficients}}}{[\\text{reactants}]^{\\text{coefficients}}} \\). This gives us \\( K = \\frac{[NO]^4 [H_2O]^6}{[NH_3]^4 [O_2]^5} \\), which corresponds to option C.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 461, "output_tokens": 148, "total_tokens": 609}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To write the expression for the equilibrium constant \\( K \\) from the given reaction \\( 4NH_3(g) + 5O_2(g) \\rightleftarrows 4NO(g) + 6H_2O(g) \\), we use the general formula \\( K = \\frac{[\\text{products}]^{\\text{coefficients}}}{[\\text{reactants}]^{\\text{coefficients}}} \\). This gives us \\( K = \\frac{[NO]^4 [H_2O]^6}{[NH_3]^4 [O_2]^5} \\), which corresponds to option C.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00015795}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3701", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An ester is made by reacting\n\nOptions: \nA. two different acids\nB. an amine and an acid\nC. an alcohol and an acid\nD. an acid and a ketone\nE. a ketone and an alcohol\nF. an acid and a base\nG. two different alcohols\nH. an alcohol and a base\nI. an alcohol and an aldehyde\nJ. an amine and an alcohol\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. An ester is formed by the reaction of an alcohol and an acid through a process known as esterification, where the hydroxyl group of the acid and the hydrogen atom of the alcohol are removed to form water and the ester. This reaction is a key part of organic chemistry and is widely used in the production of various esters.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 154, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 229}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. An ester is formed by the reaction of an alcohol and an acid through a process known as esterification, where the hydroxyl group of the acid and the hydrogen atom of the alcohol are removed to form water and the ester. This reaction is a key part of organic chemistry and is widely used in the production of various esters.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.81e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3624", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one of the following statements is true:\n\nOptions: \nA. Protons and neutrons possess orbital angular momentum only.\nB. Protons and neutrons possess spin angular momentum only.\nC. Protons possess orbital angular momentum only, neutrons possess spin angular momentum only.\nD. Protons and neutrons have orbital and spin angular momentum.\nE. Neutrons and protons possess both orbital and spin angular momentum.\nF. Neutrons possess orbital angular momentum only, protons possess both orbital and spin angular momentum.\nG. Protons and neutrons possess neither orbital nor spin angular momentum.\nH. Neutrons have orbital and spin angular momentum, protons have spin angular momentum only.\nI. Protons possess spin angular momentum only, neutrons possess orbital angular momentum only.\nJ. Protons have orbital and spin angular momentum, neutrons have spin angular momentum.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Protons and neutrons, which are both nucleons, possess both orbital and spin angular momentum. While they can exist in various quantum states that include contributions from both types of angular momentum, in the context of nuclear physics, it's established that they exhibit both forms.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 240, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 302}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Protons and neutrons, which are both nucleons, possess both orbital and spin angular momentum. While they can exist in various quantum states that include contributions from both types of angular momentum, in the context of nuclear physics, it's established that they exhibit both forms.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.32e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4156", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the limiting high-temperature molar heat capacity at constant volume (C_V) of a gas-phase diatomic molecule?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4.5R\nB. 2.2R\nC. 1R\nD. 4R\nE. 2R\nF. 2.5R\nG. 5R\nH. 3R\nI. 3.5R\nJ. 1.5R\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The limiting high-temperature molar heat capacity at constant volume (C_V) for a gas-phase diatomic molecule is determined by accounting for the translational and rotational degrees of freedom, resulting in a value of 5/2 R for translational motion and 1 R for rotational motion. Therefore, the total comes to 7/2 R, which is equal to 3.5R when expressed simply. Thus, the correct answer is \n\n\\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 160, "output_tokens": 97, "total_tokens": 257}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The limiting high-temperature molar heat capacity at constant volume (C_V) for a gas-phase diatomic molecule is determined by accounting for the translational and rotational degrees of freedom, resulting in a value of 5/2 R for translational motion and 1 R for rotational motion. Therefore, the total comes to 7/2 R, which is equal to 3.5R when expressed simply. Thus, the correct answer is \n\n\\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.219999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4408", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the maximum number of phases that can be at equilibrium with each other in a three component mixture?\n\nOptions: \nA. 6\nB. 9\nC. 2\nD. 4\nE. 10\nF. 8\nG. 7\nH. 3\nI. 1\nJ. 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The maximum number of phases that can be in equilibrium in a three-component system can be determined using the Gibbs phase rule, which states that the number of phases (P) in equilibrium is given by \\( P + F = C + 2 \\), where F is the degrees of freedom and C is the number of components. For a three-component mixture (C = 3), the maximum number of phases (when F = 0) can be calculated as \\( P = 3 + 2 - 2 = 3 \\). Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 136, "output_tokens": 121, "total_tokens": 257}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The maximum number of phases that can be in equilibrium in a three-component system can be determined using the Gibbs phase rule, which states that the number of phases (P) in equilibrium is given by \\( P + F = C + 2 \\), where F is the degrees of freedom and C is the number of components. For a three-component mixture (C = 3), the maximum number of phases (when F = 0) can be calculated as \\( P = 3 + 2 - 2 = 3 \\). Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.3e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3528", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The symbol for antimony is\n\nOptions: \nA. Am\nB. As\nC. Ab\nD. Au\nE. Fe\nF. Ag\nG. An\nH. At\nI. W\nJ. Sb\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The symbol for antimony is J. Sb. Antimony is a chemical element with the atomic number 51, and its symbol originates from the Latin word \"stibium\". Therefore, the answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 160}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The symbol for antimony is J. Sb. Antimony is a chemical element with the atomic number 51, and its symbol originates from the Latin word \"stibium\". Therefore, the answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.56e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3346", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The simplest alkene has\n\nOptions: \nA. cis-trans isomers\nB. at least four sigma bonds\nC. no sigma bonds\nD. a trigonal planar configuration\nE. a tetrahedral configuration\nF. at least three pi bonds\nG. at least two pi bonds\nH. aromatic properties\nI. at least six sigma bonds\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The simplest alkene is ethene (C2H4), which has a double bond between two carbon atoms. In terms of structure, it has a trigonal planar configuration around the double bond. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{D}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 136, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 187}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The simplest alkene is ethene (C2H4), which has a double bond between two carbon atoms. In terms of structure, it has a trigonal planar configuration around the double bond. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{D}.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.099999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3673", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A laboratory analyst puts Fehling solution in a test tube and then adds the urine of a diabetic which contains some sugar. On heating, what red copper compound precipitates?\n\nOptions: \nA. Cu_2O\nB. Cu3(PO4)2\nC. CuO\nD. Cu2SO4\nE. CuOH\nF. Cu(NO3)2\nG. CuCl2\nH. CuBr2\nI. CuCO3\nJ. CuSO4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). When Fehling's solution is heated in the presence of reducing sugars, such as glucose from diabetic urine, it reduces the copper(II) ions (Cu²⁺) to form a red precipitate of copper(I) oxide (Cu₂O). This reaction is a classic test for reducing sugars in urine.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 166, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 241}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). When Fehling's solution is heated in the presence of reducing sugars, such as glucose from diabetic urine, it reduces the copper(II) ions (Cu²⁺) to form a red precipitate of copper(I) oxide (Cu₂O). This reaction is a classic test for reducing sugars in urine.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.989999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4409", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Cobalt-60 is used in the radiation therapy of cancer and can be produced by bombardment of cobalt-59 with which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. Gamma rays\nB. Neutrons\nC. Ultraviolet light\nD. Beta particles\nE. Infrared radiation\nF. Protons\nG. Electrons\nH. X-rays\nI. Positrons\nJ. Alpha particles\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "Cobalt-60 is produced by the neutron bombardment of cobalt-59. Neutrons are used in the nuclear process to convert cobalt-59 into cobalt-60 through nuclear reactions. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 149, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 199}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "Cobalt-60 is produced by the neutron bombardment of cobalt-59. Neutrons are used in the nuclear process to convert cobalt-59 into cobalt-60 through nuclear reactions. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.235e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4053", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the conjugate acid of the H2PO4- ion?\n\nOptions: \nA. PO43-\nB. H3PO42-\nC. H3PO43-\nD. H4PO4-\nE. H2PO4-\nF. H2PO43-\nG. HPO42-\nH. H4PO4+\nI. H3PO4\nJ. H2PO42-\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The conjugate acid of the H2PO4^- ion is formed when a proton (H^+) is added to it. Therefore, adding a proton to H2PO4^- gives us H3PO4. The correct option is thus I. \n\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 148, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 210}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The conjugate acid of the H2PO4^- ion is formed when a proton (H^+) is added to it. Therefore, adding a proton to H2PO4^- gives us H3PO4. The correct option is thus I. \n\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.94e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4471", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All the silicon and most of the oxygen in the earth's crust exists in the form of silicate minerals, such as granite. If the basic chemical unit of all silicates is the Sio_4^4- ion, which consists of an Si^4+ ion and four O^2- ions, write the electronic configurations of the Si^4+ and O^2- ions in silicate materials.\n\nOptions: \nA. Si^4+ : 1s^22s^22p^6, O^2- : 1s^22s^22p^6\nB. Si^4+ : 1s^22s^22p^6, O^2- : 1s^22s^22p^4\nC. Si^4+ : 1s^22s^22p^63s^1, O^2- : 1s^22s^22p^63s^23p^4\nD. Si^4+ : 1s^22s^22p^63d^10, O^2- : 1s^22s^22p^63d^10\nE. Si^4+ : 1s^22s^22p^63s^23p^2, O^2- : 1s^22s^22p^63s^23p^2\nF. Si^4+ : 1s^22s^22p^63s^23p^6, O^2- : 1s^22s^22p^63s^23p^6\nG. Si^4+ : 1s^22s^22p^63s^23p^2, O^2- : 1s^22s^22p^6\nH. Si^4+ : 1s^22s^22p^63s^23p^4, O^2- : 1s^22s^22p^63s^1\nI. Si^4+ : 1s^22s^22p^4, O^2- : 1s^22s^22p^63s^23p^6\nJ. Si^4+ : 1s^22s^1, O^2- : 1s^22s^22p^63s^2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct electronic configuration for the Si^4+ ion, which has lost four electrons from its neutral state of Si (1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p²), is 1s² 2s² 2p⁶. For the O^2- ion, which has gained two electrons from its neutral state of O (1s² 2s² 2p⁴), it becomes 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ as well. Therefore, the correct answer is A. \n\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 569, "output_tokens": 130, "total_tokens": 699}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct electronic configuration for the Si^4+ ion, which has lost four electrons from its neutral state of Si (1s² 2s² 2p⁶ 3s² 3p²), is 1s² 2s² 2p⁶. For the O^2- ion, which has gained two electrons from its neutral state of O (1s² 2s² 2p⁴), it becomes 1s² 2s² 2p⁶ as well. Therefore, the correct answer is A. \n\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00016334999999999999}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3445", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Chlorine gas reacts most readily with\n\nOptions: \nA. butane\nB. ethylene\nC. acetic acid\nD. toluene\nE. ethanol\nF. propane\nG. ethane\nH. ethanoic acid\nI. benzene\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Chlorine gas reacts most readily with alkenes like ethylene due to the presence of a carbon-carbon double bond, which is more reactive than saturated hydrocarbons or compounds like toluene and ethanol. The double bond allows for electrophilic addition reactions, facilitating a more vigorous reaction with chlorine.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 188}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Chlorine gas reacts most readily with alkenes like ethylene due to the presence of a carbon-carbon double bond, which is more reactive than saturated hydrocarbons or compounds like toluene and ethanol. The double bond allows for electrophilic addition reactions, facilitating a more vigorous reaction with chlorine.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.879999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4405", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The most massive subatomic particle is the\n\nOptions: \nA. positron\nB. quark\nC. electron\nD. muon\nE. beta particle\nF. photon\nG. neutron\nH. neutrino\nI. alpha particle\nJ. proton\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most massive subatomic particle listed in the options is the neutron, which has a mass slightly greater than that of the proton. Quarks, while fundamental constituents of protons and neutrons, are not considered in isolation in this context. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{G}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 179}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most massive subatomic particle listed in the options is the neutron, which has a mass slightly greater than that of the proton. Quarks, while fundamental constituents of protons and neutrons, are not considered in isolation in this context. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{G}.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.34e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3391", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When a swimmer leaves cold water on a warm, breezy day, he experiences a cooling effect. Why?\n\nOptions: \nA. The cold water causes a decrease in the swimmer's metabolic rate.\nB. The swimmer feels cold due to the temperature difference.\nC. Evaporation of water from the swimmer's skin cools the body down.\nD. The swimmer feels cold due to the wind chill factor.\nE. The swimmer's body is adapting to the water temperature after exiting.\nF. The water removes heat from the swimmer's body.\nG. The sun's rays are less effective on the swimmer's wet skin.\nH. The water on the swimmer's body freezes.\nI. The breeze makes the swimmer feel cold.\nJ. The swimmer's body temperature drops below normal.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{C}. When the swimmer exits the cold water and is exposed to the warm, breezy air, the water on their skin evaporates, leading to a cooling effect as evaporation requires heat energy, which is taken from the swimmer's body. This process, combined with the wind, enhances the sensation of cooling.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 291}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{C}. When the swimmer exits the cold water and is exposed to the warm, breezy air, the water on their skin evaporates, leading to a cooling effect as evaporation requires heat energy, which is taken from the swimmer's body. This process, combined with the wind, enhances the sensation of cooling.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.56e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3450", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is classified as a conjugate acid-base pair?\n\nOptions: \nA. HCl / NaOH\nB. H+ / Cl−\nC. H3O+ / H2O\nD. O2 / H2O\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. A conjugate acid-base pair consists of two species that differ by one proton (H+). In this case, H3O+ (the conjugate acid) and H2O (the base) fit this definition, as H3O+ can donate a proton to become H2O.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 115, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 184}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. A conjugate acid-base pair consists of two species that differ by one proton (H+). In this case, H3O+ (the conjugate acid) and H2O (the base) fit this definition, as H3O+ can donate a proton to become H2O.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.8649999999999996e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3476", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of what importance are proteins to biological systems?\n\nOptions: \nA. Proteins determine the rate of photosynthesis in plants.\nB. Proteins are used for insulation in cold environments\nC. Proteins are the main constituent of cell walls in bacteria.\nD. Proteins are responsible for coloration of organisms\nE. Proteins serve as structural material and biological regulators.\nF. Proteins are used primarily for water transport in plants.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Proteins serve multiple essential functions in biological systems, including acting as structural materials (e.g., collagen in animals) and biological regulators (e.g., enzymes and hormones). While some of the other options touch on specific roles of proteins, option E encompasses their broad significance in biology.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 149, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 214}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Proteins serve multiple essential functions in biological systems, including acting as structural materials (e.g., collagen in animals) and biological regulators (e.g., enzymes and hormones). While some of the other options touch on specific roles of proteins, option E encompasses their broad significance in biology.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.134999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3529", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A sample of liquid NH3 is brought to its boiling point. Which of the following occurs during the boiling process?\n\nOptions: \nA. The hydrogen bonds within individual NH3 molecules break apart.\nB. The hydrogen bonds holding separate NH3 molecules together become stronger.\nC. The overall temperature of the solution rises as the NH3 molecules speed up.\nD. The N-H bonds within the NH3 molecules strengthen.\nE. The amount of energy within the system remains constant.\nF. The overall temperature of the solution decreases as the NH3 molecules slow down.\nG. The N-H bonds within the NH3 molecules break apart.\nH. The hydrogen bonds holding separate NH3 molecules together break apart.\nI. The overall volume of the solution decreases.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\). During the boiling process, the hydrogen bonds that hold separate NH3 molecules together break apart, allowing the molecules to escape into the gas phase. This transition occurs without a rise in temperature, as the energy added is used for overcoming intermolecular forces rather than increasing kinetic energy.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 277}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\). During the boiling process, the hydrogen bonds that hold separate NH3 molecules together break apart, allowing the molecules to escape into the gas phase. This transition occurs without a rise in temperature, as the energy added is used for overcoming intermolecular forces rather than increasing kinetic energy.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.079999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3530", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following can form hydrogen bonds?\n\nOptions: \nA. CH3F\nB. CH3OCH2Br\nC. CH4\nD. CH3CH2CH2CH3\nE. CH3NH2\nF. CH3CH3\nG. C6H6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. CH3NH2 (methylamine) can form hydrogen bonds because it contains a nitrogen atom bonded to hydrogen, allowing for hydrogen bonding with other polar molecules. In contrast, the other options either lack sufficient electronegative atoms or do not have hydrogen atoms bonded to electronegative elements necessary for hydrogen bond formation.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 198}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. CH3NH2 (methylamine) can form hydrogen bonds because it contains a nitrogen atom bonded to hydrogen, allowing for hydrogen bonding with other polar molecules. In contrast, the other options either lack sufficient electronegative atoms or do not have hydrogen atoms bonded to electronegative elements necessary for hydrogen bond formation.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.209999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3535", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Argon can be liquefied at low temperature because of\n\nOptions: \nA. its atomic structure\nB. covalent bonding\nC. instantaneous and induced dipoles\nD. metallic bonding\nE. dipole-dipole attractive forces\nF. strong ionic bonds\nG. the very low temperature\nH. hydrogen bonding\nI. presence of free electrons\nJ. high pressure conditions\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). Argon, being a noble gas, experiences instantaneous and induced dipoles due to its nonpolar nature, which allows for weak van der Waals forces to exist between its atoms. These weak interactions can be overcome at low temperatures to achieve liquefaction.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 144, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 206}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). Argon, being a noble gas, experiences instantaneous and induced dipoles due to its nonpolar nature, which allows for weak van der Waals forces to exist between its atoms. These weak interactions can be overcome at low temperatures to achieve liquefaction.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.8800000000000006e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3558", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When air is let out of an automobile tire, the air feels cold to the touch. Explain why you feel this cooling sensation.\n\nOptions: \nA. The air feels cold because it mixes with colder atmospheric air\nB. The air feels cold due to a chemical reaction within the tire\nC. The air temperature falls because it is doing work and expending energy\nD. The cooling sensation is a result of the air's rapid expansion\nE. The cooling sensation is due to the air's humidity\nF. The cooling is caused by the evaporation of water on the skin\nG. The cooling sensation is due to the air's decreased velocity upon exiting the tire\nH. The air feels cold because it is under high pressure\nI. The air feels cold because of the tire's insulation properties\nJ. The air feels cold due to the tire's heat absorption\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The cooling sensation you feel when air escapes from a tire is primarily due to the rapid expansion of the air. When the compressed air exits the tire, it expands quickly, which results in a drop in temperature, making the air feel cold to the touch.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 238, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 298}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The cooling sensation you feel when air escapes from a tire is primarily due to the rapid expansion of the air. When the compressed air exits the tire, it expands quickly, which results in a drop in temperature, making the air feel cold to the touch.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.170000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3623", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When a solid melts, the entropy change and enthalpy changes expected are\n\nOptions: \nA. Positive enthalpy change and negative entropy change\nB. negative entropy change and a negative enthalpy change\nC. No change in entropy and positive enthalpy change\nD. No change in either entropy or enthalpy\nE. Negative enthalpy change and no change in entropy\nF. Negative enthalpy change and negative entropy change\nG. Positive entropy change and no change in enthalpy\nH. positive enthalpy change and positive entropy change\nI. negative entropy change and positive enthalpy change\nJ. negative enthalpy change and positive entropy change\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "When a solid melts, it absorbs heat (positive enthalpy change) and transitions from a more ordered state (solid) to a less ordered state (liquid), which increases entropy. Thus, we expect a positive enthalpy change and a positive entropy change. The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 270}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "When a solid melts, it absorbs heat (positive enthalpy change) and transitions from a more ordered state (solid) to a less ordered state (liquid), which increases entropy. Thus, we expect a positive enthalpy change and a positive entropy change. The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.974999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3703", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Identify the Brønsted-Lowry conjugate acid-base pair in the following list.\n\nOptions: \nA. HC2H3O2 and C2H3O2-\nB. SO32- and SO22-\nC. H3PO4 and H3PO3\nD. H3O+ and OH-\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. HC2H3O2 (acetic acid) donates a proton to become C2H3O2- (acetate ion), making them a conjugate acid-base pair. In contrast, the other options do not represent pairs where one is the conjugate of the other.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 131, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 198}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. HC2H3O2 (acetic acid) donates a proton to become C2H3O2- (acetate ion), making them a conjugate acid-base pair. In contrast, the other options do not represent pairs where one is the conjugate of the other.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.9850000000000005e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3801", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The equation ΔH = ΔU + PΔV is applicable\n\nOptions: \nA. only for constant pressure processes\nB. only for exothermic reactions\nC. only for irreversible processes\nD. only for reversible processes\nE. only for endothermic reactions\nF. always\nG. only for processes under a vacuum\nH. only for constant temperature processes\nI. only for constant volume processes\nJ. only for constant entropy processes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). The equation ΔH = ΔU + PΔV is specifically derived for processes occurring at constant pressure, where ΔH (enthalpy change) accounts for both internal energy change (ΔU) and the work done due to volume change against the pressure (PΔV). This relationship is fundamentally rooted in thermodynamics for constant pressure scenarios.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 156, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 235}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). The equation ΔH = ΔU + PΔV is specifically derived for processes occurring at constant pressure, where ΔH (enthalpy change) accounts for both internal energy change (ΔU) and the work done due to volume change against the pressure (PΔV). This relationship is fundamentally rooted in thermodynamics for constant pressure scenarios.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.079999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3894", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which one sentence explains most accurately why spin trapping is often used to detect free radical intermediates?\n\nOptions: \nA. spin trapping can be used to create a visual representation of free radical intermediates\nB. spin trapping can be used to manipulate the properties of free radical intermediates\nC. spin trapping makes it easy to quantify free radical intermediates\nD. steady state concentration of free radical intermediates is often too low to enable direct detection by EPR\nE. detection of spin adducts requires lower power than direct detection of radical intermediates\nF. spin trapping does not require specialized equipment for detection\nG. spin trapping can be used to change the state of free radical intermediates\nH. spin trapping allows for longer observation periods of free radical intermediates\nI. spin trapping provides more structural information than direct detection by EPR\nJ. spin adducts can be stored and analyzed at a later date\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Spin trapping is often used to detect free radical intermediates because these radicals are typically present at very low concentrations, making direct detection by electron paramagnetic resonance (EPR) challenging. Spin trapping stabilizes the radicals, allowing for their observation and analysis at better detectable levels.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 249, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 314}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Spin trapping is often used to detect free radical intermediates because these radicals are typically present at very low concentrations, making direct detection by electron paramagnetic resonance (EPR) challenging. Spin trapping stabilizes the radicals, allowing for their observation and analysis at better detectable levels.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.634999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3968", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The bond length between any two nonmetal atoms is achieved under which of the following conditions?\n\nOptions: \nA. The point at which the repulsive forces between the two atoms are equal\nB. Where the nucleus of one atom exhibits the strongest attraction to the electrons of the other atom\nC. Where the electrons of each atom exhibits the strongest attraction to the nucleus of the other atom\nD. Where the energy of interaction between the atoms is at its minimum value\nE. The point at which the attractive forces between the two atoms outweigh the repulsive forces\nF. The furthest point at which a valence electron from one atom can transfer to the other atom\nG. Where the energy of interaction between the atoms is at its maximum value\nH. The closest point at which a valence electron from one atom can transfer to the other atom\nI. Where the nuclei of each atom exhibits the strongest attraction to the electrons of the other atom\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. The bond length between two nonmetal atoms is determined when the attractive forces between the electrons of one atom and the nucleus of the other atom outweigh the repulsive forces between the two nuclei and the electrons, achieving a state of stability in the bond formation. This balance of forces typically defines the equilibrium bond length.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 254, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 324}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. The bond length between two nonmetal atoms is determined when the attractive forces between the electrons of one atom and the nucleus of the other atom outweigh the repulsive forces between the two nuclei and the electrons, achieving a state of stability in the bond formation. This balance of forces typically defines the equilibrium bond length.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.01e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4242", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Infrared (IR) spectroscopy is useful for determining certain aspects of the structure of organic molecules because\n\nOptions: \nA. IR radiation can ionize organic molecules, providing structural information\nB. absorption of IR radiation increases with molecular complexity\nC. all molecular bonds absorb IR radiation\nD. IR spectroscopy can identify isotopes within organic molecules\nE. most organic functional groups absorb in a characteristic region of the IR spectrum\nF. IR peak intensities are related to molecular mass\nG. each element absorbs at a characteristic wavelength\nH. IR spectroscopy can determine the polarity of organic molecules\nI. the rate of IR absorption is proportional to the number of atoms in a molecule\nJ. all organic compounds reflect IR radiation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Infrared spectroscopy is effective at identifying organic molecules because most functional groups exhibit characteristic absorption patterns in the IR spectrum, which can be used to deduce aspects of their structure. Other options either misrepresent the nature of IR spectroscopy or do not accurately describe its capabilities.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 269}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Infrared spectroscopy is effective at identifying organic molecules because most functional groups exhibit characteristic absorption patterns in the IR spectrum, which can be used to deduce aspects of their structure. Other options either misrepresent the nature of IR spectroscopy or do not accurately describe its capabilities.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.78e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4309", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following indicates that a reaction is spontaneous?\n\nOptions: \nA. the value of ΔH° is greater than zero\nB. the value of ΔG° is greater than zero\nC. the reaction occurs without any input of energy\nD. the value of ΔS° is greater than zero\nE. the value of ΔS° is less than zero\nF. the value of Keq is greater than one\nG. the reaction is exothermic\nH. at equilibrium there are more products than reactants\nI. the value of Keq is less than one\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). A spontaneous reaction occurs without any input of energy, indicating that it can proceed naturally under the given conditions. Options related to ΔG°, ΔS°, and Keq can provide further context about spontaneity, but option C is the most direct and clear indicator.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 184, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 247}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). A spontaneous reaction occurs without any input of energy, indicating that it can proceed naturally under the given conditions. Options related to ΔG°, ΔS°, and Keq can provide further context about spontaneity, but option C is the most direct and clear indicator.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.539999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3462", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluate the series\n$$\nS=\\sum_{{n=0}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{1}}{{3^n}}\n$$\n\nOptions: \nA. 2 / 3\nB. 1 / 2\nC. 1 / 3\nD. 3\nE. 7 / 4\nF. 4 / 3\nG. 5 / 3\nH. 2\nI. 5 / 2\nJ.  3 / 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The series can be evaluated as a geometric series with first term \\( a = 1 \\) and common ratio \\( r = \\frac{1}{3} \\). The sum of an infinite geometric series is given by the formula \\( S = \\frac{a}{1 - r} \\). Thus, we have:\n\n\\[\nS = \\frac{1}{1 - \\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{2}{3}} = \\frac{3}{2}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 172, "output_tokens": 119, "total_tokens": 291}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The series can be evaluated as a geometric series with first term \\( a = 1 \\) and common ratio \\( r = \\frac{1}{3} \\). The sum of an infinite geometric series is given by the formula \\( S = \\frac{a}{1 - r} \\). Thus, we have:\n\n\\[\nS = \\frac{1}{1 - \\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{2}{3}} = \\frac{3}{2}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.72e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3719", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluate the series\n$$\nS=\\frac{{1}}{{2}}+\\frac{{1}}{{4}}+\\frac{{1}}{{8}}+\\frac{{1}}{{16}}+\\cdots\n$$\n\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.5\nB. 2.5\nC. 1.25\nD. 1.5\nE. 4\nF. 0.75\nG. 3\nH. 0.25\nI.  1\nJ. 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The series \\( S = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{16} + \\cdots \\) is a geometric series where the first term \\( a = \\frac{1}{2} \\) and the common ratio \\( r = \\frac{1}{2} \\). The sum of an infinite geometric series is given by the formula \\( S = \\frac{a}{1 - r} \\). Substituting the values, we get \\( S = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{1 - \\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{\\frac{1}{2}} = 1 \\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 169, "output_tokens": 169, "total_tokens": 338}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The series \\( S = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{16} + \\cdots \\) is a geometric series where the first term \\( a = \\frac{1}{2} \\) and the common ratio \\( r = \\frac{1}{2} \\). The sum of an infinite geometric series is given by the formula \\( S = \\frac{a}{1 - r} \\). Substituting the values, we get \\( S = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{1 - \\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{\\frac{1}{2}} = 1 \\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00012675}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3870", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A red signal flare for use on railroads is made by mixing strontium nitrate, carbon, and sulfur in the proportions as shown by the equation 2Sr (NO_3)_2 + 3C + 2S \\ding{{217}} Complete and balance the equation (no atmospheric oxygen is necessary).\n\nOptions: \nA. 2SrO + 2N_2 + 4CO_2 + 2SO_2\nB. 2SrO + 3N_2 + 3CO_2 + S_2\nC. SrO + 2N_2 + 3CO_2 + SO_2\nD. 2SrO + N_2 + 3CO_2 + 2SO_2\nE. SrO + N_2 + 3CO + 2SO_2\nF. SrO + 2N_2 + 3CO_2 + 2SO_2\nG. 2SrO + 2N_2 + 3CO + 3SO_2\nH. 2SrO + 2N_2 + 2CO_2 + 2SO_2\nI. 2SrO + 2N_2 + 3CO_2 + 2SO_2\nJ. 2Sr + 2N_2 + 3CO_2 + 2SO_2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To balance the given reaction of the red signal flare, we consider the products formed from strontium nitrate, carbon, and sulfur. The correct balanced equation must include proper stoichiometric coefficients for all the reactants and products. The most accurate option that fits all requirements is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{I}\\)", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 360, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 423}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To balance the given reaction of the red signal flare, we consider the products formed from strontium nitrate, carbon, and sulfur. The correct balanced equation must include proper stoichiometric coefficients for all the reactants and products. The most accurate option that fits all requirements is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{I}\\)", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.180000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4262", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Simplify the quotient [{{2x^0}} / {{(2x)^0}}].\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\nB. 0\nC. x^2\nD. 2x\nE. 1/x\nF. 2/x\nG. 2\nH. 0.5\nI. 1\nJ. x\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To simplify the quotient \\(\\frac{2x^0}{(2x)^0}\\), we first recognize that \\(x^0 = 1\\) for any non-zero \\(x\\). Therefore, \\(2x^0 = 2\\) and \\((2x)^0 = 1\\), leading to \\(\\frac{2}{1} = 2\\). Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 140, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 233}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To simplify the quotient \\(\\frac{2x^0}{(2x)^0}\\), we first recognize that \\(x^0 = 1\\) for any non-zero \\(x\\). Therefore, \\(2x^0 = 2\\) and \\((2x)^0 = 1\\), leading to \\(\\frac{2}{1} = 2\\). Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.68e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3821", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: It has been suggested that the time required for light to travel 1 cm be used as a unit of time called the \"jiffy\". How many seconds correspond to one jiffy? The speed of light is about 3.0 × 10^8 m/sec.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 jiffy = 3.3 × 10^-12 sec\nB. 1 jiffy = 4.5 × 10^-9 sec\nC. 1 jiffy = 3.3 × 10^-9 sec\nD. 1 jiffy = 7.5 × 10^-11 sec\nE. 1 jiffy = 2.2 × 10^-10 sec\nF. 1 jiffy = 6.6 × 10^-12 sec\nG. 1 jiffy = 1.0 × 10^-10 sec\nH. 1 jiffy = 5.0 × 10^-11 sec\nI. 1 jiffy = 3.3 × 10^-10 sec\nJ. 1 jiffy = 3.3 × 10^-11 sec\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine how long it takes light to travel 1 cm, we can use the speed of light, which is approximately \\(3.0 \\times 10^8 \\text{ m/s}\\). Since 1 cm is \\(0.01 \\text{ m}\\), we can calculate the time \\(t\\) it takes for light to travel that distance using the formula \\(t = \\frac{distance}{speed}\\):\n\n\\[\nt = \\frac{0.01 \\text{ m}}{3.0 \\times 10^8 \\text{ m/s}} = \\frac{0.01}{3.0 \\times 10^8} \\approx 3.33 \\times 10^{-11} \\text{ sec}\n\\]\n\nThus, 1 jiffy corresponds to \\(3.3 \\times 10^{-11}\\) seconds. The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 300, "output_tokens": 189, "total_tokens": 489}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine how long it takes light to travel 1 cm, we can use the speed of light, which is approximately \\(3.0 \\times 10^8 \\text{ m/s}\\). Since 1 cm is \\(0.01 \\text{ m}\\), we can calculate the time \\(t\\) it takes for light to travel that distance using the formula \\(t = \\frac{distance}{speed}\\):\n\n\\[\nt = \\frac{0.01 \\text{ m}}{3.0 \\times 10^8 \\text{ m/s}} = \\frac{0.01}{3.0 \\times 10^8} \\approx 3.33 \\times 10^{-11} \\text{ sec}\n\\]\n\nThus, 1 jiffy corresponds to \\(3.3 \\times 10^{-11}\\) seconds. The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001584}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4071", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Calculate the angle that the spin vector $S$ makes with the $z$ axis for an electron with spin function $\\alpha$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 180.0 $^{{\\circ}}$\nB. 90.0 $^{{\\circ}}$\nC. 120.0 $^{{\\circ}}$\nD. 0.0 $^{{\\circ}}$\nE. 135.0 $^{{\\circ}}$\nF. 30.0 $^{{\\circ}}$\nG. 60.0 $^{{\\circ}}$\nH. 75.0 $^{{\\circ}}$\nI.  54.7 $^{{\\circ}}$\nJ. 45.0 $^{{\\circ}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The spin function \\(\\alpha\\) represents the spin state of an electron that is aligned with the \\(z\\) axis, indicating that the angle between the spin vector \\(S\\) and the \\(z\\) axis is 0 degrees since it points directly along the \\(z\\) axis. Thus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{D}\\)", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 224, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 299}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The spin function \\(\\alpha\\) represents the spin state of an electron that is aligned with the \\(z\\) axis, indicating that the angle between the spin vector \\(S\\) and the \\(z\\) axis is 0 degrees since it points directly along the \\(z\\) axis. Thus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{D}\\)", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.859999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4179", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use the quadratic formula to solve for x in the equation x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0.\n\nOptions: \nA. x = -1 and x = 6\nB. x = 0 and x = 6\nC. x = 1 and x = 2\nD. x = 3 and x = 2\nE. x = 1 and x = 6\nF. x = 3 and x = 4\nG. x = 2.5 and x = -2.4\nH. x = -2 and x = -3\nI. x = 4 and x = 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To solve the equation \\(x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0\\) using the quadratic formula \\(x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), we identify \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = -5\\), and \\(c = 6\\). Calculating the discriminant: \\(b^2 - 4ac = (-5)^2 - 4(1)(6) = 25 - 24 = 1\\). Applying the formula gives \\(x = \\frac{5 \\pm 1}{2}\\), leading to solutions \\(x = 3\\) and \\(x = 2\\).\n\nThus, the correct option is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 161, "total_tokens": 363}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To solve the equation \\(x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0\\) using the quadratic formula \\(x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), we identify \\(a = 1\\), \\(b = -5\\), and \\(c = 6\\). Calculating the discriminant: \\(b^2 - 4ac = (-5)^2 - 4(1)(6) = 25 - 24 = 1\\). Applying the formula gives \\(x = \\frac{5 \\pm 1}{2}\\), leading to solutions \\(x = 3\\) and \\(x = 2\\).\n\nThus, the correct option is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001269}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3907", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the uncertainty of the momentum of an electron if we know its position is somewhere in a $10 \\mathrm{{pm}}$ interval?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4.2 $10^{{-23}} \\mathrm{{~kg}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{m}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{s}}^{{-1}}$\nB. 7.2 $10^{{-23}} \\mathrm{{~kg}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{m}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{s}}^{{-1}}$\nC. 5.0 $10^{{-23}} \\mathrm{{~kg}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{m}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{s}}^{{-1}}$\nD. 3.3 $10^{{-23}} \\mathrm{{~kg}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{m}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{s}}^{{-1}}$\nE. 7.7 $10^{{-23}} \\mathrm{{~kg}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{m}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{s}}^{{-1}}$\nF. 2.1 $10^{{-23}} \\mathrm{{~kg}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{m}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{s}}^{{-1}}$\nG. 5.5 $10^{{-23}} \\mathrm{{~kg}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{m}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{s}}^{{-1}}$\nH.  6.6 $10^{{-23}} \\mathrm{{~kg}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{m}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{s}}^{{-1}}$\nI. 8.8 $10^{{-23}} \\mathrm{{~kg}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{m}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{s}}^{{-1}}$\nJ. 9.1 $10^{{-23}} \\mathrm{{~kg}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{m}} \\cdot \\mathrm{{s}}^{{-1}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the uncertainty in momentum \\( (\\Delta p) \\) of the electron given the position uncertainty \\( (\\Delta x) \\) of \\( 10 \\mathrm{~pm} = 10 \\times 10^{-12} \\mathrm{~m} \\), we can use Heisenberg's uncertainty principle: \n\n\\[\n\\Delta p \\Delta x \\geq \\frac{\\hbar}{2}\n\\]\n\nCalculating the uncertainty in momentum yields an approximate value, which matches option B, \\( 7.2 \\times 10^{-23} \\mathrm{~kg} \\cdot \\mathrm{m} \\cdot \\mathrm{s}^{-1} \\). Thus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 506, "output_tokens": 154, "total_tokens": 660}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the uncertainty in momentum \\( (\\Delta p) \\) of the electron given the position uncertainty \\( (\\Delta x) \\) of \\( 10 \\mathrm{~pm} = 10 \\times 10^{-12} \\mathrm{~m} \\), we can use Heisenberg's uncertainty principle: \n\n\\[\n\\Delta p \\Delta x \\geq \\frac{\\hbar}{2}\n\\]\n\nCalculating the uncertainty in momentum yields an approximate value, which matches option B, \\( 7.2 \\times 10^{-23} \\mathrm{~kg} \\cdot \\mathrm{m} \\cdot \\mathrm{s}^{-1} \\). Thus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001683}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3446", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following should be named using Roman numerals after the cation?\n\nOptions: \nA. AlBr3\nB. Na2O\nC. K2Cr2O7\nD. CaCl2\nE. NH4Cl\nF. H2SO4\nG. MgSO4\nH. CuCl2\nI. Zn(NO3)2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Copper (Cu) can have multiple oxidation states, and therefore, when naming CuCl2, it is common to use Roman numerals to indicate its oxidation state, which is +2 in this case. The other compounds listed either contain cations that do not have variable oxidation states or are composed of non-metals, which do not require Roman numerals.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 141, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 222}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Copper (Cu) can have multiple oxidation states, and therefore, when naming CuCl2, it is common to use Roman numerals to indicate its oxidation state, which is +2 in this case. The other compounds listed either contain cations that do not have variable oxidation states or are composed of non-metals, which do not require Roman numerals.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.975e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3384", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Solve x^2 - 7x + 10 = 0.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3, 4\nB. 1, 3\nC. 4, 6\nD. 6, 1\nE. -5, -2\nF. -2, 5\nG. 7, 9\nH. 5, 2\nI. 0, 7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To solve the equation \\(x^2 - 7x + 10 = 0\\), we can factor it as \\((x - 2)(x - 5) = 0\\). This gives us the solutions \\(x = 2\\) and \\(x = 5\\). Therefore, the correct answer is option H, which corresponds to the roots 5 and 2.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 152, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 246}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To solve the equation \\(x^2 - 7x + 10 = 0\\), we can factor it as \\((x - 2)(x - 5) = 0\\). This gives us the solutions \\(x = 2\\) and \\(x = 5\\). Therefore, the correct answer is option H, which corresponds to the roots 5 and 2.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.92e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3367", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Calculate the percentage difference between $\\ln (1+x)$ and $x$ for $x=0.0050$\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.490 %\nB. 3.750 %\nC. 0.005 %\nD. 0.050 %\nE. 4.990 %\nF. 1.250 %\nG. 5.000 %\nH. 0.100 %\nI. 0.025 %\nJ.  0.249 %\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To calculate the percentage difference between $\\ln(1+x)$ and $x$ for $x=0.0050$, we first evaluate $\\ln(1 + 0.0050)$. Using a calculator, we find that $\\ln(1.005) \\approx 0.004988$. The absolute difference is $|0.004988 - 0.0050| \\approx 0.000012$, and the percentage difference relative to $x$ is $\\frac{0.000012}{0.0050} \\times 100 \\approx 0.00024\\%$. This corresponds to option J, hence the answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 161, "output_tokens": 141, "total_tokens": 302}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To calculate the percentage difference between $\\ln(1+x)$ and $x$ for $x=0.0050$, we first evaluate $\\ln(1 + 0.0050)$. Using a calculator, we find that $\\ln(1.005) \\approx 0.004988$. The absolute difference is $|0.004988 - 0.0050| \\approx 0.000012$, and the percentage difference relative to $x$ is $\\frac{0.000012}{0.0050} \\times 100 \\approx 0.00024\\%$. This corresponds to option J, hence the answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00010875000000000001}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3903", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $w$ be the variable defined as the number of heads that show when two coins are tossed simultaneously. Find $\\langle w\\rangle$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.25\nB.  1\nC. 3\nD. 0\nE. 2.5\nF. 2\nG. 1.25\nH. 1.5\nI. 0.75\nJ. 0.5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "When tossing two coins, the possible outcomes are: HH (2 heads), HT (1 head), TH (1 head), and TT (0 heads). The probabilities for these outcomes are: HH - 1/4, HT - 1/4, TH - 1/4, and TT - 1/4. Therefore, the expected value \\( \\langle w \\rangle \\) is calculated as \\( \\langle w \\rangle = 0 \\cdot (1/4) + 1 \\cdot (1/2) + 2 \\cdot (1/4) = 0 + 0.5 + 0.5 = 1 \\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 159, "output_tokens": 157, "total_tokens": 316}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "When tossing two coins, the possible outcomes are: HH (2 heads), HT (1 head), TH (1 head), and TT (0 heads). The probabilities for these outcomes are: HH - 1/4, HT - 1/4, TH - 1/4, and TT - 1/4. Therefore, the expected value \\( \\langle w \\rangle \\) is calculated as \\( \\langle w \\rangle = 0 \\cdot (1/4) + 1 \\cdot (1/2) + 2 \\cdot (1/4) = 0 + 0.5 + 0.5 = 1 \\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00011805}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3717", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Calculate the percentage difference between $e^x$ and $1+x$ for $x=0.0050$\n\nOptions: \nA. 7.50 $10^{{-3}} \\%$\nB. 2.50 $10^{{-3}} \\%$\nC. 0.75 $10^{{-3}} \\%$\nD. 2.00 $10^{{-3}} \\%$\nE.  1.25 $10^{{-3}} \\%$\nF. 4.50 $10^{{-3}} \\%$\nG. 6.25 $10^{{-3}} \\%$\nH. 0.50 $10^{{-3}} \\%$\nI. 5.00 $10^{{-3}} \\%$\nJ. 3.00 $10^{{-3}} \\%$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To calculate the percentage difference between \\( e^x \\) and \\( 1+x \\) for \\( x = 0.0050 \\):\n\n1. Calculate \\( e^{0.0050} \\) using the Taylor series approximation (for small \\( x \\)): \\( e^x \\approx 1 + x + \\frac{x^2}{2} = 1 + 0.0050 + \\frac{0.0050^2}{2} \\).\n2. This gives \\( e^{0.0050} \\approx 1 + 0.0050 + 0.0000125 = 1.0050125 \\).\n3. \\( 1 + 0.0050 = 1.0050 \\).\n4. The difference \\( e^{0.0050} - (1 + 0.0050) = 1.0050125 - 1.0050 = 0.0000125 \\) and the percentage difference is \\(\\frac{0.0000125}{1 + 0.0050} \\times 100 \\approx 0.00125\\%\\).\n\nThus, the most likely correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 251, "output_tokens": 251, "total_tokens": 502}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To calculate the percentage difference between \\( e^x \\) and \\( 1+x \\) for \\( x = 0.0050 \\):\n\n1. Calculate \\( e^{0.0050} \\) using the Taylor series approximation (for small \\( x \\)): \\( e^x \\approx 1 + x + \\frac{x^2}{2} = 1 + 0.0050 + \\frac{0.0050^2}{2} \\).\n2. This gives \\( e^{0.0050} \\approx 1 + 0.0050 + 0.0000125 = 1.0050125 \\).\n3. \\( 1 + 0.0050 = 1.0050 \\).\n4. The difference \\( e^{0.0050} - (1 + 0.0050) = 1.0050125 - 1.0050 = 0.0000125 \\) and the percentage difference is \\(\\frac{0.0000125}{1 + 0.0050} \\times 100 \\approx 0.00125\\%\\).\n\nThus, the most likely correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00018824999999999997}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4362", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Estimate the zero-point entropy of NO.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.98 cal mol^-1 K^-1\nB. 1.10 cal mol^-1 K^-1\nC. 3.20 cal mol^-1 K^-1\nD. 2.50 cal mol^-1 K^-1\nE. 0.00 cal mol^-1 K^-1\nF. 1.75 cal mol^-1 K^-1\nG. 0.69 cal mol^-1 K^-1\nH. 2.78 cal mol^-1 K^-1\nI. 4.00 cal mol^-1 K^-1\nJ. 1.38 cal mol^-1 K^-1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The zero-point entropy of a diatomic molecule like nitric oxide (NO) can typically be estimated using statistical thermodynamics, and for such molecules, values are often around 2.5 cal mol^-1 K^-1. Comparing the options given, the best estimate aligns with D. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 213, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 284}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The zero-point entropy of a diatomic molecule like nitric oxide (NO) can typically be estimated using statistical thermodynamics, and for such molecules, values are often around 2.5 cal mol^-1 K^-1. Comparing the options given, the best estimate aligns with D. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.455e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4029", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The unaided eye can perceive objects which have a diameterof 0.1 mm. What is the diameter in inches?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.007874 inches\nB. 0.000039 inches\nC. 0.039370 inches\nD. 3.94 ×10^3 inches\nE. 0.000787 inches\nF. 5.8 ×10^3 inches\nG. 0.000394 inches\nH. 0.003937 inches\nI. 2.54 ×10^3 inches\nJ. 1.2 ×10^3 inches\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To convert 0.1 mm to inches, we use the conversion factor where 1 mm is approximately 0.03937 inches. Therefore, 0.1 mm is equal to 0.1 × 0.03937 = 0.003937 inches. The correct answer is \\boxed{H}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 192, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 257}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To convert 0.1 mm to inches, we use the conversion factor where 1 mm is approximately 0.03937 inches. Therefore, 0.1 mm is equal to 0.1 × 0.03937 = 0.003937 inches. The correct answer is \\boxed{H}.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.78e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4064", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the orbital angular momentum quantum number, l, of the electron that is most easily removed when ground-state aluminum is ionized?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 2\nC. -1\nD. 4\nE. 6\nF. 3\nG. 7\nH. 1\nI. 0\nJ. 8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The ground-state electron configuration of aluminum (Al) is \\(1s^2 2s^2 2p^6 3s^2 3p^1\\). The electron that is most easily removed during ionization is typically the one with the highest principal quantum number, which in this case corresponds to the \\(3p^1\\) electron with an orbital angular momentum quantum number \\(l = 1\\). Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 142, "output_tokens": 101, "total_tokens": 243}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The ground-state electron configuration of aluminum (Al) is \\(1s^2 2s^2 2p^6 3s^2 3p^1\\). The electron that is most easily removed during ionization is typically the one with the highest principal quantum number, which in this case corresponds to the \\(3p^1\\) electron with an orbital angular momentum quantum number \\(l = 1\\). Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.19e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4206", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There are some 25,000ribosomesin an E. coli cell. If the structucalproteins of theseribosomeswere stretched out end to end as fully extended polypeptide chains, how many times could they encircle the E. coli cell?Assume that theribosomesare 180 \\AA in diameter, with a specific gravity of 1.0, and that they contain 40% protein. Assume that the E. coli cell is a sphere 1\\mu in diameter.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.10 × 10^4 times\nB. 1.26 × 10^4 times\nC. 0.80 × 10^4 times\nD. 3.50 × 10^4 times\nE. 1.76 × 10^4 times\nF. 3.00 × 10^4 times\nG. 4.00 × 10^4 times\nH. 2.54 × 10^4 times\nI. 1.00 × 10^4 times\nJ. 2.00 × 10^4 times\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the answer, we first calculate the total amount of protein in the ribosomes and then the length of the polypeptide chains produced from that protein. Finally, by determining the circumference of the E. coli cell, we can find how many times the extended chains can encircle the cell.\n\nAfter performing the necessary calculations, the most likely correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 300, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 379}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the answer, we first calculate the total amount of protein in the ribosomes and then the length of the polypeptide chains produced from that protein. Finally, by determining the circumference of the E. coli cell, we can find how many times the extended chains can encircle the cell.\n\nAfter performing the necessary calculations, the most likely correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.24e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3463", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Two narrow slits separated by $0.10 \\mathrm{{~mm}}$ are illuminated by light of wavelength $600 \\mathrm{{~nm}}$. What is the angular position of the first maximum in the interference pattern? If a detector is located $2.00 \\mathrm{{~m}}$ beyond the slits, what is the distance between the central maximum and the first maximum?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4 mm\nB. 18 mm\nC. 14 mm\nD. 24 mm\nE. 8 mm\nF.  12 mm\nG. 6 mm\nH. 20 mm\nI. 10 mm\nJ. 16 mm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the angular position of the first maximum in the interference pattern, we use the formula for the position of the maxima: \n\n\\[\n\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{m \\lambda}{d}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(m = 1\\) for the first maximum, \\(\\lambda = 600 \\, \\text{nm} = 600 \\times 10^{-9} \\, \\text{m}\\), and \\(d = 0.10 \\, \\text{mm} = 0.10 \\times 10^{-3} \\, \\text{m}\\). Substituting these values leads to\n\n\\[\n\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{600 \\times 10^{-9}}{0.10 \\times 10^{-3}} = 0.006.\n\\]\n\nUsing the small angle approximation \\(\\theta \\approx \\sin(\\theta)\\), we find \\(\\theta \\approx 0.006 \\, \\text{radians}\\). To find the distance \\(y\\) from the central maximum to the first maximum:\n\n\\[\ny = L \\tan(\\theta) \\approx L \\sin(\\theta) = 2.00 \\, \\text{m} \\times 0.006 = 0.012 \\, \\text{m} = 12 \\, \\text{mm}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the distance is 12 mm, corresponding to option F.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 206, "output_tokens": 309, "total_tokens": 515}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the angular position of the first maximum in the interference pattern, we use the formula for the position of the maxima: \n\n\\[\n\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{m \\lambda}{d}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(m = 1\\) for the first maximum, \\(\\lambda = 600 \\, \\text{nm} = 600 \\times 10^{-9} \\, \\text{m}\\), and \\(d = 0.10 \\, \\text{mm} = 0.10 \\times 10^{-3} \\, \\text{m}\\). Substituting these values leads to\n\n\\[\n\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{600 \\times 10^{-9}}{0.10 \\times 10^{-3}} = 0.006.\n\\]\n\nUsing the small angle approximation \\(\\theta \\approx \\sin(\\theta)\\), we find \\(\\theta \\approx 0.006 \\, \\text{radians}\\). To find the distance \\(y\\) from the central maximum to the first maximum:\n\n\\[\ny = L \\tan(\\theta) \\approx L \\sin(\\theta) = 2.00 \\, \\text{m} \\times 0.006 = 0.012 \\, \\text{m} = 12 \\, \\text{mm}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the distance is 12 mm, corresponding to option F.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00021629999999999997}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3567", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Solve 6x^2 - 7x - 20 = 0.\n\nOptions: \nA. 5/2, 4/3\nB. -5/3, 4/2\nC. 5/3, -4/2\nD. 2, -10\nE. 4, -5\nF. -5/2, 4/3\nG. -5/6, 4/5\nH. 5/2, -4/3\nI. 5, 4\nJ. 5, -4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To solve the equation \\(6x^2 - 7x - 20 = 0\\), we can use the quadratic formula \\(x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 6\\), \\(b = -7\\), and \\(c = -20\\). Applying this, we find the roots to be \\(x = \\frac{5}{2}\\) and \\(x = -\\frac{4}{3}\\). Therefore, the correct answer is option H.\n\n\\(\\boxed{H}\\)", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 186, "output_tokens": 124, "total_tokens": 310}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To solve the equation \\(6x^2 - 7x - 20 = 0\\), we can use the quadratic formula \\(x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\), where \\(a = 6\\), \\(b = -7\\), and \\(c = -20\\). Applying this, we find the roots to be \\(x = \\frac{5}{2}\\) and \\(x = -\\frac{4}{3}\\). Therefore, the correct answer is option H.\n\n\\(\\boxed{H}\\)", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001023}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3666", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Classify the bonds in the following as ionic, ionic - covalent, covalent - ionic and covalent: I_2,LiCl,MgTe, Cl_2O, H_2S.\n\nOptions: \nA. I_2 is covalent, LiCl is covalent-ionic, MgTe is ionic, Cl_2O is covalent, H_2S is ionic\nB. I_2 is ionic, LiCl is covalent, MgTe is covalent, Cl_2O is covalent-ionic, H_2S is ionic-covalent\nC. I_2 is ionic-covalent, LiCl is ionic, MgTe is covalent, Cl_2O is covalent-ionic, H_2S is ionic\nD. I_2 is covalent, LiCl is ionic-covalent, MgTe is ionic, Cl_2O is ionic, H_2S is covalent\nE. I_2 is covalent, LiCl is covalent, MgTe is ionic-covalent, Cl_2O is ionic-covalent, H_2S is ionic\nF. I_2 is ionic, LiCl is covalent, MgTe is covalent-ionic, Cl_2O is ionic, H_2S is covalent-ionic\nG. I_2 is ionic, LiCl is covalent-ionic, MgTe is ionic-covalent, Cl_2O is ionic, H_2S is covalent\nH. I_2 is covalent, LiCl is ionic, MgTe is covalent-ionic, Cl_2O is covalent-ionic, H_2S is covalent-ionic\nI. I_2 is covalent-ionic, LiCl is ionic, MgTe is covalent, Cl_2O is ionic, H_2S is covalent\nJ. I_2 is covalent-ionic, LiCl is covalent, MgTe is ionic, Cl_2O is covalent, H_2S is covalent\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). I_2 is covalent as it is a diatomic molecule of the same element. LiCl is ionic due to the transfer of electrons between lithium and chlorine, MgTe is ionic as it consists of metals and nonmetals with high electronegativity differences, Cl_2O is covalent as it involves two nonmetals, and H_2S is covalent since it is between nonmetals.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 496, "output_tokens": 96, "total_tokens": 592}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). I_2 is covalent as it is a diatomic molecule of the same element. LiCl is ionic due to the transfer of electrons between lithium and chlorine, MgTe is ionic as it consists of metals and nonmetals with high electronegativity differences, Cl_2O is covalent as it involves two nonmetals, and H_2S is covalent since it is between nonmetals.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.000132}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3983", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The duration of a $90^{{\\circ}}$ or $180^{{\\circ}}$ pulse depends on the strength of the $\\mathscr{{B}}_1$ field. If a $180^{{\\circ}}$ pulse requires $12.5 \\mu \\mathrm{{s}}$, what is the strength of the $\\mathscr{{B}}_1$ field? \n\nOptions: \nA. 3.8 $10^{{-4}} \\mathrm{{~T}}$\nB. 4.2 $10^{{-4}} \\mathrm{{~T}}$\nC. 4.7 $10^{{-4}} \\mathrm{{~T}}$\nD. 6.2 $10^{{-4}} \\mathrm{{~T}}$\nE. 7.1 $10^{{-4}} \\mathrm{{~T}}$\nF. 7.8 $10^{{-4}} \\mathrm{{~T}}$\nG. 9.3 $10^{{-4}} \\mathrm{{~T}}$\nH.  5.9 $10^{{-4}} \\mathrm{{~T}}$\nI. 5.0 $10^{{-4}} \\mathrm{{~T}}$\nJ. 8.4 $10^{{-4}} \\mathrm{{~T}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the strength of the \\( \\mathscr{B}_1 \\) field based on the duration of a \\( 180^{\\circ} \\) pulse, we can use the relationship between pulse duration, field strength, and desired flip angle. Given that a \\( 180^{\\circ} \\) pulse requires \\( 12.5 \\, \\mu \\mathrm{s} \\), the strength of the \\( \\mathscr{B}_1 \\) field can be calculated with the formula related to the specific magnetic moments involved. The value that fits this calculation closely aligns with option H, \\( 5.9 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~T} \\).\n\nThus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 348, "output_tokens": 154, "total_tokens": 502}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the strength of the \\( \\mathscr{B}_1 \\) field based on the duration of a \\( 180^{\\circ} \\) pulse, we can use the relationship between pulse duration, field strength, and desired flip angle. Given that a \\( 180^{\\circ} \\) pulse requires \\( 12.5 \\, \\mu \\mathrm{s} \\), the strength of the \\( \\mathscr{B}_1 \\) field can be calculated with the formula related to the specific magnetic moments involved. The value that fits this calculation closely aligns with option H, \\( 5.9 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~T} \\).\n\nThus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001446}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3633", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a macroscopic object of mass $1.0 \\mathrm{{~g}}$ moving with speed $1.0 \\mathrm{{~cm}} / \\mathrm{{s}}$ in a one-dimensional box of length $1.0 \\mathrm{{~cm}}$, find the quantum number $n$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 8$10^{{26}}$\nB. 1$10^{{27}}$\nC. 1$10^{{26}}$\nD. 9$10^{{26}}$\nE. 6$10^{{26}}$\nF. 2$10^{{26}}$\nG. 4$10^{{26}}$\nH. 7$10^{{26}}$\nI. 5$10^{{26}}$\nJ.  3$10^{{26}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the quantum number \\( n \\) for a macroscopic object in a one-dimensional box, we can use the de Broglie wavelength formula and the relationship to the box length. The de Broglie wavelength \\( \\lambda \\) is given by \\( \\lambda = \\frac{h}{p} \\) where \\( p = mv \\) (momentum). Given the mass \\( m = 1.0 \\, \\text{g} = 1.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\, \\text{kg} \\) and speed \\( v = 1.0 \\, \\text{cm/s} = 1.0 \\times 10^{-2} \\, \\text{m/s} \\), we calculate the momentum and then find the corresponding quantum number \\( n \\).\n\nCalculating, we have \\( p = (1.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\, \\text{kg})(1.0 \\times 10^{-2} \\, \\text{m/s}) = 1.0 \\times 10^{-5} \\, \\text{kg m/s} \\). Then, using \\( \\lambda = \\frac{h}{p} \\) and noting that \\( h = 6.626 \\times 10^{-34} \\, \\text{J s} \\), we find \\( \\lambda \\approx 6.626 \\times 10^{-29} \\, \\text{m} \\). The quantum number \\( n \\) is then determined by \\( \\lambda = \\frac{2L}{n} \\) where \\( L = 1.0 \\, \\text{cm} = 0.01 \\, \\text{m} \\), giving roughly \\( n \\approx 6.6 \\times 10^{26} \\).\n\nThus, the best answer from the options provided is \\( \\boxed{E} \\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 241, "output_tokens": 396, "total_tokens": 637}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the quantum number \\( n \\) for a macroscopic object in a one-dimensional box, we can use the de Broglie wavelength formula and the relationship to the box length. The de Broglie wavelength \\( \\lambda \\) is given by \\( \\lambda = \\frac{h}{p} \\) where \\( p = mv \\) (momentum). Given the mass \\( m = 1.0 \\, \\text{g} = 1.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\, \\text{kg} \\) and speed \\( v = 1.0 \\, \\text{cm/s} = 1.0 \\times 10^{-2} \\, \\text{m/s} \\), we calculate the momentum and then find the corresponding quantum number \\( n \\).\n\nCalculating, we have \\( p = (1.0 \\times 10^{-3} \\, \\text{kg})(1.0 \\times 10^{-2} \\, \\text{m/s}) = 1.0 \\times 10^{-5} \\, \\text{kg m/s} \\). Then, using \\( \\lambda = \\frac{h}{p} \\) and noting that \\( h = 6.626 \\times 10^{-34} \\, \\text{J s} \\), we find \\( \\lambda \\approx 6.626 \\times 10^{-29} \\, \\text{m} \\). The quantum number \\( n \\) is then determined by \\( \\lambda = \\frac{2L}{n} \\) where \\( L = 1.0 \\, \\text{cm} = 0.01 \\, \\text{m} \\), giving roughly \\( n \\approx 6.6 \\times 10^{26} \\).\n\nThus, the best answer from the options provided is \\( \\boxed{E} \\).", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00027374999999999996}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3989", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Show that l'Hôpital's rule amounts to forming a Taylor expansion of both the numerator and the denominator. Evaluate the limit\n$$\n\\lim _{{x \\rightarrow 0}} \\frac{{\\ln (1+x)-x}}{{x^2}}\n$$\nboth ways.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3/2\nB. 0\nC. -3/2\nD. 2\nE. 1/4\nF. 1\nG. -1\nH.  -1/2\nI. 1/2\nJ. -2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To evaluate the limit \\(\\lim _{{x \\rightarrow 0}} \\frac{{\\ln (1+x)-x}}{{x^2}}\\), we can apply Taylor expansions: the Taylor series for \\(\\ln(1+x)\\) at \\(x=0\\) is \\(x - \\frac{x^2}{2} + \\frac{x^3}{3} + O(x^4)\\). Thus, \\(\\ln(1+x) - x \\approx -\\frac{x^2}{2} + O(x^3)\\), leading to the limit becoming \\(-\\frac{1}{2}\\) upon substitution, yielding the final result of \\(-\\frac{1}{2}\\). \n\nThus, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 183, "output_tokens": 161, "total_tokens": 344}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To evaluate the limit \\(\\lim _{{x \\rightarrow 0}} \\frac{{\\ln (1+x)-x}}{{x^2}}\\), we can apply Taylor expansions: the Taylor series for \\(\\ln(1+x)\\) at \\(x=0\\) is \\(x - \\frac{x^2}{2} + \\frac{x^3}{3} + O(x^4)\\). Thus, \\(\\ln(1+x) - x \\approx -\\frac{x^2}{2} + O(x^3)\\), leading to the limit becoming \\(-\\frac{1}{2}\\) upon substitution, yielding the final result of \\(-\\frac{1}{2}\\). \n\nThus, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00012405}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4093", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An excellent method of making alcohols is the reaction of an aldehydeon a Grignard reagent. If you perform this reaction, you must scrupulously dry thealdehydebefore adding it to the Grignard reagent. Why?\n\nOptions: \nA. The aldehyde's structure is altered by the presence of water\nB. The aldehyde can react with other components if not dried\nC. Water increases the viscosity of the reaction mixture, reducing the efficiency\nD. Water can initiate a side reaction with the Grignard reagent, forming an unwanted byproduct\nE. Water can cause the Grignard reagent to decompose into a hydrocarbon\nF. The dry aldehyde can absorb moisture from the air, which can slow down the reaction\nG. The Grignard reagent is sensitive to temperature changes\nH. The aldehyde will polymerize if not dried\nI. The aldehyde needs to be in a dry state for the reaction to occur\nJ. The presence of water reduces or eliminates the Grignard reagent from solution\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Water can initiate a side reaction with the Grignard reagent, forming an unwanted byproduct, such as an alkane, which makes it crucial to keep both the Grignard reagent and the aldehyde dry. Any water present can react with the Grignard reagent, rendering it ineffective for the desired reaction.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 277, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 349}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Water can initiate a side reaction with the Grignard reagent, forming an unwanted byproduct, such as an alkane, which makes it crucial to keep both the Grignard reagent and the aldehyde dry. Any water present can react with the Grignard reagent, rendering it ineffective for the desired reaction.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.475e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3963", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If one increases the angle away from the Z axis, how does the wave function for a 2P_Z electron change?\n\nOptions: \nA. The wave function increases.\nB. The wave function inverts in phase.\nC. The wave function and the electron density for a 2P_Z electron decreases.\nD. The wave function becomes constant throughout all angles.\nE. There is no change in the wave function or electron density.\nF. The electron density spreads out uniformly in all directions.\nG. The electron density becomes more spherically symmetric.\nH. The electron density concentrates on the equatorial plane.\nI. The electron density increases.\nJ. The wave function decreases only along the Z axis.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). As the angle increases away from the Z axis, the probability density associated with the 2P_Z orbital decreases because the 2P_Z wave function has a specific orientation along the Z axis, resulting in lower electron density at other angles. This leads to a concentration of electron density along the Z axis rather than a uniform distribution.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 205, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 282}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). As the angle increases away from the Z axis, the probability density associated with the 2P_Z orbital decreases because the 2P_Z wave function has a specific orientation along the Z axis, resulting in lower electron density at other angles. This leads to a concentration of electron density along the Z axis rather than a uniform distribution.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.695e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3847", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In 1932, many cities showed higher sunlight levels than in the previous year. Explain this observation.\n\nOptions: \nA. The Earth's magnetic field weakened, allowing more solar radiation to reach the surface.\nB. Improved measurement techniques provided more accurate readings of sunlight levels.\nC. Fewer particles were released that could scatter or absorb the sunlight due to reduced industrial activity.\nD. A change in Earth's orbit resulted in longer days and more sunlight during the year.\nE. There were fewer tall buildings blocking the sunlight in 1932.\nF. The Earth's atmosphere had an unusually low amount of ozone, allowing more sunlight to pass through.\nG. There was a large-scale removal of forests, which previously blocked sunlight in many cities.\nH. The sun was closer to the Earth in 1932.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{C}. In 1932, the impact of the Great Depression led to reduced industrial activity, which would have decreased the emission of pollutants that scatter or absorb sunlight, resulting in higher sunlight levels reaching cities.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 222, "output_tokens": 50, "total_tokens": 272}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{C}. In 1932, the impact of the Great Depression led to reduced industrial activity, which would have decreased the emission of pollutants that scatter or absorb sunlight, resulting in higher sunlight levels reaching cities.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.33e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3953", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The number average and weight average molecular-weights are defined as M_n= [(\\sumN_i M_i) / (\\sumN_i)] = [1 / {{\\sum(w_i/ M_i)}}] and M_w = [(\\sumW_iM_i) / (\\sumW_i)] = [(\\sumN_i M^2_i) / (\\sumN_i M_i)] = \\sumw_iM_i respectively, where M_i = molecular weight of theithspecies N_i = moles of molecules with molecular weight M_i W_i= weight of material with molecular weight M_i w_i= weight fraction of molecules of theithspecies. Derive equations analogous to the ones above for the number average,X_n, and weight average,X_w, degree of polymerization.\n\nOptions: \nA. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X^2_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i)]\nB. X_n= [(\\sumW_i X_i) / (\\sumW_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i^3) / (\\sumW_i X_i)]\nC. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^0.5)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i^1.5) / (\\sumN_i)]\nD. X_n= [(\\sumw_i X_i) / (\\sumw_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i^0.5) / (\\sumN_i)]\nE. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^2)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X^2_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^2)]\nF. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i^2) / (\\sumN_i^2 X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i^2)]\nG. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i^3) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i^3)]\nH. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X^2_i) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i)]\nI. X_n= [(\\sumN_i X_i^2) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumN_i X_i) / (\\sumN_i)]\nJ. X_n= [(\\sumW_i X_i^2) / (\\sumN_i X_i)], X_w= [(\\sumW_i X_i) / (\\sumW_i X_i^2)]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). The equations for the number average and weight average degree of polymerization, analogous to their molecular weight counterparts, are defined as \\(X_n = \\left(\\sum N_i X_i\\right) / \\left(\\sum N_i\\right)\\) and \\(X_w = \\left(\\sum N_i X_i^2\\right) / \\left(\\sum N_i X_i\\right)\\). This matches the structure and reasoning provided in option A.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 650, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 753}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). The equations for the number average and weight average degree of polymerization, analogous to their molecular weight counterparts, are defined as \\(X_n = \\left(\\sum N_i X_i\\right) / \\left(\\sum N_i\\right)\\) and \\(X_w = \\left(\\sum N_i X_i^2\\right) / \\left(\\sum N_i X_i\\right)\\). This matches the structure and reasoning provided in option A.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001593}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4175", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Although all electrons spin, only molecules containing unpairedelectrons - only free radicals - giveesrspectra. Why is this? (Hint: Consider the possibility (a)thatone electron of a pair has its spin reversed, or (b)thatboth electrons of a pair have their spins reversed.)\n\nOptions: \nA. Electron pairs have a net magnetic moment\nB. Only electrons in the outermost shell contribute to the magnetic moment, regardless of pairing\nC. Each electron of a pair has a unique magnetic moment\nD. Free radicals lack electron pairs, which is why they cannot generate a magnetic moment\nE. Electron pairs always spin in the same direction, enhancing the magnetic moment\nF. Electron pairs generate a magnetic moment of the same magnitude\nG. Electron pairs have spins that cancel only in the presence of an external magnetic field\nH. Each electron of an electron pair generates a magnetic moment but of equal and opposite magnitude; the electron pair therefore has no net magnetic moment.\nI. Electron pairs generate magnetic moments only at high temperatures\nJ. The magnetic moments of electron pairs reinforce each other, resulting in a double magnetic moment\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Electron pairs in a molecule have spins that are opposite and therefore cancel each other out, resulting in no net magnetic moment. In contrast, free radicals contain unpaired electrons, which have net magnetic moments that contribute to EPR spectra.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 296, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 351}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Electron pairs in a molecule have spins that are opposite and therefore cancel each other out, resulting in no net magnetic moment. In contrast, free radicals contain unpaired electrons, which have net magnetic moments that contribute to EPR spectra.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.74e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3475", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Would you expect He_2^\\oplus to be more stable than He_2? Than He?\n\nOptions: \nA. He_2^\\oplus is the most stable among He, He_2, and He_2^\\oplus\nB. He_2^\\oplus is more stable than He_2 but less stable than He\nC. He, He_2, and He_2^\\oplus have the same stability\nD. He_2^\\oplus is the least stable among He, He_2, and He_2^\\oplus\nE. He and He_2 have the same stability, both more stable than He_2^\\oplus\nF. He_2^\\oplus is more stable than He but less stable than He_2\nG. He_2^\\oplus is less stable than both He_2 and He\nH. He_2^\\oplus and He_2 have the same stability, both more stable than He\nI. He_2^\\oplus and He have the same stability, both less stable than He_2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. He_2^\\oplus, the helium dimer cation, is expected to be less stable than both He_2 (neon-like diatomic molecule with some binding) and He (noble gas atom with a complete shell). The positive charge in He_2^\\oplus destabilizes the molecule compared to the more stable and neutral species.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 290, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 370}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. He_2^\\oplus, the helium dimer cation, is expected to be less stable than both He_2 (neon-like diatomic molecule with some binding) and He (noble gas atom with a complete shell). The positive charge in He_2^\\oplus destabilizes the molecule compared to the more stable and neutral species.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.15e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4259", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Even though 1, 3, 5-trinitrobenzene (TNB) has more shattering power (more brisance) and is no more dangerous to handle, 2, 4, 6-trinitrotoluene (TNT) has always been the high ex-plosive in more general use. Can you suggest a reason (connected with manufacture) for the popularity of TNT? (Benzene and toluene are both readily available materials; for many years benzene was cheaper.)\n\nOptions: \nA. Toluene is more easily nitrated, and therefore more easily polynitrated than benzene.\nB. The nitrating agents required for TNB are less readily available than those needed for TNT.\nC. The production of TNB generates more harmful byproducts compared to TNT.\nD. TNT is more stable than TNB.\nE. Benzene is more easily nitrated than toluene.\nF. The cost of manufacturing TNT is lower.\nG. TNB is more sensitive to friction and shock, making it less safe to manufacture.\nH. The purification process for TNB is more costly and time-consuming than that for TNT.\nI. The chemical process for synthesizing TNB is more complex and requires higher temperatures than TNT.\nJ. TNB has a shorter shelf life than TNT, making it less suitable for long-term storage.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. The synthesis of TNB is indeed more complex and typically requires higher temperatures compared to TNT, making TNT easier and more cost-effective to produce on a larger scale. This complexity in the manufacturing process contributes to TNT's popularity as a high explosive.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 343, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 400}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. The synthesis of TNB is indeed more complex and typically requires higher temperatures compared to TNT, making TNT easier and more cost-effective to produce on a larger scale. This complexity in the manufacturing process contributes to TNT's popularity as a high explosive.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.565e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3785", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following operators isHermitian; d/dx,id/dx, d^2/dx^2?\n\nOptions: \nA. none are Hermitian\nB. b and c are Hermitan\nC. only a is Hermitian\nD. all are Hermitian\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. \n\nNone of the given operators (d/dx, id/dx, d²/dx²) are Hermitian. For an operator to be Hermitian, it must satisfy the condition ⟨ψ|Aφ⟩ = ⟨Aψ|φ⟩ for all functions ψ and φ in the appropriate domain, which is not the case for these operators.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 208}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. \n\nNone of the given operators (d/dx, id/dx, d²/dx²) are Hermitian. For an operator to be Hermitian, it must satisfy the condition ⟨ψ|Aφ⟩ = ⟨Aψ|φ⟩ for all functions ψ and φ in the appropriate domain, which is not the case for these operators.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.08e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3679", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: There exists a carbohydrate that is slightly soluble in water, does not have a sweet taste, but does dissolve slowly when heated with diluteHCl. To what class of carbohydrates does it probably belong?\n\nOptions: \nA. Pentoses\nB. Disaccharides\nC. Polysaccharides\nD. Lipids\nE. Oligosaccharides\nF. Amino acids\nG. Proteins\nH. Mono-saccharides\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The carbohydrate described is slightly soluble in water, lacks sweetness, and dissolves slowly when heated with dilute HCl, which suggests it is a more complex carbohydrate. The characteristics point towards polysaccharides, as they tend to be less soluble and not sweet compared to simpler sugars. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 153, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 221}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The carbohydrate described is slightly soluble in water, lacks sweetness, and dissolves slowly when heated with dilute HCl, which suggests it is a more complex carbohydrate. The characteristics point towards polysaccharides, as they tend to be less soluble and not sweet compared to simpler sugars. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.374999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4421", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suggest a reason why liquid hydrogen fluoride is preferable to concentrated, aqueoushydrobromicacid in inducing propeneto react with benzene to produceisopropylbenzene.\n\nOptions: \nA. Hydrogen fluoride reacts more selectively with propene\nB. Hydrogen fluoride provides a better solvent environment for the reaction\nC. Hydrogen fluoride is less acidic\nD. Hydrogen fluoride has lower molecular weight, which speeds up the reaction\nE. Hydrogen fluoride will give a greater yield of product\nF. Hydrogen fluoride can be recycled more easily in the process\nG. Hydrogen fluoride is a stronger oxidizing agent\nH. Hydrogen fluoride is less reactive\nI. Hydrogen fluoride is more stable\nJ. Hydrogen fluoride has a higher boiling point, which aids in the reaction\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Hydrogen fluoride reacts more selectively with propene compared to concentrated, aqueous hydrobromic acid, which can lead to undesired side reactions. This selectivity is important in producing isopropylbenzene efficiently.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 216, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 270}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Hydrogen fluoride reacts more selectively with propene compared to concentrated, aqueous hydrobromic acid, which can lead to undesired side reactions. This selectivity is important in producing isopropylbenzene efficiently.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.479999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3349", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is incorrectly named?\n\nOptions: \nA. MgO   magnesium oxide\nB. AgNO3   silver nitrate\nC. CuCl2   copper(II) chloride\nD. H2SO4   sulfuric acid\nE. K2Cr2O7   potassium dichromate\nF. Na2SO4   sodium sulfate\nG. Fe(NO3)3   iron(III) nitrate\nH. CaCl2   calcium chloride\nI. AlBr3   aluminum tribromide\nJ. Zn(NO3)2   zinc nitrate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The incorrectly named compound is C. CuCl2 copper(II) chloride. While the name suggests the copper ion has a +2 oxidation state, the correct name should be copper(I) chloride since CuCl2 refers to copper in the +2 state, which is accurately named. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{C}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 182, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 250}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The incorrectly named compound is C. CuCl2 copper(II) chloride. While the name suggests the copper ion has a +2 oxidation state, the correct name should be copper(I) chloride since CuCl2 refers to copper in the +2 state, which is accurately named. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{C}.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.81e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4320", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A buffer is made from equal concentrations of a weak acid and its conjugate base. Doubling the volume of the buffer solution by adding water has what effect on its pH?\n\nOptions: \nA. It causes the pH to fluctuate unpredictably.\nB. It causes the pH to equalize with the water's pH.\nC. It causes the pH to become extremely basic.\nD. It neutralizes the pH completely.\nE. It significantly decreases the pH.\nF. It has little effect.\nG. It significantly increases the pH.\nH. It doubles the pH value.\nI. It changes the pH asymptotically to the pKa of the acid.\nJ. It causes the pH to become extremely acidic.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Doubling the volume of the buffer solution by adding water dilutes both the weak acid and conjugate base equally, but the ratio of their concentrations remains the same, so the pH of the buffer solution remains relatively stable.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 217, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 271}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Doubling the volume of the buffer solution by adding water dilutes both the weak acid and conjugate base equally, but the ratio of their concentrations remains the same, so the pH of the buffer solution remains relatively stable.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.494999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3855", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: From the following five statements, indicate which ones are correct when an ideal gas is allowed to escape rever-sibly and isothermally into a vacuum. [Hint: What is the average kinetic energy of an ideal gas?] 1. W = 0, \\DeltaE = q = a positive number 2. w = P\\DeltaV + V\\DeltaP 3. w = P\\DeltaV, \\DeltaE = 0, q = - P\\DeltaV and is a negative number 4. \\DeltaE = 0, q = - w = a positive number 5. w = 0, q = 0, \\DeltaE = 0\n\nOptions: \nA. All statements are correct\nB. Statements 3 and 4 are correct\nC. Statements 2 and 5 are correct\nD. Statement 1 is correct\nE. Statement 2 is correct\nF. Statements 2, 4, and 5 are correct\nG. Statements 1, 3, and 5 are correct\nH. Statement 4 is correct\nI. Statement 5 is correct\nJ. Statements 1 and 2 are correct\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "For an ideal gas escaping into a vacuum isothermally, the work done (w) is zero because there is no opposing pressure, leading to a change in internal energy (ΔE) also being zero. This means that the heat absorbed (q) is also zero since for an isothermal process ΔE = q + w. Therefore, the correct response is that statement 5 is correct, while the others contain inaccuracies regarding the relationship between work, heat, and energy changes.\n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 311, "output_tokens": 109, "total_tokens": 420}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "For an ideal gas escaping into a vacuum isothermally, the work done (w) is zero because there is no opposing pressure, leading to a change in internal energy (ΔE) also being zero. This means that the heat absorbed (q) is also zero since for an isothermal process ΔE = q + w. Therefore, the correct response is that statement 5 is correct, while the others contain inaccuracies regarding the relationship between work, heat, and energy changes.\n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00011205000000000001}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3622", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Nitrous acid, HNO2, has a pKa value of 3.3. If a solution of nitrous acid is found to have a pH of 4.2, what can be said about the concentration of the conjugate acid/base pair found in solution?\n\nOptions: \nA. [HNO2] > [NO2-]\nB. [H2NO2+] < [NO2-]\nC. [NO2-] < [H2NO2+]\nD. [H2NO2+] > [NO2-]\nE. [NO2-] > [HNO2]\nF. [NO2-] = [HNO2]\nG. [H2NO2+] > [HNO2]\nH. [HNO2] = [H2NO2+]\nI. [HNO2] > [H2NO2+]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the relationship between the concentrations of HNO2 and NO2- in the solution, we can use the Henderson-Hasselbalch equation, which states that pH = pKa + log([A-]/[HA]). In this case, since the pH (4.2) is greater than the pKa (3.3), it indicates that the conjugate base (NO2-) is present in a higher concentration compared to the acid (HNO2). Therefore, the correct choice is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{E}\\)", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 248, "output_tokens": 112, "total_tokens": 360}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the relationship between the concentrations of HNO2 and NO2- in the solution, we can use the Henderson-Hasselbalch equation, which states that pH = pKa + log([A-]/[HA]). In this case, since the pH (4.2) is greater than the pKa (3.3), it indicates that the conjugate base (NO2-) is present in a higher concentration compared to the acid (HNO2). Therefore, the correct choice is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{E}\\)", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00010439999999999999}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3976", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: During the study of the reaction A → 2B, a chemist constructs several graphs. The graph of [A] versus time and the graph of ln [A] versus time both give a curved line; however, the graph of 1/[A] versus time and gives a straight line. This implies the rate law is\n\nOptions: \nA. Rate = k[A]^4\nB. Rate = k[A]^-1\nC. Rate = k[A]^2\nD. Rate = k[A]\nE. Rate = k[A]^-2\nF. Rate = k[A]^0\nG. Rate = k[A]^1/2\nH. Rate = k[A]^-3\nI. Rate = 2k[A]\nJ. Rate = k[A]^3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The reaction A → 2B shows that the graph of 1/[A] versus time is linear, indicating that the reaction follows second-order kinetics with respect to A. A second-order reaction has the form Rate = k[A]^2. Therefore, the most likely correct answer is \n\n\\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 226, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 291}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The reaction A → 2B shows that the graph of 1/[A] versus time is linear, indicating that the reaction follows second-order kinetics with respect to A. A second-order reaction has the form Rate = k[A]^2. Therefore, the most likely correct answer is \n\n\\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.289999999999998e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4193", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \\rho/P, g/liter-atm 10 11 10 (\\rho = density) P,atm: 1 10 20 The critical pressure of this gas must then be (greater than 10atm, greater than 20atm, between 1 and 20atm, between 1 and 10atm, less than 20atm, can't tell).\n\nOptions: \nA. less than 20 atm\nB. greater than 10 atm\nC. between 1 and 10 atm\nD. exactly 20 atm\nE. cannot be determined without additional information\nF. greater than 20 atm\nG. greater than 1 atm\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "Given the information provided, specifically that the critical pressure of a gas is typically related to its behavior under varying conditions, the answer is most likely that the critical pressure must be **greater than 10 atm**. The data does not suggest a specific critical pressure limit of 20 atm, hence **less than 20 atm** could also be a consideration, but it doesn't align with the criteria presented. Thus, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 93, "total_tokens": 293}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "Given the information provided, specifically that the critical pressure of a gas is typically related to its behavior under varying conditions, the answer is most likely that the critical pressure must be **greater than 10 atm**. The data does not suggest a specific critical pressure limit of 20 atm, hence **less than 20 atm** could also be a consideration, but it doesn't align with the criteria presented. Thus, the most appropriate answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.58e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3888", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An experiment was performed to determine the moles of carbon dioxide gas formed (collected over water) when an acid reacts with limestone. To do this, a piece of dry limestone was weighed. Then carbon dioxide was collected until the limestone disappeared. The atmospheric pressure was measured at 0.965 atm. The temperature was 295 K. The volume of CO2 was measured to the nearest mL and corrected for the vapor pressure of water. The student continuously got low results from what was expected. Can you suggest why?\n\nOptions: \nA. Perhaps there was too much acid, which interfered with the results.\nB. The measurement of atmospheric pressure was incorrect.\nC. Carbon dioxide is rather soluble in water.\nD. The temperature might have affected the reaction.\nE. Limestone is Ca(HCO3)2.\nF. The limestone did not fully disappear.\nG. Limestone is never pure CaCO3.\nH. Perhaps there was not enough acid to dissolve all the limestone.\nI. The volume of CO2 was not measured correctly.\nJ. The vapor pressure of water was not correctly accounted for.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Carbon dioxide is relatively soluble in water, which means some of the CO2 generated in the reaction may have dissolved, leading to lower measured volumes than expected. This dissolution could account for the consistently low results observed by the student.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 285, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 339}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Carbon dioxide is relatively soluble in water, which means some of the CO2 generated in the reaction may have dissolved, leading to lower measured volumes than expected. This dissolution could account for the consistently low results observed by the student.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.514999999999998e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4311", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Formation of a solution can often be visualized as a three-step process. Step 1. Solvent molecules are separated from each other to make space for the solute. Step 2. Solute molecules are separated so they fit into spaces in the solvent. Step 3. Separated solute and solvent are brought together, filling in the spaces. Which of the following statements about the energy involved in the above is correct?\n\nOptions: \nA. Step 1 is endothermic, steps 2 and 3 are exothermic.\nB. All three steps are endothermic.\nC. Steps 1 and 3 are exothermic, and step 2 is endothermic.\nD. All three steps are exothermic.\nE. Steps 1 and 3 are endothermic, and step 2 is exothermic.\nF. Step 1 is exothermic, steps 2 and 3 are endothermic.\nG. Step 3 is exothermic, steps 1 and 2 are neither exothermic nor endothermic.\nH. Step 1 and 2 are exothermic, step 3 is neither exothermic nor endothermic.\nI. Steps 1 and 2 are exothermic, and step 3 is endothermic.\nJ. Steps 1 and 2 are endothermic, and step 3 is exothermic.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). Step 1 is endothermic because energy is required to separate the solvent molecules. Step 2 is endothermic as well since energy is needed to separate the solute molecules, whereas Step 3 is exothermic due to the release of energy when solute and solvent interact and form a solution.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 354, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 427}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). Step 1 is endothermic because energy is required to separate the solvent molecules. Step 2 is endothermic as well since energy is needed to separate the solute molecules, whereas Step 3 is exothermic due to the release of energy when solute and solvent interact and form a solution.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.69e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3729", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What do the differences in properties between lithium acetyl acetone (m.p. very high, insoluble in chloroform) and beryllium acetyl acetone (m.p. 108°,b.p. 270°, soluble in chloroform) suggest about their structures?\n\nOptions: \nA. Both are non-ionic compounds\nB. Lithium acetylacetonate is non-ionic and beryllium acetylacetonate is ionic\nC. Both are ionic compounds\nD. Lithium acetylacetonate is soluble in chloroform due to its polar nature, while beryllium acetylacetonate is not\nE. Beryllium acetylacetonate is polymeric due to hydrogen bonding, whereas lithium acetylacetonate is not\nF. Both exhibit similar degrees of ionic character and solubility properties\nG. Beryllium acetylacetonate is a volatile liquid at room temperature, while lithium acetylacetonate is a high melting solid\nH. Lithium acetylacetonate is ionic or salt-like and beryllium acetylacetonate is non-ionic or covalent\nI. Lithium acetylacetonate is a polymeric compound, while beryllium acetylacetonate is monomeric\nJ. Both are polymeric in nature with extensive hydrogen bonding\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{H}. The significant differences in melting point and solubility suggest that lithium acetylacetonate behaves more like an ionic compound, whereas beryllium acetylacetonate appears to have more covalent characteristics. This difference in nature reflects their respective interactions with solvents and their bonding structures.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 347, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 416}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{H}. The significant differences in melting point and solubility suggest that lithium acetylacetonate behaves more like an ionic compound, whereas beryllium acetylacetonate appears to have more covalent characteristics. This difference in nature reflects their respective interactions with solvents and their bonding structures.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.345e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3534", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A proposed mechanism for a reaction is as follows: NO2 + F2 →NO2F + F Slow step. F + NO2 → NO2F Fast step. What is the order of the overall reaction?\n\nOptions: \nA. Fourth order\nB. Second order\nC. First order\nD. Zero order\nE. Third order in NO2 and zero order in F2\nF. Second order in F2 and third order in NO2\nG. First order in NO2 and second order in F2\nH. Fifth order\nI. Third order\nJ. Second order in NO2 and first order in F2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the order of the reaction, we consider the slow step of the proposed mechanism, which is the rate-determining step: \\( \\text{NO}_2 + \\text{F}_2 \\rightarrow \\text{NO}_2\\text{F} + \\text{F} \\). The rate law for this step would be first order in NO2 and first order in F2, leading to an overall order of 2. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{B}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 195, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 297}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the order of the reaction, we consider the slow step of the proposed mechanism, which is the rate-determining step: \\( \\text{NO}_2 + \\text{F}_2 \\rightarrow \\text{NO}_2\\text{F} + \\text{F} \\). The rate law for this step would be first order in NO2 and first order in F2, leading to an overall order of 2. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{B}.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.045e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_3447", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Examining data obtained from mass spectrometry supports which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. The smell of elements\nB. The common oxidation states of elements\nC. The feel of elements\nD. The temperature at which elements melt\nE. Ionization energy trends within the periodic table\nF. The color of elements\nG. The sound produced when elements react\nH. Atomic size trends within the periodic table\nI. The taste of elements\nJ. The existence of isotopes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. Mass spectrometry is a technique used to measure the masses of ions, which allows for the identification of different isotopes of elements based on their mass-to-charge ratios. This method is widely utilized in both research and industry to determine isotopic composition and abundance.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 163, "output_tokens": 60, "total_tokens": 223}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. Mass spectrometry is a technique used to measure the masses of ions, which allows for the identification of different isotopes of elements based on their mass-to-charge ratios. This method is widely utilized in both research and industry to determine isotopic composition and abundance.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.0450000000000006e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4070", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The vibrational wavenumber of $\\mathrm{{Br}}_2$ is $323.2 \\mathrm{{~cm}}^{{-1}}$. Evaluate the vibrational partition function explicitly (without approximation) and plot its value as a function of temperature. At what temperature is the value within 5 per cent of the value calculated from the approximate formula?\n\nOptions: \nA. 7000 K\nB. 2500 K\nC. 3500$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nD. 6000 K\nE. 2000 K\nF.  4500$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nG. 4000$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nH. 5500 K\nI. 5000$\\mathrm{{~K}}$\nJ. 3000 K\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To compute the vibrational partition function \\( Z_v \\) for \\( \\mathrm{Br}_2 \\), we would use the formula:\n\n\\[\nZ_v = \\frac{1}{1 - e^{-h\\nu/kT}}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( \\nu \\) is the vibrational frequency related to the wavenumber, \\( h \\) is Planck's constant, \\( k \\) is Boltzmann's constant, and \\( T \\) is temperature. The approximate formula for high temperatures typically converges around \\( T \\) values of several thousand Kelvin. Based on typical vibrational modes, the correct temperature where approximation is close (within 5%) is typically in the range around 2500 K or higher.\n\nAfter assessing the options provided based on general vibrational characteristics and often-used approximations, the most likely correct temperature falls at option B, which is 2500 K.\n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 229, "output_tokens": 195, "total_tokens": 424}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To compute the vibrational partition function \\( Z_v \\) for \\( \\mathrm{Br}_2 \\), we would use the formula:\n\n\\[\nZ_v = \\frac{1}{1 - e^{-h\\nu/kT}}\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( \\nu \\) is the vibrational frequency related to the wavenumber, \\( h \\) is Planck's constant, \\( k \\) is Boltzmann's constant, and \\( T \\) is temperature. The approximate formula for high temperatures typically converges around \\( T \\) values of several thousand Kelvin. Based on typical vibrational modes, the correct temperature where approximation is close (within 5%) is typically in the range around 2500 K or higher.\n\nAfter assessing the options provided based on general vibrational characteristics and often-used approximations, the most likely correct temperature falls at option B, which is 2500 K.\n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00015135}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_chemistry_4318", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A student performs five titrations and obtains a mean result of 0.110 M, with a standard deviation of 0.001 M. If the actual concentration of the titrated solution is 0.100 M, which of the following is true about the titration results?\n\nOptions: \nA. Moderately accurate and precise\nB. Accurate but not precise\nC. Precise but not accurate\nD. Both accurate and precise\nE. Neither precise nor slightly accurate\nF. Neither accurate nor precise\nG. Highly accurate but imprecise\nH. Accurate but imprecise\nI. Precise and slightly accurate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The mean result of the titration is 0.110 M, which deviates from the actual concentration of 0.100 M, indicating that the results are not accurate. However, the standard deviation of 0.001 M suggests that the results are very close to each other, demonstrating high precision. Therefore, the correct answer is C. Precise but not accurate.\n\nThus, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 193, "output_tokens": 90, "total_tokens": 283}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The mean result of the titration is 0.110 M, which deviates from the actual concentration of 0.100 M, indicating that the results are not accurate. However, the standard deviation of 0.001 M suggests that the results are very close to each other, demonstrating high precision. Therefore, the correct answer is C. Precise but not accurate.\n\nThus, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.295000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7149", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose $\\Omega$ is a bounded open area in $\\mathbb{{R}}^n$. For any $f\\in L^2(\\Omega)$, the Laplace equation (with respect to a real function $u$), $\\Delta u = f$ with boundary condition $u\\mid_{{\\partial \\Omega}}=0$, has a unique weak solution. This can be proved by: 1. Poincare inequality and Riesz representation theorem; 2. Cauchy-Schwartz inequality and Hahn-Banach theorem. 3. None of the above. Return the answer as a number\n\nOptions: \nA. 2. Arzelà-Ascoli theorem and Banach fixed-point theorem\nB. 1. Arzelà-Ascoli theorem and Riesz representation theorem\nC. 1.0\nD. 3.0\nE. 2. Sobolev embedding theorem and Riesz representation theorem\nF. 1. Poincare inequality and Banach fixed-point theorem\nG. 2. Poincare inequality and Hahn-Banach theorem\nH. 2.0\nI. 1. Sobolev embedding theorem and Lax-Milgram theorem\nJ. All of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is based on the first option, which mentions the Poincaré inequality and the Riesz representation theorem, both of which are essential in proving the existence and uniqueness of weak solutions in the context of the Laplace equation with appropriate boundary conditions. Therefore, the correct letter choice is: \n\n\\[\\boxed{C}\\]", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 318, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 386}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is based on the first option, which mentions the Poincaré inequality and the Riesz representation theorem, both of which are essential in proving the existence and uniqueness of weak solutions in the context of the Laplace equation with appropriate boundary conditions. Therefore, the correct letter choice is: \n\n\\[\\boxed{C}\\]", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.849999999999998e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6590", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose C is a compact convex set in a linear normed space, and let T: C → C be a continuous mapping. Then, there exists a fixed point of T in C. Is this correct? Answer 1 for yes and 0 for no.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.0\nB. 2.5\nC. -0.5\nD. 1.5\nE. -1.0\nF. 0.5\nG. 0.0\nH. 2.0\nI. -2.0\nJ. 3.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The statement is correct according to the Brouwer Fixed Point Theorem, which asserts that any continuous mapping from a compact convex set to itself has at least one fixed point. Therefore, the answer is 1 for yes. \n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 188, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 245}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The statement is correct according to the Brouwer Fixed Point Theorem, which asserts that any continuous mapping from a compact convex set to itself has at least one fixed point. Therefore, the answer is 1 for yes. \n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.24e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6428", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A subset H of a group (G,*) is a group if\n\nOptions: \nA. a,b in H => a / b in H\nB. a,b in H => a + b in H\nC. a,b in H=> a - b^-1 in H\nD. H contains the identity element\nE. a in H => a^-1 in H\nF. a,b in H=> a * b in H\nG. a in H => a^2 in H\nH. a in H => a * a^-1 in H\nI. H contains the zero element\nJ. a,b in H=> a * b^-1 in H\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct letter choice is \\boxed{F}. For a subset H of a group (G,*) to be considered a group, it must be closed under the group operation, meaning that for any a and b in H, the product a * b must also be in H. Additionally, H must also include the identity element and inverses of its elements, but closure under the operation is the defining property of a group.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 289}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct letter choice is \\boxed{F}. For a subset H of a group (G,*) to be considered a group, it must be closed under the group operation, meaning that for any a and b in H, the product a * b must also be in H. Additionally, H must also include the identity element and inverses of its elements, but closure under the operation is the defining property of a group.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.205e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6846", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A company is interested in comparing the mean sales revenue per salesperson at two different locations. The manager takes a random sample of 10 salespeople from each location independently and records the sales revenue generated by each person during the last four weeks. He decides to use a t-test to compare the mean sales revenue at the two locations. Which of the following assumptions is necessary for the validity of the t-test?\n\nOptions: \nA. The population of the sales records at each location is not normally distributed.\nB. The population of the sales records at each location is normally distributed.\nC. The sample size at both locations is less than 30\nD. The population standard deviations at both locations are equal.\nE. The sales revenue is measured on an interval or ratio scale.\nF. The population of the sales records at each location follows a uniform distribution.\nG. The population standard deviations at both locations are not equal.\nH. The population standard deviations at both locations are known.\nI. The population mean sales revenue at both locations are not equal.\nJ. The population mean sales revenue at both locations are equal.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. For the validity of the t-test, it is essential that the sales revenue data is measured on an interval or ratio scale, which allows for appropriate calculations of means and variances. Other assumptions may exist for specific types of t-tests, but the measurement scale is foundational for conducting statistical tests.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 284, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 351}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. For the validity of the t-test, it is essential that the sales revenue data is measured on an interval or ratio scale, which allows for appropriate calculations of means and variances. Other assumptions may exist for specific types of t-tests, but the measurement scale is foundational for conducting statistical tests.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.280000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7746", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If $f(x) = 2$ for all real numbers $x$, what is the value of $f(x + 2)$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0\nB. $x^2 + 2$\nC. 4\nD. $2x$\nE. $x + 2$\nF. Undefined\nG. 1\nH. $2x + 2$\nI. 2\nJ. $4x$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "Since \\( f(x) = 2 \\) for all real numbers \\( x \\), it follows that \\( f(x + 2) \\) must also equal 2. The function \\( f \\) is constant and does not depend on the input value. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 158, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 224}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "Since \\( f(x) = 2 \\) for all real numbers \\( x \\), it follows that \\( f(x + 2) \\) must also equal 2. The function \\( f \\) is constant and does not depend on the input value. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.33e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6934", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A symmetric random walk on the three-dimensional cubic lattice Z^3 is transient or persistent? Return 1 for persistent and 0 for transient.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.0\nB. -1.0\nC. 4.0\nD. 0.5\nE. 2.5\nF. 2.0\nG. 1.5\nH. -0.5\nI. 1.0\nJ. 3.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "A symmetric random walk on the three-dimensional cubic lattice \\( \\mathbb{Z}^3 \\) is known to be transient. In mathematical terms, this means that the random walk does not return to its starting point with probability 1; rather, the probability of returning is less than 1. Therefore, the correct answer is 0 for transient. \n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 164, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 249}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "A symmetric random walk on the three-dimensional cubic lattice \\( \\mathbb{Z}^3 \\) is known to be transient. In mathematical terms, this means that the random walk does not return to its starting point with probability 1; rather, the probability of returning is less than 1. Therefore, the correct answer is 0 for transient. \n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.56e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6962", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An outlier is an observation that\n\nOptions: \nA. is the mode of the data set\nB. is the mean of the data set\nC. is seen more frequently than the other observations in the data set\nD. is always larger than the other observations in the data set\nE. is always smaller than the other observations in the data set\nF. is seen less frequently than the other observations in the data set\nG. is significantly different from the other observations in the data set\nH. is an error in the data set\nI. is the median of the data set\nJ. is exactly the same as the other observations in the data set\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. An outlier is defined as an observation that is significantly different from the other observations in the data set, either much larger or much smaller than the majority of the data points. It is not necessarily the mean, median, or mode, nor does it have to be an error.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 265}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. An outlier is defined as an observation that is significantly different from the other observations in the data set, either much larger or much smaller than the majority of the data points. It is not necessarily the mean, median, or mode, nor does it have to be an error.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.9e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6821", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What are the generators of the additive cyclic group Z?\n\nOptions: \nA. [1, -1]\nB. [1, 0]\nC. [0, 2]\nD. [-1, 1]\nE. [0, 1]\nF. [2, 0]\nG. [0, -1]\nH. [3, -3]\nI. [2, -2]\nJ. [1, 2]\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The generators of the additive cyclic group \\( \\mathbb{Z} \\) are the integers that can generate all of \\( \\mathbb{Z} \\) through addition. The elements \\( 1 \\) and \\( -1 \\) can generate all integers by adding or subtracting these values repeatedly. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 156, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 231}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The generators of the additive cyclic group \\( \\mathbb{Z} \\) are the integers that can generate all of \\( \\mathbb{Z} \\) through addition. The elements \\( 1 \\) and \\( -1 \\) can generate all integers by adding or subtracting these values repeatedly. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.84e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7770", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the trial on which a 3 is first observed in successive rolls of a six-sided die. Let $A$ be the event that 3 is observed on the first trial. Let $B$ be the event that at least two trials are required to observe a 3 . Assuming that each side has probability $1 / 6$, find (a) $P(A)$.\n\n\nOptions: \nA. $\\frac{{3}}{{6}}$\nB. $\\frac{{1}}{{3}}$\nC. $\\frac{{1}}{{12}}$\nD. $\\frac{{4}}{{6}}$\nE. $\\frac{{2}}{{6}}$\nF. $\\frac{{1}}{{6}}$\nG. $\\frac{{1}}{{2}}$\nH. $\\frac{{1}}{{36}}$\nI. $\\frac{{5}}{{36}}$\nJ. $\\frac{{5}}{{6}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The event \\( A \\) represents the scenario where a 3 is observed on the first trial of rolling a die. Since the die has six sides, the probability of rolling a 3 (which is just one specific outcome) on the first trial is \\( P(A) = \\frac{1}{6} \\). Therefore, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 244, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 322}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The event \\( A \\) represents the scenario where a 3 is observed on the first trial of rolling a die. Since the die has six sides, the probability of rolling a 3 (which is just one specific outcome) on the first trial is \\( P(A) = \\frac{1}{6} \\). Therefore, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.34e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6656", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the supplement of a 40° angle?\n\nOptions: \nA. 100°\nB. 160°\nC. 140°\nD. 120°\nE. 90°\nF. 130°\nG. 50°\nH. 110°\nI. 220°\nJ. 150°\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The supplement of an angle is determined by subtracting the angle from 180°. For a 40° angle, the supplement is 180° - 40° = 140°. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{C}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 48, "total_tokens": 175}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The supplement of an angle is determined by subtracting the angle from 180°. For a 40° angle, the supplement is 180° - 40° = 140°. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{C}.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.785e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7001", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For which integers n such that 3 <= n <= 11 is there only one group of order n (up to isomorphism)?\n\nOptions: \nA. For 3, 5, 7, and 11 only\nB. For 8, 9, 10, and 11 only\nC. For 4, 6, 8, and 10 only\nD. For 6, 7, 8, and 9 only\nE. For 3, 4, 5, and 6 only\nF. For 3, 5, 7, 9, and 11 only\nG. For 4, 5, 6, and 8 only\nH. For all integers n such that 3 <= n <= 11\nI. For no such integer n\nJ. For 5, 6, 7, 8, and 9 only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. For the integers n = 3, 5, 7, and 11, there is only one group of order n (specifically, the cyclic group of order n). For the other integers within the range, there are multiple non-isomorphic groups.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 259, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 321}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. For the integers n = 3, 5, 7, and 11, there is only one group of order n (specifically, the cyclic group of order n). For the other integers within the range, there are multiple non-isomorphic groups.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.605e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7709", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A simple random sample is defined by\n\nOptions: \nA. the statistical analysis of the sample.\nB. the location of the sample.\nC. whether or not the sample is biased.\nD. both of the above.\nE. the method of selection.\nF. how representative the sample is of the population.\nG. how diverse the sample is.\nH. examination of the outcome.\nI. how many individuals are in the sample.\nJ. the time period in which the sample is taken.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. A simple random sample is defined by the method of selection, where each member of the population has an equal chance of being included in the sample. This approach helps ensure that the sample is representative of the population, minimizing bias.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 162, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 216}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. A simple random sample is defined by the method of selection, where each member of the population has an equal chance of being included in the sample. This approach helps ensure that the sample is representative of the population, minimizing bias.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.6699999999999996e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7350", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the order of group Z_{{18}}?\n\nOptions: \nA. 30\nB. 15\nC. 12\nD. 6\nE. 24\nF. 21\nG. 18\nH. 9\nI. 36\nJ. 27\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The order of the group \\( \\mathbb{Z}_{18} \\) refers to the number of elements in the group, which is equal to 18. Therefore, the correct answer is G. \n\n\\(\\boxed{G}\\)", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 176}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The order of the group \\( \\mathbb{Z}_{18} \\) refers to the number of elements in the group, which is equal to 18. Therefore, the correct answer is G. \n\n\\(\\boxed{G}\\)", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.845e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6516", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 5.2-5. Let the distribution of $W$ be $F(8,4)$. Find the following:\n(a) $F_{{0.01}}(8,4)$.\n\n\nOptions: \nA. 16.30\nB. 15.97\nC. 9.22\nD. 18.45\nE. 17.10\nF.  14.80\nG. 13.60\nH. 10.75\nI. 11.34\nJ. 12.50\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find \\( F_{0.01}(8,4) \\), we need to look up the critical value for the F-distribution with 8 and 4 degrees of freedom at the 0.01 significance level. This value corresponds to the 99th percentile of the F-distribution, which is typically looked up in F-distribution tables or calculated using statistical software. After finding the appropriate value, the closest answer is 18.45, which is option D. \n\nTherefore, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 179, "output_tokens": 111, "total_tokens": 290}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find \\( F_{0.01}(8,4) \\), we need to look up the critical value for the F-distribution with 8 and 4 degrees of freedom at the 0.01 significance level. This value corresponds to the 99th percentile of the F-distribution, which is typically looked up in F-distribution tables or calculated using statistical software. After finding the appropriate value, the closest answer is 18.45, which is option D. \n\nTherefore, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.345e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7717", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the measure, in degrees, of an angle that is equivalent to 1/360 of a circle?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0\nB. 720\nC. 30\nD. 180\nE. 90\nF. 360\nG. 60\nH. 1\nI. 270\nJ. 45\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The measure of an angle that is equivalent to 1/360 of a circle is given by the formula \\( \\text{angle} = \\frac{1}{360} \\times 360 \\). Calculating this gives \\( 1 \\) degree. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{H}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 138, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 201}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The measure of an angle that is equivalent to 1/360 of a circle is given by the formula \\( \\text{angle} = \\frac{1}{360} \\times 360 \\). Calculating this gives \\( 1 \\) degree. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{H}.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.85e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6842", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: You need to construct a 94% confidence interval for a population proportion. What is the upper critical value of z to be used in constructing this interval?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.645\nB. 1.282\nC. 0.9699\nD. 1.88\nE. 2.81\nF. 1.40\nG. 2.33\nH. 1.96\nI. 1.555\nJ. 2.576\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the upper critical value of z for a 94% confidence interval, we need to look up the z-value that corresponds to \\(\\frac{1 - 0.94}{2} = 0.03\\) in the standard normal distribution. This gives us a z-value of approximately 1.88. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 167, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 246}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the upper critical value of z for a 94% confidence interval, we need to look up the z-value that corresponds to \\(\\frac{1 - 0.94}{2} = 0.03\\) in the standard normal distribution. This gives us a z-value of approximately 1.88. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.245e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7399", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the central limit theorem?\n\nOptions: \nA. The central limit theorem states that the mean of a large number of independent and identically distributed random variables, each with finite mean and variance, will approximately follow a normal distribution.\nB. If the population is uniformly distributed, then as the sample size increases, the sampling distribution of the sample mean becomes closer to a normal distribution.\nC. No matter how the population is distributed, as the sample size increases, the standard deviation of the sample means becomes closer to the standard deviation of the population divided by the square root of the sample size.\nD. If the population is normally distributed, then as the sample size increases, the sampling distribution of the sample mean becomes closer to a normal distribution.\nE. The central limit theorem states that the median of a large number of independent and identically distributed random variables, each with finite mean and variance, will approximately follow a normal distribution.\nF. The central limit theorem refers to something else.\nG. The central limit theorem states that as the sample size increases, the median of the sample means becomes closer to the median of the population.\nH. No matter how the population is distributed, as the sample size increases, the mean of the sample means becomes closer to the mean of the population.\nI. Regardless of the distribution of the population, the variance of the sample means will converge to the variance of the population as the sample size increases.\nJ. The central limit theorem states that the sum of a large number of independent and identically distributed random variables, each with finite mean and variance, will approximately follow a normal distribution, regardless of the shape of the original measurement distribution.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. The central limit theorem states that the mean of a large number of independent and identically distributed random variables, each with finite mean and variance, will approximately follow a normal distribution. This principle is fundamental in statistics as it allows for the use of normal distribution approximations in various sampling situations.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 399, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 465}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. The central limit theorem states that the mean of a large number of independent and identically distributed random variables, each with finite mean and variance, will approximately follow a normal distribution. This principle is fundamental in statistics as it allows for the use of normal distribution approximations in various sampling situations.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.945e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6832", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  A typical roulette wheel used in a casino has 38 slots that are numbered $1,2,3, \\ldots, 36,0,00$, respectively. The 0 and 00 slots are colored green. Half of the remaining slots are red and half are black. Also, half of the integers between 1 and 36 inclusive are odd, half are even, and 0 and 00 are defined to be neither odd nor even. A ball is rolled around the wheel and ends up in one of the slots; we assume that each slot has equal probability of $1 / 38$, and we are interested in the number of the slot into which the ball falls. Let $A=\\{{0,00\\}}$. Give the value of $P(A)$.\n\nOptions: \nA. $\\frac{{1}}{{19}}$\nB. $\\frac{{1}}{{76}}$\nC. $\\frac{{20}}{{38}}$\nD. $\\frac{{2}}{{38}}$\nE. $\\frac{{3}}{{38}}$\nF. $\\frac{{4}}{{38}}$\nG. $\\frac{{36}}{{38}}$\nH. $\\frac{{1}}{{38}}$\nI. $\\frac{{1}}{{2}}$\nJ. $\\frac{{18}}{{38}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The event \\( A \\) consists of the slots \\( \\{0, 00\\} \\), which means \\( A \\) has 2 favorable outcomes. The total number of slots is 38, so the probability \\( P(A) \\) is given by the formula \\( P(A) = \\frac{\\text{Number of favorable outcomes}}{\\text{Total outcomes}} = \\frac{2}{38} \\). This simplifies to \\( \\frac{1}{19} \\), which is not listed in the options, but the right option is \\( D: \\frac{2}{38} \\).\n\nTherefore, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 327, "output_tokens": 138, "total_tokens": 465}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The event \\( A \\) consists of the slots \\( \\{0, 00\\} \\), which means \\( A \\) has 2 favorable outcomes. The total number of slots is 38, so the probability \\( P(A) \\) is given by the formula \\( P(A) = \\frac{\\text{Number of favorable outcomes}}{\\text{Total outcomes}} = \\frac{2}{38} \\). This simplifies to \\( \\frac{1}{19} \\), which is not listed in the options, but the right option is \\( D: \\frac{2}{38} \\).\n\nTherefore, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00013184999999999998}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7594", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 5.5-15. Let the distribution of $T$ be $t(17)$. Find\n(a) $t_{{0.01}}(17)$.\n\n\nOptions: \nA. $1.789$\nB. $3.456$\nC. $4.025$\nD. $3.745$\nE. $2.110$\nF. $1.740$\nG. $2.567$\nH. $3.921$\nI. $2.898$\nJ. $2.897$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find \\( t_{0.01}(17) \\), we need the critical value of the t-distribution for a significance level of 0.01 with 17 degrees of freedom. Referring to a t-distribution table or using statistical software, we find that \\( t_{0.01}(17) \\) approximately equals \\( 2.567 \\). Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 173, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 261}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find \\( t_{0.01}(17) \\), we need the critical value of the t-distribution for a significance level of 0.01 with 17 degrees of freedom. Referring to a t-distribution table or using statistical software, we find that \\( t_{0.01}(17) \\) approximately equals \\( 2.567 \\). Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.874999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6560", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use the list of numbers: 22, 25, 14, 11, 23, 27, 46. What is the mode?\n\nOptions: \nA. 27\nB. No mode\nC. 23\nD. 22\nE. 25\nF. 24\nG. 11\nH. 35\nI. 46\nJ. 14\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the mode, we look for the number that appears most frequently in the list. The numbers provided (22, 25, 14, 11, 23, 27, 46) all appear only once. Since there are no repetitions, the correct answer is that there is no mode. \n\nThus, the correct choice is \\boxed{B}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 147, "output_tokens": 75, "total_tokens": 222}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the mode, we look for the number that appears most frequently in the list. The numbers provided (22, 25, 14, 11, 23, 27, 46) all appear only once. Since there are no repetitions, the correct answer is that there is no mode. \n\nThus, the correct choice is \\boxed{B}.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.704999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7010", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How many three-digit positive integers are there?\n\nOptions: \nA. 900\nB. 899\nC. 1001\nD. 100\nE. 801\nF. 1000\nG. 9999\nH. 999\nI. 998\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the number of three-digit positive integers, we consider that the smallest three-digit number is 100 and the largest is 999. The range of three-digit integers is from 100 to 999, inclusive. Therefore, the total count is 999 - 100 + 1 = 900. \n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 194}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the number of three-digit positive integers, we consider that the smallest three-digit number is 100 and the largest is 999. The range of three-digit integers is from 100 to 999, inclusive. Therefore, the total count is 999 - 100 + 1 = 900. \n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.15e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6553", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the opposite of the number −7.\n\nOptions: \nA. −0.77\nB. −14\nC. −7\nD. 0.7\nE. 14\nF. 7\nG. −0.07\nH. −7.7\nI. 0.77\nJ. 70\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The opposite of a number is the same number with the opposite sign. Therefore, the opposite of −7 is 7. The correct answer is F. \n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 134, "output_tokens": 44, "total_tokens": 178}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The opposite of a number is the same number with the opposite sign. Therefore, the opposite of −7 is 7. The correct answer is F. \n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.65e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7679", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: \\lim_{{x \\to c}} |f(x)| = 0. What is \\lim_{{x \\to c}} f(x)?\n\nOptions: \nA. \\infty (infinity)\nB. Does not exist\nC. 1\nD. Undefined\nE. -1\nF. c\nG. |c|\nH. 0\nI. -c\nJ. \\frac{{1}}{{c}} (1 over c)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The limit \\( \\lim_{{x \\to c}} |f(x)| = 0 \\) implies that the absolute value of \\( f(x) \\) approaches 0 as \\( x \\) approaches \\( c \\). This means that \\( f(x) \\) itself must also approach 0, since the only value with an absolute value of 0 is 0 itself. Therefore, \\( \\lim_{{x \\to c}} f(x) = 0 \\), which corresponds to option H.\n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{H}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 158, "output_tokens": 113, "total_tokens": 271}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The limit \\( \\lim_{{x \\to c}} |f(x)| = 0 \\) implies that the absolute value of \\( f(x) \\) approaches 0 as \\( x \\) approaches \\( c \\). This means that \\( f(x) \\) itself must also approach 0, since the only value with an absolute value of 0 is 0 itself. Therefore, \\( \\lim_{{x \\to c}} f(x) = 0 \\), which corresponds to option H.\n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{H}.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.149999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6521", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The set of all nth roots of unity under multiplication of complex numbers form a/an\n\nOptions: \nA. non-abelian group\nB. infinite group\nC. commutative semigroups with identity\nD. non-commutative group\nE. abelian group\nF. non-commutative semi group with identity\nG. semi group with identity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The set of all nth roots of unity under multiplication of complex numbers forms an abelian group. This is because the roots of unity can be represented as complex numbers that are evenly distributed around the unit circle, satisfying both closure and the existence of inverse elements while also being commutative. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 140, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 210}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The set of all nth roots of unity under multiplication of complex numbers forms an abelian group. This is because the roots of unity can be represented as complex numbers that are evenly distributed around the unit circle, satisfying both closure and the existence of inverse elements while also being commutative. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.3e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7513", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a clinical trial, 30 sickle cell anemia patients are randomly assigned to two groups. One group receives the currently marketed medicine, and the other group receives an experimental medicine. Each week, patients report to the clinic where blood tests are conducted. The lab technician is unaware of the kind of medicine the patient is taking. This design can be described as\n\nOptions: \nA. a completely randomized design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two treatments\nB. a completely randomized design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two blocks\nC. a matched-pairs design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine forming a pair\nD. a double-blind design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two treatments\nE. a factorial design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two factors\nF. a randomized block design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two blocks\nG. a crossover design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two treatments\nH. a randomized block design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two treatments\nI. a matched-pairs design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two blocks\nJ. a single-blind design, with the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine as two treatments\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. This study describes a double-blind design because neither the patients nor the lab technician knows which treatment the patients receive, helping to reduce bias in reporting and evaluation of the treatment effects. The two treatments are the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 339, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 397}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. This study describes a double-blind design because neither the patients nor the lab technician knows which treatment the patients receive, helping to reduce bias in reporting and evaluation of the treatment effects. The two treatments are the currently marketed medicine and the experimental medicine.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.565e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7720", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Tisha wrote the following riddle to her friend: I have 2 faces, no vertices, and I can roll. What am I? What is the answer to the riddle?\n\nOptions: \nA. hexagonal prism\nB. torus\nC. cone\nD. prism\nE. sphere\nF. rectangular prism\nG. pentagonal prism\nH. cube\nI. cylinder\nJ. pyramid\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The answer to the riddle \"I have 2 faces, no vertices, and I can roll\" is a cylinder. A cylinder has two circular faces (the top and bottom) and no vertices, and it is capable of rolling. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 149, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 210}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The answer to the riddle \"I have 2 faces, no vertices, and I can roll\" is a cylinder. A cylinder has two circular faces (the top and bottom) and no vertices, and it is capable of rolling. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.8949999999999996e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7086", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider the number pattern 5, 9, 13, 17, 21, 25, 29. Which rule could have been used to make the pattern?\n\nOptions: \nA. Start with 5. Subtract 4 each time to get the next number.\nB. Start with 5. Add 4 each time to get the next number.\nC. Start with 5. Add 5 each time to get the next number.\nD. Start with 0. Add 5 each time to get the next number.\nE. Start with 9. Subtract 4 each time to get the next number.\nF. Start with 1. Add 4 each time to get the next number.\nG. Start with 0. Add 4 each time to get the next number.\nH. Start with 0. Add 3 each time to get the next number.\nI. Start with 5. Add 3 each time to get the next number.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The number pattern starts with 5 and each subsequent number is obtained by adding 4. The sequence follows: 5, 5+4=9, 9+4=13, and so on, confirming that adding 4 each time produces the given sequence.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 265, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 329}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The number pattern starts with 5 and each subsequent number is obtained by adding 4. The sequence follows: 5, 5+4=9, 9+4=13, and so on, confirming that adding 4 each time produces the given sequence.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.815e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7603", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Statement 1 | The homomorphic image of a cyclic group is cyclic. Statement 2 | The homomorphic image of an Abelian group is Abelian.\n\nOptions: \nA. True, False\nB. False, True\nC. False, False\nD. True, True\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). \n\nBoth statements are true: the homomorphic image of a cyclic group is indeed cyclic because any image under a homomorphism of a generator will generate the entire image, and the homomorphic image of an Abelian group remains Abelian as the commutativity is preserved under homomorphisms. Thus, the correct choice is that both statements are true.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 204}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). \n\nBoth statements are true: the homomorphic image of a cyclic group is indeed cyclic because any image under a homomorphism of a generator will generate the entire image, and the homomorphic image of an Abelian group remains Abelian as the commutativity is preserved under homomorphisms. Thus, the correct choice is that both statements are true.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.795e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7091", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which set of integers is in order from least to greatest?\n\nOptions: \nA. 11, −9, 7, −6, −3\nB. 7, 11, −6, −3, −9\nC. −3, 7, −9, −6, 11\nD. −6, −3, 7, 11, −9\nE. −9, −3, 7, 11, −6\nF. −3, −6, 7, 11, –9\nG. −9, 7, −6, −3, 11\nH. −9, −6, −3, 7, 11\nI. 11, 7, −3, −6, −9\nJ. 7, −9, −6, −3, 11\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\). The integers in this option are ordered from least to greatest: \\(-9, -6, -3, 7, 11\\). All other options are either not in the correct order or contain integers out of order.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 247, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 304}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\). The integers in this option are ordered from least to greatest: \\(-9, -6, -3, 7, 11\\). All other options are either not in the correct order or contain integers out of order.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.125e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6662", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which group of numbers is in order from least to greatest?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.6 1.0 0.25\nB. 0.25 1.6 1.0\nC. 1.0 1.6 0.25\nD. 1.6 0.25 1.6\nE. 1.0 0.25 0.25\nF. 1.6 0.25 1.0\nG. 0.25 1.0 1.6\nH. 1.0 0.25 1.6\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\). The numbers in option G, 0.25, 1.0, and 1.6, are arranged from least to greatest. All other options list the numbers in an incorrect order.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 248}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\). The numbers in option G, 0.25, 1.0, and 1.6, are arranged from least to greatest. All other options list the numbers in an incorrect order.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.015e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6979", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The weekly milk order for the Tranquility Inn includes 40 gallons of low-fat milk and 15 gallons of chocolate milk. What is the ratio of the number of low-fat gallons to chocolate gallons in the Tranquility Inn’s weekly milk order?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5:03\nB. 8:04\nC. 8:05\nD. 2:01\nE. 3:01\nF. 8:03\nG. 7:03\nH. 6:03\nI. 4:01\nJ. 5:01\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the ratio of low-fat milk to chocolate milk, we compare the quantities: 40 gallons (low-fat) to 15 gallons (chocolate). The ratio can be simplified by dividing both numbers by 5, giving us 8:3. Therefore, the correct answer is option F. \n\n\\boxed{F}", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 186, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 253}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the ratio of low-fat milk to chocolate milk, we compare the quantities: 40 gallons (low-fat) to 15 gallons (chocolate). The ratio can be simplified by dividing both numbers by 5, giving us 8:3. Therefore, the correct answer is option F. \n\n\\boxed{F}", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.81e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6533", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An assembly line machine is supposed to turn out ball bearings with a diameter of 1.25 centimeters. Each morning the first 30 bearings produced are pulled and measured. If their mean diameter is under 1.23 centimeters or over 1.27 centimeters, the machinery is stopped and an engineer is called to make adjustments before production is resumed. The quality control procedure may be viewed as a hypothesis test with the null hypothesis H0: μ = 1.25 and the alternative hypothesis Ha: μ ≠ 1.25. The engineer is asked to make adjustments when the null hypothesis is rejected. In test terminology, what would a Type II error result in?\n\nOptions: \nA. An incorrect assumption about the machinery's calibration\nB. An unnecessary stoppage of the production process\nC. Continued production of wrong size ball bearings\nD. An unnecessary adjustment of the machinery\nE. A warranted halt in production to adjust the machinery\nF. A false alarm about the size of ball bearings\nG. Continued production of proper size ball bearings\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "In hypothesis testing, a Type II error occurs when we fail to reject the null hypothesis when it is actually false. In this context, if the mean diameter of the bearings is not within the acceptable range, but the test fails to signal this and production continues, it leads to producing incorrect sizes. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{C}\\)", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 275, "output_tokens": 73, "total_tokens": 348}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "In hypothesis testing, a Type II error occurs when we fail to reject the null hypothesis when it is actually false. In this context, if the mean diameter of the bearings is not within the acceptable range, but the test fails to signal this and production continues, it leads to producing incorrect sizes. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{C}\\)", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.505000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6646", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The correlation between height in inches and weight in pounds for a particular class is 0.65. If the heights are converted from inches to centimeters, what will the correlation be? (1 in. = 2.54 cm)\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.1\nB. 0.54\nC. 1.65\nD. 0\nE. 0.26\nF. -0.26\nG. 0.95\nH. 2.54\nI. -0.65\nJ. 0.65\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correlation coefficient is a unitless measure and is not affected by linear transformations such as converting inches to centimeters. Therefore, the correlation will remain the same. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 180, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 223}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correlation coefficient is a unitless measure and is not affected by linear transformations such as converting inches to centimeters. Therefore, the correlation will remain the same. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.28e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6982", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Katie is going on vacation for 3 weeks. She finds the number of days of work she will miss by multiplying 5 × 3. Which expression shows another way Katie can find the number of days of work she will miss?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5+3+3\nB. 3+3+3\nC. 5×5\nD. 5×3×3\nE. 5×2×3\nF. 5+5+5+5+5\nG. 5+5+5\nH. 3×4+5\nI. 3+5\nJ. 3×3×3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The expression that shows another way Katie can find the number of days of work she will miss is F. \\(5 + 5 + 5 + 5 + 5\\). This expression adds up the number of workdays she misses each week (5 days) for the 3 weeks of vacation, which will also equal 15 days (5 × 3). Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 202, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 290}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The expression that shows another way Katie can find the number of days of work she will miss is F. \\(5 + 5 + 5 + 5 + 5\\). This expression adds up the number of workdays she misses each week (5 days) for the 3 weeks of vacation, which will also equal 15 days (5 × 3). Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.309999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7510", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the primary difference between an experiment and an observational study?\n\nOptions: \nA. In an experiment, the researcher has no control over variables; in an observational study, the researcher can manipulate variables.\nB. Experiments are only conducted on human subjects; observational studies can be conducted on nonhuman subjects.\nC. Observational studies are conducted in a lab setting, while experiments can be conducted in any environment.\nD. Experiments must be double-blind; observational studies do not need to be.\nE. In an experiment, the researcher observes without interfering; in an observational study, the researcher manipulates the environment.\nF. Experiments can only be conducted once; observational studies can be repeated.\nG. Experiments must use randomized treatment and control groups; observational studies also use treatment and control groups, but they do not need to be randomized.\nH. Experiments involve quantitative data; observational studies involve qualitative data.\nI. In an experiment, the researcher manipulates some variable to observe its effect on a response variable; in an observational study, he or she simply observes and records the observations.\nJ. Experiments require a hypothesis; observational studies do not require a hypothesis.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. This option accurately describes the primary difference between experiments and observational studies: in experiments, researchers manipulate a variable to observe the effects, while in observational studies, they simply observe and record data without interference. This distinction is crucial for understanding the methodology and implications of different types of research.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 302, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 366}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. This option accurately describes the primary difference between experiments and observational studies: in experiments, researchers manipulate a variable to observe the effects, while in observational studies, they simply observe and record data without interference. This distinction is crucial for understanding the methodology and implications of different types of research.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.37e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7275", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The principal of a school is interested in estimating the average income per family of her students. She selects a random sample of students and collects information about their family income. A 95 percent confidence interval computed from this data for the mean income per family is ($35,095, $45,005). Which of the following provides the best interpretation of this confidence interval?\n\nOptions: \nA. 95 percent of the students in her school are from families whose income is between $35,095 and $45,005.\nB. If we were to take another sample of the same size and compute a 95 percent confidence interval, we would have a 95% chance of getting a different interval.\nC. If we were to take another sample of the same size and compute a 95 percent confidence interval, we would have a 95% chance of getting the interval ($35,095, $45,005).\nD. There is a 95% probability that the mean income per family in the school is between $35,095 and $45,005.\nE. 95 percent of the income per family in the school falls between $35,095 and $45,005.\nF. There is a 95% probability that the median income per family in the school is between $35,095 and $45,005.\nG. There is a 95% probability that the sample mean income per family in the school is between $35,095 and $45,005.\nH. The average income per family of all the students in the school is definitely between $35,095 and $45,005.\nI. There is a 95% probability that the minimum income per family in the school is between $35,095 and $45,005.\nJ. There is a 95% probability that the families of all the students in this school have an income of between $35,095 and $45,005.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. This option correctly interprets the confidence interval by stating that we are 95% confident that the true mean income of families in the school falls within the specified range. The other options either misinterpret the confidence interval or incorrectly reference probabilities related to specific students or samples.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 453, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 515}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. This option correctly interprets the confidence interval by stating that we are 95% confident that the true mean income of families in the school falls within the specified range. The other options either misinterpret the confidence interval or incorrectly reference probabilities related to specific students or samples.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00010515000000000001}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7278", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: As reported on CNN, in a May 1999 national poll 43% of high school students expressed fear about going to school. Which of the following best describes what is meant by the poll having a margin of error of 5%?\n\nOptions: \nA. There is a 0.05 probability that the 43% result is in error.\nB. The pollsters are 95% confident that the true proportion is between 38% and 48%.\nC. Five percent of the students refused to participate in the poll.\nD. The poll's results could be 5% higher or lower due to random chance.\nE. Five percent of the students surveyed did not understand the question.\nF. There is a 5% chance that the results of the poll are completely inaccurate.\nG. Only 5% of the students surveyed gave valid responses.\nH. It is likely that the true proportion of high school students afraid to go to school is between 38% and 48%.\nI. The poll's results are 5% away from the true proportion.\nJ. Between 38% and 48% of those surveyed expressed fear about going to school.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The best answer is \\boxed{B}. A margin of error of 5% means that the pollsters are 95% confident that the actual proportion of high school students who are afraid to go to school falls within 5 percentage points of the reported 43%, which translates to a range of 38% to 48%. This reflects the reliability of the poll results despite potential sampling variability.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 300, "output_tokens": 80, "total_tokens": 380}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The best answer is \\boxed{B}. A margin of error of 5% means that the pollsters are 95% confident that the actual proportion of high school students who are afraid to go to school falls within 5 percentage points of the reported 43%, which translates to a range of 38% to 48%. This reflects the reliability of the poll results despite potential sampling variability.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.3e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7286", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For the regression line, which of the following statements about residuals is true?\n\nOptions: \nA. The sum of the residuals is always one.\nB. If the correlation is 0, there will be a distinct pattern in the residual plot.\nC. The larger the residuals, the better the linear model.\nD. The residuals are always negative.\nE. If the correlation is 1, there will be a distinct pattern in the residual plot.\nF. The residual plot will always be a straight line.\nG. Influential scores have large residuals.\nH. The mean of the residuals is always zero.\nI. If the linear model is good, the number of positive residuals will be the same as the number of negative residuals.\nJ. The residuals can never be zero.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. The mean of the residuals is always zero in a regression analysis, as the residuals are calculated as the difference between the observed values and the predicted values, and the regression line is drawn to minimize these differences. Thus, when averaging the residuals, they balance out to zero.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 227, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 293}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. The mean of the residuals is always zero in a regression analysis, as the residuals are calculated as the difference between the observed values and the predicted values, and the regression line is drawn to minimize these differences. Thus, when averaging the residuals, they balance out to zero.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.365e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6853", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: To determine the average cost of running for a congressional seat, a simple random sample of 50 politicians is chosen and the politicians' records examined. The cost figures show a mean of $125,000 with a standard deviation of $32,000. Which of the following is the best interpretation of a 90% confidence interval estimate for the average cost of running for office?\n\nOptions: \nA. We are 90% confident that politicians running for a congressional seat spend between $117,500 and $132,500.\nB. 90% of politicians running for a congressional seat spend a mean dollar amount that is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nC. 90% of politicians running for a congressional seat spend a total dollar amount that is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nD. 90% of politicians running for a congressional seat spend between $117,500 and $132,500.\nE. We are 90% confident that politicians running for a congressional seat spend a maximum dollar amount that is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nF. We are 90% confident that the standard deviation of the cost of running for a congressional seat is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nG. We are 90% confident that the median cost of running for a congressional seat is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nH. We are 90% confident that politicians running for a congressional seat spend a mean dollar amount between $117,500 and $132,500.\nI. We are 90% confident that politicians running for a congressional seat spend a minimum dollar amount that is between $117,500 and $132,500.\nJ. 90% of politicians running for a congressional seat spend a median dollar amount that is between $117,500 and $132,500.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The best interpretation of a 90% confidence interval estimate for the average cost of running for office is that we are estimating the mean cost based on the sample data. Therefore, the correct answer is that we are 90% confident that politicians running for a congressional seat spend a mean dollar amount between $117,500 and $132,500. The correct letter choice is \\boxed{H}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 441, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 520}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The best interpretation of a 90% confidence interval estimate for the average cost of running for office is that we are estimating the mean cost based on the sample data. Therefore, the correct answer is that we are 90% confident that politicians running for a congressional seat spend a mean dollar amount between $117,500 and $132,500. The correct letter choice is \\boxed{H}.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00011355}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7409", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A shelf has four books on it. The weight, in pounds, of each of the four books on the shelf is 2.5, 3.2, 2.7, 2.3 Which inequality represents the weight, w, of any book chosen from the shelf?\n\nOptions: \nA. w > 3.2\nB. w > 2.9\nC. w > 2.3\nD. w > 2.5\nE. w < 3.2\nF. w < 2.4\nG. w < 2.7\nH. w > 3.0\nI. w < 3.3\nJ. w < 3.1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The weights of the books are 2.3, 2.5, 2.7, and 3.2 pounds. Any book chosen from the shelf must weigh at least the weight of the lightest book. Therefore, the correct inequality representing the weight, w, of any book chosen from the shelf is \\( w \\geq 2.3 \\). The closest option that represents this is C. \n\nThus, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 314}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The weights of the books are 2.3, 2.5, 2.7, and 3.2 pounds. Any book chosen from the shelf must weigh at least the weight of the lightest book. Therefore, the correct inequality representing the weight, w, of any book chosen from the shelf is \\( w \\geq 2.3 \\). The closest option that represents this is C. \n\nThus, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.21e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6537", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The relation between the selling price of a car (in $1,000) and its age (in years) is estimated from a random sample of cars of a specific model. The relation is given by the following formula: Selling price = 15.9 – 0.983 (age) Which of the following can we conclude from this equation?\n\nOptions: \nA. For every year the car gets older, the selling price drops by approximately $983.\nB. A new car costs on the average $9,830.\nC. A new car costs on the average $15,900.\nD. For every year the car gets older, the selling price goes down by approximately 9.83 percent.\nE. For every year the car gets older, the selling price goes up by approximately $983.\nF. For every year the car gets older, the selling price drops by approximately $159.\nG. For every year the car gets older, the selling price goes up by approximately $1,590.\nH. A new car costs on the average $983.\nI. For every year the car gets older, the selling price remains the same.\nJ. For every year the car gets older, the selling price drops by approximately $1,590.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). The formula indicates that for each additional year of age, the selling price decreases by approximately $983, as the coefficient of age (-0.983) represents the change in selling price with respect to age. Option C also suggests the price of a new car, which is derived from the equation when age is zero, equating to $15,900.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 317, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 399}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). The formula indicates that for each additional year of age, the selling price decreases by approximately $983, as the coefficient of age (-0.983) represents the change in selling price with respect to age. Option C also suggests the price of a new car, which is derived from the equation when age is zero, equating to $15,900.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.675e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6999", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which equation represents 36 less than a number, y, is equal to 13?\n\nOptions: \nA. 13 + y = 36\nB. 13 - y = 36\nC. y = 13 - 36\nD. 36 - y = 13\nE. 13 = y + 36\nF. y = 36 - 13\nG. y + 36 = 13\nH. y - 36 = 13\nI. 36 + y = –13\nJ. 36 = y + 13\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The equation that represents \"36 less than a number, y, is equal to 13\" can be expressed as \\( y - 36 = 13 \\) since subtracting 36 from y gives us 13. Among the given options, this corresponds to option H. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 183, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 253}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The equation that represents \"36 less than a number, y, is equal to 13\" can be expressed as \\( y - 36 = 13 \\) since subtracting 36 from y gives us 13. Among the given options, this corresponds to option H. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.945e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6963", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these statements correctly explains bias?\n\nOptions: \nA. It describes a process that results in a sample that does not represent the population.\nB. It describes a process that results in a sample that is too large or too small.\nC. It describes a process that uses a random sampling method.\nD. It describes a process that results in a sample that perfectly represents the population.\nE. It describes a sample that is not representative of the population.\nF. It describes a process that always results in accurate estimates.\nG. It describes the influence of the researcher's personal beliefs on the outcome of the study.\nH. It describes a lack of randomization in the sampling process.\nI. It describes a process where the sampling method has no influence on the outcome of the study.\nJ. It describes a process that creates estimates that are too high on average or too low on average.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Bias refers to systematic errors in the sampling process that lead to a sample that does not accurately reflect the characteristics of the population from which it is drawn. This can result in misleading conclusions in research or surveys.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 241, "output_tokens": 51, "total_tokens": 292}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Bias refers to systematic errors in the sampling process that lead to a sample that does not accurately reflect the characteristics of the population from which it is drawn. This can result in misleading conclusions in research or surveys.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.675e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6432", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is a binomial random variable?\n\nOptions: \nA. The number of motorists not wearing seat belts in a random sample of five drivers.\nB. The number of hearts out of five cards randomly drawn from a deck of 52 cards, without replacement.\nC. The number of tosses before a \"5\" appears when tossing a fair die.\nD. The number of green marbles drawn from a bag containing red, blue, and green marbles.\nE. The number of points a hockey team receives in 10 games, where two points are awarded for wins, one point for ties, and no points for losses.\nF. The number of red cards in a random hand of five cards drawn from a deck of 52 cards.\nG. The time it takes to complete a 1000-piece puzzle.\nH. The number of cars of a specific model sold in a month at a car dealership.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. A binomial random variable represents the number of successes in a fixed number of independent trials with two possible outcomes (success or failure). Here, the number of motorists not wearing seat belts in a sample of five drivers fits this definition, as it involves a fixed number of trials (five drivers) and a clear success criterion (not wearing a seat belt).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 249, "output_tokens": 79, "total_tokens": 328}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. A binomial random variable represents the number of successes in a fixed number of independent trials with two possible outcomes (success or failure). Here, the number of motorists not wearing seat belts in a sample of five drivers fits this definition, as it involves a fixed number of trials (five drivers) and a clear success criterion (not wearing a seat belt).", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.474999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7477", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a parametric family $\\{{p_\\theta(x)\\}}$ we know that $\\lim_{{\\theta'\\to\\theta}}\\frac{{1}}{{(\\theta-\\theta')^2}}D(p_\\theta||p_{{\\theta'}}) = \\alpha J(\\theta)$, where $J(\\theta)$ is the Fisher information. Use natural logarithm for KL divergence to compute $\\alpha$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.25\nB. 4\nC. 0.5\nD. 1\nE. 2.5\nF. -1\nG. 2\nH. 1.5\nI. 3\nJ. 0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To compute $\\alpha$, we start from the relation given according to the limit involving the Kullback-Leibler divergence (KL divergence). From the asymptotic behavior of KL divergence near a point and the relationship to Fisher information, we have $D(p_\\theta || p_{\\theta'}) \\approx \\frac{1}{2} J(\\theta) (\\theta - \\theta')^2$ for $\\theta'$ near $\\theta$. Consequently, when taking the limit, we find that $\\alpha = 0.5$. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 207, "output_tokens": 121, "total_tokens": 328}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To compute $\\alpha$, we start from the relation given according to the limit involving the Kullback-Leibler divergence (KL divergence). From the asymptotic behavior of KL divergence near a point and the relationship to Fisher information, we have $D(p_\\theta || p_{\\theta'}) \\approx \\frac{1}{2} J(\\theta) (\\theta - \\theta')^2$ for $\\theta'$ near $\\theta$. Consequently, when taking the limit, we find that $\\alpha = 0.5$. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00010365}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6917", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: compute the integral \\int_{{\\Gamma}} \\frac{{x*dy-y*dx}}{{x^2+y^2}}, where $\\Gamma$ is any piecewise smooth, closed curve that encloses the origin but does not pass through it.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3.1415926\nB. 4.6692016\nC. 1.5707963\nD. 0\nE. 2.7182818\nF. 0.5772156\nG. -3.1415926\nH. 9.8696044\nI. 6.2831852\nJ. 1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The integral \\(\\int_{\\Gamma} \\frac{x \\, dy - y \\, dx}{x^2 + y^2}\\) can be evaluated using the residue theorem or Green's theorem. This integral corresponds to the function's winding number around the origin; specifically, it equals \\(2\\pi\\) for curves enclosing the origin. Therefore, the correct answer, which is \\(2\\pi \\approx 6.2831852\\), is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 198, "output_tokens": 100, "total_tokens": 298}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The integral \\(\\int_{\\Gamma} \\frac{x \\, dy - y \\, dx}{x^2 + y^2}\\) can be evaluated using the residue theorem or Green's theorem. This integral corresponds to the function's winding number around the origin; specifically, it equals \\(2\\pi\\) for curves enclosing the origin. Therefore, the correct answer, which is \\(2\\pi \\approx 6.2831852\\), is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.97e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7357", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Compute the real integral $I=\\int_{{-\\infty}}^{{\\infty}} 1/(x^2 + 1)^2 dx$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 6.28\nB. 5.55\nC. 3.67\nD. 2.78\nE. 3.14\nF. 2.46\nG. 1.57\nH. 4.67\nI. 1.23\nJ. 0.78\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To compute the integral \\( I = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{(x^2 + 1)^2} \\, dx \\), we can use the residue theorem from complex analysis. The integrand has a pole of order 2 at \\( x = i \\). Evaluating the integral using residues gives \\( I = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\), which approximates to about 1.57. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 169, "output_tokens": 107, "total_tokens": 276}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To compute the integral \\( I = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{(x^2 + 1)^2} \\, dx \\), we can use the residue theorem from complex analysis. The integrand has a pole of order 2 at \\( x = i \\). Evaluating the integral using residues gives \\( I = \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\), which approximates to about 1.57. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.955e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6698", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: suppose F(x,y,z)=0. What is $\\frac{{\\partial x}}{{\\partial y}} \\frac{{\\partial y}}{{\\partial z}} \\frac{{\\partial z}}{{\\partial x}}$?\n\nOptions: \nA. -2.0\nB. 2.0\nC. -0.5\nD. 0\nE. 1.5\nF. 1.0\nG. Undefined\nH. -1.0\nI. 0.5\nJ. 3.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the value of \\(\\frac{{\\partial x}}{{\\partial y}} \\frac{{\\partial y}}{{\\partial z}} \\frac{{\\partial z}}{{\\partial x}}\\), we can apply the cyclic rule for partial derivatives. This rule states that for any three variables defined implicitly, the product of partial derivatives in this cyclic manner equals -1. Thus, the answer is \\(-1\\), corresponding to option H. \n\nSo, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 175, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 278}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the value of \\(\\frac{{\\partial x}}{{\\partial y}} \\frac{{\\partial y}}{{\\partial z}} \\frac{{\\partial z}}{{\\partial x}}\\), we can apply the cyclic rule for partial derivatives. This rule states that for any three variables defined implicitly, the product of partial derivatives in this cyclic manner equals -1. Thus, the answer is \\(-1\\), corresponding to option H. \n\nSo, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.805e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6595", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is \\lim_{{x \\to 0}} (csc(x) - cot(x))?\n\nOptions: \nA. -1/2\nB. Undefined\nC. 1/2\nD. 1\nE. 0\nF. -1\nG. 2\nH. -2\nI. 3\nJ. Infinity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find \\(\\lim_{{x \\to 0}} (csc(x) - cot(x))\\), we can rewrite the functions in terms of sine and cosine:\n\n\\[\ncsc(x) = \\frac{1}{\\sin(x)}, \\quad cot(x) = \\frac{\\cos(x)}{\\sin(x)}\n\\]\n\nThus, \n\n\\[\ncsc(x) - cot(x) = \\frac{1 - \\cos(x)}{\\sin(x)}\n\\]\n\nAs \\(x \\to 0\\), \\(1 - \\cos(x) \\to 0\\) and \\(\\sin(x) \\to 0\\), making the limit an indeterminate form. Applying L'Hospital's Rule, we differentiate the numerator and denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Numerator: } \\frac{d}{dx}(1 - \\cos(x)) = \\sin(x), \\quad \\text{Denominator: } \\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin(x)) = \\cos(x)\n\\]\n\nNow applying L'Hospital's Rule:\n\n\\[\n\\lim_{{x \\to 0}} \\frac{\\sin(x)}{\\cos(x)} = \\lim_{{x \\to 0}} \\tan(x) = 0\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the limit is 0. The correct answer is \n\n\\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 139, "output_tokens": 280, "total_tokens": 419}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find \\(\\lim_{{x \\to 0}} (csc(x) - cot(x))\\), we can rewrite the functions in terms of sine and cosine:\n\n\\[\ncsc(x) = \\frac{1}{\\sin(x)}, \\quad cot(x) = \\frac{\\cos(x)}{\\sin(x)}\n\\]\n\nThus, \n\n\\[\ncsc(x) - cot(x) = \\frac{1 - \\cos(x)}{\\sin(x)}\n\\]\n\nAs \\(x \\to 0\\), \\(1 - \\cos(x) \\to 0\\) and \\(\\sin(x) \\to 0\\), making the limit an indeterminate form. Applying L'Hospital's Rule, we differentiate the numerator and denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Numerator: } \\frac{d}{dx}(1 - \\cos(x)) = \\sin(x), \\quad \\text{Denominator: } \\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin(x)) = \\cos(x)\n\\]\n\nNow applying L'Hospital's Rule:\n\n\\[\n\\lim_{{x \\to 0}} \\frac{\\sin(x)}{\\cos(x)} = \\lim_{{x \\to 0}} \\tan(x) = 0\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the limit is 0. The correct answer is \n\n\\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00018884999999999998}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6954", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use Stokes' Theorem to evaluate $\\int_C \\mathbf{{F}} \\cdot d \\mathbf{{r}}$, where $\\mathbf{{F}}(x, y, z)=x y \\mathbf{{i}}+y z \\mathbf{{j}}+z x \\mathbf{{k}}$, and $C$ is the triangle with vertices $(1,0,0),(0,1,0)$, and $(0,0,1)$, oriented counterclockwise as viewed from above.\n\n\nOptions: \nA.  $-\\frac{{1}}{{2}}$\nB. $\\frac{{1}}{{2}}$\nC. $0$\nD. $\\frac{{3}}{{4}}$\nE. $\\frac{{1}}{{4}}$\nF. $-1$\nG. $\\frac{{1}}{{3}}$\nH. $\\frac{{2}}{{3}}$\nI. $-\\frac{{1}}{{4}}$\nJ. $-\\frac{{1}}{{3}}$\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To use Stokes' Theorem, we need to compute the surface integral of the curl of the vector field \\(\\mathbf{F}\\) over the region enclosed by the triangle defined by the vertices \\((1,0,0)\\), \\((0,1,0)\\), and \\((0,0,1)\\). The curl, \\(\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}\\), can be calculated and then integrated over the triangular region, which is straightforward due to the symmetry and simplicity of the triangle. The result of this computation yields \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\), so the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 265, "output_tokens": 134, "total_tokens": 399}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To use Stokes' Theorem, we need to compute the surface integral of the curl of the vector field \\(\\mathbf{F}\\) over the region enclosed by the triangle defined by the vertices \\((1,0,0)\\), \\((0,1,0)\\), and \\((0,0,1)\\). The curl, \\(\\nabla \\times \\mathbf{F}\\), can be calculated and then integrated over the triangular region, which is straightforward due to the symmetry and simplicity of the triangle. The result of this computation yields \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\), so the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00012014999999999999}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6523", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine whether the polynomial in Z[x] satisfies an Eisenstein criterion for irreducibility over Q. x^2 - 12\n\nOptions: \nA. Yes, with p=4.\nB. No, because the polynomial is reducible.\nC. Yes, with p=1.\nD. No, because the polynomial does not satisfy the Eisenstein criterion.\nE. No.\nF. Yes, with p=12.\nG. Yes, with p=3.\nH. Yes, with p=5.\nI. Yes, with p=6.\nJ. Yes, with p=2.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To apply the Eisenstein criterion, we need to determine if there is a prime \\( p \\) such that the polynomial \\( x^2 - 12 \\) can be rewritten in the form where the coefficient of \\( x^1 \\) is 0 and the constant term is divisible by \\( p \\) but not by \\( p^2 \\). The prime \\( p=3 \\) meets these criteria: \\( 12 \\) is divisible by \\( 3 \\) but not by \\( 9 \\), and there are no coefficients of \\( x \\). Thus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 185, "output_tokens": 127, "total_tokens": 312}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To apply the Eisenstein criterion, we need to determine if there is a prime \\( p \\) such that the polynomial \\( x^2 - 12 \\) can be rewritten in the form where the coefficient of \\( x^1 \\) is 0 and the constant term is divisible by \\( p \\) but not by \\( p^2 \\). The prime \\( p=3 \\) meets these criteria: \\( 12 \\) is divisible by \\( 3 \\) but not by \\( 9 \\), and there are no coefficients of \\( x \\). Thus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00010394999999999999}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6706", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: H(z) = $\\int_0^1 e^{{-z^2 t^2}} dt$, what is H'(1)?\n\nOptions: \nA. -2.3789\nB. 1.0000\nC. -0.3789\nD. -0.7461\nE. 0\nF. -1.3789\nG. 0.3789\nH. 1.3789\nI. 0.7461\nJ. 2.3789\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find \\( H'(1) \\), we first need to differentiate \\( H(z) \\) with respect to \\( z \\) under the integral sign, giving us \\( H'(z) = \\int_0^1 \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z} e^{-z^2 t^2} dt = \\int_0^1 -2z t^2 e^{-z^2 t^2} dt \\). Evaluating this at \\( z = 1 \\), we find \\( H'(1) = -2 \\int_0^1 t^2 e^{-t^2} dt \\). The integral can be evaluated, leading us to conclude that \\( H'(1) \\) approximates to \\( -0.7461 \\). \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 171, "output_tokens": 172, "total_tokens": 343}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find \\( H'(1) \\), we first need to differentiate \\( H(z) \\) with respect to \\( z \\) under the integral sign, giving us \\( H'(z) = \\int_0^1 \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z} e^{-z^2 t^2} dt = \\int_0^1 -2z t^2 e^{-z^2 t^2} dt \\). Evaluating this at \\( z = 1 \\), we find \\( H'(1) = -2 \\int_0^1 t^2 e^{-t^2} dt \\). The integral can be evaluated, leading us to conclude that \\( H'(1) \\) approximates to \\( -0.7461 \\). \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00012885000000000001}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7038", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose $f(x, y)= \\begin{{cases}}1-x-y, & x+y \\leqslant 1 \\ 0, & x+y>1\\end{{cases}}$. What is the integral of f(x,y) over the region I=[0,1]\\times[0,1]?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.33333\nB. 0.5\nC. 1.5\nD. 0\nE. 0.75\nF. 1\nG. 0.25\nH. 0.16667\nI. 0.66667\nJ. 0.83333\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the integral of \\( f(x, y) \\) over the region \\( I = [0,1] \\times [0,1] \\), we need to consider the area where \\( x+y \\leq 1 \\), which describes a triangular region with vertices at (0,0), (1,0), and (0,1). In this region, \\( f(x, y) = 1 - x - y \\). The integral can be calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\int_0^1 \\int_0^{1-x} (1 - x - y) \\, dy \\, dx = \\int_0^1 \\left[ (1 - x)y - \\frac{y^2}{2} \\right]_{0}^{1-x} \\, dx\n\\]\nCalculating further gives an area of \\( \\frac{1}{6} \\) for the triangular region \\( \\text{Area}(T) = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 1 \\times 1 = \\frac{1}{2} \\) and the integral evaluates to \\( \\frac{1}{6} \\). The total value is therefore \\( \\boxed{H} \\) for \\( 0.16667 \\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 262, "total_tokens": 463}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the integral of \\( f(x, y) \\) over the region \\( I = [0,1] \\times [0,1] \\), we need to consider the area where \\( x+y \\leq 1 \\), which describes a triangular region with vertices at (0,0), (1,0), and (0,1). In this region, \\( f(x, y) = 1 - x - y \\). The integral can be calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\int_0^1 \\int_0^{1-x} (1 - x - y) \\, dy \\, dx = \\int_0^1 \\left[ (1 - x)y - \\frac{y^2}{2} \\right]_{0}^{1-x} \\, dx\n\\]\nCalculating further gives an area of \\( \\frac{1}{6} \\) for the triangular region \\( \\text{Area}(T) = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 1 \\times 1 = \\frac{1}{2} \\) and the integral evaluates to \\( \\frac{1}{6} \\). The total value is therefore \\( \\boxed{H} \\) for \\( 0.16667 \\).", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00018735}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7579", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $W(t)$ be a Bownian motion, Let $E[exp(i*W(t))]:= E[cos(W(t))+i*sin(W(t))]$, where $i=\\sqrt{{-1}}$. Is $M(t):=exp(i*W(t))/E[exp(i*W(t))]$ a matingale? Return 1 for yes and 0 for no.\n\nOptions: \nA. i (the imaginary unit)\nB. 1.0\nC. -0.5\nD. 2.0\nE. 1.5\nF. 0.0\nG. -2.0\nH. 3.0\nI. 0.5\nJ. -1.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine whether \\( M(t) = \\frac{\\exp(i W(t))}{E[\\exp(i W(t))]} \\) is a martingale, we can use the result that the expectation of a scaled martingale remains a martingale. Since \\( E[\\exp(i W(t))] \\) is a positive constant, \\( M(t) \\) is indeed a martingale. Thus, the answer is 1 (indicating yes).\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 220, "output_tokens": 103, "total_tokens": 323}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine whether \\( M(t) = \\frac{\\exp(i W(t))}{E[\\exp(i W(t))]} \\) is a martingale, we can use the result that the expectation of a scaled martingale remains a martingale. Since \\( E[\\exp(i W(t))] \\) is a positive constant, \\( M(t) \\) is indeed a martingale. Thus, the answer is 1 (indicating yes).\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.48e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7336", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: compute the integral $\\iint_V \\frac{{d x d y d z}}{{(1+x+y+z)^3}}$, where V={{(x, y, z): x, y, z \\geq 0, x+y+z\\leq 1}}.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.092\nB. 0.042\nC. 0.050\nD. 0.025\nE. 0.018\nF. 0.056\nG. 0.028\nH. 0.075\nI. 0.065\nJ. 0.034\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To compute the integral $$\\iint_V \\frac{dx \\, dy \\, dz}{(1+x+y+z)^3}$$ over the region \\( V = \\{(x, y, z): x, y, z \\geq 0, x+y+z \\leq 1\\} \\), we can change variables to simplify the limits of integration. This integral can be computed using symmetry and geometry of the region defined by \\( x+y+z \\leq 1 \\). After evaluating, the most likely correct answer is found to be:\n\n\\(\\boxed{C}\\)", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 194, "output_tokens": 126, "total_tokens": 320}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To compute the integral $$\\iint_V \\frac{dx \\, dy \\, dz}{(1+x+y+z)^3}$$ over the region \\( V = \\{(x, y, z): x, y, z \\geq 0, x+y+z \\leq 1\\} \\), we can change variables to simplify the limits of integration. This integral can be computed using symmetry and geometry of the region defined by \\( x+y+z \\leq 1 \\). After evaluating, the most likely correct answer is found to be:\n\n\\(\\boxed{C}\\)", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001047}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6918", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use Stoke's Theorem to evaluate $\\int_C \\vec{{F}} \\cdot d \\vec{{r}}$ where $\\vec{{F}} = z^2 \\vec{{i}} + y^2 \\vec{{j}} + x \\vec{{k}}$ and $C$ is the triangle with vertices (1,0,0), (0,1,0) and (0,0,1) with counter-clockwise rotation.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.166\nB. -1.000\nC. -0.166\nD. 0.333\nE. 0.500\nF. 0.666\nG. -0.333\nH. -0.500\nI. -0.666\nJ. 1.000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To apply Stokes' Theorem, we first compute the curl of the vector field \\( \\vec{F} = z^2 \\vec{i} + y^2 \\vec{j} + x \\vec{k} \\). The curl \\(\\nabla \\times \\vec{F}\\) is calculated to be \\((0, -1, 2)\\). The area of the triangular surface defined by the vertices and the normal vector is \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\). Calculating the surface integral gives \\(\\int_S (\\nabla \\times \\vec{F}) \\cdot d\\vec{S} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 = 1\\), leading to \\(\\int_C \\vec{F} \\cdot d\\vec{r} = 1\\). Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 229, "output_tokens": 186, "total_tokens": 415}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To apply Stokes' Theorem, we first compute the curl of the vector field \\( \\vec{F} = z^2 \\vec{i} + y^2 \\vec{j} + x \\vec{k} \\). The curl \\(\\nabla \\times \\vec{F}\\) is calculated to be \\((0, -1, 2)\\). The area of the triangular surface defined by the vertices and the normal vector is \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\). Calculating the surface integral gives \\(\\int_S (\\nabla \\times \\vec{F}) \\cdot d\\vec{S} = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 = 1\\), leading to \\(\\int_C \\vec{F} \\cdot d\\vec{r} = 1\\). Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00014595}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6713", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $X_1, X_2, \\ldots$ be a sequence of independent indetically distributed random variables drawn according to the probability mass function $p(x) = N(0,1)$. Let $q(x)=N(1,1)$ be another probability mass function. Use natural logarithm to evaluate $\\lim -\\frac{{1}}{{n}}\\log{{q(X_1,X_2,\\ldots,X_n)}}$ as $n \\to \\infty$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.1\nB. 1.4\nC. 0.5\nD. 3.5\nE. 2.8\nF. 1.8\nG. 0.7\nH. 3.1\nI. 2.5\nJ. 1.1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To evaluate the limit \\(\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} -\\frac{1}{n} \\log q(X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_n)\\), we recognize that \\(q(x) = N(1,1)\\) implies \\(X_i \\sim N(1,1)\\) for each \\(X_i\\) in the sequence of random variables. The logarithm of the joint probability of independently and identically distributed \\(N(1,1)\\) random variables leads to an average term which converges to the log of the mean value for the distribution (i.e., \\(\\log(1/\\sqrt{2\\pi}) - (x^2/2)\\)). Evaluating the limit provides a numerical value, which in this case correlates approximately to option **1.8**.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 238, "output_tokens": 187, "total_tokens": 425}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To evaluate the limit \\(\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} -\\frac{1}{n} \\log q(X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_n)\\), we recognize that \\(q(x) = N(1,1)\\) implies \\(X_i \\sim N(1,1)\\) for each \\(X_i\\) in the sequence of random variables. The logarithm of the joint probability of independently and identically distributed \\(N(1,1)\\) random variables leads to an average term which converges to the log of the mean value for the distribution (i.e., \\(\\log(1/\\sqrt{2\\pi}) - (x^2/2)\\)). Evaluating the limit provides a numerical value, which in this case correlates approximately to option **1.8**.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001479}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6504", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the sum of $\\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}} (1/e^n + 1/(n*(n+1)))$\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.234\nB. 1.414\nC. 2.000\nD. 1.581\nE. 2.718\nF. 1.618\nG. 1.789\nH. 1.000\nI. 3.141\nJ. 2.345\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the sum of the given series, we can break it into two parts: the first part, \\(\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{e^n}\\), converges to \\(\\frac{1/e}{1-1/e} = \\frac{1}{e-1}\\), and the second part, \\(\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{n(n+1)}\\), converges to \\(1\\). Therefore, the total sum is \\(\\frac{1}{e-1} + 1\\). Evaluating numerically gives approximately 1.581 (since \\(\\frac{1}{e-1} \\approx 0.581\\)), matching option D.\n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 169, "output_tokens": 172, "total_tokens": 341}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the sum of the given series, we can break it into two parts: the first part, \\(\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{e^n}\\), converges to \\(\\frac{1/e}{1-1/e} = \\frac{1}{e-1}\\), and the second part, \\(\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{n(n+1)}\\), converges to \\(1\\). Therefore, the total sum is \\(\\frac{1}{e-1} + 1\\). Evaluating numerically gives approximately 1.581 (since \\(\\frac{1}{e-1} \\approx 0.581\\)), matching option D.\n\nThus, the answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00012855}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6716", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: what is the limit of $2/\\sqrt{{\\pi}}*\\sqrt{{n}}\\int_0^1(1-x^2)^n dx$ as n goes to infinity?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1/\\sqrt{{\\pi}}\nB. 2/\\sqrt{{\\pi}}\nC. Infinity\nD. 2.0\nE. 3.0\nF. -1.0\nG. 0.5\nH. 1.5\nI. 1.0\nJ. 0.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To evaluate the limit of \\(2/\\sqrt{\\pi} \\cdot \\sqrt{n} \\int_0^1 (1-x^2)^n \\, dx\\) as \\(n\\) approaches infinity, we recognize that the integral approximates the area under the curve, which becomes increasingly focused around \\(x=1\\) as \\(n\\) grows. Using the substitution \\(x=\\cos(\\theta)\\), the integral simplifies and approaches \\( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\), leading to the limit \\( 2/\\sqrt{\\pi} \\cdot \\sqrt{n} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} = 2/\\sqrt{\\pi} \\). \n\nThus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 176, "output_tokens": 173, "total_tokens": 349}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To evaluate the limit of \\(2/\\sqrt{\\pi} \\cdot \\sqrt{n} \\int_0^1 (1-x^2)^n \\, dx\\) as \\(n\\) approaches infinity, we recognize that the integral approximates the area under the curve, which becomes increasingly focused around \\(x=1\\) as \\(n\\) grows. Using the substitution \\(x=\\cos(\\theta)\\), the integral simplifies and approaches \\( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\), leading to the limit \\( 2/\\sqrt{\\pi} \\cdot \\sqrt{n} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} = 2/\\sqrt{\\pi} \\). \n\nThus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001302}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7673", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If z = arctan(e^{{1 + (1 + x)^2}}), what's the derivative of $\\frac{{\\partial z}}{{\\partial x}}$ at x = 0.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.4752\nB. 0.6210\nC. 0.4123\nD. 0.5678\nE. 0.5439\nF. 0.2896\nG. 0.3017\nH. 0.1345\nI. 0.6571\nJ. 0.2198\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the derivative \\(\\frac{{\\partial z}}{{\\partial x}}\\), we first use the chain rule. The derivative of \\(z = \\arctan(e^{1 + (1 + x)^2})\\) requires us to compute \\(\\frac{{dz}}{{dx}} = \\frac{{1}}{{1 + (e^{1 + (1 + x)^2})^2}} \\cdot e^{1 + (1 + x)^2} \\cdot \\frac{{d}}{{dx}}(1 + (1 + x)^2)\\). Evaluating this at \\(x = 0\\) gives a specific numeric value, which appears to be approximately \\(0.4123\\). \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 186, "output_tokens": 160, "total_tokens": 346}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the derivative \\(\\frac{{\\partial z}}{{\\partial x}}\\), we first use the chain rule. The derivative of \\(z = \\arctan(e^{1 + (1 + x)^2})\\) requires us to compute \\(\\frac{{dz}}{{dx}} = \\frac{{1}}{{1 + (e^{1 + (1 + x)^2})^2}} \\cdot e^{1 + (1 + x)^2} \\cdot \\frac{{d}}{{dx}}(1 + (1 + x)^2)\\). Evaluating this at \\(x = 0\\) gives a specific numeric value, which appears to be approximately \\(0.4123\\). \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001239}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6946", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is \\lim_{{x \\to 0}} (x \\lfloor 1/x \nfloor)?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0\nB. 1\nC. \\(\\infty\\)\nD. \\(\\frac{{1}}{{x}}\\)\nE. 2\nF. Undefined\nG. -\\(\\infty\\)\nH. \\(\\frac{{1}}{{2}}\\)\nI. -2\nJ. -1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To evaluate the limit \\(\\lim_{{x \\to 0}} (x \\lfloor 1/x \\rfloor)\\), we note that as \\(x\\) approaches 0 from the positive side, \\(1/x\\) approaches \\(\\infty\\), causing \\(\\lfloor 1/x \\rfloor\\) to become very large. Therefore, \\(x \\lfloor 1/x \\rfloor\\) behaves like \\(x \\cdot \\infty\\) as \\(x\\) approaches 0, but since \\(x\\) approaches 0, the product approaches 0 as well. \n\nThus, the limit is 0, so the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 156, "output_tokens": 149, "total_tokens": 305}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To evaluate the limit \\(\\lim_{{x \\to 0}} (x \\lfloor 1/x \\rfloor)\\), we note that as \\(x\\) approaches 0 from the positive side, \\(1/x\\) approaches \\(\\infty\\), causing \\(\\lfloor 1/x \\rfloor\\) to become very large. Therefore, \\(x \\lfloor 1/x \\rfloor\\) behaves like \\(x \\cdot \\infty\\) as \\(x\\) approaches 0, but since \\(x\\) approaches 0, the product approaches 0 as well. \n\nThus, the limit is 0, so the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00011279999999999999}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7233", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Suppose ${{X_n:n\\geq 1}}$ be independent and exponentially distributed with parameter 1. what is the probability $P(\\limsup _{{n \\rightarrow infty}} X_n/\\log(n)=1)? Return a numeric value.\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.5\nB. 1.0\nC. 0.1\nD. 0.36787944117 (1/e)\nE. 0.63212055882 (1 - 1/e)\nF. 0.845350936 (1 - 1/π)\nG. 0.0\nH. 0.69314718056 (1/ln(2))\nI. 0.9\nJ. 0.2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The probability \\( P(\\limsup _{n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{X_n}{\\log(n)} = 1) \\) can be derived from the properties of independent and identically distributed exponential random variables. By applying the law of large numbers and the properties of the extremes of random variables, we find that this probability corresponds to the value \\( 1 - \\frac{1}{e} \\). Therefore, the correct answer is given by option E: \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 221, "output_tokens": 105, "total_tokens": 326}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The probability \\( P(\\limsup _{n \\rightarrow \\infty} \\frac{X_n}{\\log(n)} = 1) \\) can be derived from the properties of independent and identically distributed exponential random variables. By applying the law of large numbers and the properties of the extremes of random variables, we find that this probability corresponds to the value \\( 1 - \\frac{1}{e} \\). Therefore, the correct answer is given by option E: \\(\\boxed{E}\\).", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.615e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7051", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is \\lim_{{x \\to 1}} ((x - 1) sin((\\pi)/(x - 1))?\n\nOptions: \nA. π\nB. 0\nC. 2π\nD. 1\nE. undefined\nF. e (the base of the natural logarithm)\nG. 1/2\nH. -π\nI. 1/π\nJ. -1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find \\(\\lim_{{x \\to 1}} ((x - 1) \\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{x - 1}))\\), we can substitute \\(y = x - 1\\) so that as \\(x \\to 1\\), \\(y \\to 0\\). The limit then transforms to \\(\\lim_{{y \\to 0}} y \\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{y})\\). Since \\(\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{y})\\) oscillates between -1 and 1, the whole limit approaches zero, thus the answer is 0.\n\nSo, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 154, "output_tokens": 141, "total_tokens": 295}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find \\(\\lim_{{x \\to 1}} ((x - 1) \\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{x - 1}))\\), we can substitute \\(y = x - 1\\) so that as \\(x \\to 1\\), \\(y \\to 0\\). The limit then transforms to \\(\\lim_{{y \\to 0}} y \\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{y})\\). Since \\(\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{y})\\) oscillates between -1 and 1, the whole limit approaches zero, thus the answer is 0.\n\nSo, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00010770000000000002}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7581", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Use divergence therem to evaluate $\\iint_S \\vec{{F}} \\cdot d \\vec{{S}}$ where $\\vec{{F}} = yx^2 \\vec{{i}} + (xy^2 - 3z^4)\\vec{{j}} + (x^3+y^3)\\vec{{k}}$ and the surface $S$ consists of the sphere of radius 4 with $z \\le 0$ and $y \\le 0$. Note all three surfaces of this solid are included in $S$.\n\nOptions: \nA. -2.0\nB. -3.0\nC. 5.0\nD. -4.0\nE. 4.0\nF. 3.0\nG. 2.0\nH. 1.0\nI. -1.0\nJ. 0.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To evaluate the surface integral $\\iint_S \\vec{F} \\cdot d\\vec{S}$ using the divergence theorem, we first compute the divergence of the vector field $\\vec{F} = yx^2 \\vec{i} + (xy^2 - 3z^4)\\vec{j} + (x^3+y^3)\\vec{k}$. The divergence is given by \n\n\\[\n\\nabla \\cdot \\vec{F} = \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(yx^2) + \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(xy^2 - 3z^4) + \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}(x^3+y^3) = 2yx + (2xy) + 0 = 4xy.\n\\]\n\nNext, we set up the volume integral over the region bounded by the sphere of radius 4, in the negative $z$ and negative $y$ octant, and calculate the integral of $4xy$ over that volume. The volume is an eighth of the sphere. Integrating over the specified limits suggests that the result evaluates to -4. Thus, the correct answer is \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{D}.\n\\]", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 250, "output_tokens": 255, "total_tokens": 505}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To evaluate the surface integral $\\iint_S \\vec{F} \\cdot d\\vec{S}$ using the divergence theorem, we first compute the divergence of the vector field $\\vec{F} = yx^2 \\vec{i} + (xy^2 - 3z^4)\\vec{j} + (x^3+y^3)\\vec{k}$. The divergence is given by \n\n\\[\n\\nabla \\cdot \\vec{F} = \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}(yx^2) + \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}(xy^2 - 3z^4) + \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}(x^3+y^3) = 2yx + (2xy) + 0 = 4xy.\n\\]\n\nNext, we set up the volume integral over the region bounded by the sphere of radius 4, in the negative $z$ and negative $y$ octant, and calculate the integral of $4xy$ over that volume. The volume is an eighth of the sphere. Integrating over the specified limits suggests that the result evaluates to -4. Thus, the correct answer is \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{D}.\n\\]", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001905}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6669", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which is the best buy?\n\nOptions: \nA. 7 bottles of juice for $15.75\nB. 5 bottles of juice for $11.25\nC. 9 bottles of juice for $20.25\nD. 4 bottles of juice for $9.00\nE. 11 bottles of juice for $24.86\nF. 12 bottles of juice for $27.00\nG. 16 bottles of juice for $35.68\nH. 18 bottles of juice for $40.50\nI. 14 bottles of juice for $31.50\nJ. 3 bottles of juice for $6.72\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the best buy, we calculate the cost per bottle for each option:\n\nA. $15.75 / 7 = $2.25  \nB. $11.25 / 5 = $2.25  \nC. $20.25 / 9 = $2.25  \nD. $9.00 / 4 = $2.25  \nE. $24.86 / 11 ≈ $2.26  \nF. $27.00 / 12 = $2.25  \nG. $35.68 / 16 ≈ $2.23  \nH. $40.50 / 18 ≈ $2.25  \nI. $31.50 / 14 ≈ $2.25  \nJ. $6.72 / 3 = $2.24  \n\nThe lowest cost per bottle is in option G, with a cost of approximately $2.23 per bottle. Thus, the best buy is \\boxed{G}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 201, "output_tokens": 203, "total_tokens": 404}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the best buy, we calculate the cost per bottle for each option:\n\nA. $15.75 / 7 = $2.25  \nB. $11.25 / 5 = $2.25  \nC. $20.25 / 9 = $2.25  \nD. $9.00 / 4 = $2.25  \nE. $24.86 / 11 ≈ $2.26  \nF. $27.00 / 12 = $2.25  \nG. $35.68 / 16 ≈ $2.23  \nH. $40.50 / 18 ≈ $2.25  \nI. $31.50 / 14 ≈ $2.25  \nJ. $6.72 / 3 = $2.24  \n\nThe lowest cost per bottle is in option G, with a cost of approximately $2.23 per bottle. Thus, the best buy is \\boxed{G}.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00015194999999999998}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7030", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Using Taylor's Approximation Theorem to show: What is $\\lim_{{x \\to 0}} \\frac{{e^\\frac{{x^4}}{{2}}-\\cos(x^2)}}{{x^4}}$\n\nOptions: \nA. -1.0\nB. 0.25\nC. 1.5\nD. 3.0\nE. 0.5\nF. Undefined\nG. 2.0\nH. 4.0\nI. 0.0\nJ. 1.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the limit, we can use Taylor series expansions around \\(x = 0\\). The expansion for \\(e^{\\frac{x^4}{2}} \\) gives \\(1 + \\frac{x^4}{2} + O(x^8)\\) and for \\(\\cos(x^2)\\) gives \\(1 - \\frac{x^4}{2} + O(x^8)\\). Thus, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{e^{\\frac{x^4}{2}} - \\cos(x^2)}{x^4} = \\frac{\\left(1 + \\frac{x^4}{2} + O(x^8)\\right) - \\left(1 - \\frac{x^4}{2} + O(x^8)\\right)}{x^4} = \\frac{x^4}{2} + \\frac{x^4}{2} + O(x^4) \\text{ and simplifies to } 1 + O(x^4) .\n\\]\n\nTaking the limit as \\(x \\to 0\\) gives us \\(1\\). Therefore, the answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 179, "output_tokens": 238, "total_tokens": 417}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the limit, we can use Taylor series expansions around \\(x = 0\\). The expansion for \\(e^{\\frac{x^4}{2}} \\) gives \\(1 + \\frac{x^4}{2} + O(x^8)\\) and for \\(\\cos(x^2)\\) gives \\(1 - \\frac{x^4}{2} + O(x^8)\\). Thus, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{e^{\\frac{x^4}{2}} - \\cos(x^2)}{x^4} = \\frac{\\left(1 + \\frac{x^4}{2} + O(x^8)\\right) - \\left(1 - \\frac{x^4}{2} + O(x^8)\\right)}{x^4} = \\frac{x^4}{2} + \\frac{x^4}{2} + O(x^4) \\text{ and simplifies to } 1 + O(x^4) .\n\\]\n\nTaking the limit as \\(x \\to 0\\) gives us \\(1\\). Therefore, the answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00016965}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6921", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the value of the series $\\sum_{{k=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{(-1)^{{k-1}}{{k}} \\sum_{{n=0}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{1}}{{k 2^n+1}}$?\n\nOptions: \nA. $\\frac{{\\pi}}{{2}}$\nB. 2.0\nC. $\\ln(2)$\nD. $\\pi$\nE. 1.0\nF. $\\sqrt{{2}}$\nG. 0.5\nH. $\\frac{{\\sqrt{{3}}{{2}}$\nI. 0.0\nJ. 1.5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To evaluate the series \\(\\sum_{{k=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{(-1)^{{k-1}} k \\sum_{{n=0}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{1}{{k 2^n+1}}}\\), we first find the inner sum \\(\\sum_{{n=0}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{1}{{k 2^n + 1}}\\). This sum can be simplified and analyzed, leading us to express the entire series in terms of well-known constants. Ultimately, we find that the final result simplifies to \\(\\ln(2)\\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 150, "total_tokens": 358}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To evaluate the series \\(\\sum_{{k=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{(-1)^{{k-1}} k \\sum_{{n=0}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{1}{{k 2^n+1}}}\\), we first find the inner sum \\(\\sum_{{n=0}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{1}{{k 2^n + 1}}\\). This sum can be simplified and analyzed, leading us to express the entire series in terms of well-known constants. Ultimately, we find that the final result simplifies to \\(\\ln(2)\\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00012119999999999999}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7148", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluate $\\lim _{{x \\rightarrow 1^{{-}} \\prod_{{n=0}}^{{\\infty}}(\\frac{{1+x^{{n+1}}{{1+x^n}})^{{x^n}}$?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.3456789\nB. 2.7182818\nC. $\\infty$\nD. 4.5678901\nE. 0.73575888\nF. 0\nG. 1\nH. 1.23456789\nI. 3.456789\nJ. 1.1111111\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To evaluate the limit \\(\\lim _{{x \\rightarrow 1^{-}} \\prod_{{n=0}}^{{\\infty}}(\\frac{{1+x^{{n+1}}}}{{1+x^n}})^{{x^n}}\\), we analyze the behavior of the product as \\(x\\) approaches 1 from the left. As \\(x\\) approaches 1, each term \\(\\frac{{1+x^{n+1}}}{{1+x^n}}\\) tends toward 1, making the product approach a finite limit. Evaluating reveals that the limit converges to \\(e\\), approximately \\(2.7182818\\).\n\nThus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 195, "output_tokens": 151, "total_tokens": 346}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To evaluate the limit \\(\\lim _{{x \\rightarrow 1^{-}} \\prod_{{n=0}}^{{\\infty}}(\\frac{{1+x^{{n+1}}}}{{1+x^n}})^{{x^n}}\\), we analyze the behavior of the product as \\(x\\) approaches 1 from the left. As \\(x\\) approaches 1, each term \\(\\frac{{1+x^{n+1}}}{{1+x^n}}\\) tends toward 1, making the product approach a finite limit. Evaluating reveals that the limit converges to \\(e\\), approximately \\(2.7182818\\).\n\nThus, the correct choice is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00011985000000000001}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7664", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the sum of $\\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{2}}{{n^2 + 4n + 3}}$\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.6333\nB. 0.9333\nC. 2.0333\nD. 0.7333\nE. 0.8333\nF. 1.4333\nG. 2.1433\nH. 0.4333\nI. 0.5633\nJ. 1.2333\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the sum of \\( \\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{2}}{{n^2 + 4n + 3}} \\), we can first factor the denominator: \\( n^2 + 4n + 3 = (n+1)(n+3) \\). This allows us to use partial fraction decomposition, giving us \\( \\frac{2}{(n+1)(n+3)} = \\frac{A}{n+1} + \\frac{B}{n+3} \\) to solve for \\( A \\) and \\( B \\). The sum converges to a particular value, which after calculation approximates to about \\( 1.2333 \\). Hence, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 180, "output_tokens": 165, "total_tokens": 345}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the sum of \\( \\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{2}}{{n^2 + 4n + 3}} \\), we can first factor the denominator: \\( n^2 + 4n + 3 = (n+1)(n+3) \\). This allows us to use partial fraction decomposition, giving us \\( \\frac{2}{(n+1)(n+3)} = \\frac{A}{n+1} + \\frac{B}{n+3} \\) to solve for \\( A \\) and \\( B \\). The sum converges to a particular value, which after calculation approximates to about \\( 1.2333 \\). Hence, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.000126}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7691", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find $\\gamma$ so that the solution of the initial value problem $x^2 y^{{\\prime \\prime}}-2 y=0, y(1)=1, y^{{\\prime}}(1)=\\gamma$ is bounded as $x \\rightarrow 0$.\n\nOptions: \nA. 6\nB. 5\nC. 1/2\nD. 1\nE. 0\nF. 3\nG.  2\nH. -2\nI. -1\nJ. 4\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To solve the differential equation \\(x^2 y^{\\prime\\prime} - 2y = 0\\), we can use a power series or variable substitution approach. The general solution is of the form \\(y = C_1 x + C_2 x^2\\), where constants \\(C_1\\) and \\(C_2\\) depend on initial conditions. Given \\(y(1) = 1\\) and \\(y'(1) = \\gamma\\), substituting these conditions yields equations that can be solved for \\(C_1\\) and \\(C_2\\), ultimately leading to \\(\\gamma = 2\\) for boundedness as \\(x \\rightarrow 0\\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 178, "output_tokens": 161, "total_tokens": 339}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To solve the differential equation \\(x^2 y^{\\prime\\prime} - 2y = 0\\), we can use a power series or variable substitution approach. The general solution is of the form \\(y = C_1 x + C_2 x^2\\), where constants \\(C_1\\) and \\(C_2\\) depend on initial conditions. Given \\(y(1) = 1\\) and \\(y'(1) = \\gamma\\), substituting these conditions yields equations that can be solved for \\(C_1\\) and \\(C_2\\), ultimately leading to \\(\\gamma = 2\\) for boundedness as \\(x \\rightarrow 0\\).\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00012330000000000002}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7484", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For every positive real number $x$, let $g(x)=\\lim _{{r \\rightarrow 0}}((x+1)^{{r+1}}-x^{{r+1}})^{{1/r}}$. What is the limit of $g(x)/x$ as $x$ goes to infinity?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\nB. Infinity\nC. 3.1415926\nD. 1\nE. 0\nF. 1.6180339\nG. 1.4142135\nH. 1.7320508\nI. 2.7182818\nJ. 3.1415927\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find \\( g(x) \\), we first compute:\n\n\\[\ng(x) = \\lim_{r \\to 0} ((x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1})^{1/r}\n\\]\n\nFor large \\( x \\), we can use the fact that \\( (x + 1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1} \\approx (x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1} \\) behaves like \\( (x^r) \\cdot \\frac{(1 + \\frac{1}{x})^{r+1} - 1}{r} \\). This gives us \\( g(x) \\) tending to \\( x \\) as \\( x \\to \\infty \\). Thus, we conclude that \\( \\frac{g(x)}{x} \\to 1 \\), leading us to the answer of option D.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 206, "total_tokens": 410}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find \\( g(x) \\), we first compute:\n\n\\[\ng(x) = \\lim_{r \\to 0} ((x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1})^{1/r}\n\\]\n\nFor large \\( x \\), we can use the fact that \\( (x + 1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1} \\approx (x+1)^{r+1} - x^{r+1} \\) behaves like \\( (x^r) \\cdot \\frac{(1 + \\frac{1}{x})^{r+1} - 1}{r} \\). This gives us \\( g(x) \\) tending to \\( x \\) as \\( x \\to \\infty \\). Thus, we conclude that \\( \\frac{g(x)}{x} \\to 1 \\), leading us to the answer of option D.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001542}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7472", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sum the series $\\sum_{{m=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}}\\frac{{m^2 n}}{{3^m(n3^m+m3^n)}}$\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.23456\nB. 0.41567\nC. 0.19375\nD. 0.28125\nE. 0.62500\nF. 0.14659\nG. 0.51234\nH. 0.33333\nI. 0.73145\nJ. 0.77777\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the sum of the series \\(\\sum_{{m=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{m^2 n}}{{3^m (n 3^m + m 3^n)}}\\), we can simplify the expression in the denominators and examine the series convergence. After thorough evaluation of the inner and outer sums, the most probable answer aligns with numerical evaluations leading to the value approximately 0.28125. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 196, "output_tokens": 119, "total_tokens": 315}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the sum of the series \\(\\sum_{{m=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\sum_{{n=1}}^{{\\infty}} \\frac{{m^2 n}}{{3^m (n 3^m + m 3^n)}}\\), we can simplify the expression in the denominators and examine the series convergence. After thorough evaluation of the inner and outer sums, the most probable answer aligns with numerical evaluations leading to the value approximately 0.28125. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001008}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_6697", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Is the cumulative distribution function of the standard gaussian distribution $F(x)=1/\\sqrt{{2 \\pi}} \\int_{{-\\infty}}^x e^{{-t^2/2}} dt$ is log-concave?  Return 1 for yes and 0 for no.\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.5\nB. -1.0\nC. 2.0\nD. 1.5\nE. -0.5\nF. 0.0\nG. 1.0\nH. -2.0\nI. 0.5\nJ. 3.0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The cumulative distribution function (CDF) of the standard Gaussian distribution, \\( F(x) \\), is indeed log-concave. This can be shown by examining the second derivative of the logarithm of the function; since \\( F(x) \\) increases and is smooth, its logarithm's concavity can be confirmed. Thus, the correct response to whether it is log-concave is 1.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 197, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 291}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The cumulative distribution function (CDF) of the standard Gaussian distribution, \\( F(x) \\), is indeed log-concave. This can be shown by examining the second derivative of the logarithm of the function; since \\( F(x) \\) increases and is smooth, its logarithm's concavity can be confirmed. Thus, the correct response to whether it is log-concave is 1.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.594999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_math_7346", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $F_0(x)=log(x)$. For $n\\geq 0$ and $x>0$, let $F_{{n+1}}(x)=\\int_0^x F_n(t)dt$. Evaluate $\\lim _{{n \\rightarrow \\infty}} (n! F_n(1))/(log(n))$.\n\nOptions: \nA. π (Pi)\nB. 1.0\nC. 1/n\nD. 2.0\nE. -1.0\nF. e (Euler's number)\nG. -e (Negative Euler's number)\nH. e^-1 (Inverse of Euler's number)\nI. 0.0\nJ. Infinity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The function \\( F_n(x) \\) is defined recursively, starting with \\( F_0(x) = \\log(x) \\). By integrating the previous function, we find that \\( F_n(1) \\) approaches zero as \\( n \\) increases. Therefore, evaluating \\( \\lim _{{n \\rightarrow \\infty}} (n! F_n(1))/(log(n)) \\) results in \\( 0.0 \\), because \\( F_n(1) \\) decays faster than any growth in \\( n! \\). Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 214, "output_tokens": 125, "total_tokens": 339}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The function \\( F_n(x) \\) is defined recursively, starting with \\( F_0(x) = \\log(x) \\). By integrating the previous function, we find that \\( F_n(1) \\) approaches zero as \\( n \\) increases. Therefore, evaluating \\( \\lim _{{n \\rightarrow \\infty}} (n! F_n(1))/(log(n)) \\) results in \\( 0.0 \\), because \\( F_n(1) \\) decays faster than any growth in \\( n! \\). Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\).", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001071}}
