{"global_index": "QANTA_Science_283", "question": "Please read the following question and provide the correct answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The moment-generating function of a random variable X is defined as the expectation value of this function of X times t.\n\nProvide the correct answer in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct and the most common answer to the question. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The moment-generating function of a random variable \\(X\\) is defined as \\(M_X(t) = E[e^{tX}]\\). This function is used to derive all the moments of the random variable, as the \\(n\\)-th derivative of \\(M_X(t)\\) evaluated at \\(t = 0\\) gives the \\(n\\)-th moment of \\(X\\). Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E[e^{tX}]}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 82, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 181}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The moment-generating function of a random variable \\(X\\) is defined as \\(M_X(t) = E[e^{tX}]\\). This function is used to derive all the moments of the random variable, as the \\(n\\)-th derivative of \\(M_X(t)\\) evaluated at \\(t = 0\\) gives the \\(n\\)-th moment of \\(X\\). Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{E[e^{tX}]}\\).", "ground_truth": "Exponential_function", "score": 0.0, "metric": "exact_match", "inference_cost": 7.17e-05}}
