{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5154", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: We want our measures to be as reliable as possible; reliability refers to\n\nOptions: \nA. Whether our measure is ethical to use\nB. Whether our measure has or has not been used before\nC. Whether our measure provides new insights\nD. Whether our measure is approved by an authority\nE. Whether our measure is popular among researchers\nF. Whether our measure is consistent in the information it provides\nG. Whether our measure is cost-effective\nH. Whether our measure really measure anything at all\nI. Whether our measure is really measuring what it claims to measure\nJ. Whether our measure can be easily replicated\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Reliability in the context of measurement refers to the consistency of the information that the measure provides, meaning that repeated measures under the same conditions should yield the same results. This is essential for ensuring that the data obtained is stable and trustworthy over time.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 190, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 247}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Reliability in the context of measurement refers to the consistency of the information that the measure provides, meaning that repeated measures under the same conditions should yield the same results. This is essential for ensuring that the data obtained is stable and trustworthy over time.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.27e-05}}
