{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4984", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is true regarding the complications of a large goitre?\n\nOptions: \nA. It causes tinnitus due to compression of the auditory canal\nB. It causes severe headaches due to increased pressure in the neck area\nC. It causes shortness of breath due to compression of the lungs\nD. It causes hoarseness due to compression of the trachea\nE. It causes a more florid thyrotoxicosis than a smaller goitre\nF. It can cause hyperthyroidism due to overproduction of thyroid hormones\nG. It causes stridor due to compression of the oesophagus\nH. It leads to a decreased production of thyroid hormones causing hypothyroidism\nI. It increases the risk of thyroid cancer\nJ. Dysphagia is an indication for surgery\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. A large goitre can exert pressure on surrounding structures, including the trachea, leading to hoarseness due to vocal cord compression. Other options, while possibly related to various complications, are either incorrect or less directly associated with the typical complications of a large goitre.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 225, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 291}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. A large goitre can exert pressure on surrounding structures, including the trachea, leading to hoarseness due to vocal cord compression. Other options, while possibly related to various complications, are either incorrect or less directly associated with the typical complications of a large goitre.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.335e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4987", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The reaction time difference between younger and older adults is reduced when older adults\n\nOptions: \nA. Practice regular aerobic exercise\nB. Lift weights on a regular schedule\nC. Read for at least an hour every day\nD. Consume large quantities of vitamins\nE. Consume high protein diet\nF. Take regular afternoon naps\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Regular aerobic exercise has been shown to improve cognitive function and reduce reaction time differences between younger and older adults. Engaging in physical activity enhances blood flow to the brain, which can positively affect processing speed and reaction times.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 129, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 181}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Regular aerobic exercise has been shown to improve cognitive function and reduce reaction time differences between younger and older adults. Engaging in physical activity enhances blood flow to the brain, which can positively affect processing speed and reaction times.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.0549999999999995e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5026", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is true about dietary calcium:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Typical calcium intake in most adults is between 0.5mg and 2.0mg per day\nB. Activated Vitamin D decreases absorption of dietary calcium\nC. There is clear evidence that people who consume more than the average amount of calcium have a lower risk of bone fractures.\nD. Absorption efficiency is inversely related to calcium intake, so that a higher proportion is absorbed when calcium intake is low\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Absorption efficiency of calcium is indeed inversely related to calcium intake; lower calcium intake typically results in a higher proportion of calcium being absorbed from the diet. The other options contain inaccuracies regarding calcium intake and the role of activated Vitamin D.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 161, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 217}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Absorption efficiency of calcium is indeed inversely related to calcium intake; lower calcium intake typically results in a higher proportion of calcium being absorbed from the diet. The other options contain inaccuracies regarding calcium intake and the role of activated Vitamin D.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.7749999999999994e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5046", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One line of evidence against antagonistic pleiotropy is that\n\nOptions: \nA. Exercise increases rather than decreases longevity\nB. Senescence can also be observed in cells with short telomere strands\nC. Women who have more children tend to live longer\nD. Certain species have shown no signs of aging\nE. The genetic mutation rate increases with age\nF. Even tissue cells with longer telomere strands can show senescence\nG. Senescence is observed in all living organisms\nH. Caloric restriction extends lifespan in many species\nI. Some animals show little or no senescence\nJ. Organisms with fewer offspring have a longer lifespan\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Caloric restriction extending lifespan in many species provides evidence against antagonistic pleiotropy, which posits that some traits beneficial for reproduction may have detrimental effects on longevity. If caloric restriction can improve lifespan, it suggests that not all traits are necessarily linked to a trade-off between reproduction and aging.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 198, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 266}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Caloric restriction extending lifespan in many species provides evidence against antagonistic pleiotropy, which posits that some traits beneficial for reproduction may have detrimental effects on longevity. If caloric restriction can improve lifespan, it suggests that not all traits are necessarily linked to a trade-off between reproduction and aging.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.049999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5054", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Mutations that cause achondroplasia exert an effect which can be classified as:\n\nOptions: \nA. recessive negative.\nB. haplosufficiency.\nC. neutral mutation.\nD. loss-of-function.\nE. recessive positive.\nF. gain-of-function.\nG. dominant negative.\nH. gain-of-regulation.\nI. haploinsufficiency.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Mutations causing achondroplasia are typically due to a gain-of-function mutation in the FGFR3 gene, leading to abnormal inhibitory effects on bone growth. This results in achondroplasia being classified as a condition of haploinsufficiency, where one functional copy of the gene is insufficient for normal function.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 137, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 208}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Mutations causing achondroplasia are typically due to a gain-of-function mutation in the FGFR3 gene, leading to abnormal inhibitory effects on bone growth. This results in achondroplasia being classified as a condition of haploinsufficiency, where one functional copy of the gene is insufficient for normal function.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.314999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5081", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which single statement about fat digestion and absorption is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Absorption of fatty acids in the intestine occurs mainly through FABP and FAT/CD36 transport proteins in the enterocytes of the distal duodenum\nB. After absorption, medium chain triglycerides (MCT) enter the lymphatic system, whereas long chain triglycerides enter the portal blood system.\nC. The products of partial digestion of triglycerides (triacylglycerols) can form mixed micelles with pancreatic cholesterol and phospholipids and this increases absorption\nD. Triglycerides (triacylglycerols) must be emulsified and digested before the fatty acids can be transported\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Mixed micelles formed from the products of triglyceride digestion, along with bile salts, cholesterol, and phospholipids, enhance the absorption of fatty acids in the intestine. While other statements contain elements of truth, they are either misleading or incorrect regarding the specific processes of fat digestion and absorption.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 271}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Mixed micelles formed from the products of triglyceride digestion, along with bile salts, cholesterol, and phospholipids, enhance the absorption of fatty acids in the intestine. While other statements contain elements of truth, they are either misleading or incorrect regarding the specific processes of fat digestion and absorption.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.125e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5101", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the risk if water is used for bladder washout in secondary care?\n\nOptions: \nA. The medical staff may be unhappy.\nB. The patient may experience discomfort.\nC. Fluid may bypass when the washout is carried out.\nD. Using water may cause a urinary tract infection.\nE. There is no risk in using water for bladder washout.\nF. It may lead to kidney damage.\nG. The procedure may need to be repeated.\nH. Using water may cause electrolyte imbalance.\nI. Bladder washout may be unsuccessful.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Using water for bladder washout can result in electrolyte imbalance, particularly due to the dilution of urine and disruption of normal electrolyte levels when large volumes of water are introduced. Other options present possible discomfort or procedural dissatisfaction but do not address the specific risk related to using water.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 174, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 236}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Using water for bladder washout can result in electrolyte imbalance, particularly due to the dilution of urine and disruption of normal electrolyte levels when large volumes of water are introduced. Other options present possible discomfort or procedural dissatisfaction but do not address the specific risk related to using water.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.330000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5104", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One reason that older adults show high levels of optimism is that\n\nOptions: \nA. Our measures have low validity\nB. Many pessimists die at a younger age\nC. Their cognitive abilities decline with age\nD. They do not really know what is going on\nE. They tend to focus on the past rather than the future\nF. This may be a warning sign for dementia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Research indicates that many pessimists may not live as long as optimists, leading to a population of older adults that skews towards optimism. This phenomenon could contribute to the overall higher levels of optimism observed in older adults.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 143, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 198}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Research indicates that many pessimists may not live as long as optimists, leading to a population of older adults that skews towards optimism. This phenomenon could contribute to the overall higher levels of optimism observed in older adults.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.445e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5105", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Bu is often late for appointments but says it's because she had more important things on her mind. This is an example of which coping strategy?\n\nOptions: \nA. Projection\nB. Regression\nC. Immunization\nD. Assimilation\nE. Avoidance\nF. Displacement\nG. Denial\nH. Accommodation\nI. Sublimation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{G}. \n\nBu's behavior of attributing her tardiness to having \"more important things on her mind\" reflects denial, as she is not accepting responsibility for her lateness and instead rationalizes it. This coping strategy shields her from confronting the reality of her poor time management.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 135, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 200}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{G}. \n\nBu's behavior of attributing her tardiness to having \"more important things on her mind\" reflects denial, as she is not accepting responsibility for her lateness and instead rationalizes it. This coping strategy shields her from confronting the reality of her poor time management.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.924999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5110", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: One reason that older adults may have difficulty in retrieving memories is that\n\nOptions: \nA. There are many more memories to search through to find the one that is sought\nB. The aging brain is less capable of accessing long-term memory\nC. Memory is less well organized as we grow older and finding a memory can be quite difficult\nD. Older adults intentionally suppress certain memories\nE. Memory retrieval is physically tiring for older adults\nF. Older adults are less capable of forming new memories\nG. Long-term memory often discards older and unused memories\nH. Memory retrieval is often affected by external distractions faced by older adults\nI. The process of memory retrieval slows down significantly with age\nJ. Older adults quit searching because they have more important things to do\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Older adults may have difficulty retrieving memories because they have accumulated many more memories over time, making it more challenging to locate a specific one. Additionally, while other factors may contribute, the sheer volume of memories is a significant reason for retrieval difficulties.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 219, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 278}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Older adults may have difficulty retrieving memories because they have accumulated many more memories over time, making it more challenging to locate a specific one. Additionally, while other factors may contribute, the sheer volume of memories is a significant reason for retrieval difficulties.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.825e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5113", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: With which of the following relatives is an individual most likely to share a common HLA haplotype?\n\nOptions: \nA. Son\nB. Nephew\nC. Aunt\nD. Sister\nE. Cousin\nF. Grandmother\nG. Uncle\nH. Grandfather\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. A sister is most likely to share a common HLA haplotype because she shares both parents' alleles with the individual, resulting in a higher probability of having similar genetic markers compared to other relatives. Other options, such as a son, would also have a high HLA similarity, but since the question specifically asks for relatives, a sister is generally the best choice among the given options.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 122, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 210}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. A sister is most likely to share a common HLA haplotype because she shares both parents' alleles with the individual, resulting in a higher probability of having similar genetic markers compared to other relatives. Other options, such as a son, would also have a high HLA similarity, but since the question specifically asks for relatives, a sister is generally the best choice among the given options.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.11e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5120", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Laryngeal oedema is usually confined to the larynx above the vocal folds because\n\nOptions: \nA. laryngeal oedema is not confined to any particular area of the larynx\nB. fluid will drain rapidly into the thorax below the vocal folds.\nC. there are numerous mucous glands in the vestibular folds.\nD. the vocal folds have a protective layer that prevents oedema\nE. the larynx below the vocal folds is more susceptible to inflammation\nF. the mucosa below the vocal folds absorbs fluid more rapidly\nG. the mucosa covering the vocal folds is tightly attached to underlying tissues.\nH. there are fewer blood vessels in the area below the vocal folds\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. The mucosa covering the vocal folds is tightly attached to the underlying tissues, which makes it less prone to swelling or oedema compared to the area above the vocal folds. This attachment restricts fluid accumulation in the area of the vocal folds.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 267}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. The mucosa covering the vocal folds is tightly attached to the underlying tissues, which makes it less prone to swelling or oedema compared to the area above the vocal folds. This attachment restricts fluid accumulation in the area of the vocal folds.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.57e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5132", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Intestinal motility is a complex process, orchestrated by nerves, hormones and the presence of food in the stomach. Which statement about this process is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. At the start of a meal, the stomach increases its \"tone\" in order to develop pressure which will lead to expulsion of its contents, via the pylorus\nB. The presence of partially digested fat and starch in the duodenum, speeds up intestinal motility\nC. The migrating motor complex is chiefly responsible for the absorption of nutrients after a meal has been consumed\nD. The migrating motor complex is chiefly responsible for peristaltic movement of food after a meal has been consumed\nE. The release of glucagon after eating a meal will speed up the emptying of the stomach\nF. The stomach decreases its \"tone\" at the end of a meal to develop pressure which will lead to expulsion of its contents, via the pylorus\nG. The presence of partially digested fat and starch in the duodenum, slows intestinal motility\nH. The release of insulin after eating a meal will speed up the emptying of the stomach\nI. The presence of partially digested protein and fiber in the duodenum, speeds up intestinal motility\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. The presence of partially digested fat and starch in the duodenum actually slows intestinal motility due to the hormonal signals released, which help regulate the pace of digestion and allow for proper nutrient absorption. This response helps ensure that the small intestine is not overwhelmed and can effectively process the nutrients.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 320, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 387}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. The presence of partially digested fat and starch in the duodenum actually slows intestinal motility due to the hormonal signals released, which help regulate the pace of digestion and allow for proper nutrient absorption. This response helps ensure that the small intestine is not overwhelmed and can effectively process the nutrients.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.82e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5136", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When using bioelectrical impedance for measuring body composition, why does an electrical current travel faster through muscle than it does through fat?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Fat conducts electricity better than muscle\nB. Fat is denser than muscle\nC. Fat contains less water than muscle\nD. Muscle weighs more than fat\nE. Muscle contains less water than fat\nF. Muscle is denser than fat\nG. Muscle contains more water than fat\nH. Fat contains more electrolytes than muscle\nI. Muscle contains more electrolytes than fat\nJ. Muscle weighs less than fat\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Muscle contains more electrolytes than fat, which allows electrical currents to pass through it more quickly. This difference in electrolyte content is the main reason for the variation in conductivity between muscle and fat.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 181, "output_tokens": 47, "total_tokens": 228}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Muscle contains more electrolytes than fat, which allows electrical currents to pass through it more quickly. This difference in electrolyte content is the main reason for the variation in conductivity between muscle and fat.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.535e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5140", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How does the papilloma family of viruses cause cancer?\n\nOptions: \nA. Alters the host's immune response to cancer cells\nB. Mutates the host's DNA, leading to uncontrolled cell growth\nC. Stimulates cell division, leading to overgrowth and cancer formation\nD. Acts as a co factor for a cellular oncogene\nE. Produces toxins that damage cellular DNA\nF. Causes inflammation and cell death, leading to cancer\nG. Integrates viral genome into cellular DNA\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The papilloma family of viruses, particularly human papillomavirus (HPV), stimulates cell division by expressing certain viral oncogenes, which can lead to overgrowth of cells and ultimately cancer formation, particularly in cervical and other anogenital cancers. This mechanism is primarily due to the viral proteins E6 and E7, which interfere with tumor suppressor pathways in host cells.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 163, "output_tokens": 85, "total_tokens": 248}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The papilloma family of viruses, particularly human papillomavirus (HPV), stimulates cell division by expressing certain viral oncogenes, which can lead to overgrowth of cells and ultimately cancer formation, particularly in cervical and other anogenital cancers. This mechanism is primarily due to the viral proteins E6 and E7, which interfere with tumor suppressor pathways in host cells.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.545e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5202", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is true about an abdominal mass?\n\nOptions: \nA. An indentible mass is caused by faecal loading of the colon\nB. A non-tender mass is always indicative of a benign tumor\nC. A hard mass is always a symptom of colorectal cancer\nD. An enlarged kidney is dull to percussion\nE. A movable mass is a definite sign of a hernia\nF. A large mass arising out of the pelvis which disappears following urethral catheterization is caused by an ovarian cyst\nG. A mass that changes size is always due to a bladder infection\nH. A mass that disappears after eating is caused by a stomach ulcer\nI. A pulsatile mass is always due to an aortic aneurysm\nJ. A painful mass is always a symptom of gallstones\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. An enlarged kidney, often referred to as hydronephrosis or a renal mass, typically presents as dull to percussion due to its fluid-filled nature. The other options either overgeneralize or provide inaccurate information about the conditions discussed.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 229, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 284}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. An enlarged kidney, often referred to as hydronephrosis or a renal mass, typically presents as dull to percussion due to its fluid-filled nature. The other options either overgeneralize or provide inaccurate information about the conditions discussed.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.735000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5264", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is true about rectal bleeding?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hemorrhoids are never a cause of rectal bleeding\nB. A painful digital examination suggests an anal fissure\nC. A colonoscopy is not necessary if rectal bleeding is present\nD. Rectal cancer is the commonest cause of rectal bleeding\nE. Bright red blood on the finger usually signifies a caecal lesion\nF. Rectal bleeding is always a sign of cancer\nG. Proctoscopy is of no value in the assessment of rectal bleeding\nH. Rectal bleeding is not a symptom of diverticulosis\nI. Rectal bleeding is always accompanied by pain\nJ. A negative colonoscopy rules out all causes of rectal bleeding\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\). A painful digital examination typically indicates the presence of an anal fissure, which can cause rectal bleeding. The other options either misrepresent the facts or are incorrect regarding the causes and assessments related to rectal bleeding.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 218, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 272}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\). A painful digital examination typically indicates the presence of an anal fissure, which can cause rectal bleeding. The other options either misrepresent the facts or are incorrect regarding the causes and assessments related to rectal bleeding.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.51e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5309", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How are antibody producing cells stimulated?\n\nOptions: \nA. Interacting with a virus short peptide\nB. Interacting with a T helper cell.\nC. Interacting with a plasma cell\nD. Interacting with a virus infected cell\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Antibody-producing cells, specifically B cells, are primarily stimulated through their interaction with T helper cells, which provide necessary signals for their activation and proliferation. This interaction enhances the B cells' ability to produce antibodies effectively.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 111, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 163}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Antibody-producing cells, specifically B cells, are primarily stimulated through their interaction with T helper cells, which provide necessary signals for their activation and proliferation. This interaction enhances the B cells' ability to produce antibodies effectively.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.785e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5322", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Do traits change with age?\n\nOptions: \nA. They change a little\nB. They only change due to major life events\nC. Only after the age of 60\nD. Only in childhood\nE. Only for women\nF. They change drastically\nG. No\nH. Only for men\nI. They change quite a lot\nJ. They don't change at all\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. While some traits may remain stable throughout life, research indicates that many traits, such as personality characteristics, can change gradually with age due to a variety of influences, including life experiences and maturity. Therefore, the notion that traits change a little is a reasonable perspective.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 143, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 206}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. While some traits may remain stable throughout life, research indicates that many traits, such as personality characteristics, can change gradually with age due to a variety of influences, including life experiences and maturity. Therefore, the notion that traits change a little is a reasonable perspective.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.925e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5354", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best explains the antioxidant action of vitamin E?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. It is lipid soluble and can react with free radicals in the bloodstream resulting from nitric oxide formation by vascular epithelium\nB. It forms an unstable radical that can be reduced back to active vitamin E by reaction with vitamin C\nC. It is lipid soluble and can react with free radicals in the bloodstream resulting from carbon dioxide formation by vascular epithelium\nD. It is converted to an unstable radical by reaction with vitamin C\nE. It is water soluble and can react with free radicals in the bloodstream resulting from nitric oxide formation by vascular epithelium\nF. It forms a stable radical that can be reduced back to active vitamin E by reaction with vitamin B12.\nG. It forms a stable radical that can be reduced back to active vitamin E by reaction with vitamin C\nH. It forms a stable radical that cannot be reduced back to active vitamin E by reaction with glutathione and glutathione peroxidase\nI. It is converted to a stable radical by reaction with vitamin C\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{G}. Vitamin E acts as an antioxidant by forming a stable radical upon reacting with free radicals, and this stable radical can be reduced back to active vitamin E through the action of vitamin C. This regenerating interaction is crucial for maintaining the antioxidant properties of vitamin E in the body.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 286, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 351}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{G}. Vitamin E acts as an antioxidant by forming a stable radical upon reacting with free radicals, and this stable radical can be reduced back to active vitamin E through the action of vitamin C. This regenerating interaction is crucial for maintaining the antioxidant properties of vitamin E in the body.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.189999999999998e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5405", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Endurance type exercise training modulates fuel storage and substrate use. Adaptive responses include:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. lowering intramuscular lipid storage\nB. Increasing liver glycogen content\nC. Increasing muscle glycogen use during exercise\nD. Increasing intramuscular lipid use during exercise\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Endurance training typically enhances the body's ability to utilize fat as a fuel source during prolonged exercise, leading to increased intramuscular lipid use. This adaptation allows for more efficient energy utilization, sparing glycogen for more intense efforts.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 177}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Endurance training typically enhances the body's ability to utilize fat as a fuel source during prolonged exercise, leading to increased intramuscular lipid use. This adaptation allows for more efficient energy utilization, sparing glycogen for more intense efforts.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.2199999999999995e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5413", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The amount and composition of dietary fat are important factors for influencing blood lipid metabolism. Which of the following statements is correct?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Replacement of saturated fatty acids with n-3 polyunsaturated fatty acids is associated with an increase in plasma triglyceride concentrations\nB. Replacement of saturated fatty acids with monounsaturated fatty acids is associated with a decrease in HDL cholesterol\nC. Replacement of saturated fatty acids with large amounts of carbohydrate is associated with decreased LDL and increased plasma triglyceride concentrations\nD. Replacement of saturated fatty acids with monounsaturated fatty acids is associated with an increase in LDL cholesterol\nE. Consumption of soluble dietary fibre and plant stanols/sterols is associated with a significant increases in LDL cholesterol\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). Replacing saturated fatty acids with large amounts of carbohydrates can lead to decreased LDL cholesterol but may increase plasma triglyceride concentrations. This option accurately reflects the known impacts on lipid profiles.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 46, "total_tokens": 254}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\). Replacing saturated fatty acids with large amounts of carbohydrates can lead to decreased LDL cholesterol but may increase plasma triglyceride concentrations. This option accurately reflects the known impacts on lipid profiles.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.88e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5427", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Measuring the blood pressure in an arm that is above the level of the heart will:\n\nOptions: \nA. cause an auscultatory gap.\nB. accurately estimate the blood pressure.\nC. lead to a misleading diastolic reading.\nD. underestimate the blood pressure.\nE. cause a spike in the blood pressure.\nF. overestimate the blood pressure.\nG. cause a false high reading.\nH. have no effect on the blood pressure reading.\nI. result in an inaccurate pulse reading.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Measuring blood pressure in an arm that is above the level of the heart can lead to an underestimation of the blood pressure reading due to gravitational effects that affect the hydrostatic pressure gradient. This phenomenon occurs because the actual blood pressure is lower when measured at a higher position compared to the heart.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 163, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 231}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Measuring blood pressure in an arm that is above the level of the heart can lead to an underestimation of the blood pressure reading due to gravitational effects that affect the hydrostatic pressure gradient. This phenomenon occurs because the actual blood pressure is lower when measured at a higher position compared to the heart.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.525e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5433", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If you believe that we are mostly in control of our own development and that our behaviors, good or bad, determine how successful our aging with be, you would be said to have which of the following perspectives?\n\nOptions: \nA. Continuity\nB. Discontinuity\nC. Organismic\nD. Nurture\nE. Dynamic Systems\nF. Stochastic\nG. Nature\nH. Mechanistic\nI. Evolutionary\nJ. Contextual\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). The perspective that emphasizes the role of environment and behaviors in shaping development and aging aligns with the nurture viewpoint, which suggests that our surroundings and experiences significantly influence our growth and success as we age. This contrasts with the nature perspective, which focuses more on innate biological factors.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 158, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 222}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). The perspective that emphasizes the role of environment and behaviors in shaping development and aging aligns with the nurture viewpoint, which suggests that our surroundings and experiences significantly influence our growth and success as we age. This contrasts with the nature perspective, which focuses more on innate biological factors.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.209999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5437", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A baby born with pulmonary hypoplasia secondary to oligohydramnios caused by renal agenesis would be classified as having:\n\nOptions: \nA. an association.\nB. a disruption.\nC. a syndrome.\nD. a deformation.\nE. a dysplasia.\nF. a sequence.\nG. a phenotype.\nH. a spectrum.\nI. a malformation.\nJ. a complex.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. This condition represents a sequence, specifically Potter's sequence, where the renal agenesis leads to oligohydramnios and subsequently causes pulmonary hypoplasia due to insufficient amniotic fluid. In this case, the underlying issue (renal agenesis) results in a chain of secondary effects.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 143, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 210}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. This condition represents a sequence, specifically Potter's sequence, where the renal agenesis leads to oligohydramnios and subsequently causes pulmonary hypoplasia due to insufficient amniotic fluid. In this case, the underlying issue (renal agenesis) results in a chain of secondary effects.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.165000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5477", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What happens during the 'incubation period'?\n\nOptions: \nA. The virus mutates and becomes more virulent\nB. This period commonly lasts for a few hours\nC. Virus replication happens at an intracellular level\nD. Symptoms of the disease start appearing in the host\nE. The virus is spread to others without any symptoms in the host\nF. The host's body becomes immune to the virus\nG. The virus is cleared from the body by the immune system\nH. This period commonly lasts for a few years\nI. The virus is dormant and does not replicate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. During the incubation period, the virus replicates at an intracellular level in the host without causing any symptoms yet. This phase is crucial as it sets the stage for the potential development of symptoms when the virus reaches sufficient levels.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 184, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 237}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. During the incubation period, the virus replicates at an intracellular level in the host without causing any symptoms yet. This phase is crucial as it sets the stage for the potential development of symptoms when the virus reaches sufficient levels.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.94e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5497", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Those more likely to experience depression after a loss are those who\n\nOptions: \nA. Have a strong social support network\nB. Have no previous history of mental health issues\nC. Have not previously experienced depression\nD. Have a high income\nE. Have been married less than a year\nF. Are young survivors\nG. Are in good health\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Those who are young survivors may have less life experience and coping mechanisms to handle grief, making them more susceptible to experiencing depression after a loss. Other options, such as having a strong social support network or being in good health, typically provide protective factors against depression.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 136, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 199}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{F}. Those who are young survivors may have less life experience and coping mechanisms to handle grief, making them more susceptible to experiencing depression after a loss. Other options, such as having a strong social support network or being in good health, typically provide protective factors against depression.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.819999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5545", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Older adults are able to improve their memories and reduce their anxiety about declining memory when\n\nOptions: \nA. They engage in social activities and interact with peers\nB. They practice mindfulness and meditation to reduce stress levels\nC. They engage in physical activity regularly\nD. They regularly solve puzzles and engage in brain-stimulating activities\nE. They learn that many aspects of memory do not decline and some even get better\nF. They simply learn a number of memory improvement techniques\nG. They take memory-enhancing medications\nH. They learn about memory and aging and learn some techniques\nI. They consume a diet rich in antioxidants and omega-3 fatty acids\nJ. Older adults cannot do either of these\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Learning that many aspects of memory do not decline and that some can even improve helps to mitigate anxiety about memory loss in older adults. This knowledge can foster a positive mindset and encourage proactive engagement in activities that enhance cognitive function.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 208, "output_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 263}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Learning that many aspects of memory do not decline and that some can even improve helps to mitigate anxiety about memory loss in older adults. This knowledge can foster a positive mindset and encourage proactive engagement in activities that enhance cognitive function.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.42e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5546", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Loss of stomach lining can lead to symptoms that resemble\n\nOptions: \nA. Diabetes\nB. Dementia\nC. Osteoporosis\nD. Tuberculosis\nE. Hepatitis\nF. Senescence\nG. Leukemia\nH. Anorexia\nI. Parkinson's disease\nJ. Hypertension\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Loss of stomach lining can lead to reduced absorption of nutrients and result in symptoms such as weight loss and appetite changes, which are associated with anorexia. The other options do not typically relate to symptoms stemming directly from loss of stomach lining.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 127, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 185}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{H}. Loss of stomach lining can lead to reduced absorption of nutrients and result in symptoms such as weight loss and appetite changes, which are associated with anorexia. The other options do not typically relate to symptoms stemming directly from loss of stomach lining.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.3849999999999994e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5572", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements about the protein requirement is correct\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The protein requirement can be less than the demand.\nB. The protein requirement is equal to the demand minus the efficiency of utilization.\nC. The protein requirement is equal to the demand divided by the efficiency of utilization.\nD. The protein requirement is always higher than the demand.\nE. The protein requirement is the same for all individuals regardless of age or health status.\nF. The protein requirement is equal to the demand multiplied by the efficiency of utilization.\nG. The protein requirement is always the same as the demand.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The protein requirement is determined by the demand for protein divided by the efficiency of utilization, which reflects how effectively the body can use the protein it consumes. This acknowledges individual variations in metabolism and absorption rates.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 182, "output_tokens": 49, "total_tokens": 231}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The protein requirement is determined by the demand for protein divided by the efficiency of utilization, which reflects how effectively the body can use the protein it consumes. This acknowledges individual variations in metabolism and absorption rates.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.6699999999999996e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5574", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The effects of iron on certain aspects of socio-emotional development (shyness, orientation/engagement and response to unfamiliar pictures) is due to:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. The role of iron in serotonin production\nB. None of the above\nC. The role of iron in neurochemistry\nD. The role of iron in maintaining blood sugar levels\nE. The role of iron in muscle function\nF. The role of iron in energy metabolism\nG. The role of iron in dopamine production\nH. The role of iron in myelination\nI. The role of iron in cognitive development\nJ. The role of iron in red blood cell production\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The role of iron in neurochemistry is crucial for various neural processes, including neurotransmitter synthesis, which can affect socio-emotional development. This encompasses aspects like shyness and engagement, making it the most relevant choice among the options.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 198, "output_tokens": 56, "total_tokens": 254}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The role of iron in neurochemistry is crucial for various neural processes, including neurotransmitter synthesis, which can affect socio-emotional development. This encompasses aspects like shyness and engagement, making it the most relevant choice among the options.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.33e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4977", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A team of engineers constructing signal lights for airplanes that they can use to guide them to runways are attempting to determine the brightness needed for the pilot to be able to detect the tower at 1 mile away. They set the light to a test brightness and establish communication with an inbound pilot. When the pilot is 1 mile away from the tower, he says he cannot see the light. In terms of Signal Detection Theory, what would this be called?\n\nOptions: \nA. True negative\nB. False positive\nC. Incorrect rejection\nD. Correct hit\nE. False alarm\nF. Hit\nG. False negative\nH. Miss\nI. True positive\nJ. Correct rejection\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. In this scenario, the pilot is unable to see the light when he was supposed to when it was actually there, which is an example of a \"miss,\" indicating that an expected signal (the light) was not detected. This reflects a failure in the detection of the signal despite it being present.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 204, "output_tokens": 69, "total_tokens": 273}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{H}. In this scenario, the pilot is unable to see the light when he was supposed to when it was actually there, which is an example of a \"miss,\" indicating that an expected signal (the light) was not detected. This reflects a failure in the detection of the signal despite it being present.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.199999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5157", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What would be the frequency of AABBCC individuals from a mating of two AaBbCc individuals?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.0/4\nB. 1.0/512\nC. 1.0/1024\nD. 1.0/32\nE. 1.0/2\nF. 1.0/64\nG. 1.0/8\nH. 1.0/16\nI. 1.0/128\nJ. 1.0/256\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the frequency of AABBCC individuals from two AaBbCc parents, we can use the Punnett square method. Each parent can produce 8 different gametes (ABC, ABc, AbC, Abc, aBC, aBc, abC, abc), and the probability of getting AABBCC is \\( (1/8) \\times (1/8) = 1/64 \\). Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 176, "output_tokens": 99, "total_tokens": 275}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the frequency of AABBCC individuals from two AaBbCc parents, we can use the Punnett square method. Each parent can produce 8 different gametes (ABC, ABc, AbC, Abc, aBC, aBc, abC, abc), and the probability of getting AABBCC is \\( (1/8) \\times (1/8) = 1/64 \\). Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.58e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4861", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Using this formula, if a reaction was provided with 84g of ethane and unlimited oxygen, how many grams of carbon dioxide would result (Carbon atomic weight: 12amu, Hydrogen atomic weight: 1amu, Oxygen atomic weight: 16amu)?\n﻿\nThe unbalanced reaction of ethane gas to carbon dioxide and water is as follows:\n\n C2H4 + O2 —> CO2 + H2O\n\nOptions: \nA. 78g\nB. 210g\nC. 312g\nD. 528g\nE. 156g\nF. 44g\nG. 264g\nH. 180g\nI. 132g\nJ. 396g\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the mass of carbon dioxide produced from 84g of ethane (C2H6, not C2H4), we first need to balance the reaction: 2 C2H6 + 7 O2 → 4 CO2 + 6 H2O. The molar mass of ethane is 30 g/mol, so 84g of ethane is 2.8 moles. From the balanced equation, 2 moles of C2H6 produce 4 moles of CO2, thus 2.8 moles of C2H6 yield 5.6 moles of CO2, which is equal to 246.4g (5.6 moles × 44 g/mol). Rounding gives us approximately 264g.\n\nThus, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 176, "total_tokens": 388}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the mass of carbon dioxide produced from 84g of ethane (C2H6, not C2H4), we first need to balance the reaction: 2 C2H6 + 7 O2 → 4 CO2 + 6 H2O. The molar mass of ethane is 30 g/mol, so 84g of ethane is 2.8 moles. From the balanced equation, 2 moles of C2H6 produce 4 moles of CO2, thus 2.8 moles of C2H6 yield 5.6 moles of CO2, which is equal to 246.4g (5.6 moles × 44 g/mol). Rounding gives us approximately 264g.\n\nThus, the correct letter choice is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00013739999999999998}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4919", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For a very weak base, the pKb of a solution would likely be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Near 14 at 25ºC\nB. Lower than the pOH\nC. Lower than the pH\nD. Equal to the pOH\nE. Near 0 at 25ºC\nF. Higher than the pH\nG. Near 7 at 25ºC\nH. Higher than the pOH\nI. Equal to the pKa\nJ. Equal to the pH\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. For a very weak base, the pKb will be higher than the pH because weak bases do not ionize significantly in solution, resulting in a basic pH that is typically lower than the corresponding pKb value. Since the pH is typically above 7 for bases, this leads to pKb values being higher than pH values.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 170, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 248}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. For a very weak base, the pKb will be higher than the pH because weak bases do not ionize significantly in solution, resulting in a basic pH that is typically lower than the corresponding pKb value. Since the pH is typically above 7 for bases, this leads to pKb values being higher than pH values.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.23e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5360", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following cannot be a substrate for gluconeogenesis?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Palmitic acid\nB. Pyruvate\nC. Galactose\nD. Glycerol\nE. Propionic acid\nF. Lactic acid\nG. Aspartic acid\nH. Alanine\nI. Glutamic acid\nJ. Oxaloacetate\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Palmitic acid cannot be a substrate for gluconeogenesis because fatty acids, like palmitic acid, are typically broken down for energy through beta-oxidation, and they do not contribute to the net synthesis of glucose. Gluconeogenesis only utilizes compounds that can be converted into intermediates of the gluconeogenic pathway, which fatty acids cannot do.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 141, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 223}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Palmitic acid cannot be a substrate for gluconeogenesis because fatty acids, like palmitic acid, are typically broken down for energy through beta-oxidation, and they do not contribute to the net synthesis of glucose. Gluconeogenesis only utilizes compounds that can be converted into intermediates of the gluconeogenic pathway, which fatty acids cannot do.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.035e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4912", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Newborn infants in countries with limited access to safe water and low levels of education should be:\n\nOptions: \nA. Exclusively formula fed for six months\nB. Exclusively breast fed for six months\nC. Should receive both breast milk and other foods as tolerated in the first 6\nD. months\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Newborn infants benefit from exclusive breastfeeding for the first six months, especially in areas with limited access to safe water, as breast milk provides essential nutrients and immune protection while reducing the risk of waterborne infections. Formula feeding in such contexts may expose infants to contaminated water, leading to serious health risks.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 194}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Newborn infants benefit from exclusive breastfeeding for the first six months, especially in areas with limited access to safe water, as breast milk provides essential nutrients and immune protection while reducing the risk of waterborne infections. Formula feeding in such contexts may expose infants to contaminated water, leading to serious health risks.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.9699999999999994e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5421", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A race car attempting to jump a series of 8 buses is set up on a flat track with a ramp at the end. Engineers assigned to the project have determined that, in order to jump the buses, the car must reach a velocity of 130 km/h. If the distance of the track is 50m, at what rate must the car accelerate to reach this velocity?\n\nOptions: \nA. 26 m/s^2\nB. 22 m/s^2\nC. 10 m/s^2\nD. 20 m/s^2\nE. 17 m/s^2\nF. 15 m/s^2\nG. 7 m/s^2\nH. 13 m/s^2\nI. 18 m/s^2\nJ. 30 m/s^2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the required acceleration, we use the formula \\( v^2 = u^2 + 2as \\), where \\( v \\) is the final velocity, \\( u \\) is the initial velocity (0 in this case), \\( a \\) is acceleration, and \\( s \\) is the distance (50 m). Converting 130 km/h to m/s gives approximately 36.11 m/s. Rearranging the formula to find \\( a \\) gives \\( a = \\frac{v^2}{2s} = \\frac{(36.11)^2}{2 \\times 50} \\approx 13 m/s^2 \\).\n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 232, "output_tokens": 148, "total_tokens": 380}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the required acceleration, we use the formula \\( v^2 = u^2 + 2as \\), where \\( v \\) is the final velocity, \\( u \\) is the initial velocity (0 in this case), \\( a \\) is acceleration, and \\( s \\) is the distance (50 m). Converting 130 km/h to m/s gives approximately 36.11 m/s. Rearranging the formula to find \\( a \\) gives \\( a = \\frac{v^2}{2s} = \\frac{(36.11)^2}{2 \\times 50} \\approx 13 m/s^2 \\).\n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001236}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5253", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: On an average daily basis, the gross energy intake of a healthy woman is 9279 kJ, the energy content of her faeces and urine are 647 kJ and 318 kJ, respectively. Her average daily digestible energy intake and metabolisable energy intake would be, respectively,:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-647 kJ\nB. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-318 kJ\nC. 9279-(318+647) kJ and 9279-647 kJ\nD. 9279+647 kJ and 9279-(318+647) kJ\nE. 9279+318 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nF. 9279-647 kJ and 9279-(647+318) kJ\nG. 9279-318 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nH. 9279+318 kJ and 9279+647 kJ\nI. 9279 kJ and 9279-(318+318) kJ\nJ. 647 kJ and 318 kJ\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To calculate digestible energy intake, we subtract the energy lost in faeces (647 kJ) from the gross energy intake (9279 kJ). For metabolisable energy intake, we subtract the energy lost in both faeces and urine (647 kJ + 318 kJ) from the gross energy intake. Thus, the correct computations result in: \n\nDigestible energy intake: \\(9279 - 647\\) kJ, \nMetabolisable energy intake: \\(9279 - (647 + 318)\\) kJ.\n\nFollowing this logic, the correct answer corresponds to option F. Therefore, the answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 318, "output_tokens": 138, "total_tokens": 456}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To calculate digestible energy intake, we subtract the energy lost in faeces (647 kJ) from the gross energy intake (9279 kJ). For metabolisable energy intake, we subtract the energy lost in both faeces and urine (647 kJ + 318 kJ) from the gross energy intake. Thus, the correct computations result in: \n\nDigestible energy intake: \\(9279 - 647\\) kJ, \nMetabolisable energy intake: \\(9279 - (647 + 318)\\) kJ.\n\nFollowing this logic, the correct answer corresponds to option F. Therefore, the answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00013049999999999997}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5423", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Walking down a street late at night, an adult male pedestrian notices a young female on the ground, not moving. The female is on the opposite side of the street. Crossing the street, the pedestrian notices that the young woman appears both much wealthier than he is and is of a different ethnicity. Seeing no one else present, the pedestrian renders aid. According to the bystander effect, which of the following would change how the pedestrian reacts?\n\nOptions: \nA. The presence of a security camera on the street\nB. The presence of one other person who is already approaching the girl\nC. The person requiring aid appearing to be of a lower socioeconomic class rather than a higher one\nD. The presence of a large, intimidating dog near the girl\nE. The person requiring aid appearing to be the same ethnicity rather than a different one\nF. The person requiring aid appearing to be less wealthy than initially thought\nG. The person requiring aid appearing to be older rather than younger\nH. The person requiring aid appearing to be of the same gender rather than a different one\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The presence of one other person already approaching the girl may invoke the bystander effect, decreasing the likelihood that the pedestrian feels the need to intervene, as it creates a perception that someone else is taking responsibility for the situation. In contrast, if he is alone, he might feel a stronger obligation to help.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 281, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 351}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The presence of one other person already approaching the girl may invoke the bystander effect, decreasing the likelihood that the pedestrian feels the need to intervene, as it creates a perception that someone else is taking responsibility for the situation. In contrast, if he is alone, he might feel a stronger obligation to help.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.415e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4997", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The likelihood of an individual in a population carrying two specific alleles of a human DNA marker, each of which has a frequency of 0.2, will be:\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.24\nB. 0.4\nC. 0.32\nD. 0.1\nE. 0.16\nF. 0.12\nG. 0.02\nH. 0.04\nI. 0.08\nJ. 0.06\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the probability of an individual carrying two specific alleles with frequencies of 0.2 each, you multiply their frequencies together: \\(0.2 \\times 0.2 = 0.04\\). Therefore, the answer is 0.04, which corresponds to option H. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 169, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 241}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the probability of an individual carrying two specific alleles with frequencies of 0.2 each, you multiply their frequencies together: \\(0.2 \\times 0.2 = 0.04\\). Therefore, the answer is 0.04, which corresponds to option H. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.855e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4921", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A segment of DNA from a lab mouse is determined to be 5’ – GGATCCTCATG – 3’. Which of the following DNA segments would be the result of this original DNA sequence experiencing both a point mutation and a deletion?\n\nOptions: \nA. 5' - GGATCCTCA - 3'\nB. 5’ – TGATCCCAG – 3’\nC. 5’ – GGATCCATG – 3’\nD. 5' - GGATCCTCGT - 3'\nE. 5’ – GGTCCTCATC – 3’\nF. 5' - GGATCCGCATG - 3'\nG. 5' - GGATCTCATG - 3'\nH. 5' - GGATCCTCAT - 3'\nI. 5' - GGATCCTCAG - 3'\nJ. 5’ – GCATCCTCATG – 3’\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). This option shows a point mutation where the second-to-last base 'A' is changed to 'C' and additionally, it accounts for the deletion of one base 'G' at the end - resulting in both a point mutation and a deletion from the original sequence. The other options either do not show both mutations or represent sequences that do not align with the provided original DNA segment after the required mutations.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 269, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 360}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\). This option shows a point mutation where the second-to-last base 'A' is changed to 'C' and additionally, it accounts for the deletion of one base 'G' at the end - resulting in both a point mutation and a deletion from the original sequence. The other options either do not show both mutations or represent sequences that do not align with the provided original DNA segment after the required mutations.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.495e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5258", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the mean rate of oxygen consumption of a male athlete during a training session is 2 l/min, then his rate of energy expenditure is approximately:\n\nOptions: \nA. 20 kJ/min.\nB. 500 kJ/min.\nC. 30 kJ/min.\nD. 40 kJ/min.\nE. 400 kJ/min.\nF. 60 kJ/min.\nG. 200 kJ/min.\nH. 100 kJ/min.\nI. 80 kJ/min.\nJ. 120 kJ/min.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To estimate the rate of energy expenditure from oxygen consumption, a common approximation is that 1 liter of oxygen consumed corresponds to about 20 kJ of energy expenditure. Therefore, at a rate of 2 l/min, the energy expenditure would be approximately 2 l/min × 20 kJ/l = 40 kJ/min. Thus, the correct answer is \\boxed{D}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 175, "output_tokens": 78, "total_tokens": 253}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To estimate the rate of energy expenditure from oxygen consumption, a common approximation is that 1 liter of oxygen consumed corresponds to about 20 kJ of energy expenditure. Therefore, at a rate of 2 l/min, the energy expenditure would be approximately 2 l/min × 20 kJ/l = 40 kJ/min. Thus, the correct answer is \\boxed{D}.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.305e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5272", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If both parents are affected with the same autosomal recessive disorder then the probability that each of their children will be affected equals ___.\n\nOptions: \nA. 3 in 4\nB. 1 in 3\nC. 2 in 3\nD. 2 in 4\nE. 1 in 10\nF. 1\nG. 3 in 3\nH. 4 in 4\nI. 1 in 4\nJ. 1 in 2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "Since both parents are affected with an autosomal recessive disorder, they must have the genotype \"aa.\" Each child will receive one \"a\" allele from each parent, resulting in an \"aa\" genotype for 100% of their children. Thus, the probability that each of their children will be affected equals 1, which corresponds to options F, G, and H.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{F}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 169, "output_tokens": 86, "total_tokens": 255}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "Since both parents are affected with an autosomal recessive disorder, they must have the genotype \"aa.\" Each child will receive one \"a\" allele from each parent, resulting in an \"aa\" genotype for 100% of their children. Thus, the probability that each of their children will be affected equals 1, which corresponds to options F, G, and H.\n\nThe correct letter choice is \\boxed{F}.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.695e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5434", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the frequency of males affected with an X-linked recessive condition in a human population is .10 (one in ten), what will be the expected frequency of affected females?\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.001\nB. 0.01\nC. 0.1\nD. 0.15\nE. 0.0011\nF. 0.02\nG. 0.0001\nH. 0.0002\nI. 0.05\nJ. 0.2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "In an X-linked recessive condition, males have only one X chromosome, so if the frequency of affected males is 0.10, this means that 10% of males are affected. For females to be affected, they need to inherit two copies of the affected allele (one from each parent), so the frequency of affected females is computed as \\( (0.10)^2 = 0.01 \\) or 1%. Therefore, the expected frequency of affected females is \\boxed{B}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 173, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 275}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "In an X-linked recessive condition, males have only one X chromosome, so if the frequency of affected males is 0.10, this means that 10% of males are affected. For females to be affected, they need to inherit two copies of the affected allele (one from each parent), so the frequency of affected females is computed as \\( (0.10)^2 = 0.01 \\) or 1%. Therefore, the expected frequency of affected females is \\boxed{B}.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.715e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4934", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Your first action following confirmation of cardiac arrest is to:\n\nOptions: \nA. ensure the emergency team/services are called.\nB. administer an electric shock using a defibrillator.\nC. give 30 chest compressions.\nD. check the notes to see if the patient has a DNAR order.\nE. rush the patient to the emergency room.\nF. administer adrenaline.\nG. lay the patient down and elevate the legs.\nH. perform mouth-to-mouth resuscitation.\nI. check the patient's blood pressure.\nJ. give two rescue breaths.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. In the event of a cardiac arrest, the priority is to ensure that emergency services are called immediately, as this is vital for getting advanced medical assistance. Other actions, such as starting CPR or defibrillation, should follow after confirming that help is on the way.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 174, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 238}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. In the event of a cardiac arrest, the priority is to ensure that emergency services are called immediately, as this is vital for getting advanced medical assistance. Other actions, such as starting CPR or defibrillation, should follow after confirming that help is on the way.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.45e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5548", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If an X-linked recessive disorder is in Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium and the incidence in males equals 1 in 100, then the expected incidence of affected homozygous females would be _______.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 in 10 000\nB. 1 in 50 000\nC. 1 in 5000\nD. 1 in 8000\nE. 1 in 1000\nF. 1 in 40 000\nG. 1 in 200\nH. 1 in 100 000\nI. 1 in 20 000\nJ. 1 in 4000\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the expected incidence of affected homozygous females, we first determine that for an X-linked recessive disorder, the frequency of affected males (q) is 1/100 or 0.01. Assuming Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium, the expected frequency of affected females (homozygous) would be q², which is (0.01)² = 0.0001, or 1 in 10,000. Thus, the correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 200, "output_tokens": 102, "total_tokens": 302}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the expected incidence of affected homozygous females, we first determine that for an X-linked recessive disorder, the frequency of affected males (q) is 1/100 or 0.01. Assuming Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium, the expected frequency of affected females (homozygous) would be q², which is (0.01)² = 0.0001, or 1 in 10,000. Thus, the correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.12e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5394", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 68-year-old female has a history of breast cancer that has recurred twice in the past 5 years. She has undergone both radiation and chemotherapy for metastatic carcinoma to the bone. She presents to the office today to ask for help in dealing with midthoracic back pain to enable her to use less analgesic agents. The most appropriate osteopathic manipulative technique to treat this patient's spine is\n\nOptions: \nA. direct soft tissue technique\nB. high velocity, low amplitude\nC. high velocity, high amplitude\nD. indirect myofascial release\nE. low velocity, low amplitude\nF. isotonic exercise therapy\nG. mid velocity, mid amplitude\nH. static stretching technique\nI. direct myofascial release\nJ. isotonic resistance therapy\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most appropriate osteopathic manipulative technique for this patient, who has a history of breast cancer and is experiencing back pain, is likely to be D. indirect myofascial release. This technique is gentle, which is suitable for patients with a history of malignancy and chronic pain, as it minimizes discomfort and focuses on releasing tension without applying high forces. Using indirect techniques can be beneficial in such sensitive cases. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 225, "output_tokens": 95, "total_tokens": 320}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most appropriate osteopathic manipulative technique for this patient, who has a history of breast cancer and is experiencing back pain, is likely to be D. indirect myofascial release. This technique is gentle, which is suitable for patients with a history of malignancy and chronic pain, as it minimizes discomfort and focuses on releasing tension without applying high forces. Using indirect techniques can be beneficial in such sensitive cases. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.075000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5245", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 44-year-old female presents to the office for evaluation of a lump on her neck that she noted 1 week ago. She denies any tenderness, fever, weight loss, or fatigue. Physical examination reveals a 2-cm freely movable mass in the lower left lobe of the thyroid. In addition to thyroid-stimulating hormone and free thyroxine levels, the most appropriate initial method to investigate this lesion is\n\nOptions: \nA. Thyroid biopsy\nB. Positron emission tomography (PET) scan\nC. Lymph node biopsy\nD. Computed tomography (CT) scan\nE. an iodine131 scan\nF. a nuclear thyroid scan\nG. Endoscopic examination of the throat\nH. fine-needle aspiration\nI. Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI)\nJ. ultrasonography of the thyroid gland\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most appropriate initial method to investigate a thyroid lesion is to perform fine-needle aspiration (FNA), as it is a minimally invasive procedure that allows for cytological assessment of the nodule. This approach is particularly indicated in cases of solitary thyroid nodules to evaluate for malignancy. Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 238, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 308}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most appropriate initial method to investigate a thyroid lesion is to perform fine-needle aspiration (FNA), as it is a minimally invasive procedure that allows for cytological assessment of the nodule. This approach is particularly indicated in cases of solitary thyroid nodules to evaluate for malignancy. Thus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\).", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.769999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4982", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A person is prescribed Ropinirole 1.5 mg divided into three doses. How many micrograms is each dose? Choose one answer from the following:\n\nOptions: \nA. 5\nB. 5000\nC. 0.05\nD. 500\nE. 50,000\nF. 0.005\nG. 50\nH. 5,000,000\nI. 500,000\nJ. 0.5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To find the dosage in micrograms for each dose of Ropinirole, first convert 1.5 mg to micrograms. Since 1 mg equals 1000 micrograms, 1.5 mg equals 1500 micrograms. Dividing 1500 micrograms by 3 doses yields 500 micrograms for each dose.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 163, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 246}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To find the dosage in micrograms for each dose of Ropinirole, first convert 1.5 mg to micrograms. Since 1 mg equals 1000 micrograms, 1.5 mg equals 1500 micrograms. Dividing 1500 micrograms by 3 doses yields 500 micrograms for each dose.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{D}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.425e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5227", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which muscle is the most active during a right lateral excursion of the mandible?\n\nOptions: \nA. Left masseter muscle\nB. Right buccinator muscle\nC. Right temporalis muscle\nD. Right masseter muscle\nE. Right lateral pterygoid muscle\nF. Left medial pterygoid muscle\nG. Left temporalis muscle\nH. Left buccinator muscle\nI. Left lateral pterygoid muscle\nJ. Right medial pterygoid muscle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\). During a right lateral excursion of the mandible, the left lateral pterygoid muscle is primarily active as it assists in the movement of the mandible to the right side. This action involves the contralateral muscles for lateral movement, making the left lateral pterygoid crucial for this excursion.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 165, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 237}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{I}\\). During a right lateral excursion of the mandible, the left lateral pterygoid muscle is primarily active as it assists in the movement of the mandible to the right side. This action involves the contralateral muscles for lateral movement, making the left lateral pterygoid crucial for this excursion.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.795e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5128", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A couple comes for preconceptional genetic counseling because they both have a family history of α-thalassemia. The woman has a minimally decreased hemoglobin concentration. Genetic studies show a single gene deletion. The man has microcytic anemia and a two-gene deletion. If the two-gene deletion is in trans (one deletion on the maternal gene and one deletion on the paternal gene), which of the following percentages of their offspring will have a two-gene deletion?\n\nOptions: \nA. 75%\nB. 50%\nC. 20%\nD. 80%\nE. 10%\nF. 0%\nG. 66%\nH. 33%\nI. 25%\nJ. 100%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To determine the percentage of offspring that will inherit a two-gene deletion from the couple, we need to analyze the genetic combinations. The woman has a single gene deletion (αα/-) and the man has a two-gene deletion (α-/α-), indicating that their offspring can inherit combinations of these alleles. Out of the four possible combinations (αα/α-, α-/α-, αα/α-, α-/α-), only one combination will yield a two-gene deletion (α-/α-), giving a probability of 25%.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{I}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 212, "output_tokens": 125, "total_tokens": 337}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To determine the percentage of offspring that will inherit a two-gene deletion from the couple, we need to analyze the genetic combinations. The woman has a single gene deletion (αα/-) and the man has a two-gene deletion (α-/α-), indicating that their offspring can inherit combinations of these alleles. Out of the four possible combinations (αα/α-, α-/α-, αα/α-, α-/α-), only one combination will yield a two-gene deletion (α-/α-), giving a probability of 25%.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{I}.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.0001068}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4910", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Food supplements, including trace minerals and vitamins are frequently advertised with promising health benefits. Which of the following substance could be consumed in excess, i.e. well above the recommended daily requirement?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Vitamin C\nB. Vitamin D\nC. Zinc\nD. Vitamin A\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Vitamin A can accumulate in the body and lead to toxicity when consumed in excess, unlike Vitamin C and Zinc, which have tolerable upper intake levels, although long-term excessive consumption can be harmful. Vitamin D can also lead to toxicity but is less commonly consumed above recommended levels in dietary sources compared to Vitamin A.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 121, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 192}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Vitamin A can accumulate in the body and lead to toxicity when consumed in excess, unlike Vitamin C and Zinc, which have tolerable upper intake levels, although long-term excessive consumption can be harmful. Vitamin D can also lead to toxicity but is less commonly consumed above recommended levels in dietary sources compared to Vitamin A.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.075e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5552", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A randomized controlled trial is conducted to assess the effectiveness of a new combination-drug antihypertensive therapy (Drug X) compared with a standard antihypertensive single-drug therapy. Study participants include 140 women (70%) and 60 men (30%) ages 30 to 60 years, with baseline blood pressure measurements of 150/95 mm Hg or higher. The investigators defined antihypertensive therapy as effective if the treatment resulted in a blood pressure measurement below 140/90 mm Hg. When designing the study, the investigators set the probability of wrongly finding that Drug X is more effective than the standard therapy as 1%; they set the probability of wrongly finding that the effectiveness of the two drugs is the same as 10%. Which of the following is the most accurate estimate of the statistical power in this study?\n\nOptions: \nA. 90%\nB. 80%\nC. 1%\nD. 60%\nE. 20%\nF. 40%\nG. 70%\nH. 50%\nI. 10%\nJ. 30%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To estimate the statistical power of the study, we need to consider the type I error rate (alpha) and the type II error rate (beta). The investigators set the probability of wrongly claiming that Drug X is more effective (alpha) at 1%, which typically relates to a high statistical threshold. Since they defined the probability of wrongly finding that the effectiveness of the treatments is the same at 10%, this indicates that the beta (the probability of a type II error) is 10%, leading to a power of 90% (1 - beta). Therefore, the most accurate estimate of the statistical power in this study is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{A}\\)", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 285, "output_tokens": 134, "total_tokens": 419}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To estimate the statistical power of the study, we need to consider the type I error rate (alpha) and the type II error rate (beta). The investigators set the probability of wrongly claiming that Drug X is more effective (alpha) at 1%, which typically relates to a high statistical threshold. Since they defined the probability of wrongly finding that the effectiveness of the treatments is the same at 10%, this indicates that the beta (the probability of a type II error) is 10%, leading to a power of 90% (1 - beta). Therefore, the most accurate estimate of the statistical power in this study is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{A}\\)", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00012314999999999998}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4929", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: 960 mg of the antibacterial drug Cotrimoxazole is prescribed every 12 hours. What is the daily dose in grams? Choose one answer from the following:\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.92\nB. 0.192\nC. 0.96\nD. 0.0192\nE. 19.2\nF. 3.84\nG. 1920\nH. 960\nI. 2.88\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To calculate the daily dose of Cotrimoxazole, multiply the prescribed dose of 960 mg by the number of doses per day (2 doses): 960 mg x 2 = 1920 mg. Since there are 1000 mg in a gram, convert milligrams to grams: 1920 mg ÷ 1000 = 1.92 grams. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 159, "output_tokens": 88, "total_tokens": 247}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To calculate the daily dose of Cotrimoxazole, multiply the prescribed dose of 960 mg by the number of doses per day (2 doses): 960 mg x 2 = 1920 mg. Since there are 1000 mg in a gram, convert milligrams to grams: 1920 mg ÷ 1000 = 1.92 grams. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.664999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5243", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 15-year-old male presents to the office with the complaint of painless swelling in the left testicle that has varied in size over the past several months. There is no history of trauma. The lesion transilluminates well, and no inguinal nodes are palpable. Findings from a testicular scan are normal. The most appropriate management includes\n\nOptions: \nA. ultrasonic therapy\nB. cryotherapy\nC. needle biopsy\nD. radiation therapy\nE. laser therapy\nF. chemotherapy\nG. needle aspiration\nH. injection with a sclerosing agent\nI. surgical repair\nJ. oral medication\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most appropriate management for a painless swelling in the testicle that transilluminates well, particularly in a teenager, suggests the presence of a hydrocele or a similar benign condition. Given the nature of the lesion, the best initial approach is often needle aspiration to relieve symptoms or collect fluid for analysis if necessary. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 190, "output_tokens": 76, "total_tokens": 266}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most appropriate management for a painless swelling in the testicle that transilluminates well, particularly in a teenager, suggests the presence of a hydrocele or a similar benign condition. Given the nature of the lesion, the best initial approach is often needle aspiration to relieve symptoms or collect fluid for analysis if necessary. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.410000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5489", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Under what circumstances would you use antibiotics prior to catheterization?\n\nOptions: \nA. If the patient requests them.\nB. If the patient has a broken bone.\nC. If patient has an artificial heart valve.\nD. If the patient has a skin infection.\nE. If the patient is allergic to antibiotics.\nF. If the patient has had a catheter in situ for a week.\nG. If the patient does not have urinary tract infection.\nH. If the patient has a common cold.\nI. If the patient has a history of urinary tract infections.\nJ. If the patient has a high fever.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Patients with an artificial heart valve are at increased risk for infective endocarditis and may require antibiotic prophylaxis prior to certain procedures, including catheterization, to prevent infections. This practice is based on established guidelines aimed at safeguarding such high-risk individuals.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 185, "output_tokens": 59, "total_tokens": 244}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Patients with an artificial heart valve are at increased risk for infective endocarditis and may require antibiotic prophylaxis prior to certain procedures, including catheterization, to prevent infections. This practice is based on established guidelines aimed at safeguarding such high-risk individuals.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.314999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4931", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Blood clots are responsible for repeatedly blocking a catheter. What should you do?\n\nOptions: \nA. Use a syringe to remove the clot.\nB. Remove the catheter and recatheterize.\nC. Replace the catheter with a new one without informing medical staff.\nD. Inform the patient's family.\nE. Inform the patient.\nF. Ignore it and continue with the procedure.\nG. Flush the catheter with saline.\nH. Inform medical staff.\nI. Repeatedly press the catheter to remove the clot.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most appropriate action is to inform medical staff about the issue with the catheter. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{H}. This ensures that the necessary steps are taken to manage the situation safely and effectively, as a healthcare professional will be able to assess and address the problem appropriately.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 166, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 224}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most appropriate action is to inform medical staff about the issue with the catheter. Therefore, the correct answer is \\boxed{H}. This ensures that the necessary steps are taken to manage the situation safely and effectively, as a healthcare professional will be able to assess and address the problem appropriately.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.97e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5015", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A new blood test to detect prostate cancer is evaluated in 300 male volunteers. A needle biopsy of the prostate gland is done on all men with serum prostate-specific antigen concentrations greater than 5 ng/mL (N<4). One hundred men undergo biopsy procedures; 90 are found to have prostate cancer, and five are found to have chronic prostatitis. Which of the following is necessary to calculate the sensitivity of this test?\n\nOptions: \nA. Prevalence of chronic prostatitis in the general population\nB. Prevalence of prostate cancer in the general population\nC. Prostate biopsies of men with test results greater than 5 ng/mL\nD. Prostate biopsies of men with test results equal to or below 5 ng/mL\nE. Number of men with test results greater than 5 ng/mL and chronic prostatitis\nF. Incidence of prostate cancer in the general population\nG. Number of men with test results greater than 5 ng/mL and a normal biopsy specimen\nH. Number of men with test results equal to or below 5 ng/mL and a normal biopsy specimen\nI. Number of men with test results equal to or below 5 ng/mL and chronic prostatitis\nJ. Incidence of chronic prostatitis in the general population\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To calculate the sensitivity of the test, you need to know the true positives (men with prostate cancer) and the false negatives (men with prostate cancer but test results ≤ 5 ng/mL). Therefore, you need the number of men who had prostate biopsies with results below 5 ng/mL to account for those not detected by the test. Thus, the correct answer is \\boxed{D}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 329, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 411}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To calculate the sensitivity of the test, you need to know the true positives (men with prostate cancer) and the false negatives (men with prostate cancer but test results ≤ 5 ng/mL). Therefore, you need the number of men who had prostate biopsies with results below 5 ng/mL to account for those not detected by the test. Thus, the correct answer is \\boxed{D}.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.854999999999998e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5070", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 31-year-old man with a 5-year history of HIV infection comes to the office because of anal pain, particularly on defecation, for the past 4 months. He says he has seen spots of blood on the toilet tissue but has not had any other noticeable bleeding. He reports no change in bowel habits and has not had recent fever, chills, or rectal drainage. He says he and his partner engage in anal-receptive intercourse. His most recent CD4+ T-lymphocyte count 2 months ago was 350/mm3 ; HIV viral load at that time was undetectable. He currently is being treated with antiretroviral therapy. He has had no opportunistic infections. Medical history is also significant for syphilis and genital herpes treated with penicillin and acyclovir, respectively. He does not smoke cigarettes or drink alcoholic beverages. Vital signs are normal. Physical examination shows small bilateral inguinal lymph nodes, but respiratory, cardiac, and abdominal examinations disclose no abnormalities. There are several tender fleshy lesions around the perianal area. Rectal examination produces tenderness, but there is no rectal discharge. Test of the stool for occult blood is trace positive. Which of the following is the most appropriate pharmacotherapy at this time?\n\nOptions: \nA. Acyclovir\nB. Imiquimod\nC. Levofloxacin\nD. Metronidazole\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most appropriate pharmacotherapy in this case is \\boxed{B} (Imiquimod). The patient's symptoms, including anal pain, tender fleshy lesions around the perianal area, and a history of sexual activity, suggest anogenital warts likely due to human papillomavirus (HPV) infection. Imiquimod is an immune response modifier used to treat external genital warts.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 352, "output_tokens": 82, "total_tokens": 434}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most appropriate pharmacotherapy in this case is \\boxed{B} (Imiquimod). The patient's symptoms, including anal pain, tender fleshy lesions around the perianal area, and a history of sexual activity, suggest anogenital warts likely due to human papillomavirus (HPV) infection. Imiquimod is an immune response modifier used to treat external genital warts.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00010199999999999999}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5146", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A person weighs 62 kg. Their drug dose is 15 mg/kg. How many grams is their dose? Choose one answer from the following:\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.186\nB. 0.93\nC. 18.6 x 10^-3\nD. 0.0186\nE. 186\nF. 9.3\nG. 18.6\nH. 1.86\nI. 93\nJ. 930\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To calculate the drug dose, you multiply the weight (62 kg) by the dose per kg (15 mg/kg). The calculation is 62 kg * 15 mg/kg = 930 mg. Converting this to grams (since 1000 mg = 1 g), you get 930 mg = 0.93 g. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 165, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 246}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To calculate the drug dose, you multiply the weight (62 kg) by the dose per kg (15 mg/kg). The calculation is 62 kg * 15 mg/kg = 930 mg. Converting this to grams (since 1000 mg = 1 g), you get 930 mg = 0.93 g. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\).", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.335e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5112", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In a condition such as schizophrenia the recurrence risk will be greatest for which of the following relatives of an affected individual?\n\nOptions: \nA. Aunt\nB. Nephew\nC. Brother\nD. Grandchild\nE. Great-grandchild\nF. Second cousin\nG. Cousin\nH. Uncle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The recurrence risk for schizophrenia is highest among first-degree relatives of an affected individual, which includes parents, siblings, and children. Among the options provided, a brother is a first-degree relative and would therefore have the greatest risk. The correct answer is \\boxed{C}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 180}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The recurrence risk for schizophrenia is highest among first-degree relatives of an affected individual, which includes parents, siblings, and children. Among the options provided, a brother is a first-degree relative and would therefore have the greatest risk. The correct answer is \\boxed{C}.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.129999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5297", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 35-year-old female develops nausea and vomiting after she underwent a cholecystectomy for protracted ileus. Her body mass index was 23 kg/m2 before surgery, and, except for the cholecystitis, she was in good health. The patient remains unable to eat 6 days after surgery. Which of the following forms of nutritional support is most appropriate for this patient?\n\nOptions: \nA. oral protein-rich diet\nB. feeding through a nasogastric feeding tube\nC. feeding through a jejunostomy tube\nD. central hyperalimentation\nE. intravenous saline solution\nF. peripheral hyperalimentation\nG. oral carbohydrate-rich diet\nH. feeding through a gastrostomy tube\nI. oral fat-free modular diet\nJ. intravenous dextrose solution\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most appropriate form of nutritional support for this patient, who is unable to eat 6 days after surgery due to postoperative ileus, is B. feeding through a nasogastric feeding tube. This option allows for enteral feeding while bypassing the need for oral intake, which is necessary given her current condition. Other methods may require more invasiveness or are not suitable for her immediate needs. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 233, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 327}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most appropriate form of nutritional support for this patient, who is unable to eat 6 days after surgery due to postoperative ileus, is B. feeding through a nasogastric feeding tube. This option allows for enteral feeding while bypassing the need for oral intake, which is necessary given her current condition. Other methods may require more invasiveness or are not suitable for her immediate needs. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\).", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.135e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5448", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 26-year-old woman is brought to the emergency department because of an 8-hour history of severe back and abdominal pain and mild but persistent vaginal bleeding. Ultrasonography of the abdomen shows a 2-cm ectopic pregnancy in the ampulla. The ampulla has ruptured into the surrounding tissue. Fluid from this rupture will most likely be found in which of the following locations?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lesser peritoneal cavity\nB. Mesometrium\nC. Pouch of Douglas\nD. Uterine cavity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The Pouch of Douglas, also known as the rectouterine pouch, is the lowest point in the female pelvis and is where fluid from a ruptured ectopic pregnancy in the ampulla is most likely to collect due to gravity. Other options do not represent locations where fluid would typically accumulate in this scenario.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 172, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 243}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{C}. The Pouch of Douglas, also known as the rectouterine pouch, is the lowest point in the female pelvis and is where fluid from a ruptured ectopic pregnancy in the ampulla is most likely to collect due to gravity. Other options do not represent locations where fluid would typically accumulate in this scenario.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.84e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5071", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 7-year-old male is brought to the office for evaluation of school problems. The mother says that the teacher has told her that the patient is inattentive, has difficulty following sequential instructions, and often seems to drift off to sleep during class. A polysomnogram reveals obstructive sleep apnea. The most appropriate management is\n\nOptions: \nA. referral to a psychiatrist\nB. heart rate and apnea monitoring\nC. imipramine\nD. elevation of the head of the bed\nE. speech therapy\nF. prescription of stimulant medication\nG. prescription of sleeping pills\nH. surgical evaluation\nI. administration of caffeine\nJ. use of a humidifier\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most appropriate management for obstructive sleep apnea in a 7-year-old is typically a surgical evaluation to assess for potential adenotonsillar hypertrophy, which is a common cause of the condition in children. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\). Stimulant medications might be considered later if the sleep apnea is resolved and attention issues persist, but addressing the underlying cause is the priority.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 203, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 286}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most appropriate management for obstructive sleep apnea in a 7-year-old is typically a surgical evaluation to assess for potential adenotonsillar hypertrophy, which is a common cause of the condition in children. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{H}\\). Stimulant medications might be considered later if the sleep apnea is resolved and attention issues persist, but addressing the underlying cause is the priority.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.025e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5126", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 64-year-old male presents to the emergency room with a bloody nose that has been dripping out his nares for the past 2 hours. He denies any trauma, recent upper respiratory illness, or history of prior bloody nose. Past medical history is unremarkable, and he takes no medications. He has a blood pressure of 180/90 mmHg. Examination of the nasal passages reveals that the site of the bleeding is on the septal mucosa of the right naris. The most appropriate next step in management includes\n\nOptions: \nA. anterior packing\nB. placing an ice compress over the nose\nC. catheter balloon tamponade\nD. pinching the nares together for 5 minutes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most appropriate next step in management is A. anterior packing. Given that the bleeding is from the septal mucosa and has been persistent for 2 hours without prior measures to control it, anterior nasal packing is a commonly accepted first-line treatment to help control the bleeding. Other options like placing ice compresses or pinching the nares may provide temporary relief but aren’t effective for managing significant nasal bleeding. \n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 210, "output_tokens": 92, "total_tokens": 302}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most appropriate next step in management is A. anterior packing. Given that the bleeding is from the septal mucosa and has been persistent for 2 hours without prior measures to control it, anterior nasal packing is a commonly accepted first-line treatment to help control the bleeding. Other options like placing ice compresses or pinching the nares may provide temporary relief but aren’t effective for managing significant nasal bleeding. \n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.669999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4948", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A patient cuts a peripheral motor nerve in their wrist when they fall through a plate glass window. If the nerve does not regenerate, after about 6 months the muscles it normally innervates will show signs of which of the four options below?\n\nOptions: \nA. spastic paralysis\nB. contracture\nC. fasciculations\nD. muscle stiffness\nE. atrophy\nF. hypertrophy\nG. muscle rigidity\nH. flaccid paralysis\nI. muscle spasms\nJ. hyperreflexia\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. After a peripheral motor nerve is cut and does not regenerate, the muscles that it innervates will experience atrophy due to lack of stimulation. This is a typical response to denervation and disuse over time.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 170, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 222}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{E}. After a peripheral motor nerve is cut and does not regenerate, the muscles that it innervates will experience atrophy due to lack of stimulation. This is a typical response to denervation and disuse over time.", "ground_truth": "4", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.6699999999999996e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5059", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Examination of a patient indicates that they have a medially directed strabismus (squint). This could be due to damage to the\n\nOptions: \nA. oculomotor nerve.\nB. accessory nerve.\nC. trochlear nerve.\nD. ophthalmic trigeminal nerve.\nE. optic nerve.\nF. vestibulocochlear nerve.\nG. facial nerve.\nH. hypoglossal nerve.\nI. glossopharyngeal nerve.\nJ. abducens nerve.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{J}. Damage to the abducens nerve (cranial nerve VI) can result in medially directed strabismus due to the inability to properly abduct the affected eye, leading to the inward squint. Other nerves listed do not primarily control lateral eye movement.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 165, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 227}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{J}. Damage to the abducens nerve (cranial nerve VI) can result in medially directed strabismus due to the inability to properly abduct the affected eye, leading to the inward squint. Other nerves listed do not primarily control lateral eye movement.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.195e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5341", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A physician is conducting a retrospective review of a trial involving the use of Drug X in patients with a specific disease. It is known that Drug X is associated with an increased probability of cancer in patients who use the drug. A total of 600 individuals with a specific disease were included in the trial. Of the participants, 200 individuals received Drug X and 400 individuals did not receive it. One hundred individuals who received Drug X died of a particular type of cancer and 100 individuals who did not receive the drug died of the same type of cancer. Based on these data, which of the following is the relative risk of death from this type of cancer in individuals who take Drug X as compared with individuals who do not take Drug X?\n\nOptions: \nA. Individuals who take Drug X have two times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nB. Individuals who take Drug X have four times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nC. Individuals who take Drug X have three times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nD. Individuals who take Drug X have six times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nE. Individuals who do not take Drug X have three times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nF. Individuals who take Drug X have half the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nG. Individuals who take Drug X have an equal risk of dying from this type of cancer\nH. Individuals who do not take Drug X have two times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nI. Individuals who take Drug X have five times the risk of dying from this type of cancer\nJ. Individuals who take Drug X have zero risk of dying from this type of cancer\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "To calculate the relative risk (RR) of dying from cancer for those who took Drug X compared to those who did not, we use the formula: \n\n\\[ \\text{RR} = \\frac{\\text{Risk in Drug X group}}{\\text{Risk in non-Drug X group}} \\]\n\nFrom the data, the risk in the Drug X group is 100 deaths out of 200 users (0.5), and in the non-Drug X group, it's 100 deaths out of 400 users (0.25). Thus, the RR = 0.5 / 0.25 = 2. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 413, "output_tokens": 140, "total_tokens": 553}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "To calculate the relative risk (RR) of dying from cancer for those who took Drug X compared to those who did not, we use the formula: \n\n\\[ \\text{RR} = \\frac{\\text{Risk in Drug X group}}{\\text{Risk in non-Drug X group}} \\]\n\nFrom the data, the risk in the Drug X group is 100 deaths out of 200 users (0.5), and in the non-Drug X group, it's 100 deaths out of 400 users (0.25). Thus, the RR = 0.5 / 0.25 = 2. \n\nThe correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\).", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00014595}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4953", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 30-year-old woman, gravida 2, para 0, aborta 1, at 28 weeks' gestation comes to the office for a prenatal visit. She has had one previous pregnancy resulting in a spontaneous abortion at 12 weeks' gestation. Today, her vital signs are within normal limits. Physical examination shows a uterus consistent in size with a 28-week gestation. Fetal ultrasonography shows a male fetus with no abnormalities. Her blood group is O, Rh-negative. The father's blood group is B, Rh-positive. The physician recommends administration of Rho\n\nOptions: \nA. Development of polycythemia\nB. Formation of antibodies to RhB\nC. Development of lymphocytosis\nD. Formation of antibodies to RhO\nE. immune globulin to the patient. This treatment is most likely to prevent which of the following in this mother?\nF. Development of leukocytosis\nG. Formation of antibodies to RhD\nH. Development of anemia\nI. Formation of antibodies to RhC\nJ. Development of natural killer cells\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. Administering Rho(D) immune globulin to an Rh-negative mother helps prevent the formation of antibodies to RhD, which can occur if fetal Rh-positive blood enters the maternal circulation. This is crucial for preventing hemolytic disease of the newborn in current and future pregnancies.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 285, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 350}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. Administering Rho(D) immune globulin to an Rh-negative mother helps prevent the formation of antibodies to RhD, which can occur if fetal Rh-positive blood enters the maternal circulation. This is crucial for preventing hemolytic disease of the newborn in current and future pregnancies.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.174999999999998e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5023", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An 18-year-old primigravid woman comes for her initial prenatal visit at 16 weeks' gestation. She is not sure about the date of her last menstrual period but says that the pregnancy probably occurred immediately after she stopped taking oral contraceptives 5 months ago. Maternal serum α-fetoprotein (MSAFP) concentration is increased to 3 multiples of the median. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Amniocentesis for measurement of α-fetoprotein concentration\nB. Immediate cesarean section\nC. Hormone therapy to balance MSAFP levels\nD. Monitor patient without taking action\nE. Triple screening for MSAFP, serum β-hCG, and serum estriol concentrations\nF. Administer a pregnancy test\nG. Prescribe oral contraceptives\nH. Ultrasonography\nI. Repeat measurement of MSAFP concentration\nJ. Conduct a pelvic exam\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most appropriate next step in management after an increased maternal serum α-fetoprotein (MSAFP) concentration is to perform an ultrasound. This helps assess for potential neural tube defects or other anomalies that may be associated with elevated MSAFP. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{H}\\)", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 262, "output_tokens": 63, "total_tokens": 325}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most appropriate next step in management after an increased maternal serum α-fetoprotein (MSAFP) concentration is to perform an ultrasound. This helps assess for potential neural tube defects or other anomalies that may be associated with elevated MSAFP. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n\\(\\boxed{H}\\)", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.71e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5288", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Three weeks ago a 45-year-old man was admitted to the hospital because of frostbite of both feet. He was treated by rapid rewarming and protective care of the feet. All the toes on the right foot have turned black. He has become slightly febrile and progressively more confused during the past few days. Examination discloses cellulitis in the midfoot. Which of the following is the most appropriate treatment?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hyperbaric oxygen\nB. Skin grafting\nC. Intravenous fluids and electrolytes\nD. Application of topical collagenase\nE. Application of silver sulfadiazine\nF. Amputation\nG. Antibiotic therapy\nH. Application of warm compresses\nI. Placement of a wound VAC\nJ. Debridement of necrotic skin over the toes\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "Given the scenario of frostbite with blackened toes, fever, and progressive confusion indicating possible infection, the most appropriate treatment is **antibiotic therapy** to manage cellulitis and prevent further complications. Options like amputation or debridement may be necessary later, but initial empirical treatment for the suspected infection is crucial. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 232, "output_tokens": 77, "total_tokens": 309}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "Given the scenario of frostbite with blackened toes, fever, and progressive confusion indicating possible infection, the most appropriate treatment is **antibiotic therapy** to manage cellulitis and prevent further complications. Options like amputation or debridement may be necessary later, but initial empirical treatment for the suspected infection is crucial. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.099999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5518", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 13-month-old child is brought to the emergency department because of urticaria, swelling of the lips, and difficulty breathing immediately after eating an egg. A potential risk for hypersensitivity reaction is posed by vaccination against which of the following illnesses?\n\nOptions: \nA. Hepatitis\nB. Influenza\nC. Pertussis\nD. Poliomyelitis\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Vaccination against influenza can pose a risk for hypersensitivity reactions, particularly in children with a history of egg allergies, as many influenza vaccines are produced using egg-based methods. The other vaccines listed do not have a similar risk associated with egg allergy.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 138, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 196}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Vaccination against influenza can pose a risk for hypersensitivity reactions, particularly in children with a history of egg allergies, as many influenza vaccines are produced using egg-based methods. The other vaccines listed do not have a similar risk associated with egg allergy.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.5499999999999994e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4958", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 2-month-old female is brought to the office for her first routine health maintenance examination and for her immunization update. In order to determine whether or not any contraindications exist for diphtheria, tetanus, pertussis (DtaP) immunization, the parents should be questioned regarding\n\nOptions: \nA. allergy to eggs\nB. previous seizures\nC. dietary habits\nD. gestational age at birth\nE. family history of diabetes\nF. any chronic conditions\nG. history of heart disease\nH. Apgar scores at birth\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\). Previous seizures can be a contraindication to the DTaP vaccine, particularly if the seizures are related to prior vaccinations or neurological disorders. Therefore, it’s important to ask about the child's seizure history before administration.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 180, "output_tokens": 53, "total_tokens": 233}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{B}\\). Previous seizures can be a contraindication to the DTaP vaccine, particularly if the seizures are related to prior vaccinations or neurological disorders. Therefore, it’s important to ask about the child's seizure history before administration.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.8800000000000006e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5490", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of these is not necessary when examining the jugular venous pulse?\n\nOptions: \nA. Checking the pulse on both sides of the neck\nB. Using a magnifying glass\nC. Using a stethoscope\nD. Patient should be in a standing position\nE. Patient holding their breath\nF. Good lighting\nG. Turning the patient's head to the right\nH. Timing the pulsation with the radial pulse\nI. Patient's neck muscles should be relaxed\nJ. Patient lying at 45 degree angle\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The patient does not need to be in a standing position to examine the jugular venous pulse; it is typically assessed with the patient lying at a 45-degree angle for optimal visualization. Other options listed are important for an accurate assessment of the jugular venous pulse.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 171, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 235}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. The patient does not need to be in a standing position to examine the jugular venous pulse; it is typically assessed with the patient lying at a 45-degree angle for optimal visualization. Other options listed are important for an accurate assessment of the jugular venous pulse.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.405e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5007", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: When you examine a patient who has suffered an unfavourable fracture of the body of the mandible, you would expect the\n\nOptions: \nA. anterior fragment to be displaced anteriorly by the action of the lateral pterygoid muscle.\nB. posterior fragment to be displaced downwards by the action of the digastric muscle.\nC. anterior fragment to be displaced backwards by action of the temporalis muscle.\nD. posterior fragment to be displaced laterally by the action of the medial pterygoid muscle.\nE. anterior fragment to be displaced medially by the action of the medial pterygoid muscle.\nF. posterior fragment to be displaced upwards by the action of the masseter muscle.\nG. posterior fragment to be displaced anteriorly by the action of the lateral pterygoid muscle.\nH. anterior fragment to be displaced upwards by the action of the masseter muscle.\nI. anterior fragment to be displaced downwards by the action of the digastric muscle.\nJ. posterior fragment to be displaced medially by action of the medial pterygoid muscle.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. In an unfavourable fracture of the mandible, the posterior fragment is typically displaced anteriorly due to the action of the lateral pterygoid muscle, which pulls the head of the mandible forward. Other options do not accurately describe the expected displacement pattern associated with an unfavorable fracture of the mandible.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 283, "output_tokens": 71, "total_tokens": 354}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{G}. In an unfavourable fracture of the mandible, the posterior fragment is typically displaced anteriorly due to the action of the lateral pterygoid muscle, which pulls the head of the mandible forward. Other options do not accurately describe the expected displacement pattern associated with an unfavorable fracture of the mandible.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.505e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5236", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 51-year-old man comes to the office because of a 6-month history of a lump on his tongue that is interfering with his speech and eating; he also has had a 6.8-kg (15-lb) weight loss during this period. He has smoked 1 pack of cigarettes daily and has consumed six 12-oz bottles of beer on weekend nights during the past 30 years. His vital signs are within normal limits. Physical examination shows a 1.5-cm mass on the apex of the tongue. Further evaluation of the mass confirms squamous cell carcinoma. It is most appropriate to evaluate which of the following lymph nodes first for evidence of metastasis in this patient?\n\nOptions: \nA. Parotid\nB. Retropharyngeal\nC. Subclavian\nD. Submental\nE. Supraclavicular\nF. Popliteal\nG. Inferior deep cervical\nH. Preauricular\nI. Axillary\nJ. Inguinal\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "In cases of squamous cell carcinoma of the tongue, the most common initial sites for lymphatic spread are the cervical lymph nodes. Specifically, the inferior deep cervical nodes (level IV) are the most relevant to evaluate first for metastasis in tongue cancers. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 270, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 334}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "In cases of squamous cell carcinoma of the tongue, the most common initial sites for lymphatic spread are the cervical lymph nodes. Specifically, the inferior deep cervical nodes (level IV) are the most relevant to evaluate first for metastasis in tongue cancers. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{G}\\).", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.89e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5185", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 40-year-old man with paranoid schizophrenia is transferred to the emergency department from the residential facility where he lives 2 hours after having swallowed a nail. The patient says he does not have any symptoms. Medical history is otherwise unremarkable. His only current medication is haloperidol. The patient is not in acute distress. Vital signs are normal. Physical examination shows no abnormalities. Mental status examination discloses a flat affect, distractibility, and derailment of thoughts. X-ray of the abdomen is obtained and shows a 4-cm nail in the left upper quadrant. No free air is visible. After admitting the patient to the hospital, which of the following is the most appropriate management?\n\nOptions: \nA. Open laparotomy and removal of the nail through a gastrotomy incision\nB. Insertion of a nasogastric tube to suction out the nail\nC. Administration of activated charcoal to bind the nail and facilitate its removal\nD. Removal of the nail through endoscopic esophagogastroscopy\nE. Administration of a barium swallow to track the nail's passage\nF. Administration of ipecac to induce vomiting and expectoration of the nail\nG. Administering a laxative to expedite the passage of the nail\nH. Observation to allow passage of the nail via normal peristalsis\nI. Use of a magnet to draw out the nail\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most appropriate management in this case is \\boxed{H}. The patient is asymptomatic, with the nail situated in the left upper quadrant and no signs of perforation or obstruction; therefore, a conservative observation approach is warranted to allow the nail to pass through the gastrointestinal tract. Surgical intervention or other invasive measures should be reserved for patients showing symptoms or complications.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 346, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 418}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most appropriate management in this case is \\boxed{H}. The patient is asymptomatic, with the nail situated in the left upper quadrant and no signs of perforation or obstruction; therefore, a conservative observation approach is warranted to allow the nail to pass through the gastrointestinal tract. Surgical intervention or other invasive measures should be reserved for patients showing symptoms or complications.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.510000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5049", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A problem in comparing older adults' memory for recent events and events that happened a long time ago is that recent events\n\nOptions: \nA. Can be verified while older events often cannot\nB. Are influenced by current mental state\nC. May be very well rehearsed\nD. Are more likely to be distorted or embellished\nE. Are often less significant than older events\nF. Have a different emotional impact\nG. Have no denominator to help in computing an average\nH. Can be easily confused with older events\nI. Are more likely to be forgotten\nJ. Are far more meaningful\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Recent events can often be verified through documentation or other reliable sources, while older events may lack such verification, leading to challenges in comparison. This makes establishing accurate memories between the two categories difficult for older adults.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 185, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 237}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Recent events can often be verified through documentation or other reliable sources, while older events may lack such verification, leading to challenges in comparison. This makes establishing accurate memories between the two categories difficult for older adults.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.8949999999999996e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5038", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A source emits a sound from one medium with a certain velocity, intensity, frequency and wavelength. When the sound exits the first medium and enters a denser medium, all of the following changes EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. tone\nB. amplitude\nC. wavelength\nD. direction\nE. pitch\nF. frequency\nG. resonance\nH. volume\nI. intensity\nJ. velocity\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. When sound enters a denser medium, its frequency remains the same; only the wavelength, velocity, intensity, and direction may change. Therefore, frequency is the only characteristic among the options provided that does not change as the sound moves from one medium to another.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 146, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 207}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{F}. When sound enters a denser medium, its frequency remains the same; only the wavelength, velocity, intensity, and direction may change. Therefore, frequency is the only characteristic among the options provided that does not change as the sound moves from one medium to another.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.85e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5255", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The group that permits analysis of the entire natural history of HIV/AIDS is:\n\nOptions: \nA. Non-seroconverters\nB. Seroconverters\nC. Short-term survivors with low levels of CD4+ cells\nD. Long-term survivors\nE. Long-term survivors with high levels of CD4+ cells\nF. Persistent seronegatives\nG. Short-term survivors\nH. Seroconverters with fluctuating levels of CD4+ cells\nI. Persistent seropositives\nJ. Long-term survivors with low levels of CD4+ cells\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Long-term survivors provide valuable insights into the natural history of HIV/AIDS, as they represent individuals who have managed to live with the virus for an extended period, often showing varied immunological responses and health outcomes. Analyzing their cases can enhance understanding of the virus's progression and potential treatment strategies.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 177, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 245}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Long-term survivors provide valuable insights into the natural history of HIV/AIDS, as they represent individuals who have managed to live with the virus for an extended period, often showing varied immunological responses and health outcomes. Analyzing their cases can enhance understanding of the virus's progression and potential treatment strategies.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.735e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4924", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following best accounts for the negative slope of the liquid-solid equilibrium line in the phase diagram for water?\n\nOptions: \nA. H2O(s) has a greater density than H2O(l), which is the result of the van der Waals forces between water molecules.\nB. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l) which results from the crystalline framework that forms due to hydrogen bonds.\nC. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l) which causes the solid to form liquid under low pressure conditions.\nD. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l), this is caused by the metallic bonds formed between water molecules.\nE. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l), which causes the solid to form liquid under high pressure conditions.\nF. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l), which is a result of the covalent bonds formed between water molecules.\nG. H2O(s) has a greater density than H2O(l), which results from the hydrogen bonds formed between water molecules.\nH. H2O(s) has a greater density than H2O(l), which results in the solid forming liquid under low pressure conditions.\nI. H2O(s) has a greater density than H2O(l), which is due to the ionic bonds formed between water molecules.\nJ. H2O(s) has a greater density than H2O(l), which causes the solid to form liquid under high pressure conditions.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l) because of the crystalline structure formed by hydrogen bonds in ice, which takes up more space than the liquid state. This is why the liquid-solid equilibrium line in the phase diagram for water has a negative slope.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 383, "output_tokens": 65, "total_tokens": 448}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. H2O(s) has a lower density than H2O(l) because of the crystalline structure formed by hydrogen bonds in ice, which takes up more space than the liquid state. This is why the liquid-solid equilibrium line in the phase diagram for water has a negative slope.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.644999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5142", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A police officer carries out hundreds of traffic stops every year. When his supervisor is reviewing the officer’s records for the past year, he notices that the officer is equally likely to stop people of various genders, ages, and races. However, he is significantly more likely to write tickets for middle-aged white males with dark hair and eyes. When confronted with this fact, the officer truthfully states that he has no idea why that is, and that it must simply be a coincidence. Unbeknownst to the officer, this behavior is tied to the fact that these men look like his father, with whom he had an abusive relationship as a child. What psychological framework would directly address the unconscious bias in his behavior? \n\nOptions: \nA. Gestalt\nB. Developmental\nC. Biopsychological\nD. Humanistic\nE. Cognitive behavioral\nF. Positive psychology\nG. Evolutionary\nH. Behaviorist\nI. Social cognitive\nJ. Psychoanalytic\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\). The psychoanalytic framework addresses unconscious motivations and biases, stemming from early life experiences—such as the officer's abusive relationship with his father—leading to his discriminatory behavior despite his conscious beliefs. This framework emphasizes how unconscious factors influence behavior, which aligns with the officer's lack of awareness regarding his bias.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 261, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 331}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{J}\\). The psychoanalytic framework addresses unconscious motivations and biases, stemming from early life experiences—such as the officer's abusive relationship with his father—leading to his discriminatory behavior despite his conscious beliefs. This framework emphasizes how unconscious factors influence behavior, which aligns with the officer's lack of awareness regarding his bias.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.115e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4991", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Grandparents with grandchildren in college report feeling especially loved when such grandchildren\n\nOptions: \nA. Buy them college merchandise as a token of love and appreciation\nB. Pay a surprise visit and ask for advice\nC. Dedicate a social media post to them\nD. Ask them to attend college events and introduce them to friends\nE. Visit during the holidays and bring gifts\nF. Send a text message every day\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Grandparents often feel especially loved when their grandchildren actively include them in their college experience, such as asking them to attend events and introducing them to friends, which fosters deeper connections. This choice emphasizes the importance of shared experiences and recognition of their role in the grandchild's life, which likely resonates with them.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 148, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 218}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. Grandparents often feel especially loved when their grandchildren actively include them in their college experience, such as asking them to attend events and introducing them to friends, which fosters deeper connections. This choice emphasizes the importance of shared experiences and recognition of their role in the grandchild's life, which likely resonates with them.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.419999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4966", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What nutritional strategies will not improve performance during prolonged endurance type exercise?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Tapering\nB. The classic glycogen loading regime\nC. Hydration during exercise\nD. Exogenous carbohydrate ingestion during exercise\nE. Carbohydrate loading\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Tapering refers to a reduction in training load prior to an event to allow the body to recover and adapt; it does not directly improve performance during prolonged endurance exercises like the other options listed, which all focus on nutrition and hydration strategies that can enhance performance.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 116, "output_tokens": 61, "total_tokens": 177}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Tapering refers to a reduction in training load prior to an event to allow the body to recover and adapt; it does not directly improve performance during prolonged endurance exercises like the other options listed, which all focus on nutrition and hydration strategies that can enhance performance.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.4e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5052", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A cross between two true breeding lines one with dark blue flowers and one with bright white flowers produces F1 offspring that are light blue. When the F1 progeny are selfed a 1:2:1 ratio of dark blue to light blue to white flowers is observed. What genetic phenomenon is consistent with these results?\n\nOptions: \nA. overdominance\nB. polygenic inheritance\nC. epistasis\nD. pleiotropy\nE. lethal alleles\nF. genetic drift\nG. genetic linkage\nH. codominance\nI. incomplete dominance\nJ. inbreeding depression\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. The F1 offspring being light blue indicates that the flower color trait exhibits incomplete dominance, where neither allele is completely dominant over the other. The observed 1:2:1 ratio of phenotypes in the F2 generation further supports this inheritance pattern, as it reflects the mixing of the two parental traits.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 188, "output_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 258}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. The F1 offspring being light blue indicates that the flower color trait exhibits incomplete dominance, where neither allele is completely dominant over the other. The observed 1:2:1 ratio of phenotypes in the F2 generation further supports this inheritance pattern, as it reflects the mixing of the two parental traits.", "ground_truth": "8", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.02e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5303", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: In terms of price per calorie, which of the following foods is the cheapest and most nutritious?\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Bag of chips\nB. Chicken breast\nC. Banana\nD. Slice of bread\nE. Pasta\nF. Slice of pizza\nG. Apple\nH. Broccoli\nI. Can of soda\nJ. Cheese burger\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "In terms of price per calorie and nutritional value, the most likely correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Pasta is typically low in cost, offers a significant number of calories, and can provide essential carbohydrates and some nutrients, making it a balance of affordability and nutritional value compared to the other options listed. Foods like bagged chips and soda are low in nutrition despite their calorie content, while items like chicken breast and broccoli, though nutritious, tend to cost more per calorie.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 135, "output_tokens": 94, "total_tokens": 229}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "In terms of price per calorie and nutritional value, the most likely correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Pasta is typically low in cost, offers a significant number of calories, and can provide essential carbohydrates and some nutrients, making it a balance of affordability and nutritional value compared to the other options listed. Foods like bagged chips and soda are low in nutrition despite their calorie content, while items like chicken breast and broccoli, though nutritious, tend to cost more per calorie.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.664999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5484", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: All of the following are true regarding the function of neurons EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. The refractory period prevents the neuron from initiating a new action potential.\nB. The transmitting neuron secretes neurotransmitters into the synaptic cleft from its dendrites.\nC. An action potential is initiated when the axon hillock reaches the threshold potential.\nD. The action potential travels along the axon away from the cell body.\nE. Hyperpolarization occurs when the membrane potential becomes more negative than the resting potential.\nF. The flow of sodium into the neuron depolarizes the membrane in the first phase of an action potential.\nG. Hyperpolarization at the end of an action potential is one mechanism by which neurons limit the rate at which action potentials may fire.\nH. The neuron releases neurotransmitters into the synaptic cleft from the axon terminals.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Neurons secrete neurotransmitters from their axon terminals into the synaptic cleft, not from their dendrites. All other statements about neuronal function are accurate.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 238, "output_tokens": 43, "total_tokens": 281}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. Neurons secrete neurotransmitters from their axon terminals into the synaptic cleft, not from their dendrites. All other statements about neuronal function are accurate.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.15e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5199", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Each of the following are aspects of the McDonaldization of Society EXCEPT:\n\nOptions: \nA. The extensive use of technology in everyday life\nB. Rationalization of decisions into cost/benefit analysis structures and away from traditional modes of thinking\nC. A focus on efficiency and predictability in all aspects of society\nD. An intense effort on achieving sameness across diverse markets\nE. Increased emphasis on quantity over quality\nF. The prioritization of profit over societal well-being\nG. Bureaucratic organization that formalizes well-establish division of labor and impersonal structures\nH. The standardization of societal norms and practices\nI. A shift from individual craftsmanship to mass production\nJ. A dissolution of hierarchical modes of authority into collaborative teambased decision protocols\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. The McDonaldization of Society emphasizes bureaucratic organization and formal structures, while a dissolution of hierarchical modes of authority into collaborative team-based decision protocols does not align with the principles of McDonaldization, which typically promotes more standardized and rationalized approaches. Therefore, option J stands out as the exception.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 221, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 289}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{J}. The McDonaldization of Society emphasizes bureaucratic organization and formal structures, while a dissolution of hierarchical modes of authority into collaborative team-based decision protocols does not align with the principles of McDonaldization, which typically promotes more standardized and rationalized approaches. Therefore, option J stands out as the exception.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.395e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5198", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why do vigorous CD8 cell responses in chronically infected HIV-positive individuals fail to eliminate the virus?\n\nOptions: \nA. Inadequate MHC Class I presentation\nB. Suboptimal CTL\nC. Overproduction of interferon gamma\nD. Overactive T-helper cells\nE. Absence of dendritic cells\nF. CTL exhaustion\nG. Presence of neutralizing antibodies\nH. Epitope escape\nI. Insufficient natural killer cell activity\nJ. Lack of B cell response\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\). CTL (cytotoxic T lymphocyte) exhaustion occurs in the context of chronic HIV infection due to persistent antigenic stimulation, leading to a progressive decline in the functionality and number of CD8 T cells. This exhaustion prevents the effective elimination of the virus despite the presence of vigorous immune responses.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 167, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 239}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\(\\boxed{F}\\). CTL (cytotoxic T lymphocyte) exhaustion occurs in the context of chronic HIV infection due to persistent antigenic stimulation, leading to a progressive decline in the functionality and number of CD8 T cells. This exhaustion prevents the effective elimination of the virus despite the presence of vigorous immune responses.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.825e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4873", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A problem for immune system theories of senescence is\n\nOptions: \nA. Determining what first causes the senescence in the immune system\nB. The immune system theories do not explain the role of lifestyle in senescence\nC. Immune system theories do not explain the role of genetic factors in senescence\nD. Immune system theories are too complex to test effectively\nE. The lack of information about senescence in general\nF. That the immune system improves with age\nG. Immune system theories cannot account for the environmental factors in senescence\nH. That the immune system does not decline with age\nI. The difficulty of isolating the immune system from other bodily systems\nJ. Auto-immune disorders are far too rare\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Determining what first causes the senescence in the immune system presents a significant challenge in understanding how and why the immune system deteriorates as individuals age. This issue underscores the complexities of the relationship between immune function and the aging process.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 57, "total_tokens": 272}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Determining what first causes the senescence in the immune system presents a significant challenge in understanding how and why the immune system deteriorates as individuals age. This issue underscores the complexities of the relationship between immune function and the aging process.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.644999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4955", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A phase 2, multicenter trial was conducted to determine the efficacy of a new vaccine for prevention of HIV infection. The study enrolled 4000 subjects, aged 20 to 65 years. Of these subjects, 2100 were men and 1900 were women; 2500 were white, 1000 were African American, 300 were Hispanic, and 200 were Asian/Pacific Islanders. Results of the trial showed no overall benefit of the vaccine. However, post hoc analysis disclosed a small but statistically significant vaccine protection among African American subjects. Which of the following is the most accurate rationale for questioning the validity of efficacy analysis of the HIV vaccine among the African American study subjects?\n\nOptions: \nA. HIV infection is more prevalent among African American populations\nB. The vaccine had no overall benefit\nC. The study was not blinded\nD. The age of the subjects could have affected the results\nE. The study did not disclose the number of subjects who were actually infected with HIV\nF. There was a Type II error\nG. Vaccine response among African American subjects was not the primary outcome measure\nH. The vaccine response varied across different ethnicities\nI. There was a Type I error\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most accurate rationale for questioning the validity of efficacy analysis of the HIV vaccine among the African American study subjects is: \\(\\boxed{B}\\). Since the study showed no overall benefit of the vaccine, any statistically significant result observed in the African American subgroup may not be reliable or meaningful, and could be a chance finding rather than a true effect. Therefore, interpreting a small benefit in the context of no overall efficacy raises concerns about its validity.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 309, "output_tokens": 89, "total_tokens": 398}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most accurate rationale for questioning the validity of efficacy analysis of the HIV vaccine among the African American study subjects is: \\(\\boxed{B}\\). Since the study showed no overall benefit of the vaccine, any statistically significant result observed in the African American subgroup may not be reliable or meaningful, and could be a chance finding rather than a true effect. Therefore, interpreting a small benefit in the context of no overall efficacy raises concerns about its validity.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.974999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5141", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If the human norovirus cannot be cultured in cell cultures how can it best be studied?\n\nOptions: \nA. Volunteer studies\nB. Animal studies using non-human primates\nC. Through computer simulation models of the virus\nD. By studying the virus's effect on plant cells\nE. In cells using replicon systems\nF. Animal models\nG. By isolating the virus in a laboratory setting\nH. In cells using non-replicon systems\nI. Deductions from the 3 human ORF's of the virus genome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Replicon systems allow researchers to study the virus's genetic material and replication mechanisms without needing to culture the virus in traditional cell cultures, making it an effective method for studying norovirus. This approach can provide insights into its biology, pathogenesis, and potential treatments.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 175, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 239}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{E}. Replicon systems allow researchers to study the virus's genetic material and replication mechanisms without needing to culture the virus in traditional cell cultures, making it an effective method for studying norovirus. This approach can provide insights into its biology, pathogenesis, and potential treatments.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.465e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5212", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which level of personality description appears to show the most change with age?\n\nOptions: \nA. Values\nB. Communication skills\nC. Identity\nD. Traits\nE. Self-esteem\nF. Interests\nG. Social roles\nH. Emotional responses\nI. Coping strategies\nJ. Personal concerns\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Identity tends to show the most change with age as individuals navigate different life stages, experiences, and transitions which can significantly alter their sense of self and how they perceive their roles in society. Other aspects may also change, but identity is generally more fluid and subject to transformation throughout life.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 126, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 193}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{C}. Identity tends to show the most change with age as individuals navigate different life stages, experiences, and transitions which can significantly alter their sense of self and how they perceive their roles in society. Other aspects may also change, but identity is generally more fluid and subject to transformation throughout life.", "ground_truth": "9", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.91e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4954", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Over 1 year, a study is conducted to assess the antileukemic activity of a new tyrosine kinase inhibitor in patients with chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis. All patients enrolled in the study are informed that they would be treated with the tyrosine kinase inhibitor. They are assigned to successive dose cohorts of 300 to 1000 mg/day of the drug. Six to eight patients are assigned to each dose. Treatment efficacy is determined based on the results of complete blood counts and bone marrow assessments conducted regularly throughout the study. This study is best described as which of the following?\n\nOptions: \nA. Prospective observational study\nB. Randomized clinical trial\nC. Quasi-experimental study\nD. Retrospective study\nE. Cohort study\nF. Open-labeled clinical trial\nG. Case-control study\nH. Crossover study\nI. Double-blind clinical trial\nJ. Longitudinal study\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The study is best described as an open-labeled clinical trial because all patients are informed they will be treated with the tyrosine kinase inhibitor and are assigned to successive dose cohorts. The study assesses the drug's efficacy over time with direct treatment allocation, distinguishing it from other study types. Therefore, the correct choice is \\boxed{F}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 256, "output_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 324}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The study is best described as an open-labeled clinical trial because all patients are informed they will be treated with the tyrosine kinase inhibitor and are assigned to successive dose cohorts. The study assesses the drug's efficacy over time with direct treatment allocation, distinguishing it from other study types. Therefore, the correct choice is \\boxed{F}.", "ground_truth": "5", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.92e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5412", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: For Binge Eating Disorder it is incorrect that:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. BED patients have higher odds of developing obesity\nB. Binge Eating episodes in BED are usually richer in calories than those of BN, leading patients to obesity\nC. Spontaneous remission is a possible outcome\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. \n\nWhile binge eating episodes in Binge Eating Disorder (BED) may be calorie-rich, the comparison to Bulimia Nervosa (BN) is not always about calorie density leading directly to obesity. It is also important to note that BED can result in various eating patterns that do not consistently align with those seen in BN. Therefore, option B may be misleading.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 120, "output_tokens": 83, "total_tokens": 203}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{B}. \n\nWhile binge eating episodes in Binge Eating Disorder (BED) may be calorie-rich, the comparison to Bulimia Nervosa (BN) is not always about calorie density leading directly to obesity. It is also important to note that BED can result in various eating patterns that do not consistently align with those seen in BN. Therefore, option B may be misleading.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.78e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5570", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Inviduals suffering from inhalant allergies may also react to cross- reacting food allergens. A person suffering from a natural latex allergy might not react to one of the following allergens\n\n\nOptions: \nA. peanuts\nB. figs\nC. tomato\nD. avocado\nE. peach\nF. kiwi\nG. strawberries\nH. mango\nI. chestnuts\nJ. banana\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Individuals with a natural latex allergy often show cross-reactivity with certain foods, particularly those that contain proteins similar to those in latex. Chestnuts are one of the few foods considered less likely to provoke a reaction in latex-allergic individuals, whereas other fruits and nuts may cause issues.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 143, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 210}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Individuals with a natural latex allergy often show cross-reactivity with certain foods, particularly those that contain proteins similar to those in latex. Chestnuts are one of the few foods considered less likely to provoke a reaction in latex-allergic individuals, whereas other fruits and nuts may cause issues.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.165000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_4906", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Vitamin D deficiency can often be found as a single nutrient deficiency, that is, in an otherwise well-nourished person. The main reason this can happen is because:\n\n\nOptions: \nA. Vitamin D is not essential for the body, therefore, its deficiency doesn't affect the overall nourishment.\nB. Vitamin D is a rare nutrient and can only be found in a few expensive food items.\nC. Vitamin D absorption is not affected by the presence of other nutrients in the body.\nD. The content of vitamin D in foods depends on the soil in which the food was grown so is not related to wealth or age.\nE. Overconsumption of Vitamin D can lead to its deficiency.\nF. Diets containing sufficient other nutrients to promote growth can increase the requirement of vitamin D so that it becomes limiting.\nG. Most vitamin D in the body does not come from food so access to food is not an important determinant of vitamin D status.\nH. Foods containing large amounts of vitamin D are eaten by both poor and wealthy people according to various cultural reasons.\nI. Vitamin D is present in all types of food, therefore, its deficiency is usually accompanied by other nutrient deficiencies.\nJ. Vitamin D is only produced in the body during certain times of the year.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{G}. Most of the vitamin D in the body is synthesized through skin exposure to sunlight, rather than from dietary sources, making access to food less critical for maintaining vitamin D levels compared to sun exposure. This explains why vitamin D deficiency can occur in an otherwise well-nourished individual.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 315, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 381}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The most likely correct answer is \\boxed{G}. Most of the vitamin D in the body is synthesized through skin exposure to sunlight, rather than from dietary sources, making access to food less critical for maintaining vitamin D levels compared to sun exposure. This explains why vitamin D deficiency can occur in an otherwise well-nourished individual.", "ground_truth": "6", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.685e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5312", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A new enzyme is found in a transgenic mice that participates in synthesis of an unknown product using two reactants. When using radiolabeled compounds to study the enzyme, it is found that the enzyme catalyzes a process that switches a nitrogen group on one reactant to the other reactant. Which of the following categories would this new enzyme fall under?\n\nOptions: \nA. Ligase\nB. Hydrolase\nC. Transferase\nD. Synthetase\nE. Phosphatase\nF. Lyase\nG. Oxidoreductase\nH. Decarboxylase\nI. Kinase\nJ. Isomerase\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The new enzyme described in the question participates in switching a nitrogen group from one reactant to another. This process is indicative of transferring a functional group from one molecule to another, which classifies the enzyme as a transferase. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 199, "output_tokens": 58, "total_tokens": 257}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The new enzyme described in the question participates in switching a nitrogen group from one reactant to another. This process is indicative of transferring a functional group from one molecule to another, which classifies the enzyme as a transferase. Therefore, the correct answer is \\(\\boxed{C}\\).", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.465e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5180", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A 57-year-old man receives radiation therapy for a squamous cell carcinoma of the lung. Despite therapy, the tumor progressively increases in size, and he dies 6 months later. His tumor cells contain a point mutation in the p53 gene (TP53), leading to an inactive gene product. Based on this finding, the progressive tumor growth despite irradiation therapy is most likely to be related to a defect in cell cycle arrest in which of the following phases of the cell cycle?\n\nOptions: \nA. Metaphase\nB. G1\nC. Prophase\nD. G0\nE. Prometaphase\nF. S phase\nG. Anaphase\nH. M\nI. Telophase\nJ. G2\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The p53 protein plays a critical role in the G1 phase of the cell cycle by inducing cell cycle arrest in response to DNA damage. A mutation in the p53 gene leads to a failure of this checkpoint, allowing cells with damaged DNA to continue to proliferate, contributing to tumor progression even after radiation therapy.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 215, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 287}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. The p53 protein plays a critical role in the G1 phase of the cell cycle by inducing cell cycle arrest in response to DNA damage. A mutation in the p53 gene leads to a failure of this checkpoint, allowing cells with damaged DNA to continue to proliferate, contributing to tumor progression even after radiation therapy.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.544999999999999e-05}}
{"global_index": "MMLUPro_health_5143", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sauna use, sometimes referred to as \"sauna bathing,\" is characterized by short-term passive exposure to extreme heat. This exposure elicits mild hyperthermia – an increase in the body's core temperature – that induces a thermoregulatory response involving neuroendocrine, cardiovascular, and cytoprotective mechanisms that work together to restore homeostasis and condition the body for future heat stressors… In recent decades, sauna bathing has emerged as a means to increase lifespan and improve overall health, based on compelling data from observational, interventional, and mechanistic studies. Of particular interest are the findings from studies of participants in the Kuopio Ischemic Heart Disease Risk Factor (KIHD) Study, an ongoing prospective population-based cohort study of health outcomes in more than 2,300 middle-aged men from eastern Finland, which identified strong links between sauna use and reduced death and disease… The KIHD findings showed that men who used the sauna two to three times per week were 27 percent less likely to die from cardiovascular-related causes than men who didn't use the sauna.[2] Furthermore, the benefits they experienced were found to be dose-dependent: Men who used the sauna roughly twice as often, about four to seven times per week, experienced roughly twice the benefits – and were 50 percent less likely to die from cardiovascular-related causes.[2] In addition, frequent sauna users were found to be 40 percent less likely to die from all causes of premature death. These findings held true even when considering age, activity levels, and lifestyle factors that might have influenced the men's health.[2]... The KIHD also revealed that frequent sauna use reduced the risk of developing dementia and Alzheimer's disease in a dose-dependent manner. Men who used the sauna two to three times per week had a 66 percent lower risk of developing dementia and a 65 percent lower risk of developing Alzheimer's disease, compared to men who used the sauna only one time per week… The health benefits associated with sauna use extended to other aspects of mental health, as well. Men participating in the KIHD study who used the sauna four to seven times per week were 77 percent less likely to develop psychotic disorders, regardless of the men's dietary habits, socioeconomic status, physical activity, and inflammatory status (as measured by C-reactive protein)…Exposure to high temperature stresses the body, eliciting a rapid, robust response. The skin and core body temperatures increase markedly, and sweating ensues. The skin heats first, rising to 40°C (104°F), and then changes in core body temperature occur, rising slowly from 37°C (98.6°F, or normal) to 38°C (100.4°F) and then rapidly increasing to 39°C (102.2°F)…  Cardiac output, a measure of the amount of work the heart performs in response to the body's need for oxygen, increases by 60 to 70 percent, while the heart rate (the number of beats per minute) increases and the stroke volume (the amount of blood pumped) remains unchanged.[5] During this time, approximately 50 to 70 percent of the body's blood flow is redistributed from the core to the skin to facilitate sweating. The average person loses approximately 0.5 kg of sweat while sauna bathing.[11] Acute heat exposure also induces a transient increase in overall plasma volume to mitigate the decrease in core blood volume. This increase in plasma volume not only provides a reserve source of fluid for sweating, but it also acts like the water in a car's radiator, cooling the body to prevent rapid increases in core body temperature and promoting heat tolerance… Repeated sauna use acclimates the body to heat and optimizes the body's response to future exposures, likely due to a biological phenomenon known as hormesis, a compensatory defense response following exposure to a mild stressor that is disproportionate to the magnitude of the stressor. Hormesis triggers a vast array of protective mechanisms that not only repair cell damage but also provide protection from subsequent exposures to more devastating stressors… The physiological responses to sauna use are remarkably similar to those experienced during moderate- to vigorous-intensity exercise. In fact, sauna use has been proposed as an alternative to exercise for people who are unable to engage in physical activity due to chronic disease or physical limitations.[13]\n\nThe review article sources a lot of data from Finland population studies, where the incidence of sauna use is substantially higher than most countries. Using the data, which of the following is something that is more plausible in Finland than elsewhere?\n\nOptions: \nA. Lower rates of cardiovascular-related deaths among frequent sauna users.\nB. More gold medals in adolescent skiing.\nC. A higher percentage of the population with optimized body's response to heat.\nD. Higher incidence of sauna-related injuries.\nE. Increased prevalence of heat tolerance in the population.\nF. Decreased rates of psychotic disorders among frequent sauna users.\nG. Improved marriage satisfaction rates.\nH. An 86-year old male mayor who is revered in the community.\nI. Decreased risk of dementia and Alzheimer's disease due to frequent sauna use.\nJ. Increased rate of pets in the household.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Based on the findings from the KIHD Study, frequent sauna use is associated with a decreased risk of dementia and Alzheimer's disease, which is particularly relevant to Finland where sauna culture is prevalent. Therefore, it is more plausible to see this health benefit manifest in the Finnish population compared to other countries.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 1094, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 1161}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{I}. Based on the findings from the KIHD Study, frequent sauna use is associated with a decreased risk of dementia and Alzheimer's disease, which is particularly relevant to Finland where sauna culture is prevalent. Therefore, it is more plausible to see this health benefit manifest in the Finnish population compared to other countries.", "ground_truth": "7", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 0.00020429999999999998}}
