{"global_index": "MusicTheoryBench_197", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is the harmonic minor scale of G♯?\n\nOptions: \nA. L:1/4\nM:none\nK:C\n F4 | G4 | A4 | B4 | c4 | =d4 | e4 | f4 |] %8\nB. L:1/4\nM:none\nK:C\n E4 | F4 | ^G4 | A4 | B4 | _c4 | ^d4 | e4 |] %8\nC. L:1/4\nM:none\nK:C\n A,,4 | B,,4 | ^C,4 | D,4 | E,4 | ^F,4 | G,4 | A,4 |] %8\nD. All the first three options are incorrect\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The harmonic minor scale of G♯ consists of the notes G♯, A♯, B, C♯, D♯, E, and F♯. Analyzing the provided options, none represent the harmonic minor scale of G♯. Therefore, the correct answer is option D, as all the first three options are incorrect.\n\nThe answer is \\boxed{D}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 229, "output_tokens": 81, "total_tokens": 310}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The harmonic minor scale of G♯ consists of the notes G♯, A♯, B, C♯, D♯, E, and F♯. Analyzing the provided options, none represent the harmonic minor scale of G♯. Therefore, the correct answer is option D, as all the first three options are incorrect.\n\nThe answer is \\boxed{D}.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 8.295000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MusicTheoryBench_203", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following is a different enharmonic interval from the double-augmented fifth?\n\nOptions: \nA. Major sixth\nB. Diminished seventh\nC. Double-augmented fourth\nD. Major sixth and diminished seventh\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. A major sixth and a diminished seventh are both distinct from the nature of a double-augmented fifth, as they represent different intervals altogether. Therefore, option D correctly identifies both a major sixth and diminished seventh as not enharmonically equivalent to a double-augmented fifth.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 112, "output_tokens": 64, "total_tokens": 176}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{D}. A major sixth and a diminished seventh are both distinct from the nature of a double-augmented fifth, as they represent different intervals altogether. Therefore, option D correctly identifies both a major sixth and diminished seventh as not enharmonically equivalent to a double-augmented fifth.", "ground_truth": "3", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.52e-05}}
{"global_index": "MusicTheoryBench_204", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements about chords are correct? ( )\n① There are 2 common chords between C major harmony and c natural minor harmony\n② The Neapolitan sixth chords in C major and c minor are identical\n③ The chords adjacent to the Neapolitan sixth chord are composed of minor third and perfect fourth intervals\n\nOptions: \nA. 0\nB. 1\nC. 2\nD. 3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "Let's evaluate each statement:\n\n① There are indeed 2 common chords between C major and C natural minor (C major and A minor).\n② The Neapolitan sixth chord in C major (Db6) and C minor (Db6) consists of the same notes, so this statement is correct.\n③ The chords adjacent to the Neapolitan sixth are typically based on a combination of intervals that include minor thirds and perfect fourths, but the precise intervals may vary based on context.\n\nTherefore, two statements are correct (① and ②), making the answer \\boxed{2}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 151, "output_tokens": 117, "total_tokens": 268}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "Let's evaluate each statement:\n\n① There are indeed 2 common chords between C major and C natural minor (C major and A minor).\n② The Neapolitan sixth chord in C major (Db6) and C minor (Db6) consists of the same notes, so this statement is correct.\n③ The chords adjacent to the Neapolitan sixth are typically based on a combination of intervals that include minor thirds and perfect fourths, but the precise intervals may vary based on context.\n\nTherefore, two statements are correct (① and ②), making the answer \\boxed{2}.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 9.285000000000001e-05}}
{"global_index": "MusicTheoryBench_205", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following options represent two notes that form a diatonic semitone?\n\nOptions: \nA. L:1/4\nM:4/2\nK:Ab\n ^G4 A4 |] %1\nB. L:1/4\nM:4/2\nK:B\n [E,F,]4 |] %1\nC. L:1/4\nM:4/2\nK:Eb\n [=A,B,]4 |] %1\nD. L:1/4\nM:4/2\nK:Db\n B,4 =B,4 |] %1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. In this option, the notes E and F are a diatonic semitone apart, as they represent consecutive notes in the C major scale (E and F are adjacent). The other options do not provide pairs of notes that represent a diatonic semitone.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 198, "output_tokens": 62, "total_tokens": 260}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{B}. In this option, the notes E and F are a diatonic semitone apart, as they represent consecutive notes in the C major scale (E and F are adjacent). The other options do not provide pairs of notes that represent a diatonic semitone.", "ground_truth": "2", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.69e-05}}
{"global_index": "MusicTheoryBench_209", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following combinations contains a syncopation?\n\nOptions: \nA. L:1/4\nM:6/8\nK:C\n F F/ F F/ |] %1\nB. L:1/4\nM:3/4\nK:C\n  F F/ F F/ |] %1\nC. L:1/8\nM:2/4\nK:C\n  F2 z F |] %1\nD. L:1/16\nM:4/4\nK:C\n F4 FF z F F4 F4 |] %1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). In option A, the rhythm consists of a combination of quarter notes with the notation suggesting the presence of emphasis on off-beats (syncopation) due to the phrasing of the notes. The other options do not display the same rhythmic complexity indicative of syncopation.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 191, "output_tokens": 66, "total_tokens": 257}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\(\\boxed{A}\\). In option A, the rhythm consists of a combination of quarter notes with the notation suggesting the presence of emphasis on off-beats (syncopation) due to the phrasing of the notes. The other options do not display the same rhythmic complexity indicative of syncopation.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 0.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.825e-05}}
