{"global_index": "MusicTheoryBench_62", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of the following, what is the best technique for using recordings in score study?\n\nOptions: \nA. Listen to a variety of interpretations\nB. Use recordings at every rehearsal\nC. Listen to famous recordings\nD. Practice conducting to the recording\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The best technique for using recordings in score study is to listen to a variety of interpretations. This allows you to understand different approaches to the piece and to consider various artistic choices. It broadens your perspective and can inform your own interpretation more effectively than focusing on a single famous recording.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 113, "output_tokens": 67, "total_tokens": 180}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The best technique for using recordings in score study is to listen to a variety of interpretations. This allows you to understand different approaches to the piece and to consider various artistic choices. It broadens your perspective and can inform your own interpretation more effectively than focusing on a single famous recording.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{A}.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 5.715e-05}}
{"global_index": "MusicTheoryBench_94", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of the following choral settings, which is better suited for homophonic pieces, but can create issues of the singers being able to listen to other parts?\n\nOptions: \nA. Blocked formation\nB. Matrix formation\nC. Columnar formation\nD. Mixed formation\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Blocked formation is better suited for homophonic pieces because it allows the singers to sing together more cohesively. However, this arrangement can lead to challenges in being able to hear and blend with other parts effectively.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 119, "output_tokens": 52, "total_tokens": 171}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. Blocked formation is better suited for homophonic pieces because it allows the singers to sing together more cohesively. However, this arrangement can lead to challenges in being able to hear and blend with other parts effectively.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 4.905e-05}}
{"global_index": "MusicTheoryBench_111", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: How can conductors best promote cultural diversity in their music programs?\n\nOptions: \nA. Take yearly trips to non-Western countries.\nB. Include non-Western musical repertoire into concerts.\nC. Have a non-Western music day camp.\nD. Assign non-Western textbooks to all the students.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The best option for conductors to promote cultural diversity in their music programs is B. Include non-Western musical repertoire into concerts. This approach allows for the direct incorporation of diverse cultural elements into the music being performed and experienced by the audience, fostering an appreciation for different musical traditions within the program. The other options may be beneficial but are not as effective in actively integrating diversity into the music itself. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{B}.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 123, "output_tokens": 91, "total_tokens": 214}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The best option for conductors to promote cultural diversity in their music programs is B. Include non-Western musical repertoire into concerts. This approach allows for the direct incorporation of diverse cultural elements into the music being performed and experienced by the audience, fostering an appreciation for different musical traditions within the program. The other options may be beneficial but are not as effective in actively integrating diversity into the music itself. \n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{B}.", "ground_truth": "1", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 7.305e-05}}
{"global_index": "MusicTheoryBench_159", "question": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements about harmonics and overtones is incorrect?\n\nOptions: \nA. Harmonics and overtones have the same definition, for example: the frequency of the first overtone is twice the frequency of the fundamental.\nB. The frequency of overtones and harmonics are in an integer multiple relationship with the fundamental frequency.\nC. Partial frequencies may not have an integer multiple relationship with the fundamental frequency.\nD. In instruments with clear pitch, the fundamental frequency is usually the most obvious to the ear.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.", "llm_selected": "gpt-4o-mini", "generated_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. This statement is incorrect because harmonics refer to frequencies that are integer multiples of the fundamental frequency (first harmonic is the fundamental, second harmonic is twice the frequency, etc.), while overtones refer to frequencies above the fundamental; thus, the first overtone is actually the second harmonic, not the same as the fundamental.", "token_usage": {"input_tokens": 166, "output_tokens": 72, "total_tokens": 238}, "success": true, "provider": "openai", "error": null, "evaluation_result": {"extracted_answer": "The correct answer is \\boxed{A}. This statement is incorrect because harmonics refer to frequencies that are integer multiples of the fundamental frequency (first harmonic is the fundamental, second harmonic is twice the frequency, etc.), while overtones refer to frequencies above the fundamental; thus, the first overtone is actually the second harmonic, not the same as the fundamental.", "ground_truth": "0", "score": 1.0, "metric": "mcq_accuracy", "inference_cost": 6.81e-05}}
